      "exp_en": "The pulse is empty especially on the front right position. The diagnosis is Lung Qi Deficiency. The Lung Qi can be weak due to hereditary weakness, emotional stress (sadness, grief), poor habits (prolonged stooping over a desk), or from improper treatment of external pathogens (wind-cold, wind-heat) the expected pulse in this pattern is an Empty pulse, particularly in the right front pulse position. An Empty pulse feels soft and gives in and offers no resistance when extra pressure is applied to the pulse. It indicates a qi deficiency. The expected tongue in this pattern is a pale tongue. As qi moves the blood, when there is a deficiency of qi the tongue will be pale from the weak qi not bringing blood to the tongue. Just having a little shortness of breath and an empty pulse are sufficient to make the diagnosis of Lung Qi Deficiency. The treatment principle is Tonify Lung Qi and Warm Yang. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 573; 2005 Edition, page 545; 1989 Edition, page 232",
      "exp_hant": "脈象呈虛脈，尤以右寸為甚。診斷為肺氣虛。肺氣虛弱可由先天不足、情志耗傷（悲傷、憂愁）、不良習慣（長期伏案）、或外邪（風寒、風熱）治療不當所致。本證預期脈象為虛脈，尤其明顯於右寸部位。虛脈按之柔軟、稍加重按即無力抵抗，主氣虛。本證預期舌象為淡舌。因氣能行血，氣虛則無力將血帶至舌面，故舌色淡白。僅需輕微氣短加上虛脈，即足以診斷為肺氣虛。治療原則為補肺氣、溫陽。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, 第573頁；2005年版，第545頁；1989年版，第232頁"
