      "exp_en": "The T stands for thymus which is the organ involved in their final stage of development. Lymphocytes originate in the bone marrow and then migrate to other parts of the lymphatic system such as the lymph nodes, spleen, and then to the thymus. There are two main types of lymphatic cells, T cells (thymus cells) and B cells (bursa-derived cells), which are found in the lymph fluid. T cells defend the body from inside the cell. B cells produce antibodies against pathogens but after an attack, some B cells retain the ability to produce an antibody to serve as a \"memory\" system if the body is attacked by a similar pathogen in the future. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 144",
      "exp_hant": "T代表胸腺（thymus），是這類細胞完成最後發育階段的器官。淋巴細胞起源於骨髓，隨後遷移至淋巴系統其他部位，如淋巴結、脾臟，最後到達胸腺。淋巴細胞主要分為兩大類：T細胞（胸腺細胞）與B細胞（源自法氏囊），兩者皆存在於淋巴液中。T細胞在細胞內部防禦身體；B細胞則產生抗體對抗病原體，且部分B細胞在病原體攻擊後仍保有產生抗體的能力，作為未來遭受類似病原體攻擊時的「記憶」系統。Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 第7版, Pagana, 第144頁"
