      "exp_en": "There are three pulses which focus on rhythm. These are the hurried pulse (cu mai), the knotted pulse (jie mai), and the intermittent pulse (dai mai). The hurried pulse (cu mai) is rapid and irregularly skips beats. It can indicate Heat agitating the Blood. It is a Yang pulse. The knotted pulse (jie mai) is a slow pulse that irregularly skips beats. It can indicate Cold blocking the Qi and Blood or Deficient Qi, Blood, or Jing. It is a Yin pulse. An intermittent pulse (dai mai) skips beats at a regular interval and skips more beats than either a hurried or knotted pulse. An intermittent pulse (dai mai) is often caused by a serious Heart problem or it can indicate that the zang fu are exhausted. It is a Yin pulse. The Web That Has No Weaver, Kaptchuk, 2000, page 201",
