      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Kidney Yang Deficiency, Kidney Qi not Firm. The treatment principle is to Tonify and Raise Qi, Consolidate Bladder Qi, Tonify-Warm Kidney Yang. REN-6 and DU-20 raise the qi and is a combo that can treat enuresis, incontinence, and prolapses. REN-6 also tonifies the qi. KI-3, BL-23, and REN-4 tonify and warm the Kidneys. LU-7 and KI-6 can also be used to open the Directing Vessel to tonify the Kidneys. ST-36, SP-6, and BL-20 can also be used to tonify qi in general. Feeling tired, cold, frequent urination, pale tongue, and deep-weak pulse indicate a Kidney yang deficiency. Losing urine when coughing points to the Kidney qi not being firm. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1994, page 529; this case is not included in the 2008 edition",
      "exp_hant": "診斷為腎陽虛、腎氣不固。治療原則為補氣升提、固攝膀胱之氣、溫補腎陽。氣海配百會能升提中氣，是治療遺尿、失禁及臟器下垂的常用組合，氣海亦能補氣；太谿、腎俞、關元能溫補腎陽。足三里、三陰交、脾俞則可用於一般補氣。疲倦怕冷、頻尿、舌淡、脈沉弱，皆指向腎陽虛；咳嗽時漏尿則顯示腎氣不固。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1994年版, 第529頁；此案例未收錄於2008年版"
    },
    {
      "number": 48,
      "question_en": "A 63 year-old female patient complains of dizziness and drowsiness. These symptoms started two months ago. The symptoms were mild at first and occurred occasionally with a slight headache on the lateral side of the head. After a strong emotional upset last week, the dizziness, drowsiness, and headache all worsened. She now also complains of palpitations, insomnia, general lassitude, intercostal and epigastric distention, poor appetite, sour-bitter mouth taste, and dry stool. Thirst and urination are normal. The tongue has a dark-pale body with a thick-greasy and slightly yellow coating. The pulse is wiry-slippery and a little rapid. The physical exam shows Blood Pressure 110/60, Pulse 76, Respirations 18, and weight 110 lbs. Electrocardiogram shows right bundle branch block, chronic. MRI of the head is within normal limits. The treatment given was PC-6 (nei guan), SP-4 (gong sun), GB-13 (ben shen), and LR-5 (li gou); After five treatments she reported that her headaches were gone and that her dizziness was less frequent. However, she still complained of intercostal and epigastric distention and poor sleep. How would you modify the acupuncture treatment?",
      "question_hant": "一名63歲女性患者主訴頭暈與嗜睡，症狀始於兩個月前。初期症狀輕微，偶爾發作，並伴隨頭部側面輕微頭痛。上週經歷強烈情緒波動後，頭暈、嗜睡及頭痛皆加重。她現在還主訴心悸、失眠、全身倦怠、脅肋及胃脘脹滿、食慾不振、口苦口酸，以及大便乾燥。口渴與小便情況正常。舌質暗淡，苔厚膩且略黃，脈弦滑略數。理學檢查顯示血壓110/60，脈搏76，呼吸18次，體重110磅。心電圖顯示慢性右束支傳導阻滯，頭部核磁共振檢查結果正常。原治療處方為內關、公孫、本神、蠡溝；治療五次後，她表示頭痛已消失，頭暈發作頻率降低，但仍主訴脅肋及胃脘脹滿、睡眠不佳。你會如何調整針灸治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
