      "exp_en": "The Eight Principles associated with this case are Internal, Empty, Hot. As there are no symptoms-signs of an exterior syndrome (aversion to cold/wind, body aches, feverish, floating pulse, etc), this patient has an interior syndrome. An interior syndrome involves internal organs or an internal excess pathogenic factor. The symptoms and signs point to an internal deficiency of yin. If yin qi is chronically weak, the yin is consumed by the yang which leaves the yang in relative excess. It is important to note that the yin deficiency (night sweats, dry stools, dry throat, thirst, dark scanty urine, floating-empty-rapid pulse) can be deficient for years before any symptoms-signs of empty heat manifest (feeling hot in the afternoon, five-palms heat, red tongue without coating). The empty heat shows a worsening of the chronic yin deficiency Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 458",
      "exp_hant": "此案例之八綱辨證為裡、虛、熱。由於並無表證之症狀徵象（惡寒／惡風、身痛、發熱、浮脈等），故此患者屬裡證。裡證涉及內臟器官或內在實邪。其症狀徵象指向內在陰虛。若陰氣長期虛弱，陰為陽所耗，使陽相對呈現偏亢之勢。值得注意的是，陰虛（盜汗、大便乾燥、咽乾、口渴、小便短赤、浮虛數脈）可能已存在多年，之後才出現虛熱的症狀徵象（午後發熱、五心煩熱、舌紅無苔）。虛熱的出現，顯示慢性陰虛正在加重。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015年版, 第458頁"
