        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "LU-9 (tai yuan), BL-13 (fei shu), DU-12 (zhen zhu)",
          "hant": "太淵、肺俞、身柱",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis is a combination of Channel-Collateral and Internal Patter, Cold, and a combination of Excess and Deficiency. The etiology is Pathogenic Cold Invasion. The channel pattern is Channel Obstruction by Pathogenic Cold. The organ pattern is Heart Qi Injury (Heart Painful Obstruction). The treatment principle is Expel Pathogenic Cold, Remove Channel Obstruction, Alleviate Pain, Tonify Heart Qi and Calm the Shen. LI-4 threaded to PC-8 expels external wind, relieves the exterior pattern, removes channel obstruction. Warm needle at this point expels external cold in the channels. DU-14 is the point where all the yang channels meet. It is selected to remove du mai obstruction and strengthen the antipathogenic qi (zheng qi) by tapping the energy of all the yang channels. ST-36 is selected to strengthen the zheng qi, remove channel obstruction in the legs and alleviate pain. This original prescription did not address one of the underlying causes of the problem, which is Heart Painful Obstruction. In this case, there is an external invasion of cold in the joints which then progresses to the interior and affects the Heart (palpitations, insomnia, stifling chest sensation). PC-4 was selected to calm the Shen and, as the xi-cleft point, remove chest obstruction and stifling chest sensations. As a local point, it treats elbow and wrist pain by clearing channel obstruction. BL-15 regulates the Heart, calms the Shen, and harmonizes ying and wei qi. DU-9 removes the stifling chest sensation and regulates the qi. It is located below T7 and has a strong local effect in alleviating spine pain and tonifying the Heart qi. The prescription with SP-9 aims at resolving accumulated Dampness via the Spleen but the edema is caused by a water metabolism disruption which always happens when the symptoms of the chest are at their worst. This is due to a zhong qi (chest qi) stagnating giving rise to water accumulation and SOB. This explains the lack of thirst and urine output and shortness of breath. Resolving the Heart Injury by Cold will allow the water metabolism to return to normal and Lung qi to descend. The prescription with BL-17 focuses on tonifying Blood which is not part of the diagnosis. The prescription with LU-9 focuses on strengthening the Lung qi which is not the main issue here. Even though the pulse is rapid, there is no heat in this case. The rapid pulse is due to the Heart disharmony forcing the Heart to increase output due to weakness. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 113-117",
      "exp_hant": "八綱辨證屬經絡與裡證合併，性寒，虛實夾雜。病因為寒邪外襲。經絡辨證為寒邪阻滯經絡；臟腑辨證為心氣受損（心痺）。治療原則為祛寒邪、通經絡、止痛、補心氣、安神。合谷透勞宮能祛外風、解表、通經絡，溫針於此穴則可祛除經絡中之外寒。大椎為諸陽經交會之處，取之可袪除督脈之阻滯，並藉諸陽經之氣以扶助正氣。足三里能扶助正氣、疏通下肢經絡阻滯並止痛。此原處方未能針對本病根本病因之一，即心痺。本案為寒邪外襲關節，繼而入裡影響於心（表現為心悸、失眠、胸悶）。故選郄門以安神，並以其郄穴之性通利胸中阻滯、緩解胸悶；作為局部穴，亦可清通經絡以治肘腕疼痛。心俞能調心、安神、調和營衛。至陽能除胸悶、理氣，其位於第七胸椎下方，對緩解脊背疼痛及補益心氣有明顯之局部作用。方中選用陰陵泉旨在藉脾以化除蓄積之濕，然本案水腫實因水液代謝失常所致，此常於胸中症狀最劇時發生，乃因中氣（胸中之氣）鬱滯致水液停聚而生氣短，此亦可解釋患者口不渴、尿量減少及氣短之表現。若能解除寒邪所傷之心氣，水液代謝自可復常，肺氣亦得以肅降。選用膈俞之處方著重於補血，與本證診斷不符。選用太淵之處方著重於補益肺氣，並非本案主要問題所在。雖然脈數，然本案並無熱象，脈數乃因心臟功能失調，心臟因虛弱而被迫加強搏動所致。Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi，第113-117頁"
    },
