      "exp_en": "The Chinese term \"fa re\" is often translated as fever but it literally means \"emission of heat\". The fever translation is not totally correct as a patient can have an objective sensation of heat on the forehead without having an actual fever. When the forehead feels hot on palpation while the patient complains of fear of cold, then that indicates external invasion of Wind. When the forehead feels hot on palpation and the patient has a subjective experience of feeling hot, then that indicates internal Heat. If the forehead feels hotter than the palms, this can indicate external Heat but if the palms feel hotter than the forehead, this can indicate interior Heat. Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 517",
      "exp_hant": "中文「發熱」一詞常譯為fever，但字面意義為「熱之外發」。譯為fever並不完全準確，因患者可能主觀上並無實際發燒，卻在額頭有客觀之發熱感。若觸診額頭發熱，且患者兼有惡寒之訴，則提示風邪外襲；若觸診額頭發熱，且患者自覺發熱，則提示內熱。若額頭較手掌更熱，可提示外感熱邪；若手掌較額頭更熱，則可能提示裡熱。Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004年版，第517頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 77,
      "question_en": "Last week a 43 year-old female patient had a continuous fever. She had sweating which did not relieve the fever. She also had belching, thirst without a desire to drink, loose stools, and abdominal fullness. She has a red tongue with a sticky-yellow coating. Yesterday her fever increased, was very thirsty for cold drinks, sweated profusely, and the tongue was red and the coating was no longer sticky but was dry and yellow. What is the point prescription for this patient?",
      "question_hant": "一位43歲女性患者上週出現持續發熱，汗出而熱不解，並伴有噯氣、口渴不欲飲、大便溏薄、腹脹。舌紅，苔黃膩。昨日發熱加重，口渴喜冷飲，大汗淋漓，舌紅，舌苔不再黏膩而轉為乾黃。此患者應選用何種穴位處方？",
      "image": null,
