      ],
      "exp_en": "The disease progression for this patient can be seen from different perspectives. The progression is from the middle burner to the middler burner using Triple Burner differentiation. It can be from qi level to qi level using the Four Level differentiation. Using a mixed differentiation the progression can be from qi level to yang ming stage. This is a sequence that begins with damp-heat and then the heat intensifies and burns up the dampness. The first clinical picture is Spleen-Stomach Damp-Heat. This pattern can be categorized as belonging to the middle burner of the Triple Burner pattern differentiation and the qi level of the Four Levels pattern differentiation. The second clinical picture is Stomach Heat. This pattern can be categorized as belonging to the middle burner, the qi level, and also as a yang ming channel pattern of the Six Stages pattern differentiation. The Six stages do not have a pattern corresponding to Spleen-Stomach Damp-Heat. The two yang ming patterns are yang ming channel and yang ming organ patterns, both involving heat but not dampness. The treatment principle for yang ming channel pattern of the Six Stages is to Clear Stomach Heat. The combination of LI-11 and DU-14 are global points to reduce excess heat. The combination of ST-44 and ST-43 specifically reduce excess heat in the Stomach. Other points that can be included are ST-25 if there is constipation and heat in the intestines. ST-21 can be add to support the other points in clearing Stomach Heat. ST-34, the xi-cleft point, can also be added to treat the acute nature of the disorder. The Rx with SP-6 is more for the original presentation of symptoms (Stomach-Spleen Damp-Heat) where the focus is on clearing heat in the Stomach-Spleen and resolving dampness. Other points to include there would be REN-12, REN-9, BL-20, and BL-22. The Rx with GB-34 treats Gallbladder heat at the qi level. The Rx with LI-4 is more applicable to the wei qi level with external pathogenic Dry-Heat which is drying up fluids where the focus of treatment would be to release the exterior, clear heat, and promote fluids. . Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 757, 773, 775, 784",
      "exp_hant": "此患者之病程可由不同角度分析。若依三焦辨證，病程由中焦傳至中焦；若依衛氣營血辨證之四層次，則由氣分傳至氣分；若採混合辨證，則可視為由氣分傳至陽明階段。此一演變乃先見濕熱，繼而熱漸熾盛而灼耗濕邪。第一階段之證候為脾胃濕熱，屬三焦辨證之中焦，亦屬衛氣營血辨證之氣分。第二階段之證候為胃熱，屬三焦辨證之中焦、衛氣營血之氣分，亦屬六經辨證之陽明經證。六經辨證中並無與脾胃濕熱相對應之證型。陽明證有陽明經證與陽明腑證二者，皆屬熱證而非濕證。六經辨證中陽明經證之治療原則為清胃熱。曲池配大椎為清洩實熱之全身性要穴組合；內庭配陷谷則專治胃中實熱。若兼有便秘腸熱，可加天樞；天樞可加強清胃熱之效；亦可加郄穴梁丘以治其病勢之急。以三陰交為主之處方則較適用於原先脾胃濕熱之表現，著重於清脾胃之熱並化濕，可再加中脘、水分、脾俞、胃俞。以陽陵泉為主之處方則治氣分之膽熱。以合谷為主之處方較適用於衛分階段外感燥熱傷津之證，治療重點在於解表、清熱、生津。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015年版，第757、773、775、784頁"
    },
