      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. The DEEP PULSE is one of the eight basic types of pulses. This pulse can only be palpated at the middle and deep levels but particularly at the deep level. The pulse feels sunken as if underneath the muscle. Deepness is relative to the body build. What is normal for an obese patient might be abnormal for a thin patient. The deep pulse indicates that the patient has an interior pattern. A deep-full pulse indicates inner and full Cold, Heat, food retention, stuck qi or Blood. A deep-weak pulse indicates yang xu. The SCATTERED PULSE is an empty type pulse. Rather than the pulse flowing, the scattered pulse feels like it is broken into tiny dots. The pulse is relatively superficial and disappears with stronger palpation. The scattered pulse indicates severe qi and Blood xu, especially xu of Kidney qi and Original Qi. This pulse indicates a serious disorder. If this pulse manifests in pregnancy, it can indicate a miscarriage can occur. The FINE PULSE is a type of empty pulse. It is a thin pulse like a thread and yet clear, straight, and soft. It feels like a fine line under the palpating finger. The fine pulse indicates severe xu of Blood and also qi. A fine-weak pulse in young patients indicates weak Original Qi. The CHOPPY PULSE is one of the eight basic pulses. This pulse feels rough, jagged, and is short. It does not have a wave like a normal pulse does which flows from the rear to the front in a smooth and continuous wave. The choppy pulse does not have this continuous wave movement through the three positions. The choppy pulse is felt in each of the three positions separately. The choppy pulse indicates xu of Blood or Essence. It can also manifest after profuse sweating, vomiting, or diarrhea. It is a bad sign to have this pulse during pregnancy and can indicate a miscarriage is about to happen. Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 497",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確之答案。沉脈為八種基本脈象之一，僅能於中候與深候（尤以深候為主）觸得，脈感如沉伏於肌肉之下。沉之程度須視患者體型而定，肥胖患者之正常脈象對瘦弱患者而言可能屬異常。沉脈提示患者屬裡證。沉而有力提示裡實之寒、熱、食滯、氣滯或血瘀；沉而無力則提示陽虛。散脈屬虛脈之一種，脈搏並非連續流動，而是感覺如破碎成細點，脈位偏浮，重按則消失。散脈提示氣血嚴重虧虛，尤以腎氣與元氣之虛為甚，屬病情嚴重之徵象；若孕婦見此脈，可能提示流產之虞。細脈屬虛脈之一種，脈細如線，然清晰、平直而柔軟，觸感如細線。細脈提示血虛及氣虛皆嚴重；年輕患者見細弱脈，則提示元氣虛弱。澀脈為八種基本脈象之一，脈感粗澀、不流利且短促，不若正常脈搏般自尺至寸呈平順連續之波動。澀脈於三部分別觸得，並無連續之波動感。澀脈提示血虛或精虛，亦可見於大汗、嘔吐或腹瀉之後。孕婦見此脈為不良徵兆，可能提示流產將至。Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004年版，第497頁"
