        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Valgus and Varus Stress Test",
          "hant": "外翻與內翻應力測試",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Lachman's Test is done with the knee at 15 degrees flexion (some sources use 20 or 30 degrees), the outside hand stabilizes the femur, the inside hand is around the tibia at the tibial tubercle. An anterior directed force is then applied. More than about 2 mm of anterior translation compared to the uninvolved knee suggests a torn ACL (\"soft endpoint\"), as does 10 mm of total anterior translation. This is the most accurate exam maneuver for acute ACL tears. False- negative tests occur when hamstrings spasm, tense effusion or bucket handle tears of meniscus. False-positive tests occur with posterior cruciate ligament tears. Rotation Handout Family Medicine Residence Orthopedic Rotation Monteleone Jr. Dept. of Family Medicine West Virginia School of Medicine with further references to Magee's Orthopedic Physical Assessment and Hoppenfeld's Examination of the Spine and Extremities; Medicinehsc.wvu.edu",
      "exp_hant": "拉赫曼測試（Lachman's Test）之操作方式為屈膝約15度（部分文獻採20或30度），檢查者以外側手固定股骨，內側手則環握脛骨結節處，並施加向前之作用力。若脛骨前移程度較健側多約2毫米以上，即提示ACL撕裂（呈「軟性終點」），前移總量達10毫米亦可提示撕裂。此為診斷急性ACL撕裂最準確之檢查手法。假陰性結果可見於膕繩肌痙攣、關節嚴重積液或半月板桶柄狀撕裂之情形；假陽性結果則可見於後十字韌帶撕裂之患者。Rotation Handout Family Medicine Residence Orthopedic Rotation, Monteleone Jr., Dept. of Family Medicine, West Virginia School of Medicine，另參考Magee's Orthopedic Physical Assessment及Hoppenfeld's Examination of the Spine and Extremities；Medicinehsc.wvu.edu"
    },
