      "exp_en": "Lung channel symptoms include distension and fullness of the chest, supraclavicular fossa pain, shoulder pain extending to the chest, chest oppression, hot palms, feeling of cold or numbness or pain along the channel. The Lung channel disorders commonly manifest on the chest and the lateral area of the thumb and wrist. The Lung channel disorders manifest on the whole chest instead of the heart area which is on the left side of the chest. There can be a sense of oppressive sensations in the chest or a sense of tightness. The Lung channel treats the lateral area of the thumb and wrist. This is a common area for repetitive strain type of pain. The point LU-3 is an important point for treating an inability to extend the arm or pain that is located on the inner part of the arm. LU-7 is the most important point to select for the Lung primary channel symptoms. The Lung channel starts at the Stomach, goes to the Lungs, and through the mouth. This points to the 5-Element connection between Earth and Metal. REN-12, for example, can be selected to tonify the Lung as the channel starts at the Stomach. It is important to differentiate channel from organ symptoms which are often included in a channel symptom list. Organ symptoms for the Lung channel include cough. The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 82, 99",
      "exp_hant": "肺經症狀包括胸部脹滿、缺盆疼痛、肩痛連及胸部、胸悶、掌心發熱，以及沿經脈出現之發冷、麻木或疼痛。肺經病變常表現於胸部及拇指與腕部外側。肺經病變表現於整個胸部，而非僅限於胸部左側之心臟區域，可有胸悶或胸緊之感。肺經主治拇指與腕部外側，此區常見反覆性勞損之疼痛。肺經之列缺為治療臂不能伸或臂內側疼痛之重要穴位。太淵為治療肺經症狀最重要之穴位。肺經起於胃，行至肺，再經口，此點出五行中土與金之關係。例如中脘可用以補肺，因肺經起於胃。須注意區分經絡症狀與臟腑症狀，臟腑症狀常一併列於經絡症狀之中；肺臟腑症狀包括咳嗽。The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006年版，第82、99頁"
