    {
      "number": 114,
      "question_en": "During her period, a 39 year-old female experiences heavy menstrual flow, deep pelvic pain, painful urination, and painful intercourse. The pelvic exam reveals abnormal tissue growth between the uterus and rectum that is painful when touched. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位39歲女性於經期出現經量過多、盆腔深部疼痛、排尿疼痛及性交疼痛。骨盆檢查發現子宮與直腸間有異常組織增生，觸壓則痛。最可能之診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "endometriosis",
          "hant": "子宮內膜異位症",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Uterine fibroids",
          "hant": "子宮肌瘤",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Pelvic inflammatory disease",
          "hant": "骨盆腔炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "polycystic ovary syndrome",
          "hant": "多囊性卵巢症候群",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Endometriosis is a painful disorder in which the endometrium (tissue that lines the inside of the uterus) grows outside the uterus. This extra endometrial tissue is non-cancerous. Endometriosis occurs when the endometrium rather than being expelled through the vagina during the menstrual cycle, it detaches itself and instead spreads and attaches to structures outside of the uterus. Endometriosis is estrogen-dependent and estrogen-responsive. Endometriosis commonly affects the ovaries, fallopian tubes, bladder, and large intestine. Endometrial tissue rarely spreads beyond the pelvic organs. Symptoms of endometriosis include menorrhagia (heavy periods), menometrorrhagia (bleeding between periods), dysmenorrhea (pain before or during menstrual cycle), pain with bowel movements or urination, pain during or after sex. Additional symptoms can include fatigue, diarrhea, constipation, bloating or nausea, especially during menstrual periods.Endometriosis is a leading cause of infertility that results from the endometrial growth in the fallopian tubes blocking the egg passage. Endometriosis and uterine fibroids can have similar symptoms. The difference is that while endometriosis affects the uterus and structures outside of it, uterine fibroids affects the uterine wall itself. In doing a pelvic exam for endometriosis, the ovaries can also be painful when touched, can be enlarged, or are not movable (all of which indicate adhesions). Endometriosis is sometimes mistaken for other disorders that can cause pelvic pain (pelvic inflammatory disease, ovarian cysts, uterine fibroids, or irritable bowel syndrome). An ultrasound can only detect signs of larger endometrial adhesions and cysts. Smaller endometrial adhesions and other adhesions do not show up in ultrasound image. Laparoscopic surgery is a treatment option. Differential Diagnosis, Rhoads, 2015 page 220",
      "exp_hant": "子宮內膜異位症是一種疼痛性疾病，其子宮內膜（子宮內壁之組織）生長於子宮之外，此增生之子宮內膜組織為良性。子宮內膜異位症之發生機轉，是子宮內膜於月經週期中未能經陰道排出，反而剝離後擴散並附著於子宮以外之結構。子宮內膜異位症屬雌激素依賴性且對雌激素有反應之疾病，常侵犯卵巢、輸卵管、膀胱及大腸，極少擴散至骨盆器官以外之部位。子宮內膜異位症之症狀包括月經過多、經間出血、痛經（月經前或經期疼痛）、排便或排尿疼痛，以及性交時或性交後疼痛，亦可伴有疲倦、腹瀉、便秘、腹脹或噁心，尤以經期為甚。子宮內膜異位症為不孕之主要原因之一，乃因子宮內膜組織生長於輸卵管中阻塞卵子通行所致。子宮內膜異位症與子宮肌瘤症狀可能相似，兩者差異在於子宮內膜異位症侵犯子宮及其外部結構，而子宮肌瘤則侵犯子宮壁本身。進行子宮內膜異位症之骨盆檢查時，卵巢亦可能因觸壓而疼痛、腫大或活動度降低（皆提示沾黏）。子宮內膜異位症有時易與其他可致骨盆疼痛之疾病（如骨盆腔炎、卵巢囊腫、子宮肌瘤或腸躁症）混淆。超音波僅能偵測較大之子宮內膜沾黏及囊腫，較小之子宮內膜沾黏及其他沾黏則無法於超音波影像中顯現。腹腔鏡手術為治療選項之一。Differential Diagnosis, Rhoads, 2015年版，第220頁"
    },
