        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Treat the manifestation first, then the root",
          "hant": "先治標，後治本",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This treatment strategy is often used in practice with elderly patients where it is important to treat both the root and the manifestation. For example, an elderly patient with Spleen Yang Xu (root) with severe and debilitating diarrhea. In a relatively healthy and young patient it would be sufficient to treat the manifestation (severe diarrhea) but in an elderly patient whose overall qi is weak, it is necessary to treat both. This approach is also employed when the manifestation would reinforce the root pattern disharmony. For example, for a woman with deficient qi (root) with excess menstrual bleeding (qi not hold the Blood), it would be necessary to treat both because the chronic menstrual bleeding will increase the deficient qi (root) because Blood is the mother of qi. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 1176; 2005 Edition, page 1120",
      "exp_hant": "此治療策略常用於臨床上年老體弱之患者，此類患者須兼顧治本與治標。例如年老患者本屬脾陽虛（本），兼見嚴重且耗人之腹瀉，若為相對健康之年輕患者，僅治其標（嚴重腹瀉）即已足夠，然對於整體正氣已虛之年老患者，則須標本同治。此法亦適用於標證會加重本證病機之情形，例如氣虛（本）之婦女兼見經血過多（氣不攝血），此時亦須標本同治，因慢性經血過多將因血為氣之母而進一步耗損本已不足之氣。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015年版，第1176頁；2005年版，第1120頁"
    },
    {
