      "exp_en": "Irregular menstruation can be due to deficient Qi, deficient Blood, Cold in the Blood, Liver Qi stagnation, or Kidney Deficiency. The original clinical picture pointed to a deficient Qi condition. As such, REN-6 tonifies whole body qi. As Qi is the commander of Blood, when Qi is sufficient the Blood is properly controlled. SP-6, REN-12, and ST-36 tonify the Spleen Qi to produce and control Blood. The first presentation of symptoms points to deficient qi. On return, the clinical picture changed to deficient Blood. REN-4 and SP-6 nourishes yin and Blood. REN-6 adjusts the qi and Blood in the ren mai and chong mai to regulate the menses. HT-7 is selected as the deficient Blood is affecting the Heart (insomnia, palpitations). The prescription with LR-14 would be the treatment for Liver Qi stasis. The prescription with BL-23 treats Kidney deficiency. The prescription with REN-3 treats Blood Heat. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 471; CAM, 4th Edition, page 571",
      "exp_hant": "月經不規律可因氣虛、血虛、血寒、肝氣鬱結或腎虛所致。原先之臨床表現指向氣虛，故取氣海以補益周身之氣；氣為血之帥，氣足則血得統攝，三陰交、中脘、足三里能健脾益氣以生血、統血。首次就診之症狀提示氣虛，複診時臨床表現則轉為血虛，取關元、三陰交以滋陰養血，氣海調理任脈與衝脈之氣血以調經。神門則因血虛已影響及心（失眠、心悸）而選用。以期門為主之處方適用於肝氣鬱滯；以腎俞為主之處方治腎虛；以中極為主之處方治血熱。CAM, 3rd Edition，第471頁；CAM, 4th Edition，第571頁"
