    {
      "number": 124,
      "question_en": "A 32 year-old male has a mild itchy skin rash on the scalp. The rash is red, thick, and scaly. Physical examination also reveals plaques on the right elbow and pitted discolored nails. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位32歲男性頭皮出現輕度搔癢性皮疹，皮疹發紅、增厚且有脫屑。理學檢查另發現右肘有斑塊，並有點狀凹陷變色之指甲。最可能之診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "scabies",
          "hant": "疥瘡",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "eczema",
          "hant": "濕疹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "psoriasis",
          "hant": "牛皮癬（乾癬）",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Tinea versicolor",
          "hant": "汗斑（花斑癬）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Psoriasis consists of plaques of red skin (often with silver scales) that can be itchy and painful. The plaques can also crack and bleed. There can also be pitting discolored nails that can detach from the nail bed. The common sites for psoriasis are knees, elbows, scalp, torso, palms, and soles. With psoriasis the immune system is overactive causing skin inflammation. New skin cells are pushed to the surface in 3-4 days (28-30 days is normal) and accumulate causing dead skin to pile up and forming plaques. Diagnosis of psoriasis is usually done through medical history and physical exam that looks at the skin, nails, and scalp. A skin biopsy is rarely done unless to rule out other diseases.There is one eczema type but there are multiple types of psoriasis. The most common form of psoriasis is plaque psoriasis which most clearly resembles eczema. Itching is a significant differences between the two. Psoriasis has mild itching while eczema causes intense itching to the point of scratching until bleeding. In eczema scratched skin become swollen and raw. With eczema the itching is usually worse at night. Eczema does not typically have joint swelling nor nail disorders while psoriasis can. Tinea is a ringworm infection. Tinea versicolor changes the color pigmentation of the skin. Scabies is a contagious skin caused by microscopic burrowing mites. Scabies have intense uncontrollable itching (especially at night) but the rash consists of pimple like bumps where the mite has penetrated the skin. medlineplus.gov",
      "exp_hant": "牛皮癬（乾癬）表現為皮膚上之紅色斑塊（常伴銀白色鱗屑），可有搔癢與疼痛，斑塊亦可能龜裂、出血，並可能伴有點狀凹陷變色之指甲，甚至指甲自甲床剝離。牛皮癬常見部位為膝部、肘部、頭皮、軀幹、手掌及足底。牛皮癬患者免疫系統過度活化，導致皮膚發炎，新生皮膚細胞於3至4日內即被推至皮膚表面（正常為28至30日），因而堆積形成斑塊。牛皮癬之診斷通常依病史及理學檢查（觀察皮膚、指甲及頭皮）而定，皮膚切片極少施行，除非為排除其他疾病。濕疹僅有一種類型，而牛皮癬則有多種亞型，其中最常見者為斑塊型牛皮癬，外觀最類似濕疹。兩者之重要區別在於搔癢程度：牛皮癬搔癢輕微，濕疹則搔癢劇烈，甚至抓至出血。濕疹搔抓後皮膚會腫脹、破損，且濕疹之搔癢通常於夜間加重。濕疹通常不伴關節腫脹或指甲異常，而牛皮癬則可有此類表現。癬為一種黴菌感染（俗稱金錢癬）；汗斑（花斑癬）則會改變皮膚色素沉著；疥瘡則是由肉眼難見之疥蟲鑽入皮膚所致之傳染性皮膚病，其特徵為劇烈難耐之搔癢（尤以夜間為甚），皮疹則呈疥蟲侵入處之丘疹樣突起。medlineplus.gov"
    },
