      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Acupuncturists or physicians may use any method of communication (e-mail, oral conversations, written letters, faxes) as long as the acupuncturist or physician uses \"reasonable and appropriate safeguards\" to protect the communication and means of communication. These include protecting against downloading malicious software or viruses, strong passwords, computer user login, etc. A physician is not required to apply the minimum necessary standard (only give the minimum PHI needed) when discussing the PHI (protected health information) of a patient with another acupuncturist or physician involved in the treatment of the patient. The HIPAA Security Rule allows for e-PHI (electronic protected health information) to be sent over an electronic open network as long as it is adequately protected. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確之答案。針灸師或醫師可使用任何溝通方式（電子郵件、口頭對話、書面信件、傳真），惟須採取「合理且適當之防護措施」以保護溝通內容及溝通方式，例如防止下載惡意軟體或病毒、使用強密碼、電腦使用者登入等。醫師與另一位參與該病患治療之針灸師或醫師討論病患之受保護健康資訊（PHI）時，並不需要適用「最小必要」原則（即僅提供所需之最少PHI）。HIPAA安全規則允許電子受保護健康資訊（e-PHI）經由開放式電子網路傳送，惟須有適當之保護措施。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
