      "exp_en": "Possible meningitis. Meningitis is inflammation of the protective membranes covering the brain and spinal cord, known collectively as the meninges. The inflammation may be caused by an infection from a virus, bacteria, or other microorganism, and less commonly by certain drugs. Meningitis can be life-threatening because of the proximity of the inflammation to the brain and spinal cord. It is classified as a medical emergency. The most common symptoms are headache, neck stiffness associated with fever, confusion, vomiting, and an inability to tolerate light (photophobia) or loud noises (phonophobia). In small children, only nonspecific symptoms maybe present, such as irritability and drowsiness. A rash that's red, tender and warm or a red streak on the arm or leg can indicate possible infection of skin or lymph. Fever comes and goes, night sweats, swollen lymph nodes can indicate possible AIDS, TB. Short of breath, cough that produces yellow, green or tan mucus can indicate possible bronchitis, pneumonia. tcmtests.com, December 2019",
