      "exp_en": "CAM 3rd Edition calls the Internal Genitalia point Uterus/Seminal Palace and describes the point as located in the triangular fossa and in the depression close to the midpoint of the helix. CAM 4th Edition calls it Internal Genitalia which is located in the lower part of the anterior 1/3 of the triangular fossa. Bensky describes it as located slightly above the parting of the two crura of the anti-helix, in the triangular fossa. CAM also calls this point the Seminal Palace. This points supports yang and nourishes essence, regulates menstruation, and harmonizes blood. The Uterus or Seminal Palace point treats obstetrical and gynecological disorders in women and sexual dysfunction in men. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 519; CAM 4th Edition, page 424; Bensky, 1981, page 485",
