          "key": "D",
          "en": "Is the least common form of diabetes",
          "hant": "為最少見之糖尿病類型",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Diabetes mellitus (DM) is related to an insulin deficiency or resistance leading to high blood glucose. In DM the body does not produce or properly use insulin which is a necessary hormone to convert sugar into energy. DM has three main forms: type 1 diabetes, type 2 diabetes, and gestational diabetes (affects about 4% of pregnant women). Type 1 diabetes is an immune disorder in which the immune system attacks the insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. As a result, the pancreas cannot produce sufficient insulin resulting in high blood glucose levels that can damage organ systems. Patients with type 1 diabetes need to have external insulin to survive. As type 1 DM mostly affects children, it is known as insulin-dependent or juvenile-onset diabetes. In type 2 DM the pancreas does not produce enough insulin or the cells ignore the insulin. Just like in type 1 DM, type 2 also has high blood glucose levels that can damage organ systems. Type 2 DM is commonly classified as adult-onset diabetes. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 891-892; 4th Edition page 969",
      "exp_hant": "糖尿病（DM）與胰島素分泌不足或阻抗有關，可導致血糖過高。糖尿病患者體內無法正常產生或有效利用胰島素——一種將糖轉化為能量所必需之激素。糖尿病主要有三種類型：第一型糖尿病、第二型糖尿病，以及妊娠糖尿病（約影響4%之孕婦）。第一型糖尿病屬免疫疾病，免疫系統攻擊胰臟中分泌胰島素之β細胞，致使胰臟無法產生足夠胰島素，造成高血糖，進而可能損害多個器官系統，第一型糖尿病患者須依賴外源性胰島素方能存活。由於第一型糖尿病多見於兒童，故又稱為胰島素依賴型或幼年型糖尿病。第二型糖尿病則是胰臟胰島素分泌不足，或細胞對胰島素反應不佳；與第一型相同，第二型亦有高血糖，可損害多個器官系統。第二型糖尿病通常歸類為成年型糖尿病。Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana，第891-892頁；4th Edition，第969頁"
    },
