      "exp_en": "ST-4 and REN-24 are at different levels. ST-4 is located 0.4 cun lateral to the corner of the mouth. REN-24 is located on the mentolabial groove between the chin and lower lip. The two sets of points in the other answers are on the same level. ST-3 is located directly below the pupil with the patient looking directly forward, level with the lower border of the ala nasi, on the lateral side of the naso-labial groove. SI-18 is located directly below the outer canthus, in the depression at the lower border of the zygomatic arch. BL-3 is directly superior to BL-2, 0.5 cun within the hairline, level with DU-24. DU-24 is at the top of the head on the midline, 0.5 cun posterior to the anterior hairline and 0.5 cun anterior to DU-23. LI-19 is below the lateral margin of the nostril, lateral to DU-26. DU-26 is above the upper lip on the midline, at the junction of the upper third and lower two thirds of the philtrum. ST-3 is the meeting point of the Stomach channel and the Yang Motility vessel. ST-3 eliminates wind, dissipates swelling, and alleviates pain. SI-18 is the meeting point of the Small Intestine and Triple Burner channels. SI-18 eliminates wind, alleviates pain, clears heat and reduces swelling. BL-3 expels wind, clears the head, alleviates pain, and benefits the eyes and nose. DU-24 is the meeting point of the Du Mai with the Bladder and Stomach channels. DU-24 benefits the brain, calms the spirit, eliminates wind, benefits the head, and benefits the nose and eyes. LI-19 eliminates wind and opens the nose. DU-26 is the meeting point of the Du Mai with the Large Intestine and Stomach channels. DU-26 restores consciousness, calms the spirit, benefits the face and nose, expels wind, and benefits the spine and treats acute lumbar sprain. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 119, 131, 132, 246, 557, 559, 588",
