      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "At least six years",
          "hant": "至少六年",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "three months",
          "hant": "三個月",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Until the death of the patient",
          "hant": "直到病患過世為止",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Unto perpetuity",
          "hant": "永久保存",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Although there are no HIPAA retention requirements for medical records because state laws take precedence, there is a requirement covering how long HIPAA-related documents should be retained. The HIPAA Privacy Act requires that written policies and procedure, the accounting of disclosures, and other documentation related to PHI be retained for six years. Covered Entities must maintain the policies and procedures implemented to comply with HIPAA and records of any action, activity or assessment. Documents must be retained for a minimum of six years from when the document was created. If a new policy is implemented for three years before being revised, a record of the original policy must be retained for a minimum of nine years after its creation. HIPAA requirements preempt state laws if they require shorter periods of document retention. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "雖然HIPAA對於病歷本身並無保存期限規定（因為州法優先適用），但對於HIPAA相關文件的保存期限則有明確要求。HIPAA隱私法規定，書面政策與程序、揭露紀錄，以及其他與PHI相關的文件，須保存六年。受規範實體（Covered Entities）必須保存為遵循HIPAA而制定的政策與程序，以及任何行動、活動或評估的紀錄。文件自訂定之日起，至少須保存六年。若某項新政策實施三年後被修訂，則原始政策的紀錄自訂定之日起，至少須保存九年。若州法規定的保存期限較短，則以HIPAA的規定為準。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
    },
