    {
      "number": 148,
      "question_en": "A 42 year-old female has been receiving treatment for anxiety for the past three months. Her anxiety started when she and her husband separated. Her symptoms have included palpitations, chest oppression, a slight feeling of lump in the throat, frequent sighing, shortness of breath, poor appetite and nausea, and a pale complexion. The tongue has been pale-purple on the sides. The pulse has been slightly overflowing on the left-front position. The treatment principle was Move Heart Qi, Open the Chest, and Calm the Mind. Her symptoms diminished about 60%. A month after her last treatment, she returned to report she is now going through the divorce proceedings. Her anxiety is now worse particularly in the evening. She has been waking up in the middle of the night with a sense of panic. The chest oppression has now become a sense of pressure on the chest. The tongue is unchanged but the pulse is now choppy. What treatment principle will you now choose?",
      "question_hant": "一位42歲女性因焦慮已接受治療三個月。她的焦慮始於與丈夫分居之時。症狀包括心悸、胸悶、咽喉有異物感、時常嘆氣、氣短、食慾不振與噁心，面色蒼白。舌兩側呈淡紫色。脈象在左寸部略帶洪象。治療原則原為行心氣、寬胸、安神，症狀已改善約六成。最後一次治療後一個月，她回診表示現正進行離婚訴訟。她的焦慮加重，尤以夜間為甚，並常於半夜驚醒且伴有恐慌感。原本的胸悶感現已轉為胸口壓迫感。舌象未變，但脈象轉為澀脈。此時您會選擇的治療原則為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
