        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Move Heart Qi, Open the Chest, Calm the Mind",
          "hant": "行心氣、寬胸、安神",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "There is no TCM term for anxiety. Traditionally, it has been attributed to \"Fear and Palpitations\" or \"Panic Throbbing\", the latter referring to panic attacks. The original presentation of symptoms and signs indicate Heart Qi stasis. Chest distention, sighing, feeling of lump in throat all indicate qi stasis. The palpitations point to involvement of the Heart. Heart qi stasis involved the chest and can cause slight shortness of breath. The complexion is pale not because of Qi/Blood xu but because the qi stasis prevents the Blood ascending to the face. The poor appetite and nausea is due to the Heart qi not descending due to stasis and impacting Stomach function. The tongue indicates that the qi stasis is beginning to impact Blood. An overflowing pulse on the left front position is a key sign for this pattern. The second clinical presentation indicates a worsening of the condition from Heart Qi Stasis to Heart Blood Stasis due to the stress from the divorce. Blood stasis is characterized by symptoms being worse at night and sleep when Blood circulation slows down. Because of the preceding, the treatment principle was changed to Invigorate Heart Blood, Eliminate Stasis, Calm the Mind. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 402; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 506, 1141, 1142",
      "exp_hant": "中醫並無「焦慮」這一病名，傳統上多將其歸為「驚悸」或「怔忡」，後者專指恐慌發作。病患最初的症狀與體徵顯示心氣鬱結：胸悶、嘆氣、咽喉異物感皆屬氣鬱之象；心悸則顯示病位在心。心氣鬱結累及胸部，可致輕微氣短。面色蒼白並非因氣血虛，而是氣鬱使血無法上榮於面。食慾不振與噁心則因心氣鬱結不降，影響胃之功能所致。舌象顯示氣鬱已開始波及血分，左寸脈洪為此證的重要指標。第二次就診時的臨床表現顯示，因離婚訴訟之壓力，病情已由心氣鬱結加重為心血瘀阻。血瘀的特徵為夜間及睡眠時（血行減緩）症狀加重。基於上述原因，治療原則改為活心血、化瘀、安神。《The Practice of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2008年，402頁；《Foundations of Chinese Medicine》，Maciocia，2015年，506、1141、1142頁"
    },
