      "exp_en": "The main actions of the formula are to tonify the middle burner, strengthen the Spleen, transform dampness, and stop vaginal discharges. Vaginal discharges can be associated with the Liver, Spleen and the dai mai. The dai mai wraps around the lower trunk like a belt which binds all the channels the go through the areas. The dai mai has a close relationship with the Spleen and Liver. When the dai mai is unable to secure and bind the channels there can be discharges from the lower part in women through the vagina. The Spleen controls transformation-transportation. When the Spleen is weak, fluid accumulates in the form of internal dampness which slowly becomes turbid. The turbid dampness seeps down and is removed through the vagina. The Liver controls the free flow of qi in the body. When this Liver function is impaired there is a failure to distribute the ministerial fire to the middle jiao which further weakens the Spleen, resulting in an increase of dampness. The vaginal discharge caused by Spleen xu and dampness is profuse, white or pale yellow , and with a thin consistency. Since there is no heat involved in this pattern, the discharge will not be foul smelling. A weak Spleen fails to nourish the limbs resulting fatigue and lethargy. Not enough qi and blood going to the face results in a pale-shiny facial complexion. The loose stools are symptom of Spleen xu with the accumulation of dampness that blocks the function of the Spleen to raise qi and fluids up. The pale tongue with white coating and the soggy-frail pulse reflect Spleen xu with dampness. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 447",
      "exp_hant": "此方的主要功用為補益中焦、健脾、化濕、止帶。帶下病與肝、脾及帶脈皆有關聯。帶脈如帶狀環繞腰腹，約束通過此處的諸經脈，且與脾、肝關係密切。當帶脈失於約束固攝時，婦女下部便可能經陰道產生分泌物。脾主運化，脾虛則水濕內停，日久化為濁液；濁濕下滲，經由陰道排出。肝主疏泄一身之氣，肝失疏泄則相火不能布散於中焦，致脾更加虛弱，濕邪隨之加重。因脾虛夾濕所致之帶下，量多，色白或淡黃，質稀薄；因本證無熱，故分泌物不會腥臭。脾虛不能榮養四肢，故見疲倦乏力；氣血不足以上榮於面，故面色淡白而有光澤；大便溏薄則為脾虛濕聚、脾失升清所致。舌淡苔白、脈濡弱皆為脾虛夾濕之徵。《Formulas and Strategies》，Bensky，第2版，447頁"
