      "exp_en": "The Blood heat manifested as feeling hot, red face, rapid-overflowing pulse, heavy period, red tongue with yellow coating, and mouth ulcers. Profuse menstrual bleeding due to Blood Heat has profuse bleeding which is bright-red or dark-red. It can cause either flooding or trickling. Often times the Blood Heat is generated from Liver Fire which in turn can be generated by emotional issues. The Liver stores Blood and is connected to the ren and chong mai. Heat or Fire in the Liver can heat up the Blood and make it spill out of the blood vessels. The Liver Fire manifested as red face, dizziness, feeling hot, pounding headaches, red tongue, and wiry pulse. There was some Liver qi stasis which manifested as premenstrual tension, irritability, and distention. The yellow coating further confirms Heat, as yellow specifically indicates the transformation of pathogenic factors into a \"hot\" state, often linked to the blazing of Liver Fire or Heat in the Blood (evident here in the bright-red, profuse menstrual bleeding and short cycle). In Liver Fire patterns, the coating is classically yellow (and often dry) to denote Full Heat rather than deficient types.The thickness of the yellow coating points to an excess condition where the Heat is more entrenched or accumulated, potentially over time due to chronic Liver Qi Stasis \"brewing\" into Fire (as seen in the PMS-related distension, swelling, and wiry-overflowing pulse). Thickness can also suggest a mild overlay of dampness or phlegm, which may arise secondarily when stagnant Liver Qi impairs Spleen function, leading to poor fluid transformation. Though this is not the primary pattern here, it subtly ties into the overall excess presentation without shifting the core diagnosis. Together, these tongue features reinforce the Heat-dominant pattern while highlighting its full, excess quality. Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1st Edition, page 313; 2nd Edition, page 233",
