        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "chlamydia",
          "hant": "披衣菌感染（衣原體感染）",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "HPV (human papillary virus) is the most prevelant virally transmitted STD. Most HPV infections have no symptoms and resolve spontaneously. In some patients, an HPV infection persists and results in warts or precancerous lesions which increase the risk of cancer of the cervix, vulva, vagina, penis, anus, mouth, or throat. Chlamydia is the most common bacteria transmitted through sexual contact (penis, vagina, mouth, anus) of an infected partner. Ejaculation is not necessary for chlamydia transmission. Chlamydia can also spread prenatally from an untreated mother during childbirth. Any sexually active person can be infected with chlamydia. Chlamydia is known as a \"silent infection\" because infected patients are asymptomatic and have an absence of abnormal physical examination findings. Symptoms in women can include mucopurulent cervical discharge, endocervical bleeding, urethritis, anal itching, pelvic inflammatory disease (PID) with pelvic pain, cervical motion tenderness, and uterine tenderness. Infected men can have urethritis, with a mucoid or watery urethral discharge and dysuria. Chlamydia can also be found in the throat from oral sex with an infected partner, but it is typically asymptomatic and not an important cause of pharyngitis. Untreated chlamydia can increase the risk of acquiring or transmitting HIV. Because chlamydia is generally asymptomatic, patients need to be screened to identify infections. Chlamydia is the most commonly reported bacterial-sexually transmitted infection in the US. Chlamydia prevalence among sexually-active young persons, 14-24 years old, is nearly three times more than among persons aged 25-39 years old. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 662; 4th Edition, page 763",
      "exp_hant": "HPV（人類乳突病毒）是最常見經由病毒傳染的性傳染病。大多數HPV感染並無症狀，且會自行痊癒。少數患者的HPV感染會持續存在，導致疣或癌前病變，進而增加子宮頸癌、外陰癌、陰道癌、陰莖癌、肛門癌、口腔癌或咽喉癌的風險。披衣菌感染則是最常見經性接觸（陰莖、陰道、口腔、肛門）由感染伴侶傳播的細菌性感染。射精並非傳播披衣菌所必需的條件。披衣菌亦可能在生產過程中，由未經治療的母親傳染給新生兒。任何有性行為的人皆可能感染披衣菌。披衣菌感染被稱為「無聲感染」，因為感染者通常無症狀，理學檢查亦無異常發現。女性患者的症狀可能包括子宮頸黏液膿性分泌物、子宮頸內出血、尿道炎、肛門搔癢，以及伴隨骨盆疼痛、子宮頸舉痛與子宮壓痛的骨盆腔炎（PID）。男性感染者則可能出現尿道炎，伴有黏液性或水樣尿道分泌物及排尿困難。披衣菌亦可能因與感染伴侶口交而出現於咽喉部，但通常無症狀，也非咽炎的主要病因。未經治療的披衣菌感染會提高感染或傳播HIV的風險。由於披衣菌感染通常無症狀，患者需要接受篩檢以確認感染與否。披衣菌是美國通報案例最多的細菌性性傳染病。在14至24歲有性行為的年輕族群中，披衣菌的盛行率幾乎是25至39歲族群的三倍。《Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests》，第7版，Pagana，662頁；第4版，763頁"
