      ],
      "exp_en": "Examining the lungs and chest uses all four approaches. Inspection is visually observing the chest (thin, barrel shaped, retraction of intercostal spaces during breathing, amount of effort to breathe, etc). Percussion is striking the chest wall as if it were a drum and listening to the sound produced (solid, hollow, etc). Auscultation is using the stethoscope to listen to breathing sounds (rhonchi, wheezes, rales, etc). Palpation is the placement of the hands on the lower-posterior chest wall to feel for the expansion of the chest wall during breathing and look for your thumbs separating. It is also palpating for tender areas. Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 37-44",
      "exp_hant": "檢查肺部與胸部需運用全部四種診察方法。視診是用眼睛觀察胸部（如是否消瘦、呈桶狀胸、呼吸時肋間隙是否凹陷、呼吸所需之用力程度等）。叩診是以叩擊胸壁的方式，如同敲鼓一般，聆聽所產生的聲音（實音、鼓音等）。聽診則是使用聽診器聆聽呼吸音（如鼾音、喘鳴音、囉音等）。觸診則是將雙手置於下背部胸壁，感受呼吸時胸壁的擴張情形，並觀察雙手拇指是否隨之分開，同時觸診有無壓痛部位。《Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine》，2009年，Robinson, Wolfe，37-44頁"
    },
