      "exp_en": "COMMON: All three herbs calm Liver wind, clear Liver Heat and relieve spasms.DIFFERENCES: The herb Gou Teng calms Liver yang, and more effectively clears wind secondary to heat in the Heart and Liver. It is sweet and cool. It enters the Liver and Pericardium. The herb Tian Ma calms Liver wind, stops spasms, and relieves painful obstruction syndrome. It is sweet and neutral. It enters the Liver channel. The herb Di Long clears heat, opens channels and collaterals, relieves wheezing, and promotes urination. It is salty and cold. It enters the Liver, Spleen, Bladder, and Lung channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRAS: The herb Gou Teng does not have a caution/contra listed. The herb Tian Ma should be used cautiously with patients driving or operating heavy machinery due to its sedative effect. The herb Di Long is contraindicated with Spleen and Stomach deficiency or without heat symptoms. It should be used with caution during pregnancy. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herb Gou Teng reverses the effects of caffeine but does not potentiate the effects of sedatives. The herb Tian Ma potentiates the effects of sedatives. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 809, 783, 785, 794",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：這三味藥皆能平肝熄風、清肝熱、緩解痙攣。差異：鉤藤能平肝陽，且更能有效清除因心、肝有熱所致之風邪，其性味甘涼，歸肝、心包經。天麻能平肝熄風、止痙、除痹痛，性味甘平，歸肝經。地龍能清熱、通經活絡、平喘、利尿，性味鹹寒，歸肝、脾、膀胱、肺經。注意事項／禁忌：鉤藤並無特別列出之注意事項或禁忌。天麻因具鎮靜作用，駕駛或操作重型機械者應謹慎使用。地龍禁用於脾胃虛寒或無熱象者，孕婦應謹慎使用。藥物交互作用：鉤藤會逆轉咖啡因的作用，但不會增強鎮靜劑的效果；天麻則會增強鎮靜劑的效果。《Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology》，Chen and Chen，2004年，809、783、785、794頁"
