    {
      "number": 203,
      "question_en": "A 32 year-old male has fever, swollen glands, and a rash in both palms (reddish brown spots, no itching). He indicates that he had a sore on his penis about two months ago. The enzyme immunoassay (EIA) indicates antibodies specific to treponema. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位32歲男性有發熱、淋巴腺腫大，雙手掌出現皮疹（紅褐色斑點，不會癢）。他表示約兩個月前陰莖曾出現潰瘍。酵素免疫分析法（EIA）檢測顯示對梅毒螺旋體具特異性抗體。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "chlamydia",
          "hant": "披衣菌感染",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "genital herpes",
          "hant": "生殖器疱疹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "syphilis",
          "hant": "梅毒",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "HPV",
          "hant": "人類乳突病毒（HPV）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Syphilis is caused by the bacteria treponema pallidum. Testing is usually a two step blood test: 1) nontreponemal test and 2) treponemal tests. Nontreponemal tests (VDRL and RPR) are often used for screening. But they are not specific for syphilis and can produce false-positives. These first tests are followed by treponemal tests (FTA-ABS, TP-PA, various EIAs) to detect specific antibodies to the bacteria treponema pallidum. The syphilis bacteria is transmitted via direct contact with a syphilitic sore (chancre). Chancres can occur on the genitals, around the anus, in the rectum, or the mouth. The average time between syphilis infection and the appearance of the first symptom is 21 days (can range 10 to 90 days). Syphilis has been called \"The Great Pretender\" because the symptoms can mimic other diseases. Syphilis occurs in stages. PRIMARY STAGE There is the appearance of a single (can be more) chancre in the primary stage. The chancre is (but not always) firm, round, and painless. These painless chancres can occur in \"hidden\" locations such as inside the vagina or anus that make them difficult to notice. The chancre lasts 3 to 6 weeks and heals regardless of treatment. SECONDARY STAGE: Skin rashes and/or mucous membrane sores (in mouth, vagina, or anus) marks the second stage. Secondary syphilis rashes can appear when the primary chancre is healing or several weeks after healed. The rash usually does not cause itching. The skin rash appears rough, red, or reddish brown spots both on the palms of the hands and the bottoms of the feet. The secondary stage can also have fever and swollen glands. LATENT STAGE: The latent or hidden stage of syphilis has no visible signs or symptoms of syphilis. This stage can occur from 12 months to years after the original infection. TERTIARY STAGE: This is rare and arises from an untreated syphilis infection. It can appear 10-30 years after the original infection. Tertiary syphilis can affect the brain, nerves, eyes, heart, blood vessels, liver, bones, and joints. This stage of syphilis is terminal. www.cdc.gov",
      "exp_hant": "梅毒是由梅毒螺旋體（treponema pallidum）這種細菌所引起。檢測通常分為兩個步驟的血液檢查：一、非梅毒螺旋體試驗；二、梅毒螺旋體試驗。非梅毒螺旋體試驗（VDRL與RPR）常用於篩檢，但對梅毒並無特異性，可能產生偽陽性結果。這些初步檢測之後，會再進行梅毒螺旋體試驗（FTA-ABS、TP-PA及各種EIA）以檢測針對梅毒螺旋體的特異性抗體。梅毒細菌透過直接接觸梅毒硬下疳（chancre）傳播，硬下疳可能出現於生殖器、肛門周圍、直腸或口腔。從感染梅毒到首發症狀出現，平均時間為21天（範圍可為10至90天）。梅毒被稱為「偉大的模仿者」，因其症狀可能與其他疾病相似。梅毒的病程分為以下階段：初期：出現一個（或多個）硬下疳，通常（但非絕對）質硬、圓形且無痛。這些無痛的硬下疳可能出現於「隱蔽」部位，如陰道內或肛門內，因而不易察覺。硬下疳持續3至6週，無論是否治療皆會自行癒合。二期：出現皮疹及／或黏膜潰瘍（於口腔、陰道或肛門），標誌著第二階段的開始。二期梅毒的皮疹可能於初期硬下疳癒合期間出現，或於癒合後數週出現。此皮疹通常不會發癢，表現為手掌與足底出現粗糙、紅色或紅褐色斑點。二期亦可能伴隨發熱與淋巴腺腫大。潛伏期：梅毒的潛伏（隱藏）期並無任何可見的徵象或症狀，此階段可自初次感染後12個月起持續數年之久。三期：此階段較為罕見，源自未經治療的梅毒感染，可能於初次感染後10至30年出現。三期梅毒可影響腦部、神經、眼睛、心臟、血管、肝臟、骨骼及關節，屬於梅毒的末期階段。www.cdc.gov"
    },
