        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. There is no test (including abdominal ultrasound) that can definitely diagnose irritable bowel syndrome (IBS). Physicians rely on history, physical examination, and bowel patterns. Researchers have developed what is called the Rome criteria for helping to diagnose inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). The most important criteria is abdominal pain-discomfort lasting at least 12 weeks. There must also be at least two of the following manifestations: 1) a change in the frequency or consistency of the stool. 2) straining, urgency or a feeling that the colon cannot be emptied. 3) mucous in the stool. 4) abdominal bloating-distention. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 82",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。目前並無任何檢查（包括腹部超音波）能確診腸躁症（IBS），醫師須仰賴病史、理學檢查與排便型態來診斷。研究者制定了所謂的「羅馬準則」，以協助診斷發炎性腸道疾病（IBD）。其中最重要的準則為腹痛或腹部不適至少持續12週，並須至少符合下列兩項表現：一、排便頻率或糞便性狀改變；二、排便費力、急迫感，或有排便不盡之感；三、糞便中帶有黏液；四、腹脹。《The Merck Manual》，第18版，82頁"
    },
