      "exp_en": "The red flag is the dark area in her central vision. A detached retina is assumed present until proven otherwise. Retinal detachment results in sudden and painless vision loss in one eye. The patient will report one of the following in one eye: 1) lots of eye floaters in one eye. 2) sudden flashes of light in one eye. 3) a sudden shadow over the visual field. 4) sudden and persistent blurry vision. The possible consequences of missing the condition is permanent blindness. A referral should be done on a semi-urgent basis. The PCP will refer to an ophthalmologist to prevent further retinal detachment. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 183-184",
      "exp_hant": "此案的紅旗警訊為中心視野出現暗區。在排除其他可能性之前，應假設為視網膜剝離。視網膜剝離會導致單眼突發且無痛的視力喪失。病患在單眼可能出現下列其中一種症狀：一、大量眼前飛蚊；二、單眼突發閃光；三、視野中突發陰影；四、突發且持續性的視力模糊。若未能及時察覺此病症，可能導致永久性失明。此情況應以半緊急方式轉診，基層照護醫師將再轉診至眼科醫師，以避免視網膜剝離進一步惡化。《An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals》，2012年，Anzaldua，183-184頁"
