      "exp_en": "In younger patients, spinal fractures are most often due to a violent trauma (car accidents, jumps or falls from a height). In older patients, lumbar compression fractures can occur with no or just a minor trauma. The most common cause for these fractures in geriatric patients, especially women, is osteoporosis. In osteoporosis, there is a generalized decrease in bone density which weakens the bone so that even a minor fall or strenuous lifting can result in one or more compression fractures. Patients with cancer that has spread to the bones are also susceptible to spinal compression fractures. Most compression fractures are never diagnosed because patients ascribe the back pain to aging and arthritis. Moreover, not every patient experiences spinal pain with compression fracture. Multiple compression fractures can cause a bulging abdomen, constipation, and poor appetite due to a shorter spine compressing the stomach. Multiple compression fractures can also result in loss of height, curved back (kyphosis), and problems with breathing, an x-ray of the spine will show vertebra broken or with hairline fractures. A CT scan, MRI, and bone density tests can be ordered after a positive x-ray for fractures. Treatment is usually conservative and consists of pain medications, decreasing activity, and wearing a back brace. Minimally invasive surgical procedures (vertebroplasty, kyphoplasty) can be considered.",
      "exp_hant": "年輕患者的脊椎骨折多因劇烈創傷（如車禍、高處跳落或墜落）所致。年長患者的腰椎壓迫性骨折則可能在沒有創傷或僅有輕微創傷的情況下發生。老年患者（尤其是女性）發生此類骨折最常見的原因是骨質疏鬆症。骨質疏鬆症會使骨密度普遍下降，骨骼因而變得脆弱，即使是輕微跌倒或用力抱舉也可能導致一處或多處壓迫性骨折。癌症已轉移至骨骼的患者同樣容易發生脊椎壓迫性骨折。大多數壓迫性骨折從未被確診，因為患者常將背痛歸因於老化或關節炎。此外，並非每位壓迫性骨折患者都會出現脊椎疼痛。多發性壓迫性骨折可能因脊椎縮短、壓迫胃部而造成腹部隆起、便秘及食慾不振。多發性壓迫性骨折也可能導致身高變矮、駝背（脊椎後凸）及呼吸問題，脊椎X光會顯示椎體斷裂或有髮絲狀骨折。X光確診骨折後，可再安排電腦斷層掃描、核磁共振及骨密度檢查。治療通常採保守方式，包括止痛藥物、減少活動量及配戴背架。也可考慮採用微創手術（椎體成形術、後凸成形術）。"
