      "exp_en": "Still's disease is a severe form of arthritis that tends to occur in children (less common in adults). Most patients with this disorder have joint pain (hot, swollen, stiff), sore throat, fever (acute once per day, in the afternoon or evening), and rashes (salmon-pink rash that comes-goes with fever). In this condition, the spleen or the liver can become enlarged and there can be inflammation in the lung and heart. The patient has been prescribed aspirin for pain control. Aspirin is a causative factors for Reye's syndrome. Which is a life-threatening metabolic disorder that occurs mostly in children. Initial symptoms can include acute vomiting, fatigue, staring behavior, slurred speech, sleepiness. If the disease progresses there can be liver and brain damage with symptoms of confusion (inability to recognize people), hyperventilation, violent behavior, seizures, and eventually coma. This is a red-flag requiring immediate emergency care. Failure to treat can result in permanent brain damage. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 116, 707",
      "exp_hant": "史提爾氏病是一種好發於兒童（成人較少見）的嚴重關節炎。大多數患者會出現關節疼痛（紅、腫、僵硬）、喉嚨痛、發燒（每日一次急性發作，多於下午或傍晚出現），以及皮疹（隨發燒而時隱時現的鮭肉色皮疹）。此病可能伴隨肝脾腫大，並出現肺部與心臟發炎。此患者為控制疼痛而服用阿斯匹靈，而阿斯匹靈正是雷氏症候群的致病因素之一。雷氏症候群是一種好發於兒童、可能危及生命的代謝性疾病。初期症狀可能包括急性嘔吐、疲倦、目光呆滯、口齒不清、嗜睡。若病情惡化，可能出現肝臟與腦部損傷，症狀包括意識混亂（無法辨認他人）、過度換氣、暴力行為、癲癇發作，最終陷入昏迷。這是需要立即緊急處理的警訊，若未及時治療可能造成永久性腦損傷。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學執業者教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第116、707頁"
