      "question_hant": "一名42歲女性患者於坐直時發生鼻出血。下列何種情況需要緊急（1至8小時內）轉診至耳鼻喉科？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Blood goes out right nostril",
          "hant": "血液從右側鼻孔流出",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Bleeding does not stop with direct pressure after 2 minutes",
          "hant": "直接加壓2分鐘後出血仍未止住",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Blood goes out left nostril",
          "hant": "血液從左側鼻孔流出",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Blood goes down the back of throat",
          "hant": "血液流向喉嚨後方",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In most cases, epistaxis comes from the front part of the nose, what is called the septum. A less common type of epistaxis is bleeding from the middle or back of the nose. Most of the time this bleeding is related to an acute episode of hypertension. Emergency care should be sought if the bleeding does not stop after more than 15 to 20 minutes of applying direct pressure, if the bleeding is rapid or there is more than a cupful of blood loss. The blood goes down the back of the throat rather than out front even though the patient is sitting down with body and head leaning slightly forward. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "大多數鼻出血源自鼻腔前部，也就是鼻中隔。較少見的鼻出血類型則來自鼻腔中段或後段。這類出血多與急性高血壓發作有關。若直接加壓超過15至20分鐘後仍未止血，或出血速度快、失血量超過一杯，則應立即就醫。即使患者採坐姿並將身體與頭部略微前傾，血液仍會流向喉嚨後方而非向前流出。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
    {
      "number": 219,
      "question_en": "A 30-year old male patient has a history of drinking a pack of beer every day. His wife says that he takes ibuprofen daily for his headache. He has upper abdominal pain. During the interview, he feels nauseated and starts retching. Visible blood and food is seen in the vomit. After the vomiting, the patient no longer feels nauseated. The physical examination revealed significant mid-epigastric tenderness to deep palpation. Which course of action would you take?",
      "question_hant": "一名30歲男性患者長期每天飲用一手（六罐裝）啤酒。其妻表示他每天服用布洛芬以緩解頭痛。他有上腹部疼痛。問診期間，他感到噁心並開始乾嘔，嘔吐物中可見明顯血絲與食物殘渣。嘔吐後，噁心感隨即消失。理學檢查發現深觸診時上腹部中央有明顯壓痛。你會採取何種處置？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "provide acupuncture treatment",
          "hant": "提供針灸治療",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "have wife take him to ER",
          "hant": "請其妻將他送往急診室",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "referral to their primary care physician",
          "hant": "轉診至基層醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency assistance",
          "hant": "撥打911求助",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is upper abdominal pain and vomiting blood. Upper GI bleeding is assumed present until proven otherwise. Upper GI hemorrhage from inner lining of stomach and/or esophagus is assumed present until proven otherwise. Bleeding into the stomach or esophagus causes nausea and vomiting. Retching may further break already fragile blood vessels leading to a vicious cycle. NSAIDs can damage the mucosal lining of the stomach. Excess alcohol intake can lead to varices. Since the bleeding had stopped and the patient was no longer nauseated the patient should be transported to the nearest ED by a friend or family member. This red flag can be severe but in most cases the symptoms are milder which can mislead the acupuncturist about the severity of the underlying condition. If the patient has a primary care physician, a semi-urgent referral is also OK. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 87-88",
      "exp_hant": "此案例的警訊為上腹部疼痛併嘔血。在排除其他可能性之前，應假設患者為上消化道出血，來源可能是胃和／或食道內壁。血液流入胃部或食道會引起噁心與嘔吐，而乾嘔動作可能進一步撕裂原本已脆弱的血管，形成惡性循環。非類固醇消炎止痛藥（NSAIDs）會損傷胃黏膜，過量飲酒則可能導致靜脈曲張。由於出血已停止且患者已不再感到噁心，應由親友將其送往最近的急診室。此警訊可能相當嚴重，但多數情況下症狀較輕微，容易讓針灸師低估病情的嚴重程度。若患者已有固定的基層醫師，以半緊急方式轉診亦屬合宜。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第87-88頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 220,
      "question_en": "In many public health care settings, what is important?",
      "question_hant": "在許多公共醫療照護場所中，何者是重要事項？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gloves be worn at all times",
          "hant": "全程配戴手套",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "all patients receive treatment in a prone position",
          "hant": "所有患者皆採俯臥姿勢接受治療",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "needles be accounted for by counting the needles used",
          "hant": "清點所使用的針具數量",
          "correct": true
