        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "practitioners wear a white lab coat",
          "hant": "執業者穿著白色實驗袍",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In settings like a jail, the patient cannot leave until all of the needles are accounted for. In detox clinics, where the patient can remove their own needles, the acupuncturist should check and count the needles in case some have fallen on the floor or chair or if bleeding occurred. Chairs and the surrounding area should be checked before, during, and after each session. The detox clinic patient should be instructed not to handle the needles if they fall after removing them. Many public health settings (public acupuncture detox clinics, prison clinics, HIV clinics) acupuncture is given to multiple patients sitting in a chair. All chair surfaces need to be cleaned between patients. Hand sanitation is very important in a public treatment setting. As many of these settings may not have a sink or have one that is not easily accessible, it is critical that acupuncturists use alcohol-based hand sanitizers between each patient treatment. The CNT protocol in regards to needles, cotton balls, hand washing, etc. is the same whether acupuncture is done in a private acupuncture clinic, in a travel situation, or in a public health setting. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 89, 92",
      "exp_hant": "在監獄等場所，患者在所有針具清點確認之前不得離開。在戒毒診所，由於患者可自行取下針具，針灸師應檢查並清點針具數量，以防有針具掉落於地板或椅子上，或發生出血情況。每次治療前、中、後都應檢查椅子及周圍區域。應告知戒毒診所的患者，若針具自行取下後掉落，切勿自行處理。許多公共醫療場所（如公共針灸戒毒診所、監獄診所、愛滋病診所）會讓多名患者同時坐在椅子上接受針灸治療，每位患者使用後都必須清潔椅面。在公共治療場所中，手部清潔尤其重要。由於這些場所往往沒有水槽，或水槽不易使用，針灸師在為每位患者治療之間務必使用酒精性乾洗手液。無論是在私人針灸診所、外出出診或公共醫療場所執行針灸，其針具、棉球、洗手等潔淨針法（CNT）規範皆相同。《潔淨針法》第7版，第89、92頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 221,
      "question_en": "A 75 year-old male was brought to the acupuncture clinic by his son. The 75 year-old has been showing an increase in confusion and forgetfullness for the past two months. The father did not drink alcohol and had not been exposed to any environmental toxins. The son reported that three months earlier his father hit his head against a kitchen cabinet. During the interview the father was oriented to person, place, and time but was slow to answer questions. Heart and lung sounds were normal. He did not report chest pain or SOB. Which action would you take?",
      "question_hant": "一名75歲男性由其兒子帶至針灸診所就診。這位75歲長者近兩個月來意識混亂與健忘的情況逐漸加重。父親並無飲酒習慣，也未曾接觸任何環境毒素。兒子表示三個月前父親曾撞到頭部（撞上廚房櫥櫃）。問診時，父親對人物、地點、時間皆能正確定向，但回答問題的速度較慢。心音與呼吸音皆正常，患者亦未主訴胸痛或呼吸困難。你會採取何種處置？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
