      "exp_en": "The red flag is sudden leg weakness and possible unconsciousness in an elderly person when turning the head. Drop attacks from vertebrobasilar artery insufficiency (VBI) is assumed present until proven otherwise. The cause of VBI is significant decrease in blood flow to the brain due most often to cervical spine osteoarthritis and atherosclerosis in the elderly. The rotation of the head compresses the arteries thereby reducing blood flow to the brain. As long as the patient avoids extreme neck rotation or extreme exertion the referral can be timely. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 22-23",
      "exp_hant": "此案例的警訊為老年人轉頭時突發下肢無力，甚至可能意識喪失。在排除其他可能性之前，應假設患者為椎基底動脈供血不足（VBI）所引起的猝倒發作。VBI的成因多為老年人頸椎骨關節炎及動脈粥狀硬化，導致腦部血流明顯減少；頭部轉動時會壓迫動脈，進一步降低腦部血流量。只要患者避免劇烈轉頭或過度用力，即可採限期轉診。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第22-23頁"
