      "exp_en": "If the acupuncturist is unable to offer treatments due to illness, cancelling or postponing the appointments until the fever improves is the appropriate course of action. You do not provide treatment if you are ill. Options can include: 1) providing a treatment in a day or two later with the understanding that you will let the patients know in case you have not improved; 2) for the out of town patient or for the most urgent patients, you can refer to a local acupuncturist. In regards to body temperature, the average normal oral body temperature is 98.6F (37 Â°C). An axilla temperature is usually 0.5F (0.3C) to 1F (0.6C) lower than an oral temperature. A rectal temperature is 0.5F (0.3C) to 1F (0.6C) higher than an oral temperature. An ear temperature is 0.5F (0.3C) to 1F (0.6C) higher than an oral temperature. A forehead scanner is usually 0.5F (0.3C) to 1F (0.6C) lower than an oral temperature. Ethics Handbook for Energy Healing Practitioners, Kindle Edition, Feinstein, page 77",
      "exp_hant": "若針灸師因生病而無法提供治療，取消或延後預約直到發燒改善，才是適當的做法。生病時不應為患者提供治療。可行的做法包括：1) 延後一兩天再提供治療，並事先告知患者，若屆時仍未康復會再另行通知；2) 對於外地患者或病情較急迫者，可轉介至當地其他針灸師。關於體溫方面，正常口溫平均為98.6°F（37°C）。腋溫通常比口溫低0.5°F（0.3°C）至1°F（0.6°C）。肛溫通常比口溫高0.5°F（0.3°C）至1°F（0.6°C）。耳溫通常比口溫高0.5°F（0.3°C）至1°F（0.6°C）。額溫槍測得的體溫通常比口溫低0.5°F（0.3°C）至1°F（0.6°C）。《能量療癒執業者倫理手冊》，Kindle版，Feinstein著，第77頁"
