      ],
      "exp_en": "Systolic refers to the top number which is 160 in this patient. Anything above 120 systolic pressure is considered hypertension. Systolic pressure measures the blood vessel pressure when the heart beats. Anything above 80 for diastolic pressure (lower number) is considered hypertension. Diastolic pressure measures the blood vessel pressure when the heart rests between beats. Pulmonary hypertension (PHT) is high blood pressure occuring in the arteries in the lungs. PHT is a reading of the pressure/effort the heart must do to pump blood from the heart through lung arteries. PHT is measured with a special catheter (flexible tube) inserted into the right ventricle and pulmonary artery. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, pages 645, 714",
      "exp_hant": "收縮壓是指血壓數值中較高的那個數字，此患者為160。收縮壓高於120即屬高血壓範圍，收縮壓測量的是心臟收縮時血管所承受的壓力。舒張壓（較低的數字）高於80則屬高血壓範圍，舒張壓測量的是心臟兩次跳動之間放鬆時血管所承受的壓力。肺動脈高血壓（PHT）是指發生於肺動脈的高血壓，反映心臟將血液經肺動脈輸出時所需施加的壓力／做的功。PHT須以特殊導管（軟管）插入右心室及肺動脈方式測量。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學執業者教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第645、714頁"
