      "number": 234,
      "question_en": "A 72 year-old female has Obstructive Sleep Apnea. What are her symptoms?",
      "question_hant": "一名72歲女性罹患阻塞型睡眠呼吸中止症。她會出現哪些症狀？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "pursed lip breathing, prolonged expiratory period with grunting, dyspnea, barrel-shaped chest",
          "hant": "噘嘴呼吸、呼氣時間延長並伴隨呻吟聲、呼吸困難、桶狀胸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "productive cough for at least 3 months per year for 2+ years, cyanosis, dyspnea, wheezing",
          "hant": "連續兩年以上、每年至少三個月出現有痰咳嗽、發紺、呼吸困難、喘鳴",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "chest pain, dyspnea, anxiety, diminished breath sounds, lung hyperresonance on affected side",
          "hant": "胸痛、呼吸困難、焦慮、呼吸音減弱、患側肺部叩診呈過度回響音",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "loud snoring, snorting during sleep, restless sleep, unrefreshed sleep, fatigue",
          "hant": "大聲打鼾、睡眠中發出鼾鼻聲、睡眠不安穩、睡醒後仍感疲累、疲勞",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "There are two types of sleep apnea: obstructive (the most common) and central. In central sleep apnea, the brain fails to send signals to breathe whereas in obstructive sleep apnea the airways are blocked by the relaxed tongue, swollen tonsils, narrow throat, thick neck, etc. Obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is a serious sleep disorder where breathing stops (10 seconds or more) during sleep, sometimes 100s of times per evening. In OSA there are repetitive episodes of a complete or partial upper airway blockage. As a result, the diaphragm and respiratory muscles overwork to try to open the lung airways causing inhalation to start with a loud gasp or with the body twitching. Nighttime symptoms can include loud and disruptive snoring, sensation of choking during sleep, snorting, recurrent waking, unrefreshing sleep. Daytime symptoms include fatigue, sleepiness, poor concentration. If untreated, sleep apnea can lead to hypertension, an enlarged heart (cardiomyopathy), arrhythmias, diabetes, and congestive heart failure. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 500",
      "exp_hant": "睡眠呼吸中止症分為兩種類型：阻塞型（最常見）與中樞型。中樞型睡眠呼吸中止症是因大腦未能發出呼吸訊號所致，而阻塞型則是因舌根鬆弛後墜、扁桃腺腫大、咽喉狹窄、頸部粗厚等因素而阻塞呼吸道。阻塞型睡眠呼吸中止症（OSA）是一種嚴重的睡眠障礙，患者在睡眠中會反覆停止呼吸（達10秒以上），有時一夜之間可發生數百次。OSA的特徵是上呼吸道反覆發生完全或部分阻塞，導致橫膈膜及呼吸肌必須加倍用力，試圖打開呼吸道，使吸氣時伴隨大聲喘氣或身體抽動。夜間症狀包括大聲擾人的鼾聲、睡眠中感覺窒息、發出鼾鼻聲、反覆醒來、睡眠品質不佳。日間症狀則包括疲勞、嗜睡、注意力不集中。若未加以治療，睡眠呼吸中止症可能導致高血壓、心臟肥大（心肌病變）、心律不整、糖尿病及充血性心臟衰竭。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第500頁"
    },
