      "exp_en": "Pelvic inflammatory disease (PID) is an infection of the upper female genital tract: the cervix, uterus, fallopian tubes, and ovaries. An abscess may occur. PID may be sexually transmitted. Common symptoms and signs include lower abdominal pain, cervical discharge, and irregular vaginal bleeding. Long term complications of PID include infertility, chronic pelvic pain, and ectopic pregnancy. Gonorrhea , Chlamydia, and pathogens involved in vaginosis are common causes of PID. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2087",
      "exp_hant": "骨盆腔發炎疾病（PID）是女性上生殖道（子宮頸、子宮、輸卵管及卵巢）的感染，可能形成膿瘍，且可能透過性行為傳染。常見症狀與徵象包括下腹部疼痛、子宮頸分泌物增加，以及陰道不規則出血。PID的長期併發症包括不孕、慢性骨盆疼痛及子宮外孕。淋病、披衣菌感染，以及與陰道炎相關的病原體，皆為PID常見病因。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第2087頁"
