      "question_en": "A 7 year-old child presents to the clinic with her mother. The child has had a rash for the past two days. She also has had a runny nose and cough for three days. Her maximum temperature at home was 100.2 F (oral). She has had no vomiting or diarrhea. Her appetite is normal and her diet is balanced. She is not currently taking any medications or supplements. She appears alert, cooperative, well hydrated, and well nourished. Her temperature taken is slightly high at 100.2 F (oral). Examination of the skin shows a maculopapular rash on her back and chest. Two vesicles are visible on the upper right side of the chest. The rest of the body does not have a rash. An otoscopic examination reveals normal tympanic membranes. There is no inflammation in her tonsils and no cervical lymphatic nodes. Heart rate and respiratory rate are within normal ranges. The lungs are clear in all lobes. The heart has no murmurs. She has normal bowel sounds. What is the most likely diagnosis for the rash?",
      "question_hant": "一名7歲女童由母親陪同至診所就診。該女童過去兩天出現皮疹，並已有流鼻水及咳嗽三天。在家測得的最高體溫為100.2°F（口溫）。無嘔吐或腹瀉，食慾正常，飲食均衡。目前未服用任何藥物或營養補充品。她看起來意識清楚、配合度高、水分充足、營養良好。目前測得體溫略高，為100.2°F（口溫）。皮膚檢查顯示背部及胸部有斑丘疹，胸部右上方可見兩個水泡。身體其餘部位無皮疹。耳鏡檢查顯示鼓膜正常，扁桃腺無發炎，頸部淋巴結未觸及腫大。心跳速率與呼吸速率皆在正常範圍內，雙肺各葉呼吸音清晰，心臟無雜音，腸鳴音正常。此皮疹最可能的診斷為何？",
