      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Laparoscopy is used to detect endometriosis. An hysterogram or hysterosalpingography investigates the shape of the uterine cavity and fallopian tubes. A contrast dye is used to evaluate if the dye remains within the uterine cavity and fallopian tubes or if the dye spills out. Hysterogram diagnoses uterine malformations, Asherman's syndrome (intrauterine adhesions/scarring), and fallopian tubal occlusion. This test is extensively used in the work-up of infertile women to determine if there is a fallopian tube obstruction. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition,Pagana, page 1018-1021; 4th Edition page 1092-1093",
