      "question_en": "Roger is a 29-year-old corporal in special forces. He complains of a low-grade fever and a rash over his entire body and flu-like symptoms. He has just returned from Thailand two days ago. About six weeks before this he had sex with a sex worker at a bar. Roger thinks he has AIDS. Examination reveals stable vital signs and a temperature of 100 degrees. He has palpable lymph nodes in the neck which are slightly tender. He does not have any chancre sores on his penis. The rest of his history is unremarkable. What is the most probable diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "羅傑是一名29歲的特種部隊下士。他主訴輕度發燒、全身皮疹及類流感症狀。他兩天前才剛從泰國返國。大約在六週前，他曾與酒吧中的性工作者發生性行為。羅傑懷疑自己感染了愛滋病。理學檢查顯示生命徵象穩定，體溫為100°F，頸部可觸及輕微壓痛的淋巴結，陰莖上並無硬性下疳。其餘病史並無特殊之處。最可能的診斷為何？",
