      "exp_en": "He engaged in risky sexual behavior and probably has an acute HIV infection. The most common symptoms of an HIV infection include a body rash, fever, sore throat, severe headaches, fatigue, swollen lymph nodes, mouth or genitals ulcers, muscle pain, nausea/vomiting, and night sweats. History and symptoms fit perfectly and will probably get AIDS within 10 years. He needs an HIV ELISA test. If it is positive, he will then need a Western Blot test. If the ELISA test is negative, he can possibly convert to a positive test later. The ELISA test is a sensitive immunoassay that uses enzymes linked to an antibody or antigen as a marker for detecting a specific protein. Is ordered to determine exposure to an infectious agent, such as AIDS virus, by identifying antibodies that are present the blood sample. Western Blot test is another blood test which helps to confirm the diagnosis. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, pages 473, 712",
      "exp_hant": "他曾有高風險性行為，很可能罹患急性愛滋病毒感染。愛滋病毒感染最常見的症狀包括全身皮疹、發燒、喉嚨痛、劇烈頭痛、疲勞、淋巴結腫大、口腔或生殖器潰瘍、肌肉疼痛、噁心／嘔吐，以及夜間盜汗。此患者的病史與症狀完全吻合，若不治療，很可能在十年內發展為愛滋病。他需要接受愛滋病毒ELISA檢測；若結果為陽性，則需再進行西方墨點法（Western Blot）檢測以確認。若ELISA檢測為陰性，日後仍有可能轉為陽性。ELISA檢測是一種靈敏的免疫檢驗法，利用與抗體或抗原連結的酵素作為標記，以偵測特定蛋白質，可用於判斷是否曾暴露於感染源（如愛滋病毒），方法是偵測血液檢體中是否存在相應抗體。西方墨點法則是另一種血液檢驗，有助於確認診斷。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學執業者教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第473、712頁"
