      "exp_en": "Bacterial vaginosis is a mild bacterial infection of the vagina. The most common symptom is a fishy vaginal discharge that looks grayish white or yellow. The fishy smell can be worse after sex. Almost 50% of women who have bacterial vaginitis have no symptoms. The whiff test adds a small amount of potassium hydroxide to a microscopic slide which is smeared with vaginal discharge. A fishy odor is considered a positive whiff test. This is suggestive of bacterial vaginitis in about 75% of the cases. A sample of vaginal discharge can also be checked for bacteria, white blood cells, and clue cells. This is done with a vaginal wet mount (vaginal smear or wet prep) under a microscope. Clue cells are epithelial vaginal cells that are covered with bacteria. Clue cells indicate the presence of bacterial vaginosis. Differential Diagnosis, Rhoads, 2015 page 284-288",
      "exp_hant": "細菌性陰道炎是一種輕度的陰道細菌感染，最常見的症狀是呈灰白色或黃色、帶有魚腥味的陰道分泌物，且性交後氣味可能加重。約有50%罹患細菌性陰道炎的女性並無明顯症狀。胺臭味試驗是在塗有陰道分泌物的顯微鏡玻片上加入少量氫氧化鉀，若出現魚腥味即為陽性反應，此結果約有75%的機率提示細菌性陰道炎。陰道分泌物檢體也可在顯微鏡下以陰道濕式抹片（陰道抹片或濕式製片）檢查細菌、白血球及線索細胞。線索細胞是指表面覆蓋大量細菌的陰道上皮細胞，其存在即顯示有細菌性陰道炎。《鑑別診斷》，Rhoads著，2015年，第284-288頁"
