          "hant": "站立後15分鐘",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The procedure is to have the patient lie down for 5 minutes, then measure blood pressure and pulse rate. Have the patient stand. Repeat blood pressure and pulse rate measurements after standing 1 and 3 minutes. A drop in BP of greater or equal than 20 mm Hg, or in diastolic BP of greater or equal 10 mm Hg, or experiencing lightheadedness or dizziness is considered abnormal. In a supine position, blood flows more easily to the brain and feet because gravity is evenly affecting your body. The heart does not have to fight against gravity to push blood to the brain. The supine or reclining position is favored way to measure blood pressure because it is less stressful on the body. If one moves from a supine position to a standing position, there may be a momentary drop in blood pressure. This drop occurs because the body experiences a temporary drop in blood volume and then the blood pools in the lower legs. tcmtests.com, April 2020",
      "exp_hant": "測量程序為：先讓患者平躺5分鐘，測量血壓與脈搏；接著讓患者站立，於站立後1分鐘及3分鐘再次測量血壓與脈搏。若收縮壓下降達20 mmHg以上、舒張壓下降達10 mmHg以上，或出現頭暈目眩的感覺，即視為異常。平躺姿勢下，重力對全身的影響較為均勻，血液較容易流向腦部及雙腳，心臟不需對抗重力將血液推送至腦部，因此平躺或半躺姿勢較常用於測量血壓，對身體造成的負擔較小。若由平躺姿勢轉為站立，血壓可能會短暫下降，這是因為身體血液容積暫時降低，血液積聚於小腿所致。tcmtests.com，2020年4月"
