      ],
      "exp_en": "The most common mode of transmission of pathogens is via hands. Clean hands are the most important factor in preventing the spread of pathogens and antibiotic resistance in a health care setting. Hand washing reduces the incidence of infections associated with health care. Hand hygiene includes hand washing with antiseptics or alcohol-based disinfectants. The CDC recommends washing hands with liquid soap and water when the hands are visibly dirty, contaminated or soiled. When hands are not visibly soiled, an alcohol-based hand rub can be used when soap and water cannot be used to reduce bacterial counts. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 69",
      "exp_hant": "病原體最常見的傳播途徑是透過雙手。保持雙手清潔，是預防醫療場所中病原體傳播及抗生素抗藥性最重要的因素。洗手可降低醫療照護相關感染的發生率。手部衛生包括以消毒劑或酒精性消毒液洗手。美國疾病管制與預防中心（CDC）建議，當雙手明顯髒污或受到污染時，應以液態肥皂及清水洗手；若雙手並無明顯髒污，且無法使用肥皂與清水時，可使用酒精性乾洗手液以降低細菌數量。《潔淨針法》第7版，第69頁"
