      "exp_en": "Unless licensed to do so, it is illegal for acupuncturists to diagnose or treat medical diseases. The training of an acupuncturist involves 1) assessing the energetic configurations of qi, blood, yin/yang affecting the organ systems (zangfu); 2) performing procedures (acupuncture, moxibustion, herbal prescription, etc) outlined within their scope of practice; and 3) educating the patient about the TCM view of their disorder. If the acupuncturist assesses or suspects that the patient has a severe disease, certain guidelines need to be followed. These include: 1) practicing within the scope of practice; 2) perform procedures where the acupuncturist has received training or supervised experience. If after taking a comprehensive TCM assessment, the acupuncturist is still alarmed it can be pointed out to the patient that you have assessed strong energetic irregularities from feeling the pulse and seeing the tongue These irregularities have you concerned. It is also very important to let the patient know that you are unsure if something is seriously wrong. The acupuncturist can say something along the lines of \"I am concerned by what I'm feeling in your pulse and seeing in your tongue. I do not know what they really mean but to be professionally responsible I insist that you get a medical check up.\" Ethics Handbook for Energy Healing Practitioners, Kindle Edition, Feinstein, page 50",
      "exp_hant": "除非取得相關執照，否則針灸師對疾病進行醫學診斷或治療是違法的。針灸師的訓練內容包括：1) 評估氣、血、陰陽等能量狀態對臟腑系統的影響；2) 在其執業範圍內執行相關療法（如針灸、艾灸、中藥處方等）；3) 以中醫觀點向患者說明其病症。若針灸師評估或懷疑患者罹患嚴重疾病，應遵循特定原則，包括：1) 於執業範圍內執業；2) 僅執行自己曾受過訓練或有督導經驗的療法。若在完整的中醫辨證後，針灸師仍感到擔憂，可向患者說明：透過把脈及觀舌，評估出強烈的能量異常現象，這些異常讓你感到擔心。同時，務必讓患者知道你並不確定是否真的有嚴重問題。針灸師可以這樣告訴患者：「我對你脈象與舌象所顯示的狀況感到擔憂。我並不清楚這代表什麼意義，但基於專業責任，我堅持你必須接受醫學檢查。」《能量療癒執業者倫理手冊》，Kindle版，Feinstein著，第50頁"
