      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. Mycobacterium tuberculosis is associated with TB and spread through the air. The other bacteria are MOT (Mycobacteria Other than Tuberculosis). MOT is associated with acupuncture related skin lesions due to inadequate needle sterilization or unclean puncture site or dirt carried in by the patient or left in towels. MOT are often found in wet soil, streams or rivers. MOT bacteria grows slowly and can cause disease in individuals who have either a strong or weak immune system. Most commonly, MOT skin infections present with suppurative and ulcerated skin nodules. To prevent MOT it is important to follow hand washing, CNT procedures, disinfecting the treatment room and tables, replacing sheets or towels after each patient, and refer patients that may be infected for appropriate treatment. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 153, 154",
