      "exp_en": "AST is an enzyme which is found in highly active tissues (heart, liver, kidneys, brain, pancreas, skeletal muscles). When there is an injury or death of a cell, AST is released into the blood circulation. Any disease in which there is tissue injury in these highly metabolically active tissues will increase the AST enzyme in the blood. The higher the AST number, the more cells are damaged. The AST level rises in 12 hours after tissue injury/death and stays elevated for about the next five days. This test is mainly used to evaluate liver and heart disease. A Manual of Laboratory and Diagnostic Tests, 7th Edition, Fischbach, page 394",
      "exp_hant": "AST是一種存在於高度活躍組織（心臟、肝臟、腎臟、腦部、胰臟、骨骼肌）中的酵素。當細胞受損或死亡時，AST便會釋放進入血液循環。任何造成這些代謝活躍組織受損的疾病，皆會使血液中的AST濃度升高；AST數值越高，代表細胞受損程度越嚴重。組織受損或死亡後約12小時，AST濃度開始上升，並維持升高約五天。此檢驗主要用於評估肝臟與心臟疾病。《實驗室與診斷檢驗手冊》第7版，Fischbach著，第394頁"
