          "en": "Electroencephalography",
          "hant": "腦電圖檢查",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Electrocardiography",
          "hant": "心電圖檢查",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The EEG (electroencephalogram) test evaluates patients with seizures, brain tumors, brain strokes. The EEG can also be used to confirm brain death the EEG is a graphical recording of the electrical activity of the brain. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 4th Edition, Pagana, page 573-575; 2nd Edition, page 504",
      "exp_hant": "腦電圖（EEG）檢查用於評估癲癇發作、腦瘤、腦中風等患者的病情，也可用於確認腦死。腦電圖是以圖形方式記錄腦部電氣活動的檢查。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢驗手冊》第4版，Pagana著，第573-575頁；第2版，第504頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 253,
      "question_en": "Which knee exam tests for a meniscus injury?",
      "question_hant": "哪一項膝關節檢查用於檢測半月板損傷？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Varus Test",
          "hant": "內翻應力試驗",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "McMurray test",
          "hant": "麥莫瑞氏試驗（McMurray test）",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Valgus Test",
          "hant": "外翻應力試驗",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Lachman test",
          "hant": "拉赫曼氏試驗（Lachman test）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The meniscus is a rubbery, C-shaped disc that cushions the knee with each knee having two menisci. One meniscus is located at the outer edge of the knee and the other at the inner edge. The menisci stabilize the knee by balancing the weight across the knee. A tear in the meniscus is usually caused by twisting or turning quickly, often with the foot planted while the knee is bent. In a minor meniscus tear there can be slight pain and swelling which usually resolves itself in 2-3 weeks. A moderate meniscus tear causes pain at the side or center of the knee with swelling slowly worsening over 2-3 days. The knee can feel stiff but the patient can usually walk. There can be a sharp pain when twisting the knee or squatting. The symptoms of a moderate meniscus tear may resolve themselves in 1-2 weeks but can return with overuse of the knee. With a severe meniscus tear, fragments from the torn meniscus can move into the joint space and make the knee lock or pop. The knee may swell and stiffen right after the injury or within 2-3 days. The patient may not be able to straighten the knee and the knee may give way without warning. The Lachman tests the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL). The Valgus tests for the medial collateral ligament (MCL). The Varus tests for the lateral collateral ligament (LCL). Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 807-809; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 632",
      "exp_hant": "半月板是一種橡膠般、呈C形的軟骨盤，可緩衝膝關節的壓力，每側膝關節各有兩個半月板，分別位於膝關節外側緣及內側緣，透過平衡膝關節承受的重量來穩定膝關節。半月板撕裂通常是因快速扭轉動作所致，常發生於腳掌著地、膝蓋彎曲時。輕度半月板撕裂會出現輕微疼痛與腫脹，通常於2至3週內自行緩解。中度半月板撕裂則會造成膝關節側邊或中央疼痛，腫脹在2至3天內逐漸加劇，膝關節可能感覺僵硬，但患者通常仍可行走，扭轉膝關節或蹲下時可能出現劇烈疼痛。中度撕裂的症狀可能於1至2週內緩解，但過度使用膝關節時可能再次發作。嚴重半月板撕裂時，撕裂碎片可能移位至關節腔內，導致膝關節卡住或發出彈響，受傷後立即或2至3天內即可能出現腫脹與僵硬，患者可能無法伸直膝蓋，且膝關節可能毫無預警地突然無力。拉赫曼氏試驗用於檢測前十字韌帶（ACL），外翻應力試驗用於檢測內側副韌帶（MCL），內翻應力試驗則用於檢測外側副韌帶（LCL）。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第807-809頁；第10版，第632頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 254,
      "question_en": "One of your patients has fainted, is unresponsive, and without a pulse. You took CPR training a while back and have forgotten what to do. What is your next step?",
      "question_hant": "你的一位患者昏倒，失去反應且沒有脈搏。你先前曾接受過CPR訓練，但現在已經忘記該怎麼做。你接下來該採取什麼行動？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "needle DU-26 (ren zhong)",
          "hant": "針刺人中",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "call 911 and then start chest compression",
          "hant": "撥打911後開始施行胸外按壓",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "do rescue breathing first and call 911 emergency service",
          "hant": "先進行人工呼吸再撥打911緊急救護服務",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "go get your CPR notes",
          "hant": "去拿你的CPR筆記",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The American Heart Association recommends that anyone who sees an adult suddenly collapse should call 911 and push hard and fast on the center of the chest (100-120/min), a technique known as Hands-Only CPR. If you have forgotten CPR or are an untrained lay rescuer you should provide compression-only (Hands-Only) CPR, with or without dispatcher guidance, for adult victims of cardiac arrest. The rescuer should continue compression-only CPR until the arrival of 911 or rescuers with additional training. All lay rescuers should, at a minimum, provide chest compressions for victims of cardiac arrest. In addition, if the trained lay rescuer is able to perform rescue breaths, he or she should add rescue breaths in a ratio of 30 compressions to 2 breaths. The rescuer should continue CPR until emergency help arrives or the victim starts to move and become responsive. First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 44",
      "exp_hant": "美國心臟協會建議，任何人若目睹成人突然倒下失去意識，應撥打911，並在胸部正中央用力且快速按壓（每分鐘100至120次），此技術稱為「純按壓CPR」（Hands-Only CPR）。若你已忘記CPR的做法，或屬於未受過訓練的一般民眾，對於心臟停止的成人患者，應施行純按壓（Hands-Only）CPR，無論是否有調度員在電話中指導皆可進行。施救者應持續進行純按壓CPR，直到911救護人員或受過進階訓練的救援人員抵達。所有一般民眾施救者，至少都應為心臟停止患者施行胸外按壓；此外，若受過訓練的一般民眾能夠施行人工呼吸，則可加入人工呼吸，以30次按壓配合2次人工呼吸的比例進行。施救者應持續施行CPR，直到緊急救護人員抵達，或患者開始有動作並恢復反應為止。《紅十字會急救／CPR／AED學員手冊》，2016年，第44頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 255,
      "question_en": "Regarding email/SMS communication with a patient regarding their health, which of the following is FALSE?",
      "question_hant": "關於以電子郵件／簡訊與患者溝通其健康事項，下列敘述何者為錯誤？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Do not use direct patient identifiers in the subject line",
          "hant": "主旨欄不應使用可直接識別患者身分的資訊",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Double-check that the email/phone number is correct before sending",
          "hant": "傳送前應再次確認電子郵件地址／電話號碼是否正確",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "The patient must make a request to receive unencrypted email/SMS",
          "hant": "患者必須提出要求才能以未加密的電子郵件／簡訊接收訊息",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Email/SMS patient communication must be encrypted at all times",
          "hant": "與患者以電子郵件／簡訊溝通時，必須全程加密",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "SMS stands for Short Message Services that includes texting. The Privacy Rule allows covered health care providers to communicate electronically, such as through e-mail, with their patients, provided that reasonable safeguards are practiced when doing so. The highest level of patient protection is through encrypted email. Any covered entity should be internally communicating ePHI (electronic Protected Health Information) using encryption technology, which is not a problem with intra-organizational communication. However, using encrypted emails when communicating with a patient can be problematic as it would require the patient to install a compatible program to view encrypted emails. The HIPAA Privacy Rule recognizes this issue and grants patient access to ePHI in the format that the patient request, i.e. unencrypted email, as long as the patient is made aware of the risk involved in using unencrypted emails. Moreover, HIPAA Standard164.312(d) requires implementing procedures that verify that patients seeking access to ePHI are who they claim to be through verifying and double checking email addresses or phone numbers. Also, the HIPAA Standard 164.306(b) requires implementation of reasonable security measures which in this case would include not using the patient's name, initials, or medical record number in the subject line or using direct patient identifiers in the message content such as name, address, phone numbers, etc. and also not to disclose sensitive information (domestic abuse, STDs, drug abuse, etc.) via email. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "SMS是指簡訊服務，包含發送文字簡訊。隱私規則允許受規範的醫療照護提供者在採取合理防護措施的前提下，透過電子郵件等電子方式與患者溝通。對患者隱私保護程度最高的方式是使用加密電子郵件。任何受規範機構在內部溝通電子化受保護健康資訊（ePHI）時，皆應使用加密技術，此於組織內部溝通並無問題。然而，若在與患者溝通時使用加密電子郵件，可能會產生問題，因為患者必須安裝相容程式才能檢視加密郵件。HIPAA隱私規則已意識到此問題，因此允許以患者所要求的格式（例如未加密的電子郵件）提供ePHI存取，但前提是必須讓患者了解使用未加密電子郵件所涉及的風險。此外，HIPAA標準164.312(d)要求執行相關程序，透過核對並再次確認電子郵件地址或電話號碼，以驗證要求存取ePHI的患者身分是否屬實。同時，HIPAA標準164.306(b)則要求採取合理的安全措施，在此情境下包括：不得在主旨欄使用患者姓名、姓名縮寫或病歷號碼，也不得在訊息內容中使用可直接識別患者身分的資訊（如姓名、地址、電話號碼等），並且不得透過電子郵件揭露敏感資訊（如家庭暴力、性傳染病、藥物濫用等）。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
    },
    {
      "number": 256,
      "question_en": "A 16-year-old girl complains of lethargy, irregular menses, and depression. She says that she dropped out of all her after school activities because she feels unattractive and overweight. The physical examination shows ragged-appearing enamel over the front her teeth and thickened skin over her knuckles. She has a height and weight in the 95th and 85th percentile, respectively. Based on these findings, what do her symptoms suggest?",
      "question_hant": "一名16歲女孩主訴倦怠、月經不規則及憂鬱。她表示自己因覺得外貌沒有吸引力且過重，而退出了所有課後活動。理學檢查顯示她前排牙齒的琺瑯質呈現粗糙不平的外觀，指節皮膚增厚。她的身高與體重分別位於第95百分位及第85百分位。根據這些發現，她的症狀提示為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Hypothyroidism",
          "hant": "甲狀腺功能低下",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "anorexia nervosa",
          "hant": "厭食症",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "body dysmorphic disorder",
          "hant": "身體臆形症",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "bulimia nervosa",
          "hant": "暴食症",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Common clinical findings that suggest bulimia nervosa include callus formation on the knuckles and decayed tooth enamel. The calluses form due to the frequent use of the hand to induce vomiting. The decayed enamel forms due to the acidic nature of the vomitus. In contrast with anorexia nervosa bulimia patients may have normal body weight. The DSM-V (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders) characterizes bulimia nervosa as binge eating disorder which occurs at least once a week for at least 3 months with a lack of control. It most commonly effects young women. It is coupled with behaviors to prevent weight gain (vomiting, laxative use, enema use, aggressive exercising). Bulimia can have abdominal pain, irregular menses, irritability and lethargy. Classical signs of self-induced vomiting include eroded teeth, Russel sign (calluses on knuckles), and esophagitis. In order to differentiate anorexia from bulimia, bulimia patients usually have a normal or high BMI. Anorexic patients often have a BMI below the 85th percentile. Hypothyroidism can have weight gain with lethargy and depression. But it does not usually include damaged tooth enamel and callus formation. Body dysmorphic disorder has a distorted body image. A common scenario dysmorphic disorder is a patient obsessing with a facial feature and then wanting frequent plastic surgeries. DSM-5 (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders) Chapter 10",
      "exp_hant": "提示暴食症的常見臨床表現包括指節出現繭狀增厚及牙齒琺瑯質腐蝕。指節長繭是因頻繁用手指誘發嘔吐所致，琺瑯質腐蝕則是因嘔吐物具有酸性所致。與厭食症不同的是，暴食症患者的體重可能維持在正常範圍。DSM-5（精神疾病診斷與統計手冊第五版）將暴食症定義為一種暴食性疾患，特徵為每週至少發作一次、持續至少三個月，且患者對進食缺乏控制感。此病最常見於年輕女性，通常合併有預防體重增加的行為（如嘔吐、使用瀉藥、使用灌腸劑、過度運動）。暴食症可能伴隨腹痛、月經不規則、易怒及倦怠。自我誘發嘔吐的典型徵象包括牙齒腐蝕、羅素氏徵象（指節長繭），以及食道炎。要區分厭食症與暴食症，暴食症患者的身體質量指數（BMI）通常正常或偏高，而厭食症患者的BMI則常低於第85百分位。甲狀腺功能低下可能出現體重增加、倦怠及憂鬱，但通常不會伴隨牙齒琺瑯質損傷及指節長繭。身體臆形症則是對自身外貌有扭曲的認知，常見情境是患者過度執著於某項臉部特徵，進而反覆要求整形手術。DSM-5（精神疾病診斷與統計手冊）第10章"
    },
    {
      "number": 257,
      "question_en": "Sleep apnea is characterized by",
      "question_hant": "睡眠呼吸中止症的特徵為：",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Shortness of breath at night, Lack of movement during sleep, Early morning headache, Loud intermittent snoring",
          "hant": "夜間呼吸急促、睡眠中缺乏活動、清晨頭痛、間歇性大聲打鼾",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Loud intermittent snoring, Shortness of breath at night",
          "hant": "間歇性大聲打鼾、夜間呼吸急促",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Shortness of breath at night, Early morning headache, Loud intermittent snoring",
          "hant": "夜間呼吸急促、清晨頭痛、間歇性大聲打鼾",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Lack of movement during sleep, Loud intermittent snoring",
          "hant": "睡眠中缺乏活動、間歇性大聲打鼾",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "An apnea is the complete cessation of breathing for 10 or more seconds. Sleep apnea is a potentially serious disorder. There are three major types of sleep apnea: 1) obstructive sleep apnea, the more common form, is the result of the throat muscles relaxing so much that they block or narrow the airway. 2) central sleep apnea is result of the brain not sending signals to those muscles which control breathing. 3) complex sleep apnea syndrome has both obstructive sleep apnea and central sleep apnea. The most common cause of central sleep apnea is heart failure. Symptoms of sleep apnea include: excess sleepiness during the day, morning headache, loud snoring, breathing cessation during sleep, choking or gasping during sleep, suddenly waking up with SOB, difficulty staying asleep, and loud frequent snoring. Lack of movement during sleep is not a key part of the diagnosis. tcmtests.com, April 2020",
      "exp_hant": "呼吸中止是指呼吸完全停止達10秒以上。睡眠呼吸中止症是一種可能相當嚴重的疾病，主要分為三種類型：1) 阻塞型睡眠呼吸中止症，為較常見的類型，是因喉部肌肉過度放鬆而阻塞或狹窄呼吸道所致；2) 中樞型睡眠呼吸中止症，是因大腦未發出訊號至控制呼吸的肌肉所致；3) 複合型睡眠呼吸中止症候群，則同時具有阻塞型與中樞型的特徵。中樞型睡眠呼吸中止症最常見的病因是心臟衰竭。睡眠呼吸中止症的症狀包括：白天過度嗜睡、晨間頭痛、大聲打鼾、睡眠中呼吸停止、睡眠中出現窒息或喘氣、突然因呼吸困難而驚醒、難以維持睡眠，以及頻繁的大聲打鼾。睡眠中缺乏活動並非診斷的關鍵要素。tcmtests.com，2020年4月"
    },
    {
      "number": 258,
      "question_en": "A patient has recently been diagnosed with hypertension. Where would you place the stethoscope to hear possible bruit sounds?",
      "question_hant": "一名患者近期被診斷罹患高血壓。應將聽診器放置於何處以聽取可能的血管雜音（bruit）？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "left upper quadrant",
          "hant": "左上腹象限",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "the costovertebral angles",
          "hant": "肋脊角",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "mid abdomen just below the navel",
          "hant": "腹部中央、肚臍下方",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "right upper quadrant",
          "hant": "右上腹象限",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Bruits are \"swishing\" sounds heard over major arteries. The area over the aorta, both renal arteries, and the iliac arteries should be examined carefully for bruits. The costovertebral angle is the acute angle formed on either side of the back between the twelfth rib and the vertebral column. It is the location of the kidneys and renal arteries. A bruit sound (buzzing or swishing) can be heard over the renal arteries in all patients who have been diagnosed with recent onset hypertension. This indicates the presence of renal stenosis. Hypertension from renal stenosis is more common in women and can be cured, unlike essential hypertension which is treatable but not curable. One can also hear aortic bruits when the stethoscope is placed mid abdomen just below the navel and suggests advanced aortic atherosclerosis. Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 71, 72",
      "exp_hant": "血管雜音是指在大動脈上方聽到的「咻咻聲」。應仔細檢查主動脈、兩側腎動脈及髂動脈上方是否有血管雜音。肋脊角是指背部兩側由第十二肋骨與脊椎所形成的銳角區域，為腎臟及腎動脈所在位置。所有近期被診斷為高血壓的患者，皆應於腎動脈上方聽診是否有血管雜音（嗡嗡聲或咻咻聲），此徵象顯示可能存在腎動脈狹窄。腎動脈狹窄所引起的高血壓較常見於女性，且此類高血壓可被治癒，不同於原發性高血壓僅能控制而無法根治。此外，若將聽診器放置於腹部中央、肚臍下方，聽到主動脈血管雜音則提示已有進展性的主動脈粥狀硬化。《亞洲醫學執業者西醫理學檢查技巧》，2009年，Robinson、Wolfe著，第71、72頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 259,
      "question_en": "A 72 year-old female is taking Lotrel (amlodipine/benazepril). What is the drug treating?",
      "question_hant": "一名72歲女性正在服用Lotrel（amlodipine／benazepril）。此藥物是用來治療什麼病症？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
