      "exp_en": "Varicella is a common childhood infection. The symptoms are fever, malaise, poor appetite, headache, sore throat, and an itchy rash. Measles and chicken pox and mumps are caused by different viruses. Measles can have a sore throat and a rash of white spots inside the cheeks. Children with chickenpox tend to have a headache or stomach ache. The fever of measles is higher than that of chicken pox. Chickenpox has sores that fill with fluid and then turn into blisters. The sores manifest in groups but the blisters are usually separate and do not join to each other. On the other hand, measles sores do not have fluid, are small-raised-red areas on the skin, and usually join together to create larger rash patches. The classic sign of mumps is swollen salivary glands that make the cheeks puff out. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1603",
      "exp_hant": "水痘是常見的兒童傳染病，症狀包括發燒、倦怠、食慾不振、頭痛、喉嚨痛及搔癢性皮疹。麻疹、水痘與腮腺炎皆是由不同病毒所引起。麻疹可能伴隨喉嚨痛，並在雙頰內側出現白色斑點狀皮疹；水痘患兒則常出現頭痛或腹痛。麻疹的發燒程度通常高於水痘。水痘的皮疹會先充滿液體再轉變為水泡，皮疹雖成群出現，但水泡通常各自獨立、不會相互融合；相對地，麻疹皮疹則不含液體，呈現小而突起的紅色斑點，通常會相互融合形成較大片的皮疹。腮腺炎的典型徵象則是唾液腺腫大，使雙頰鼓起。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第1603頁"
