          "hant": "冠狀動脈斑塊形成",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Calcium, magnesium, potassium are electrolytes as well as chloride, phosphorus, sodium. Electrolytes are minerals in the blood and body fluids that have an electric charge. Electrolytes regulate body fluids, blood pH, and muscle contraction (including heart). The electrolytes sodium, potassium, magnesium and calcium are involved in heart contraction and relaxation. Electrolytes trigger and sustain the electrical impulses of the heart. Blood pressure has a relation to electrolytes found in the diet. If there is a high sodium diet, it can lead to hypertension. Insufficient amounts of potassium, calcium, and magnesium can also trigger hypertension. Further, a potassium imbalance is the most common electrolyte affecting cardiac arrhythmias. mayoclinic.org",
      "exp_hant": "鈣、鎂、鉀與氯、磷、鈉皆屬於電解質。電解質是存在於血液與體液中、帶有電荷的礦物質，負責調節體液平衡、血液酸鹼值，以及肌肉收縮（包括心肌）。鈉、鉀、鎂及鈣等電解質皆參與心臟的收縮與舒張，能誘發並維持心臟的電氣衝動。血壓與飲食中的電解質攝取有關：高鈉飲食可能導致高血壓，鉀、鈣及鎂攝取不足同樣可能引發高血壓。此外，鉀失衡是最常見、會影響心律不整的電解質異常。mayoclinic.org"
    },
