      "exp_en": "The examiner places the stethoscope over four areas of the chest to listen to the heart valves. The order of listening is: 1) To listen to the aortic valve the stethoscope is first placed in the area of the 2nd intercostal space near the sternal border on the right side of the patient's sternum. 2) To listen to the pulmonary valve the stethoscope is then placed in the area of the 2nd intercostal space near the sternal border on the left side of the patient's sternum. The closing of the aortic and pulmonary valves produce the S2 (heart sound two or \"dub\"). 3) To listen to the tricuspid valve the stethoscope is then placed in the area of the 4th intercostal space near the sternal border on the left side of the patient's sternum. 4) To listen to the mitral valve the stethoscope is then placed on the 5th intercostal space on the mid clavicular line on the left side of the patient's chest. The closing of the tricuspid valve and mitral valves produce the S1 (heart sound one or \"lub\"). Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 54",
      "exp_hant": "檢查者會將聽診器放置於胸部四個部位，以聽診心臟瓣膜，聽診順序如下：1) 聽診主動脈瓣時，先將聽診器放置於患者胸骨右側、第二肋間、靠近胸骨緣處；2) 聽診肺動脈瓣時，再將聽診器移至患者胸骨左側、第二肋間、靠近胸骨緣處，主動脈瓣與肺動脈瓣關閉時會產生第二心音（S2，即「登」聲）；3) 聽診三尖瓣時，將聽診器移至患者胸骨左側、第四肋間、靠近胸骨緣處；4) 聽診二尖瓣時，將聽診器移至患者胸部左側、第五肋間、鎖骨中線處，三尖瓣與二尖瓣關閉時則會產生第一心音（S1，即「撲」聲）。《亞洲醫學執業者西醫理學檢查技巧》，2009年，Robinson、Wolfe著，第54頁"
