      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Anti-depressants are not used in the treatment of the depressive phase of bipolar disorders because they are ineffective and because they can shift the patient into a mania phase. Bipolar disorder was previously termed as manic-depression. There are various categories of Bipolar Disorders which vary according to the severity of the mania. Bipolar I has more severe mania than the Bipolar II subtype. Bipolar I has episodes of mania and depression while Bipolar II has episodes of depression with the less severe form of mania called hypomania. The mania phase is characterized by persistent elevated mood lasting for at least one week with at least three of the following symptoms. Grandiosity, decrease need of sleep, talkativeness, flight of ideas, distractibility, increased goal directed activity, and excess involvement in pleasurable actions (buying sprees, sex, gambling) with possible negative consequences. LITHIUM is widely used in the treatment of bipolar disorder, helping to reduce the severity and frequency of mania and can also help relieve/prevent bipolar depression. It takes weeks before its mood stabilizing effect are experienced Because of possible toxicity to the kidneys and thyroid, periodic blood tests are done. Lithium can be prescribed for long periods of time, even between episodes, as a maintenance therapy. Lithium can significantly reduce suicide risk. ANTICONVULSANTS inhibit voltage gated sodium channels, which accounts for their anticonvulsant property. They also increase the neurotransmitter GABA, which accounts for their calming property. If the anticonvulsant increases GABA then they are used in the manic phase. If the anticonvulsant only affects the sodium channel without increasing GABA then they are used for the depressive phase. ATYPICAL ANTIPSYCHOTICS refers to the second generation of antipsychotics which affect serotonin receptors more than dopamine receptors. They are used used \"off label\" as sedatives (for insomnia, anxiety, agitation) and for their mood stabilizing properties helping to control depression and mania They are also used to control psychotic symptoms (hallucinations, delusions) that can occur in very severe depressive or manic episodes. tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。抗憂鬱藥並不用於治療雙相情感障礙的憂鬱期，因為它們效果不佳，且可能使患者轉入躁期。雙相情感障礙過去稱為躁鬱症。雙相情感障礙依躁狂嚴重程度可分為不同類型。第一型雙相情感障礙的躁狂程度比第二型更為嚴重。第一型有躁狂與憂鬱發作，第二型則有憂鬱發作與較輕微的躁狂（稱為輕躁狂）發作。躁狂期的特徵是持續性情緒高漲至少一週，並伴隨下列症狀中至少三項：自大誇大、睡眠需求減少、多話、意念飛躍、注意力不集中、目標導向活動增加，以及過度從事享樂行為（如揮霍購物、性行為、賭博）且可能帶來不良後果。鋰鹽廣泛用於治療雙相情感障礙，有助於降低躁狂的嚴重程度與發作頻率，也能協助緩解／預防雙相憂鬱。其穩定情緒的效果需數週才能顯現。由於鋰鹽可能對腎臟及甲狀腺具毒性，須定期進行血液檢查。鋰鹽可長期使用，甚至在發作間期作為維持治療。鋰鹽可顯著降低自殺風險。抗癲癇藥能抑制電壓門控鈉離子通道，此為其抗癲癇特性的來源；同時也能增加神經傳導物質GABA，因而具有鎮靜作用。若抗癲癇藥能增加GABA，則多用於躁期；若僅作用於鈉離子通道而不增加GABA，則多用於憂鬱期。非典型抗精神病藥指第二代抗精神病藥物，其對血清素受體的作用大於對多巴胺受體的作用。這類藥物常「仿單標示外」用作鎮靜劑（治療失眠、焦慮、躁動），並因具有穩定情緒的特性而有助於控制憂鬱與躁狂，也用於控制嚴重憂鬱或躁狂發作時可能出現的精神病症狀（幻覺、妄想）。tcmtests.com，2020年7月"
    },
