    {
      "number": 289,
      "question_en": "A 60 year-old male commodities broker complains of chest pain. He reports that the pain is +5/10 and has been increasing during the past three days. When he walks, he has both chest pain and dyspnea. The chest pain lessens by sitting upright and leaning forward. He denies radiation to his jaw, back, or to his arms. Family history: father died at age 58 from an MI and mother died at age 75 with COPD. His medications include allopurinol for gout, ibuprofen for joint pain, and famotidine for acid reflux. He has no allergies. His facial complexion is ashen. Vital signs: BP 142/94; Pulse 95; Respiration 28; Body temperature 100.8 F; Height 6 ft 4; Weight 247 lbs. HEENT is negative. Cardiovascular: S1/S2 are strong with pericardial friction rub. He has ankle edema. What is the most likely diagnosis for the chest pain?",
      "question_hant": "60歲男性期貨經紀人主訴胸痛。他表示疼痛程度為+5/10，且過去三天持續加劇。走路時會同時出現胸痛與呼吸困難。採坐姿並向前傾身時胸痛會減輕。他否認疼痛放射至下顎、背部或手臂。家族病史：父親於58歲時死於心肌梗塞，母親於75歲時因慢性阻塞性肺病（COPD）過世。他目前服用之藥物包括治療痛風的allopurinol（別嘌醇）、治療關節痛的ibuprofen（布洛芬），以及治療胃酸逆流的famotidine（法莫替丁）。他無藥物過敏史。他的面色蒼白灰暗。生命徵象：血壓142/94；脈搏95；呼吸28；體溫100.8°F；身高6呎4吋；體重247磅。頭頸耳鼻喉（HEENT）檢查為陰性。心血管系統：第一、二心音強而有力，並可聽到心包摩擦音。他有踝部水腫。此胸痛最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "GERD",
          "hant": "胃食道逆流",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Pericarditis",
          "hant": "心包炎",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "myocardial infarction",
          "hant": "心肌梗塞",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "dilated cardiomyopathy",
          "hant": "擴張型心肌病變",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The most likely diagnosis is pericarditis which refers to an inflammation of the pericardium. The pericardium consists of two thin sack layers surrounding the heart with a small amount of fluid to prevent the layers from rubbing against each other. When present, symptoms of pericarditis can include chest pain, low-grade fever (100.0 F), and increased heart rate (pulse 95). The sharp chest pain is caused by the heart rubbing against the pericardium. The pain can worsen with coughing, swallowing, taking deep breaths, or in a supine position. The pain improves when sitting up and leaning forward. There can also be the need to bend over to breathe more comfortably. When listening to the heart, pericarditis the doctor can hear a rubbing or creaking sound caused by the rubbing of the inflamed lining of the pericardium. This is called the \"pericardial rub\" and is best heard when the patient leans forward and holds his breath and breathes out. Pericarditis can cause edema of the feet, legs and ankles. This swelling may be a symptom of what is called constrictive pericarditis. In this situation, the pericardium thickens. When this happens, the heart muscle cannot expand and becomes compressed, resulting in blood and fluids backing up into the lungs, abdomen and legs to cause edema. Diagnostic tests for pericarditis include chest x-ray (look at heart size), ECG to detect heart rhythm changes, echocardiogram to check for fluid flow around the heart, cardiac MRI to check thickening or heart compression. As there is a history of heart attack in the family, a myocardial infarction needs to be ruled out for this patient via blood tests to detect cardiac markers (cardiac troponins T and I, creatine kinase) for the presence of a heart attack. Many patients develop pericarditis after a major heart attack. Dilated cardiomyopathy occurs when the blood pumping function of the heart is decreased because its main pumping chamber (the left ventricle) is enlarged and weakened. Symptoms include SOB, leg edema, fatigue, weight gain, fainting, palpitations, dizziness, and blood clots. Symptoms of GERD (gastroesophageal reflux disease) usually occurs after a meal, when the patient lies down or goes to bed closely after eating. These symptoms include heartburn, regurgitation and vomiting, sour mouth taste, indigestion, sore throat from the acid, cough, difficulty swallowing (dysphagia). GERD and other digestive disorder (ulcers, muscle spasms in the esophagus, a gallbladder attack, and pancreatitis) can all cause chest pain and other symptoms that can mimic those of a heart attack or angina. If the problem is heart-related there will likely be tightness, burning, or pressure in the chest that worsens with exercise or severe emotional stress. The pain may spread to the back, neck, jaw, or arms, and is often associated with sweating, dizziness, nausea, difficulty breathing, or an irregular pulse. If the problem is related to the digestive system, the chest pain is often precipitated by eating a fatty or spicy meal and is affected by a change in position (worse lying down or bending over). Some patients get angina after eating a big meal because blood flow is diverted from the heart for digestion. If there is chest pain that seems to be digestive related, antacids should improve the symptoms. Taking a crushed aspirin, which is a blood thinner, can bring relief for those suffering from heart problems while waiting for medical care. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 275-277",
      "exp_hant": "最可能的診斷是心包炎，即心包膜的發炎。心包膜由兩層薄膜組成，包覆著心臟，兩層之間有少量液體以防止彼此摩擦。心包炎的症狀可能包括胸痛、低度發燒（100.0°F）及心跳加快（脈搏95次）。劇烈的胸痛是由於心臟與心包膜摩擦所致。此疼痛可能因咳嗽、吞嚥、深呼吸或平躺而加劇，在坐直並前傾時則會減輕，患者有時也需要彎腰才能較舒適地呼吸。聽診心臟時，心包炎患者可聽到摩擦或吱嘎聲，這是由發炎的心包內膜相互摩擦所致，稱為「心包摩擦音」，在患者前傾並閉氣吐氣時最容易聽到。心包炎可造成足部、小腿及踝部水腫，此種腫脹可能是所謂「縮窄性心包炎」的徵兆。在此情況下，心包膜增厚，使心肌無法擴張而受到壓迫，導致血液與體液回流積聚於肺部、腹部及下肢而造成水腫。心包炎的診斷檢查包括胸部X光（觀察心臟大小）、心電圖（偵測心律變化）、心臟超音波（檢查心臟周圍的液體流動）、心臟核磁共振（檢查心包增厚或心臟受壓情形）。由於此患者有心臟病家族史，須透過血液檢查偵測心臟指標（心肌旋轉蛋白T及I、肌酸激酶）以排除心肌梗塞的可能。許多患者是在嚴重心臟病發作後併發心包炎。擴張型心肌病變是指心臟主要幫浦腔室（左心室）擴大且無力，導致心臟打血功能下降。其症狀包括呼吸急促、下肢水腫、疲勞、體重增加、暈厥、心悸、頭暈及血栓。胃食道逆流（GERD）的症狀通常於進食後、患者平躺或飯後不久上床時出現，包括火燒心、逆流與嘔吐、口中有酸味、消化不良、因胃酸引起的喉嚨痛、咳嗽及吞嚥困難。GERD及其他消化系統疾病（潰瘍、食道肌肉痙攣、膽囊發作、胰臟炎）皆可能造成胸痛及其他類似心臟病發作或心絞痛的症狀。若問題與心臟有關，胸部通常會有緊縮感、灼熱感或壓迫感，且在運動或情緒劇烈波動時會加劇，疼痛可能擴散至背部、頸部、下顎或手臂，並常伴隨盜汗、頭暈、噁心、呼吸困難或脈搏不整。若問題與消化系統有關，胸痛則常於進食油膩或辛辣食物後誘發，且會因姿勢改變而變化（平躺或彎腰時加劇）。部分患者在飽餐一頓後會出現心絞痛，這是因為血流被分流至消化系統所致。若懷疑胸痛與消化系統有關，服用制酸劑應能改善症狀。在等待醫療救助時，服用一顆壓碎的阿斯匹靈（具抗凝血作用）可為心臟疾病患者帶來緩解。《家庭護理師臨床病例研究》，Leslie Neal-Boylan著，2011年，第275-277頁"
    },
    {
