      ],
      "exp_en": "A dermatome is an area of the skin that is mainly supplied by branches of a single spinal sensory nerve root. These spinal sensory nerves enter the nerve root at the spinal cord, and their branches reach to the periphery of the body to the skin. The sensory nerves on the skin transmit signals from sensations (pain symptoms, touch, temperature) to the spinal cord from that specific area of the skin. The spinal column is divided into 31 segments. Each segment has right and left pair of anterior and posterior nerve roots. Anterior nerve roots are responsible for motor signals to the body. Posterior nerve roots receive sensory signals from the body. The anterior and posterior nerve roots combine on each side to form the spinal nerves as they exit the vertebral canal. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 884-885; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 694-695",
      "exp_hant": "皮節是指主要由單一脊髓感覺神經根所支配的皮膚區域。這些脊髓感覺神經在脊髓處進入神經根，其分支延伸至身體周邊的皮膚。皮膚上的感覺神經會將該皮膚區域的感覺（疼痛症狀、觸覺、溫度）訊號傳回脊髓。脊柱共分為31個節段，每個節段左右兩側各有一對前根與後根。前根負責將運動訊號傳至身體，後根則接收來自身體的感覺訊號。前根與後根在椎管出口處於兩側各自匯合，形成脊神經。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第884-885頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第694-695頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 292,
      "question_en": "You have your patient lie supine and you place the painful knee in 15 degrees of flexion with a slight external rotation. You stabilize the distal femur with one hand just proximal to the knee, and grasp the proximal tibia with the other hand just distal to the knee, positioning the thumb along the medial joint line. Apply a firm anterior force to the tibia while holding the femur steady to assess anterior tibial translation. You are performing which test?",
      "question_hant": "您讓患者仰臥，將疼痛的膝關節置於屈曲15度並輕微外旋的姿勢。您以一手固定股骨遠端，位於膝關節近端處；另一手握住脛骨近端，位於膝關節遠端處，並將拇指置於內側關節線上。對脛骨施加穩定的前向力，同時固定股骨，以評估脛骨的前向位移。您正在進行的是哪一項測試？",
