      ],
      "exp_en": "The Lachman test is a passive movement test of the knee performed to identify the integrity of the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL). Bate's recommends external rotating the knee while other sources do not. Bate's (page 633) says to put the knee in 15 degrees of flexion while other sources say 20-30 degrees of flexion. Interpretation: a healthy ACL prevents a forward excursion movement (\"firm endpoint\") while an injured ACL knee will show increased forward excursion without a decisive \"end-point\" that feels like a soft or mushy endpoint which means a positive test. A positive test a 17.0 increase of having a torn ACL. More than about 2 mm of anterior translation compared to the healthy knee implies a torn ACL (\"soft endpoint\") as does 10 mm of total anterior translation. A healthy ACL prevents a forward excursion movement (\"firm endpoint\") while an injured ACL knee will show increased forward excursion without a decisive \"end-point\" that feels like a soft or mushy endpoint indicative which means a positive test. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 807-809; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 633",
      "exp_hant": "拉赫曼測試是一種膝關節被動運動測試，用以評估前十字韌帶（ACL）的完整性。Bate氏建議在測試時將膝關節外旋，而其他文獻則無此建議。Bate氏（第633頁）建議將膝關節屈曲15度，而其他文獻則建議屈曲20-30度。判讀：健康的前十字韌帶會阻止脛骨前移（呈現「明確終點」），而受損的前十字韌帶膝關節則會出現前移增加，且沒有明確的「終點」，感覺呈現柔軟或鬆軟的終點，即為陽性結果。陽性結果顯示前十字韌帶撕裂的可能性大幅增加。若前向位移較健側膝關節多出約2毫米以上，即提示前十字韌帶撕裂（「鬆軟終點」），總前向位移達10毫米亦同。健康的前十字韌帶會阻止脛骨前移（呈現「明確終點」），而受損的前十字韌帶膝關節則會出現前移增加，且無明確的「終點」，呈現柔軟或鬆軟的終點，即為陽性結果。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第807-809頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第633頁"
    },
