      ],
      "exp_en": "The negative urine culture rules out an UTI. The normal TSH levels most likely rule out hyperthyroidism. TSH levels in school-age children normally ranges from 0.4 to 5.0 microunits per milliliter of blood. The lab tests negate seeing the incontinence as just childhood enuresis. The American Diabetic Association (2010) has three criteria for diagnosing diabetes: 1) HbA1c &gt;= 6.5% OR 2) fasting plasma glucose &gt;= 126 mg/dL OR 3)two hour plasma glucose &gt;= 200 mg/DL during an oral glucose tolerance test with a glucose load of 75 grams dissolved in water. Any of these three criteria must be confirmed by a repeat test for a diagnosis. In Type 1 diabetes, an auto-immune disorder, the pancreas fail to produce insulin. In type 2 diabetes diet related insulin release is so large and frequent that receptor cells have become less sensitive to the insulin. This insulin resistance results in less sugar being removed from the blood. The age of the patient can be considered but is not reliable. There is currently no available test to definitely differentiate between type 1 and type 2 diabetes. Age is one factor with type 1 occurring more frequently with children and type 2 with adults. The presence of certain antibodies (glutamic acid decarboxylase or GAD) in the pancreas can suggest type 1 but this is not definitive. Clinical monitoring or the patient is important in making the differentiation. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 117-120",
      "exp_hant": "尿液培養陰性可排除泌尿道感染。TSH數值正常則多可排除甲狀腺機能亢進；學齡兒童的TSH正常範圍約為0.4至5.0微單位／毫升。實驗室檢查結果顯示此尿失禁並非單純的兒童遺尿症。美國糖尿病協會（2010年）提出三項糖尿病診斷標準：1）糖化血色素≧6.5%；或2）空腹血漿葡萄糖≧126 mg/dL；或3）口服葡萄糖耐受試驗中，以75公克葡萄糖溶於水中作為負荷後，兩小時血漿葡萄糖≧200 mg/dL。上述任一項標準皆須以重複檢測確認方能診斷。第一型糖尿病是一種自體免疫疾病，胰臟無法製造胰島素；第二型糖尿病則因飲食因素導致胰島素釋放過量且頻繁，使受體細胞對胰島素的敏感度降低，此胰島素阻抗導致血糖無法有效被清除。患者年齡可作為參考，但並非可靠指標；目前尚無檢測方法可明確區分第一型與第二型糖尿病。年齡是其中一項參考因素，第一型較常見於兒童，第二型則較常見於成人。胰臟中特定抗體（麩胺酸去羧酶抗體，GAD）的存在可能提示第一型糖尿病，但並非決定性依據。持續的臨床觀察對於區分兩者相當重要。《家庭護理師臨床病例研究》，Leslie Neal-Boylan著，2011年，第117-120頁"
