      "exp_en": "Biceps, C5-6, musculocutaneous nerve, brachialis, C5-6 musculocutaneous nerve are the prime movers. The brachioradialis and supinator are secondary movers. Rotation Handout Family Medicine Residence Orthopedic Rotation Monteleone Jr. Dept. of Family Medicine West Virginia School of Medicine with further references to Magee's Orthopedic Physical Assessment and Hoppenfeld's Examination of the Spine and Extremities; Medicinehsc.wvu.edu",
      "exp_hant": "肱二頭肌（受C5-6神經根、肌皮神經支配）與肱肌（受C5-6神經根、肌皮神經支配）為肘關節屈曲的主要作用肌，肱橈肌與旋後肌則為次要作用肌。《西維吉尼亞醫學院家庭醫學住院醫師骨科輪訓講義》，Monteleone Jr.，家庭醫學系，並參考Magee《骨科理學評估》及Hoppenfeld《脊椎與四肢檢查》；Medicinehsc.wvu.edu"
    },
    {
      "number": 297,
      "question_en": "A 12 year-old patient with a history of asthma has had an itchy rash for the past two years. The itch is so intense, particularly at night, that he scratches it until the skin bleeds. The rash is dry with areas of thickened skin affecting the inner creases of the knees and elbows. He is taking the drug fluticasone. The skin prick test is positive for animal dander. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一名12歲患者有氣喘病史，過去兩年出現搔癢性皮疹。搔癢感非常劇烈，尤其在夜間，患者會抓到皮膚出血。皮疹乾燥，膝窩及肘窩內側皮膚有增厚的區域。他正在服用fluticasone（fluticasone）。皮膚點刺試驗對動物皮屑呈陽性反應。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Drug reaction",
          "hant": "藥物反應",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "psoriasis",
          "hant": "乾癬",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "eczema",
          "hant": "濕疹",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "scabies",
          "hant": "疥瘡",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In the US, eczema affects about 10-20% of infants and about 3% of adults. Most of the time eczema resolves itself as a child grows older. Eczema is a general term for skin conditions that have rashes. There are many types of eczema: atopic dermatitis, contact eczema, seborrhoeic eczema, mummular eczema, neurodermatitis, etc. The most common form of eczema is atopic dermatitis. Atopic means it is caused by an allergic reaction. The term atopic describes an inherited tendency to have asthma, hay fever, and dermatitis. Eczema is commonly found in family with a history of other allergies or asthma. Eczema often starts in patients with a family history of asthma or allergies. There can be patches of itchy, dry, and thickened skin (crusts). There can be fluid-filled blisters that can ooze. The location is usually on the hands, neck, face, and legs, but can be anywhere. In children, the inner creases of the knees and elbows are often involved. The trigger for the eczema can be contact with rough materials, feeling hot or too cold, exposure to house cleaning products, diet, animal dander, upper respiratory tract infections, or stress. The diagnosis is made via medical history and inspecting the skin. Many patients with eczema can also have allergies. A skin allergy test can be done to determine possible allergens. The skin can develop a yellowish to light brown crust or pus-filled blisters over existing patches of eczema. This may indicate a bacterial infection that should be treated with an antibiotic. Treatments can consist of topical creams (hydrocortisone), corticosteroids ointments, antihistamines, and photo-therapy. If a yellowish crust or pus-filled blisters develop over the eczema patches, it can indicate an infection and antibiotics can be prescribed. The drug fluticasone (Flovent) is prescribed for the treatment of asthma. medlineplus.gov",
      "exp_hant": "在美國，濕疹約影響10-20%的嬰幼兒及約3%的成人。多數情況下，濕疹會隨孩童年齡增長而自行緩解。濕疹是對出現皮疹之皮膚病症的統稱，種類眾多，包括異位性皮膚炎、接觸性濕疹、脂漏性濕疹、錢幣狀濕疹、神經性皮膚炎等。最常見的濕疹型態為異位性皮膚炎。「異位性」（atopic）意指由過敏反應所引起，此詞用以描述具有氣喘、花粉熱及皮膚炎的遺傳傾向。濕疹常見於有其他過敏或氣喘家族病史的族群，且常始於具有氣喘或過敏家族病史的患者。可能出現搔癢、乾燥、增厚（結痂）的皮膚斑塊，也可能出現滲液的水泡。好發部位通常為手部、頸部、臉部及腿部，但也可能出現於身體任何部位；兒童患者則常見於膝窩及肘窩內側。誘發濕疹的因素可能包括接觸粗糙材質、過熱或過冷、接觸居家清潔用品、飲食、動物皮屑、上呼吸道感染或壓力。診斷主要依靠病史詢問與皮膚檢視。許多濕疹患者也同時患有過敏，可透過皮膚過敏測試找出可能的過敏原。若濕疹斑塊上出現黃褐色結痂或化膿水泡，可能顯示細菌感染，須以抗生素治療。治療方式包括外用藥膏（氫化可體松）、皮質類固醇軟膏、抗組織胺及光照療法。若濕疹斑塊上出現黃色結痂或化膿水泡，可能表示已併發感染，需開立抗生素治療。fluticasone（Flovent）是用於治療氣喘的藥物。medlineplus.gov"
    },
    {
      "number": 298,
      "question_en": "What is drug dependence?",
      "question_hant": "何謂藥物依賴（drug dependence）？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "increased urge to use more of the drug",
          "hant": "使用更多藥物的渴望增加",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "withdrawal syndrome after stopping a drug",
          "hant": "停藥後出現戒斷症候群",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "uncontrollable compulsion to use a drug",
          "hant": "無法控制的用藥衝動",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "diminished response to a drug",
          "hant": "對藥物反應減弱",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Tolerance and dependence refer to the physical consequences of drug use. Addiction refers to a compulsive need to use the drug even when it causes harm. TOLERANCE: Tolerance is a diminished response to a drug as a result of repeated use. Tolerance can develop to both illicit drugs and prescription drugs. Tolerance is not necessarily a sign of addiction. Chronic pain patients develop tolerance to prescription pain medications without developing an addiction to them. A person can also develop tolerance to meth, for example, when more of it is needed to produce the same result. DEPENDENCE: The words dependence and addiction are often used as meaning the same thing. Dependence is often a part of addiction. Dependence is when the body has adapted to the presence of a drug, whether the drug is addictive or not. When the drug is stopped there are withdrawal symptoms. Not all drugs that cause dependence are addictive. Prednisone, a non-addictive drug, reduces cortisol production leaving the body without a normal level. When long-term use of prednisone is abruptly stopped it results in steroid withdrawal symptoms (nausea, blood sugar level change, joint pain, menstrual changes, depression, mood changes) until the cortisol balance is established again. On the other hand, meth has both dependent and addictive aspects. ADDICTION: According to NIDA (National Institute on Drug Abuse) addiction is a \"chronic, relapsing brain disease that is characterized by compulsive drug seeking and use, despite harmful consequences\". Addiction is an overwhelming need to use a drug with an urge that can unexpectedly return after a period of improvement. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "耐受性（tolerance）與依賴性（dependence）指的是藥物使用所造成的生理後果，成癮（addiction）則是指即使造成傷害仍出現強迫性用藥需求。耐受性：耐受性是指因重複使用藥物而使藥效反應減弱的現象。無論是非法藥物或處方藥物皆可能產生耐受性，耐受性本身並非成癮的徵象。慢性疼痛患者對處方止痛藥產生耐受性，並不代表已對其成癮。舉例而言，使用甲基安非他命者也可能產生耐受性，需要更大劑量才能達到相同效果。依賴性：依賴與成癮兩詞常被交替使用，依賴通常是成癮的一部分。依賴是指身體已適應某藥物的存在，無論該藥物是否具成癮性；一旦停藥，即會出現戒斷症狀。並非所有會造成依賴的藥物都具成癮性。例如，普賴松（prednisone）是一種非成癮性藥物，會抑制皮質醇的分泌，使體內皮質醇低於正常水準；若長期使用後突然停藥，會出現類固醇戒斷症狀（噁心、血糖變化、關節痛、月經改變、憂鬱、情緒變化），直到皮質醇平衡重新建立為止。相對地，甲基安非他命則兼具依賴性與成癮性。成癮：根據美國國家藥物濫用研究所（NIDA）的定義，成癮是一種「以強迫性尋藥與用藥行為為特徵的慢性、易復發之腦部疾病，即使造成有害後果仍持續發生」。成癮是一種對藥物難以抗拒的強烈需求，即使症狀曾一度改善，此衝動仍可能在意外情況下再度出現。tcmtests.com，2019年2月"
    },
    {
      "number": 299,
      "question_en": "You are taking blood pressure readings. Why should you inflate the blood pressure cuff while simultaneously feeling the radial artery with one hand and inflating the cuff with the other hand until the radial artery pulse is obliterated?",
      "question_hant": "您在測量血壓時，為何應一手觸診橈動脈脈搏、同時以另一手為血壓計袖帶充氣，直到橈動脈脈搏消失為止？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "to avoid using a stethoscope to determine blood pressure",
          "hant": "避免使用聽診器測量血壓",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "to avoid repeated painful cuff inflations",
          "hant": "避免反覆充氣造成疼痛",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "to determine the diastolic pressure",
          "hant": "用以判定舒張壓",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "to assess blood pressure properly",
          "hant": "用以正確評估血壓",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In order to prevent repeated cuff inflations that may be painful to the patient, the practitioner should feel the patient's radial pulse with his/her one hand while inflating the blood pressure cuff with his/her other hand until he/she can no longer feel the patient's pulse. This reading is approximately the systolic blood pressure. After about 30 seconds, inflate the cuff 30 mm Hg higher than the systolic pressure, then gradually deflate the cuff about 2-3 mm HG per second listening for the first two consecutive beats to determine the systolic pressure. Slowly allow the cuff to deflate until the beats become muted. At the point the beats become silent, you have the best reading of the diastolic pressure, however, continue to deflate the cuff to be sure of the diastolic pressure reading for another 20 mm Hg before dropping to zero. Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 26-27",
      "exp_hant": "為避免反覆為袖帶充氣造成患者疼痛，施術者應一手觸診患者橈動脈脈搏，同時以另一手為血壓計袖帶充氣，直到再也無法觸及脈搏為止，此讀數即約為收縮壓。約30秒後，將袖帶充氣至高於此收縮壓30 mmHg，再以每秒2-3 mmHg的速度緩慢放氣，聆聽連續兩次心跳聲以確定收縮壓。持續緩慢放氣，直到心跳聲變得低沉；當心跳聲完全消失時，即可獲得最準確的舒張壓讀數；然而仍應繼續放氣約20 mmHg，以確認舒張壓讀數無誤，再將袖帶完全放氣至零。《東方醫學執業者西醫理學檢查技能》，2009年，Robinson、Wolfe著，第26-27頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 300,
      "question_en": "The Urine Sodium test is useful in evaluating patients with",
      "question_hant": "尿液鈉檢測有助於評估下列哪些患者？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
