        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate answer. For urinary tract infections the Urine Culture and Sensitivity (Urine C&amp;S) is ordered. The urine sodium test is used to detect abnormal levels of sodium in the urine. Hyponatremia is the term for low sodium levels while hypernatremia is the term for high sodium levels. Urine sodium levels are usually tested in patients who have abnormal blood sodium levels and helps to maintain the acid-base balance (pH). Sodium, both an electrolyte and mineral, helps to maintain normal water volume in the body. Sodium also assists in the functioning of nerves and muscles. About 85% of the sodium is in the blood and lymph. The hormone that controls body sodium levels is aldosterone which is produced by the adrenals. Aldosterone instructs the kidneys how much sodium to retain and when to excrete it in the urine. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 913; 4th Edition page 989",
      "exp_hant": "此為最準確的答案。泌尿道感染應開立尿液培養及藥物敏感性試驗（Urine C&S）。尿液鈉檢測用於偵測尿液中鈉濃度的異常。低血鈉稱為hyponatremia，高血鈉稱為hypernatremia。尿液鈉檢測通常用於血鈉異常的患者，有助於維持酸鹼平衡（pH值）。鈉同時是電解質與礦物質，有助於維持體內正常的水分容積，並協助神經與肌肉功能的運作。體內約85%的鈉存在於血液與淋巴液中。控制體內鈉濃度的荷爾蒙為醛固酮（aldosterone），由腎上腺分泌，指示腎臟應保留多少鈉，以及何時將其排出於尿液中。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第913頁；第4版，第989頁"
    },
