      "exp_en": "Narcotics such as heroin, hydrocodone, opium, morphine, and fentanyl constrict the pupils. At high doses, one of the symptoms of overdose is pinpoint pupils that do not respond to changes in light. Hallucinogens such as mescaline, LSD, and others cause the pupils to dilate. The user experiences hallucinations, which may be visual. Stimulants such as cocaine, adderal, and amphetamines stimulate the brain and releases endorphins and adrenaline and the body will react by dilating the pupils. Depressants such as benzodiazepines, non-benzodiazepine sleep medication, and barbiturates dilate the pupils. Common signs of intoxication indicated by the eyes include changes in pupil size (constricted or dilated), nystagmus (rapid involuntary eye movements), and bloodshot eyes. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "麻醉性鎮痛藥，如海洛因、氫可酮、鴉片、嗎啡及吩太尼，會使瞳孔縮小；高劑量使用時，過量症狀之一即為對光線變化無反應的針尖狀瞳孔。迷幻藥，如麥司卡林、LSD等，會使瞳孔放大，使用者會出現幻覺，可能為視幻覺。興奮劑，如古柯鹼、阿德拉（adderall）及安非他命，會刺激大腦並釋放腦內啡與腎上腺素，身體因而反應性地使瞳孔放大。抑制劑，如苯二氮平類、非苯二氮平類安眠藥及巴比妥類藥物，則會使瞳孔放大。眼睛所呈現的常見中毒徵象包括瞳孔大小改變（縮小或放大）、眼球震顫（快速不自主眼球運動）及眼睛充血。tcmtests.com，2019年2月"
