      ],
      "exp_en": "The most common risk factor for prostate cancer is age. The older a man is, the greater the risk of prostate cancer. Some men are at increased risk for prostate cancer. African-American (AA) men are more likely to get prostate cancer than other men. AA men more than twice as likely to die from prostate cancer than white men. AA men tend to have a more severe type of prostate cancer than other men. Family History: men who have a father, son, or brother who has had prostate cancer are at increased risk for prostate cancer. Men with three or more first-degree relatives (father, son, or brother), or two close relatives on the same side of the family who have had prostate cancer may have a type of prostate cancer caused by genetic changes that are inherited. Men who are not African-American and do not have a family history of prostate cancer are at average risk. The two common screening tests are Two tests that are the Prostate Specific Antigen (PSA) Test and Digital Rectal Examination (DRE). The PSA test measures levels of PSA in the blood. PSA can be higher in men who have prostate cancer. As a rule, the higher the PSA level in the blood, the more likely there is a problem with the prostate. However, many factors (age and race) can affect PSA levels. Also some prostate glands make more PSA than others. If the PSA test is abnormal, a biopsy is advised. Digital rectal examination (DRE) is where the physician inserts a gloved, lubricated finger into the rectum to detect any abnormality. However, in 2018, the U.S. Preventive Services Task Force has not recommended DRE as a screening test because of lack evidence on the benefits. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 737-739, 743; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 558; www.cdc.gov",
      "exp_hant": "攝護腺癌最常見的風險因子是年齡，男性年齡越大，罹患攝護腺癌的風險越高。部分男性罹患攝護腺癌的風險較高：非裔美籍男性罹患攝護腺癌的機率高於其他族群，且因攝護腺癌死亡的機率是白人男性的兩倍以上，其攝護腺癌類型也往往較為嚴重。家族病史：父親、兒子或兄弟曾罹患攝護腺癌者，其罹患攝護腺癌的風險較高。若有三位以上一等親（父親、兒子或兄弟），或家族同一側有兩位近親曾罹患攝護腺癌，則可能罹患由遺傳基因變異所引起的攝護腺癌類型。非非裔美籍且無攝護腺癌家族病史的男性則屬於一般風險族群。常見的兩項篩檢方式為攝護腺特異抗原（PSA）檢測與肛門指診（DRE）。PSA檢測測量血液中PSA的濃度，罹患攝護腺癌的男性PSA濃度可能較高，一般而言血液中PSA濃度越高，攝護腺出現問題的可能性也越高；然而許多因素（年齡與種族）皆可能影響PSA濃度，且部分攝護腺本身分泌的PSA就較多。若PSA檢測結果異常，則建議進行切片檢查。肛門指診是由醫師以戴手套並潤滑的手指伸入直腸，以偵測是否有任何異常。然而，美國預防服務工作小組（U.S. Preventive Services Task Force）於2018年已不再建議將肛門指診作為篩檢工具，原因是缺乏支持其效益的證據。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第737-739、743頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第558頁；www.cdc.gov"
    },
