      ],
      "exp_en": "About 75% of cholesterol in the body is bound to LDL (low-density lipoprotein) while the other is bound to HDL (high-density lipoprotein). Cholesterol cannot dissolve in the blood. It is transported to and from the cells by carrier proteins (lipoproteins). LDL, HDL, triglycerides and Lp(a) cholesterol, compose total cholesterol count. Lp(a) cholesterol is a genetic variation of LDL cholesterol. A high level of Lp(a) is a significant risk factor for the premature development of fatty deposits in the arteries. When there is too much LDL cholesterol in the blood circulation, it can slowly accumulate in the inner arterial walls that feed the brain and the heart. Along with other substances, an arterial plaque can form that narrows the arteries, making them less flexible which is condition known as atherosclerosis. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition,Pagana, page 451-454",
      "exp_hant": "體內約75%的膽固醇與低密度脂蛋白（LDL）結合，其餘則與高密度脂蛋白（HDL）結合。膽固醇無法溶於血液，須靠攜帶蛋白（脂蛋白）在細胞間運送。LDL、HDL、三酸甘油脂及Lp(a)膽固醇共同構成總膽固醇數值。Lp(a)膽固醇是LDL膽固醇的一種基因變異型，Lp(a)濃度過高是動脈脂肪沉積早發的重要風險因子。當血液循環中LDL膽固醇過多時，會緩慢堆積於供應大腦與心臟的動脈內壁，並與其他物質共同形成動脈斑塊，使動脈狹窄、失去彈性，此病症即稱為動脈粥狀硬化。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第451-454頁"
