      "exp_en": "Optic neuritis visual loss usually affects only one eye (unilateral). Optic neuritis causes one sided visual loss, pain, loss of color vision, and flashing lights. Scotoma is an area of partial change in the field of vision consisting of a partially diminished or entirely degenerated visual acuity that is surrounded by a field of relatively clear vision. Though it is unknown what causes optic neuritis, it is associated with Multiple Sclerosis, Lupus, infections (Lyme disease, cat-scratch fever and syphilis, or viruses, such as measles, mumps and herpes). Some antibiotics can also cause optic neuritis. along with ischemic optic neuropathy and compressive lesions. This optic atrophy and optic disc swelling is visual on funduscopic examination. Textbook of Clinical Neurology, Christopher G. Goetz, MD and Eric J. Pappert, 1999, W.B., Saunders Company, page 103",
      "exp_hant": "視神經炎所造成的視力喪失通常只影響單眼（單側）。視神經炎會引起單側視力喪失、疼痛、色覺喪失及閃光感。暗點是指視野中一部分視覺敏銳度部分或完全喪失，且周圍仍保有相對清晰視野的區域。雖然視神經炎的確切病因不明，但與多發性硬化症、紅斑性狼瘡、感染（萊姆病、貓抓病及梅毒），或麻疹、腮腺炎、疱疹等病毒感染有關，某些抗生素也可能引起視神經炎，此外也與缺血性視神經病變及壓迫性病灶有關。眼底鏡檢查可見視神經萎縮與視神經盤水腫。《臨床神經學教科書》，Christopher G. Goetz醫師與Eric J. Pappert著，1999年，W.B. Saunders公司出版，第103頁"
