      "exp_en": "VII = facial. The facial nerve, cranial nerve VII, controls the muscles of facial expression and relays taste sensations from the anterior two-thirds of the tongue and mouth. Symptoms of injury include complete or partial paralysis of the face (bell's palsy) and/or an unusual or impaired sense of taste can occur following. There are close functional and anatomical relationships between cranial nerves V and VII in both their sensory and motor divisions. Sensation on the face is innervated by the trigeminal nerves (V) as are the muscles of mastication, but the muscles of facial expression are innervated mainly by the facial nerve (VII) as is the sensation of taste. It has both sensory and motor branches. tcmtests.com, September 2019",
      "exp_hant": "VII＝顏面神經。顏面神經（第七對腦神經）控制臉部表情肌肉，並負責傳遞舌前三分之二及口腔的味覺訊號。此神經受損的症狀包括臉部完全或部分麻痺（貝爾氏麻痺）及味覺異常或減退。第五對與第七對腦神經在感覺與運動分支上皆有密切的功能與解剖關聯：臉部的感覺由三叉神經（第五對）負責，咀嚼肌也由其支配；而臉部表情肌肉則主要由顏面神經（第七對）支配，味覺亦然。顏面神經兼具感覺與運動分支。tcmtests.com，2019年9月"
