      "exp_en": "A patient can inspect their PHI can takes notes, use a smart phone or other device to take pictures of their PHI. There are remedies for patients who are denied copies of their medical records to get access to them. Suing is not one of them. The patient may file a formal complaint on the HHS web site. If the violation is serious enough the medical care provider may be fined $25,000 or up to 10 years in jail and a $250,000 fine. Payment history problems can get reported to the Medical Information Bureau which services life insurance companies, among others, and ties together health and credit. Many experts believe that eventually this information will be put together with credit scores to draw conclusions about the FICO scores of individual patients. If the violation of protecting PHI is due to reasonable cause and not willful neglect, the penalty can range from $1,000 to $50,000 per violation. A provider cannot deny you a copy of medical records because the patient has not paid for the services received. However, a provider may charge for the reasonable costs for copying and mailing the records. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "患者可以檢視其個人健康資訊（PHI），並可做筆記，或使用智慧型手機或其他裝置拍攝其PHI。若患者被拒絕取得病歷副本，仍有救濟途徑可取得，但提起訴訟並非其中之一；患者可於衛生及公共服務部（HHS）網站提出正式申訴。若違規情節嚴重，醫療提供者可能被處以25,000美元罰款、最高10年徒刑，並處250,000美元罰款。付款紀錄問題可能會被通報至醫療資訊局（Medical Information Bureau），該機構服務於人壽保險公司等單位，並將健康與信用資訊相互連結；許多專家認為，未來這類資訊終將與信用評分結合，用以推斷個別患者的FICO信用分數。若保護PHI的違規行為是出於合理原因而非故意疏忽，罰款範圍則為每次違規1,000至50,000美元。醫療提供者不得因患者尚未支付醫療費用而拒絕提供病歷副本，但可就複印及郵寄病歷收取合理費用。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
