          "hant": "97813",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "97810",
          "hant": "97810",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "97810 and 97811",
          "hant": "97810與97811",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "97813 and 97814",
          "hant": "97813與97814",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Insurance codes 97810 and 97811 are both used for acupuncture treatment, but they cover different parts of the treatment. Code 97810 is used for the initial 15 minutes of acupuncture treatment. This includes the following procedures of consultation, diagnosis, point selection and needle insertion. Code 97811 is used for each additional 15 minutes of acupuncture treatment. This includesfollowing procedures monitoring, stimulation (electrical stimulation or other techniques to increase the effectiveness of the acupuncture treatment) and needle removal. In summary, code 97810 covers the initial consultation, diagnosis, and point selection, while code 97811 covers the monitoring, stimulation, and needle removal. tcmtests.com, July 2018",
      "exp_hant": "保險代碼97810與97811皆用於針灸治療，但涵蓋治療的不同部分。代碼97810用於針灸治療最初的15分鐘，包含問診、診斷、選穴及進針等程序；代碼97811則用於針灸治療每增加15分鐘，包含監測、刺激（電針或其他增進針灸療效的技術）及出針等程序。簡言之，97810涵蓋初步問診、診斷及選穴，97811則涵蓋監測、刺激及出針。tcmtests.com，2018年7月"
    },
    {
      "number": 314,
      "question_en": "In comparing atopic dermatitis with contact dermatitis, which of the following is an accurate comparison?",
      "question_hant": "比較異位性皮膚炎與接觸性皮膚炎，下列敘述何者正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "contact dermatitis occurs where joints fold while atopic dermatitis can occur anywhere on the body",
          "hant": "接觸性皮膚炎發生於關節皺褶處，而異位性皮膚炎則可能發生於身體任何部位",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "contact dermatitis is a form of eczema while atopic dermatitis is a form of psoriasis",
          "hant": "接觸性皮膚炎屬於濕疹的一種，而異位性皮膚炎屬於乾癬的一種",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "contact dermatitis is often genetic while atopic dermatitis is mostly an immune system response",
          "hant": "接觸性皮膚炎多為遺傳所致，而異位性皮膚炎則多為免疫系統反應",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "contact dermatitis is diagnosed with skin patch testing while atopic dermatitis is diagnosed with skin prick testing",
          "hant": "接觸性皮膚炎以皮膚貼膚試驗診斷，而異位性皮膚炎則以皮膚點刺試驗診斷",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Both atopic dermatitis and contact dermatitis are forms of eczema. Often the difference between the two is obvious. But some patients can have both types which makes assessment difficult. The term eczema refers to the skin rash and is not in itself a specific diagnosis. Eczema is a catch all term used to describe itchy, swollen, rough, skin. Eczema can have three phases: 1) acute eczema can have itchy blisters or vesicles on inflamed-red skin. 2) sub-acute eczema is itchy, dry, flaky, crusting, or oozing of the skin. 3) chronic eczema is characterized by a leathery thickening of the skin that occurs as a result of chronic scratching. This is called lichenification. Atopic dermatitis is often an inherited allergic condition which can occur with asthma, hay fever, and allergies. Patients with atopic dermatitis can have a genetic mutation in a skin protein (filaggrin) that leads to a breakdown of the epidermal cells which allows allergens like pet dander and dust mites to penetrate the skin. Contact dermatitis occurs as the result of the skin coming in contact with certain chemicals (poison oak, nickel, cosmetic agents, hair dye, etc). The immune system (T-lymphocytes) in contact dermatitis recognizes the chemical as a foreign agent and reacts to it via the eczema reaction of contact dermatitis. Most patients with atopic dermatitis are five years old or younger. Contact dermatitis is not as common in young kids. Atopic dermatitis most often occurs in flexural skin locations (folds of the elbows, behind the knees, front of the neck folds of the wrists, ankles) while the location of the contact dermatitis depends where the contact with the chemical occurs. There are two types of allergy tests: skin prick test and the RAST (radioallergosorbent test). Patch testing is used in contact dermatitis to test reaction to various chemicals. This involves another part of the immune system.",
      "exp_hant": "異位性皮膚炎與接觸性皮膚炎皆屬於濕疹的一種，兩者的差異通常十分明顯，但部分患者可能同時患有這兩種類型，使得判斷變得困難。「濕疹」一詞是指皮膚出現皮疹的病症，本身並非具體的診斷名稱，而是用來泛指搔癢、腫脹、粗糙的皮膚狀況的通稱。濕疹可分為三個階段：1）急性濕疹在發炎泛紅的皮膚上出現搔癢的水泡或囊泡；2）亞急性濕疹則為搔癢、乾燥、脫屑、結痂或滲液的皮膚；3）慢性濕疹則因長期搔抓而形成皮革樣增厚，此現象稱為苔癬化。異位性皮膚炎通常是一種遺傳性過敏疾病，可能與氣喘、花粉熱及過敏並存；異位性皮膚炎患者可能帶有皮膚蛋白（絲聚蛋白，filaggrin）的基因突變，導致表皮細胞結構破壞，使寵物皮屑與塵蟎等過敏原得以穿透皮膚。接觸性皮膚炎則是皮膚接觸特定化學物質（如毒漆藤、鎳、化妝品成分、染髮劑等）所產生的反應，接觸性皮膚炎中的免疫系統（T淋巴球）將該化學物質辨識為外來物並產生反應，形成接觸性皮膚炎的濕疹反應。多數異位性皮膚炎患者為五歲以下的幼童，接觸性皮膚炎在幼童中則較不常見。異位性皮膚炎最常發生於屈側皮膚部位（肘窩、膝窩後側、頸部前方皮膚皺褶、腕部、踝部），而接觸性皮膚炎的部位則取決於接觸化學物質的位置。過敏測試共有兩種：皮膚點刺試驗與放射性過敏原吸附試驗（RAST）。貼膚試驗則用於接觸性皮膚炎，測試對各種化學物質的反應，涉及免疫系統的另一部分機制。"
    },
    {
      "number": 315,
      "question_en": "A month ago, a 40 year-old African American male has had history of severe and extreme abdominal pain which required hospitalization one year ago. His pain at that time was described as being in the upper left side of the abdomen as severe and improving by leaning forward. The pain was associated with nausea and vomiting. He does not have a known history of gallstones. He has a history of drinking two six packs of beer every weekend. He wants to receive acupuncture treatment to prevent a repeat of his previous symptoms. The physical exam is now normal. Which course of action would you take now?",
      "question_hant": "一名40歲非裔美籍男性，一個月前有嚴重且劇烈腹痛病史，曾於一年前因此住院。當時的疼痛描述為位於腹部左上方，程度劇烈，前傾時可緩解，並伴隨噁心與嘔吐。他並無膽結石病史。他有每週末飲用兩手（十二罐）啤酒的病史。他希望接受針灸治療以預防先前症狀再次發生。目前理學檢查結果正常。此時您應採取下列何種處置？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "have family member drive patient to ED",
          "hant": "請家屬送患者至急診室",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "refer to primary care physician to sign off to acupuncture treatment",
          "hant": "轉介至主治醫師以取得針灸治療同意",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency assistance",
          "hant": "撥打911尋求緊急協助",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "no referral necessary as patient is now stable",
          "hant": "患者目前狀況穩定，無需轉介",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is severe abdominal pain (better leaning forward) with nausea and vomiting. Acute pancreatitis, now asymptomatic, is assumed present until proven otherwise. 40% of acute pancreatitis cases are due to cholelithiasis, 40% are due to alcohol abuse. The patient should be advised of the link between the abdominal pain and alcohol. As the patient is between attacks a primary care physician referral should be given for future therapy should it occur again. Patients with an acute pancreatic attack should be directed to the nearest emergency department. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 90-91",
      "exp_hant": "此警訊徵象為劇烈腹痛（前傾可緩解）合併噁心與嘔吐。急性胰臟炎雖目前無症狀，仍應假定其存在，直至排除為止。40%的急性胰臟炎病例源於膽結石，另有40%源於酒精濫用。應告知患者其腹痛與飲酒之間的關聯。由於患者目前處於發作間期，應轉介至主治醫師，以便未來若再度發作時能及時處理。急性胰臟炎發作的患者應立即轉送至最近的急診室。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉介指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第90-91頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 316,
      "question_en": "Which test best identifies supraspinatus tendon impingement?",
      "question_hant": "哪一項測試最能辨識棘上肌肌腱夾擠？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
