      "exp_en": "Cushing's syndrome is a condition caused by excess corticosteroids in an individual's body. These steroids can be produced by the body itself or can result from high doses of medical steroids. Cushing's syndrome is characterized by a large, round face and a thick torso with fatty tissue deposit between the shoulder blades (buffalo hump) with comparatively thin arms and legs. Muscle weakness, depression, thin skin that bruises easily and heals slowly, and purple streaks on the abdomen are also common signs and symptoms of this condition. tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "庫欣氏症候群是一種因體內皮質類固醇過多所造成的病症，這些類固醇可能由身體自行產生，也可能來自高劑量的藥用類固醇。庫欣氏症候群的特徵為臉部圓大、軀幹粗厚，並在肩胛骨之間有脂肪堆積（水牛肩），而四肢則相對纖細。其他常見徵象與症狀還包括肌肉無力、憂鬱、皮膚薄且容易瘀傷、癒合緩慢，以及腹部出現紫紋。tcmtests.com，2020年7月"
    },
    {
      "number": 321,
      "question_en": "Antihyperlipidemic is a class of drugs that reduces cholesterol by inhibiting",
      "question_hant": "降血脂藥物（Antihyperlipidemic）是透過抑制下列何者以降低膽固醇的一類藥物？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "blood lipids",
          "hant": "血脂",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "an enzyme",
          "hant": "一種酵素",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "liver cell receptors",
          "hant": "肝細胞受體",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "DNA and RNA cholesterol synthesis",
          "hant": "DNA與RNA膽固醇合成",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Antihyperlipidemics are statin drugs. Antihyperlipidemics block the liver enzyme HMG-CoA (3-hydroxy-3-methyl-glutaryl-coenzyme A) by controlling the metabolic pathway that produces cholesterol in the body. HMG-CoA reductase slows down the liver enzyme necessary for the cholesterol production process. Cholesterol is necessary for normal cell functions but at high levels can produce plaque build up in the arteries that can then block blood flow. As such, statins can lower the risk for angina, heart attack, and stroke. Statins are prescribed for patients with potential heart disease, stroke and atherosclerosis due to arterial wall plaque, diabetes (higher risk for developing cholesterol-related diseases), and patients with elevated LDL cholesterol (190 milligrams or higher). Both generic statin drugs share a common suffix (-statin) and brand name statins also share a common suffix (-or/-ol). The most popular lipid regulators are Lipitor (atorvastatin), Pravachol (pravastatin), Crestor (rosuvastatin), Zocor (simvastatin) and Lescol (fluvastatin). Lipitor and Crestor are the most potent while Lescol is the least potent. Treatment with statins usually continue even after cholesterol levels are controlled. The most common side effects of statins are headache, insomnia, muscle pain/weakness, drowsiness/dizziness, nausea/vomiting, and abdominal cramps. Though rare, the two most serious side effects are liver failure and skeletal muscle damage. Research indicates that statins also can block the endogenous production of CoQ10. Hence, the frequent recommendation of CoQ10 supplementation with statins. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "降血脂藥物即為他汀類藥物（statins）。降血脂藥物透過阻斷肝臟酵素HMG-CoA（3-羥基-3-甲基戊二醯輔酶A）的作用，控制體內膽固醇生成的代謝途徑；HMG-CoA還原酶會減緩肝臟中膽固醇生成過程所需的酵素作用。膽固醇是細胞正常功能所必需的物質，但濃度過高時會在動脈中形成斑塊堆積，阻礙血流；因此，他汀類藥物可降低心絞痛、心臟病發作及中風的風險。他汀類藥物適用於有潛在心臟病風險、中風及因動脈壁斑塊而形成之動脈粥狀硬化的患者、糖尿病患者（罹患膽固醇相關疾病的風險較高），以及LDL膽固醇偏高（190毫克以上）的患者。學名他汀類藥物皆共用字尾（-statin），品牌名稱他汀類藥物則共用字尾（-or/-ol）。最常見的降血脂藥物包括立普妥（Lipitor，atorvastatin）、Pravachol（pravastatin）、冠脂妥（Crestor，rosuvastatin）、素果（Zocor，simvastatin）及來適可（Lescol，fluvastatin）。其中立普妥與冠脂妥效力最強，來適可效力最弱。即使膽固醇濃度已獲控制，他汀類藥物的治療通常仍會持續進行。他汀類藥物最常見的副作用包括頭痛、失眠、肌肉疼痛／無力、嗜睡／頭暈、噁心／嘔吐及腹部絞痛；雖然罕見，但兩項最嚴重的副作用為肝衰竭與骨骼肌損傷。研究顯示，他汀類藥物也可能阻斷體內內源性輔酶Q10的生成，因此常建議在服用他汀類藥物時同時補充輔酶Q10。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
