      ],
      "exp_en": "Peripheral nervous system (PNS) that part of the nervous system which is outside the brain and spinal cord which is the central nervous system (CNS). The nerves in the PNS connect the (CNS) to sensory organs, skin, body organs, muscles, blood vessels, and glands. The superficial peroneal nerve (also called superior fibular nerve), innervates the peroneus longus and peroneus brevis muscles and the skin over the antero-lateral aspect of the leg along with the greater part of the top of the foot. Both peroneus muscles are associated with L5 and S1. These two muscles are involved in plantar flexion and foot eversion. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 884-885; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 694-695",
      "exp_hant": "周邊神經系統（PNS）是指位於腦與脊髓（即中樞神經系統，CNS）以外的神經系統部分，PNS中的神經負責連結中樞神經系統與感覺器官、皮膚、身體器官、肌肉、血管及腺體。淺腓神經（又稱為腓淺神經）支配腓骨長肌與腓骨短肌，以及小腿前外側與足背大部分區域的皮膚。這兩條腓骨肌皆與L5及S1神經根相關，並參與蹠屈與足外翻的動作。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第884-885頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第694-695頁"
