          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "anytime your personal stethoscope is touched, before answering phone, anytime after you touch your face or hair",
          "hant": "觸碰個人聽診器後、接電話前、觸摸臉部或頭髮後",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. It is not a strict protocol to wash hands after anytime a personal stethoscope is touched or before answering the phone. The CNT manual recommends that acupuncturists always wash their hands: 1) just before giving the acupuncture treatment. 2) after any contact with blood or body fluids. 3) at the end of the acupuncture treatment. The acupuncturist needs to wash their hands between patients, before and after needle insertion, and anytime there is contact with body fluids. The CNT manual also says to wash hands before/after answering the phone, using a computer, and after touching one's face or hair. The CDC recommends hand washing for: 1) with visibly dirty hands use soap and water. 2) if hands are not visibly soiled, use soap and water or an alcohol disinfectant. 3) wash hands before contact with patient. 4) wash hands after touching the intact skin of the patient. 5) wash hands after contact with fluids or patient's dressing. 6) wash hands after gloves are removed. 7) wash hands before and after eating. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 172",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整的答案。並非嚴格規定每次觸碰個人聽診器或接電話前都必須洗手。《清潔針法技術手冊》建議針灸師應於下列時機洗手：1）進行針灸治療之前；2）接觸血液或體液後；3）針灸治療結束後。針灸師需在為每位患者治療之間、進針前後，以及任何接觸體液的情況下洗手。《清潔針法技術手冊》也建議在接聽電話前後、使用電腦後，以及觸摸臉部或頭髮後洗手。CDC建議在下列情況下洗手：1）手部明顯髒污時使用肥皂與清水；2）手部無明顯髒污時可使用肥皂與清水，或使用酒精性消毒液；3）接觸患者前洗手；4）觸摸患者完整皮膚後洗手；5）接觸體液或患者敷料後洗手；6）脫除手套後洗手；7）用餐前後洗手。《清潔針法技術》第7版，第172頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 325,
      "question_en": "A 59 year-old male patient has had chest pain since the morning. The sharp pain is on the center of the chest and worsens on inhale. Body temperature is 99.8 F. Pulse rate is 95 beats per minute. During heart auscultation, a grating sound can be heard. Which aspect of the clinical picture most indicate a red flag referral?",
      "question_hant": "一名59歲男性患者從當天早上開始出現胸痛，疼痛為銳痛，位於胸部中央，吸氣時加劇。體溫為99.8°F，脈搏每分鐘95次。聽診心臟時可聽到摩擦音。下列臨床表現中，何者最能提示需要進行警訊轉介？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "chest pain, heart sound, body temp",
          "hant": "胸痛、心音、體溫",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "body temp, pulse rate, patient age",
          "hant": "體溫、脈搏、患者年齡",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "chest pain worse inhaling",
          "hant": "吸氣時胸痛加劇",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "heart sound, pulse rate",
          "hant": "心音、脈搏",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the best overall answer. Pericarditis, is inflammation of any of the three layers of the pericardium. The inner visceral layer (visceral pericardium) envelopes the entire heart. The middle fluid layer prevents friction between the visceral layer and the parietal layer. The fibrous parietal layer is the outer layer. Pericarditis can be caused by an infection, tumor, post heart surgery or heart attack. The main symptoms are chest pain, fever, and increase heart rate. The chest pain is sharp, on the center of the chest, worse on inhaling, and worse on leaning forward or lying down. The fever is low-grade (slightly above normal of 98.6 F). The heart rate is less than 100 bpm. During heart auscultation acute pericarditis can be associated with the sound called friction rub. This sounds like a rub, scratching or grating sound similar to leather rubbing against leather. If pericarditis is suspected the patient should be referred for further assessment. The patient can have uncomplicated pericarditis with sharp central chest pain, elevated heart rate, low grade fever, pain while inhaling, and a friction rub heart sound. The patient can also present these signs and symptoms associated with other disorders such as a) heart failure with breathlessness and edema, 2) arrhythmia, 3) heart attack or unstable angina. Pericarditis associated with the preceding disorders is a more complicated situation and requires a more urgent referral. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 36; wwww.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "此為最佳的整體答案。心包炎是心包膜三層中任一層的發炎，內層（臟層心包）包覆整個心臟，中間的液層可防止臟層與壁層之間相互摩擦，外層則為纖維性的壁層心包。心包炎可能由感染、腫瘤、心臟手術後或心臟病發作所引起，主要症狀為胸痛、發燒及心跳加快。此胸痛為銳痛，位於胸部中央，吸氣時加劇，前傾或平躺時亦會加劇。發燒為低度發燒（略高於正常體溫98.6°F），心跳速率則低於每分鐘100次。急性心包炎在心臟聽診時可聽到稱為摩擦音的聲音，類似皮革相互摩擦的摩擦聲、刮擦聲或吱嘎聲。若懷疑心包炎，應轉介患者接受進一步評估。單純性心包炎患者可能出現胸部中央銳痛、心跳加快、低度發燒、吸氣時疼痛及心臟摩擦音；然而，患者也可能同時出現與其他病症相關的徵象與症狀，例如：1）心臟衰竭合併呼吸急促與水腫；2）心律不整；3）心臟病發作或不穩定型心絞痛。若心包炎併發上述病症，情況則更為複雜，需要更緊急的轉介。《輔助療法師紅旗警訊轉介指南》，Stephenson著，2013年，第36頁；wwww.webmd.com"
    },
