      "exp_en": "The red flag is sharp chest pain and SOB with unilateral or bilateral asymmetric ankle swelling. A pulmonary embolus (PE) is assumed present until proven otherwise. This is an emergency event requiring 911 emergency transport. Patients with PE appear acutely ill with fast breathing, fast pulse, symptoms of poor oxygenation such as cyanosis, pleuritic chest pain, and SOB. It is important to measure the circumference of the ankles to detect significant differences between the two ankles. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 105-106",
      "exp_hant": "此警訊徵象為銳利胸痛與呼吸急促，並伴隨單側或雙側不對稱的踝部腫脹。應假定為肺栓塞（PE），直至排除為止，此為緊急事件，需要撥打911進行緊急後送。肺栓塞患者外觀通常呈急性病容，呼吸急促、脈搏加快，並有缺氧徵象（如發紺）、肋膜性胸痛及呼吸急促等症狀。測量雙側踝部周徑以偵測是否有顯著差異相當重要。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉介指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第105-106頁"
