      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Dystonia is abnormal muscle tone associated with muscular spasm and poor posture. It is typically associated with neurological disorders. Symptoms include involuntary movements and muscle contractions. Symptoms that point to possible diabetes include constant thirst and drinking six big water bottles per day. Symptoms that point to hypothyroidism include weight gain, fatigue, dizziness, headache, and blurred vision. She is most likely using alcohol abuse as self-medication for the depression arising from separating from her husband. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 299, 710",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。肌張力不全（dystonia）是一種伴隨肌肉痙攣與姿勢不良的異常肌張力表現，通常與神經系統疾病相關，症狀包括不自主動作與肌肉收縮。可能提示糖尿病的症狀包括持續口渴及每日大量飲水（六大瓶）；可能提示甲狀腺機能低下的症狀則包括體重增加、疲勞、頭暈、頭痛及視力模糊。她很可能是以酒精作為自我治療的方式，用以緩解因與丈夫分居所引發的憂鬱情緒。《生醫學：針灸與東方醫學執業者教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第299、710頁"
