      "exp_en": "Essential tremor (ET) is a nerve disorder that different parts of the body (head, hands, arms, voice, tongue, chin) have uncontrollable movement or shaking. Essential tremor does not usually affect the lower body. The cause of essential tremor is unknown but it is postulated that it can be due to a disorder in electrical brain activity. About 50% of patients with ET have had a parent with ET. Head tremor is unusual in early Parkinson's disease (PD). ET tends to worsens when the body part moves rather than when it is at rest. In PD tremors tend to decrease or stop when the body part moves. PD is a dopamine related disorder. A deficiency in dopamine (a neurotransmitter) causes a nerve function disorder that causes a loss in the ability to control body movements. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 858; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 901",
      "exp_hant": "本態性震顫（ET）是一種神經性疾病，身體不同部位（頭部、雙手、手臂、聲音、下巴）出現無法控制的動作或顫抖，通常不影響下半身。本態性震顫的成因不明，推測可能與大腦電活動異常有關。約50%的本態性震顫患者其父母之一也曾患有此病。早期帕金森氏症中，頭部震顫較為少見。本態性震顫在該部位活動時會加劇，而非在靜止時；帕金森氏症的震顫則多在該部位活動時減輕或停止。帕金森氏症與多巴胺相關：多巴胺（一種神經傳導物質）不足會導致神經功能失調，使身體動作控制能力喪失。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第858頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第901頁"
