      "exp_en": "This patient has anorexia nervosa. Anorexia nervosa can be a life-threatening eating disorder where the patient is unable to maintain a minimally normal weight associated with a devastating fear of weight gain, compulsive dietary habits to prevent weight gain, and a body image disorder that distorts body weight and shape. Anorexia nervosa could be associated with bulimic and nonbulimic episodes. Current guidelines recommend anorexia as the major diagnosis for any patient with a BMI below 18.5 associated with an eating disorder. Anorexia nervosa could lead to secondary amenorrhea. It is one of the cardinal features of anorexia nervosa and is associated with hypothalamic dysfunction disruption with low levels of FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone) and LH (luteinizing hormone). Primary amenorrhea is the failure of menses to occur by age 16 years, in the presence of normal growth and secondary sexual characteristics. Associated with delayed puberty features. This feature is however not consistent with the history of the patient. Hypothyroidism can manifests as slowing of physical and mental activity. Patients with abnormal menstruation caused by hypothyroidism tend to have an abnormal TSH level. This patient has normal TSH levels. Normal TSH levels are between 0.4-4.0. Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1701",
      "exp_hant": "此患者罹患厭食症。厭食症是一種可能危及生命的飲食障礙，患者無法維持最低限度的正常體重，並伴隨對體重增加的強烈恐懼、為防止體重增加而形成的強迫性飲食習慣，以及扭曲體重與體型認知的身體意象障礙。厭食症可能伴隨暴食或非暴食發作。目前指引建議，凡BMI低於18.5並合併飲食障礙者，應以厭食症作為主要診斷。厭食症可能導致續發性閉經，是厭食症的重要特徵之一，並與下視丘功能障礙有關，出現濾泡刺激素（FSH）與黃體成長激素（LH）濃度低下的情形。原發性閉經是指在生長發育及第二性徵正常的情況下，至16歲仍未來經，通常與青春期延遲有關，但此特徵與該患者的病史並不相符。甲狀腺機能低下可表現為身體與心智活動遲緩，因甲狀腺機能低下而導致月經異常的患者，其TSH濃度通常也會異常，而此患者的TSH濃度正常（正常範圍為0.4-4.0）。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第1701頁"
    },
