          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "75 percent",
          "hant": "75%",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "90% of individuals who die by suicide have a mental disorder at the time of their deaths. There are biological and psychological treatments that can assist the underlying health issues that put people at risk for suicide. Psychotherapies are used to treat the the depression of the suicidal patient. These therapies can include Cognitive Behavior Therapy (CBT), Interpersonal Therapy (IPT), and Behavioral Activation (BH), among many others. If the depression is mild, the physician can begin with psychotherapy by itself and then add medications later if symptoms fail to improve. There are many medications that treat depression such as Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIS). An important consideration is that when antidepressants are started or when dosage is increased, a few patients (especially children, adolescents and young adults) may experience an increase in anxiety or anger which can lead to suicidal thoughts or attempts. Patients with bipolar disorder can begin treatment with a mood stabilizers such as lithium, anticonvulsants, or antipsychotics. Prescribing lithium in patients with bipolar disorder has been shown to reduce suicide risk. Patients with alcohol and drug abuse issues need to have their addiction treated through various means (psychotherapy, drug therapy) but always includes a strong psychosocial component such as AA or drug addiction support groups. Patients who suffer from SAD (seasonal affective disorder) can be prescribed light therapy. If the depression does not respond or if the depression is very severe or if the patient exhibits psychotic symptoms, then electroconvulsive therapy can be used. Electroconvulsive therapy can be given as an out or inpatient, but it requires anesthesia and subjecting the brain to a small dose of electric current. www.afsp.org",
      "exp_hant": "90%因自殺身亡的個案，在死亡當下患有精神疾病。針對造成自殺風險的潛在健康問題，有生物性與心理性的治療方式可提供協助。心理治療用於治療有自殺傾向患者的憂鬱症，這些療法包括認知行為治療（CBT）、人際關係治療（IPT）及行為激發治療（BH）等。若憂鬱程度輕微，醫師可先單獨採用心理治療，若症狀未見改善，再加入藥物治療。有許多藥物可用於治療憂鬱症，例如選擇性血清素回收抑制劑（SSRIs）。須注意的重點是，當開始服用抗憂鬱藥或增加劑量時，部分患者（尤其是兒童、青少年及年輕成人）可能會出現焦慮或憤怒感增加的情形，進而導致自殺意念或企圖。患有雙相情感障礙的患者可先以情緒穩定劑（如鋰鹽、抗癲癇藥或抗精神病藥）開始治療，研究顯示，為雙相情感障礙患者開立鋰鹽可降低自殺風險。有酒精及藥物濫用問題的患者，需透過各種方式（心理治療、藥物治療）治療其成癮問題，且應始終包含強而有力的社會心理支持，例如戒酒無名會（AA）或藥物成癮支持團體。患有季節性情感障礙（SAD）的患者可採用光照療法。若憂鬱症未見改善，或病情非常嚴重，或患者出現精神病症狀，則可採用電痙攣療法，此療法可於門診或住院時進行，但需要麻醉，並使大腦承受微量電流刺激。www.afsp.org"
    },
