      "exp_en": "This test is also called the Adduction Stress Test. Pain or a gap in the lateral joint line indicates that the medial ligaments are lax and there can possibly be a tear in the lateral collateral ligament (LCL). The LCL is a band of tissue on the Lateral side of the knee connecting the femur with the fibula. The LCL prevents the knee from bending outward. In an LCL injury or tear to the lateral collateral ligament there can be pain, stiffness, swelling, tenderness along the outside of the knee, and feeling that the knee may give away, lock, or catch when the knee is under stress. However, most knee injuries involve the MCL (medial collateral ligament). Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 807-809; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 633",
      "exp_hant": "此測試又稱為內收應力測試（Adduction Stress Test）。若外側關節間隙出現疼痛或間隙增大，代表內側韌帶鬆弛，且外側副韌帶（LCL）可能有撕裂情形。LCL是位於膝關節外側、連結股骨與腓骨的一條組織帶，可防止膝關節向外彎曲。若外側副韌帶受傷或撕裂，可能出現疼痛、僵硬、腫脹、膝關節外側壓痛，以及膝關節在受力時有鬆脫、卡住或卡頓的感覺。然而，大多數膝關節損傷涉及的是內側副韌帶（MCL）。《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第13版，第807-809頁；《Bate氏理學檢查指南》第10版，第633頁"
