      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. A cystoscopy is performed to visualize the bladder, kidneys, and ureters. Tumors in the intestine can ulcerate due to repeated trauma from the movement of feces. This bleeding can be so small that it cannot be seen in the stool. The main function of the fecal occult blood test (FOBT) is to screen for early colon cancer. That is because blood in the stool is often the only symptom of early colon cancer. The occult blood study does not diagnose colon cancer. However, if the FOBT is positive for occult blood, follow up procedures are ordered to identify the cause of gastrointestinal bleeding. This is necessary to differentiate colon cancer from an ulcer, for example. An occult blood (OB) is done as part of routine lab work for at risk colon cancer patients, for routine screening of asymptomatic adults over the age of 50, and for evaluating abdominal pain. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 552, 549, 982",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。膀胱鏡檢查用於觀察膀胱、腎臟及輸尿管。腸道中的腫瘤可能因糞便反覆摩擦而潰爛出血，此出血可能極為輕微而無法在糞便中肉眼觀察到。糞便潛血檢測（FOBT）的主要功能為篩檢早期大腸癌，因為糞便帶血往往是早期大腸癌唯一的症狀；然而，潛血檢測本身並無法診斷大腸癌。若糞便潛血檢測呈陽性反應，則須安排後續檢查以找出腸胃道出血的原因，例如區分是大腸癌還是潰瘍所致。糞便潛血檢測可作為大腸癌高風險患者常規檢查的一部分，也用於50歲以上無症狀成人的常規篩檢，以及評估腹痛的病因。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第552、549、982頁"
