      "exp_en": "All cups used for wet cupping or gua sha tools used on non-intact skin require as a first step the cleaning with soap and water for the removal of soil, skin cells, and lubricants. The second step involves either a) autoclaving the cups or gua sha tools or b) the use of a high-level disinfectant such as Sporox, Endospore, Peract, or Acedide. Cups or gua sha tools used over intact skin also first require the cleaning with soap and water and then an intermediate level disinfectant such as Sterilox, Sani-Cloth, or Cavicide. Blood pressure cuffs, stethoscopes, e-stim clips requires first a cleaning with soap and water and then followed with a low or intermediate level disinfectant. There is a caveat here: it is unknown how much microscopic blood and fluid extravasation seeps through the skin irregardless of what type of cupping or over what type of skin. The author of the CNT book considers it prudent to use high-level disinfection on all cups and gua sha tools until it is ascertained the degree to which cups and gua sha allow blood and body fluids to seep through. Equipment that breaks the skin or enters the vascular system should be sterilized (no acupuncture tools/equipment fall into this category). However, single-use sterilized needles are critical. Disposable 7-star hammers, lancets, and press tacks cannot be reused. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 194-196",
      "exp_hant": "所有用於濕拔罐，或於未完整皮膚上使用的刮痧工具，第一步皆須以肥皂與清水清潔，以去除污垢、皮屑及潤滑劑。第二步則須進行a）高壓滅菌處理罐具或刮痧工具，或b）使用高層級消毒劑，如Sporox、Endospore、Peract或Acedide。用於完整皮膚上的罐具或刮痧工具，同樣須先以肥皂與清水清潔，再使用中層級消毒劑，如Sterilox、Sani-Cloth或Cavicide。血壓計袖帶、聽診器及電針夾則須先以肥皂與清水清潔，再使用低層級或中層級消毒劑。此處須注意一項但書：無論採用何種拔罐方式或作用於何種皮膚類型，目前尚不清楚有多少微量血液及體液會滲透皮膚而外滲。《清潔針法技術》一書作者認為，在確認拔罐及刮痧工具滲透血液與體液的程度之前，對所有罐具與刮痧工具採行高層級消毒較為謹慎。凡會破壞皮膚完整性或進入血管系統的器材，皆須進行滅菌處理（針灸相關工具／器材並不屬於此類別）；然而，一次性滅菌針具至關重要，拋棄式七星針錘、採血針及壓豆針皆不可重複使用。《清潔針法技術》第7版，第194-196頁"
