      "exp_en": "Iron deficiency anemia is the most common type of anemia and is usually the result of blood loss, a lack of iron in the diet, or an inability of the body to absorb iron. An iron deficiency anemia develops in stages. In first stage, the body needs more iron than is taken in from the diet. The body taps iron stores in the bone marrow and eventually this leads to impaired RBCs production. There will be pallor, fatigue, loss of stamina. If the iron deficiency is severe and prolonged there can be unusual symptoms such as pica (abnormal cravings (ice, dirt, paint, etc), concave nails, glossitis. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1038",
      "exp_hant": "缺鐵性貧血是最常見的貧血類型，通常由失血、飲食中鐵質攝取不足，或身體吸收鐵質能力不佳所致。缺鐵性貧血的發展分階段進行：在第一階段，身體所需的鐵質超過飲食攝取量，此時身體會動用骨髓中的鐵儲備，最終導致紅血球生成受損，出現面色蒼白、疲勞及耐力下降的情形。若缺鐵情形嚴重且持續，可能出現異食癖（異常渴望攝取冰塊、泥土、油漆等非食物物質）、匙狀甲（指甲凹陷），以及舌炎等較不常見的症狀。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第1038頁"
