      ],
      "exp_en": "The CDC recommends hand washing for: 1) with visibly soiled dirty hands use soap and water. 2) if hands are not visibly soiled, use soap and water or an alcohol disinfectant. 3) wash hands before contact with patient. 4) wash hands after touching the intact skin of the patient. 5) wash hands after contact with fluids or patient's dressing. 6) wash hands after gloves are removed because as gloves can harbor contaminants on their exterior. 7) wash hands before and after eating. Gloves are not required for routine acupuncture needling if hands are properly washed and no bleeding is anticipated. However, they are critical or strongly recommended when anticipating contact with blood, body fluids, mucous membranes, non-intact skin, or contaminated surfaces - or if the practitioner has skin breaks. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 182",
      "exp_hant": "CDC建議在下列情況下洗手：1）手部明顯髒污時使用肥皂與清水；2）手部無明顯髒污時可使用肥皂與清水，或使用酒精性消毒液；3）接觸患者前洗手；4）觸摸患者完整皮膚後洗手；5）接觸體液或患者敷料後洗手；6）脫除手套後洗手，因為手套外側可能藏有污染物；7）用餐前後洗手。若手部已妥善清潔且預期不會出血，一般針灸進針並不需要配戴手套；然而，若預期會接觸血液、體液、黏膜、非完整皮膚或受污染表面，或施術者本身皮膚有破損，則配戴手套至關重要或應強烈建議。《清潔針法技術》第7版，第182頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 349,
      "question_en": "Which of the following antiemetic drug classes treat motion sickness with a patch?",
      "question_hant": "下列哪一類止吐藥物是以貼片形式治療暈動病？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Anticholinergics competitively inhibit the binding of acetylcholine to muscarinic receptors",
          "hant": "抗膽鹼藥物：以競爭性方式抑制乙醯膽鹼與蕈毒鹼受體結合",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Cholinergic receptor antagonists: prevent nausea/vomiting by blocking M1 receptors in afferent nerves to the medulla",
          "hant": "膽鹼受體拮抗劑：藉由阻斷傳入延腦之傳入神經上的M1受體以防止噁心／嘔吐",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Serotonin receptor antagonists: prevent nausea/vomiting by blocking 5-HT3 receptors in the vagus nerve and medulla",
          "hant": "血清素受體拮抗劑：藉由阻斷迷走神經與延腦中的5-HT3受體以防止噁心／嘔吐",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Dopamine receptor antagonists: prevent nausea/vomiting by blocking D2 receptors in the medullary chemoreceptor trigger zone",
          "hant": "多巴胺受體拮抗劑：藉由阻斷延腦化學感受觸發區中的D2受體以防止噁心／嘔吐",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Vomiting is controlled by two distinct brain areas, the vomiting center and the chemoreceptor trigger zone (CTZ), both located in the medulla oblongata. The CTZ can receive input from the body that is then communicated to the vomiting reflex. Cholinergic blockers are used for nausea/vomiting, particularly in the prevention of motion sickness. These drugs block muscarinic 1 acetylcholine receptors (M1) receptor in the afferent nerves that send signals to the vomiting center in the medulla. The major drug in this class for motion sickness is SCOPOLAMINE which is also available as a skin patch (Transderm Scop). Scopolomine can also be used for post-surgical nausea/vomiting. Common side effects are dry mouth, drowsiness and blurred vision. HISTAMINE blockers are used to treat motion sickness. They block Histamine 1 (H1) receptors. This results in dulling the ability of the ear to sense motion thus preventing signals from reaching the medulla to trigger the vomiting reflex. Not all antihistamines are effective in the treatment of motion sickness. Examples are Dramamine (dimenhydrinate) and Antivert (meclizine). These drugs are also used whenever there is nausea/vomiting associated with allergies. Common side effects are drowsiness. DOPAMINE blockers inhibit the stimulation of dopamine 2 (D2) receptors in the CTZ. This results in blocking the vomiting reflex. These drugs are used for post-surgical nausea/vomiting. This class of drugs does not treat motion sickness. Examples are Reglan (metoclopramide), and Compazine (prochlorperazine). Metoclopramide also can prevent nausea from chronic GERD and diabetic gastroparesis by facilitating stomach movement. Compazine, an antipsychotic drug, acts an antiemetic at lower dosages. Common side effects include drowsiness and restlessness. SERATONIN blockers inhibit a subclass of serotonin receptors called 5-HT3 (5-hydroxytryptamine). In the CNS, the 5-HT3 receptors are located in the gut (terminals of vagus nerve) and the vomiting center in the brain stem (medulla). These drugs suppress 5-HT3 from triggering the vomiting reflex. These drugs are used for severe nausea/vomiting in the ER, for post-surgery nausea. It is the drug that is considered for post-chemotherapy nausea. This class of drugs does not treat motion sickness. This class of antiemetic drugs is known as \"setrons\". Examples include Zofran (ondansetron), Granisol (granisetron), Aloxi (palonosetron) and Anzemet (dolasetron). There are other setrons (olosetron, cilansetron) which are not antiemetic but are instead used to treat IBS. Common side effects for this class include headaches, drowsiness, dizziness and constipation. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "嘔吐是由大腦中兩個不同的區域所控制，分別為嘔吐中樞與化學感受觸發區（CTZ），兩者皆位於延腦。CTZ可接收來自身體的訊號，並將其傳遞至嘔吐反射。膽鹼阻斷劑用於治療噁心／嘔吐，特別是用於預防暈動病，這類藥物會阻斷傳入延腦嘔吐中樞之傳入神經上的M1蕈毒鹼型乙醯膽鹼受體。此類藥物中主要用於暈動病的藥物為東莨菪鹼（SCOPOLAMINE），亦有皮膚貼片劑型（Transderm Scop），東莨菪鹼也可用於術後噁心／嘔吐，常見副作用包括口乾、嗜睡及視力模糊。組織胺阻斷劑用於治療暈動病，其作用機轉為阻斷組織胺1（H1）受體，使耳朵感應運動的能力鈍化，從而防止訊號傳至延腦而引發嘔吐反射；並非所有抗組織胺藥物皆對暈動病有效，例如Dramamine（dimenhydrinate）及暈車寧（Antivert，meclizine），這類藥物也用於過敏所引起的噁心／嘔吐，常見副作用為嗜睡。多巴胺阻斷劑則抑制CTZ中多巴胺2（D2）受體的刺激，藉以阻斷嘔吐反射，這類藥物用於術後噁心／嘔吐，並不用於治療暈動病，例如Reglan（metoclopramide）及Compazine（prochlorperazine），metoclopramide也可透過促進胃部蠕動來預防慢性胃食道逆流及糖尿病性胃輕癱所引起的噁心；Compazine為一種抗精神病藥物，在較低劑量時具有止吐作用，常見副作用包括嗜睡及躁動不安。血清素阻斷劑則抑制血清素受體的一個亞型，稱為5-HT3（5-羥色胺）；在中樞神經系統中，5-HT3受體位於腸道（迷走神經末梢）及腦幹（延腦）的嘔吐中樞，這類藥物可抑制5-HT3引發嘔吐反射，多用於急診中嚴重的噁心／嘔吐、術後噁心，也是化療後噁心的首選藥物，這類藥物並不用於治療暈動病，此類止吐藥物統稱為「西曲類」（setrons），例如Zofran（ondansetron）、Granisol（granisetron）、Aloxi（palonosetron）及Anzemet（dolasetron）；另有其他西曲類藥物（如olosetron、cilansetron）並非止吐藥，而是用於治療大腸激躁症（IBS）。此類藥物常見副作用包括頭痛、嗜睡、頭暈及便秘。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
