      ],
      "exp_en": "Pepto-Bismol and Kaopectate have the active ingredient bismuth subsalicylate, which is related to aspirin. It should not be used in children younger than 12 years of age without consulting a physician. Children are more sensitive to the effects of salicylates, especially with a fever or if the child has lost large amounts of body fluid because of vomiting, diarrhea, or sweating. Salicylates or aspirin has been linked with Reye's syndrome. Caution when giving aspirin to children or teenagers especially if they have fever Reye's syndrome is a rapidly progressing brain disorder. It typically develops in patients recovering from a viral infection and also in children. It is linked to the use of aspirin (acetylsalicylic acid or ASA). Though uncommon, Reye's syndrome is associated with a more than 20 percent chance of death. Most of the cases are seen in children taking aspirin to treat the flu and chickenpox. Symptoms can start with lethargy, nausea, and hyperventilation but quickly progress to vomiting, seizures, and even coma. Regular use Pepto-Bismol and Koapectate which contain bismuth subsalicylate, which is related to aspirin, is a concern. Since 2003, the FDA has advised against the use of bismuth subsalicylate in children under 12. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "Pepto-Bismol與Kaopectate的活性成分為次水楊酸鉍（bismuth subsalicylate），與阿斯匹靈相關。未經醫師諮詢，不應用於12歲以下兒童。兒童對水楊酸鹽的作用較為敏感，尤其是在發燒或因嘔吐、腹瀉或流汗而大量流失體液時。水楊酸鹽或阿斯匹靈與雷氏症候群（Reye's syndrome）有關。給兒童或青少年服用阿斯匹靈時應謹慎，尤其是發燒時。雷氏症候群是一種快速進展的腦部疾病，通常發生於病毒感染恢復期的患者及兒童，與使用阿斯匹靈（乙醯水楊酸，ASA）有關。雖不常見，但雷氏症候群的死亡率超過百分之二十。大多數病例見於兒童因流感或水痘而服用阿斯匹靈。症狀可從嗜睡、噁心與過度換氣開始，並迅速進展為嘔吐、癲癇發作甚至昏迷。經常使用含次水楊酸鉍（與阿斯匹靈相關）的Pepto-Bismol與Kaopectate令人擔憂。自2003年起，FDA已建議12歲以下兒童不應使用次水楊酸鉍。tcmtests.com，2019年2月"
