      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate answer. Goiter is a neck or larynx swelling that results from an enlarged thyroid gland (thyromegaly). It is associated with a dysfunctional thyroid gland. Over 90 percent of goiters are due to an iodine deficiency in the diet. Although anyone can get a goiter, it is more common in women. This includes other types of goiter caused by autoimmune disorders and not only those caused by deficiency in iodine. Goiters are associated with underlying thyroid disorder (hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism). If the goiter is associated with hyperthyroidism there can also be tachycardia, palpitations, nervousness, tremor, and hypertension. If the goiter is associated with hypothyroidism there can also be weight gain despite poor appetite, cold intolerance, constipation and fatigue. Thyroiditis is an inflammatory condition that can cause pain and swelling in the thyroid and it can cause the body to produce too much or too little thyroxine. mayoclinic.org",
      "exp_hant": "此為最準確的答案。甲狀腺腫是因甲狀腺腫大（thyromegaly）而造成頸部或喉部腫脹，與甲狀腺功能失調有關。超過百分之九十的甲狀腺腫是由飲食中碘缺乏所致。雖然任何人都可能罹患甲狀腺腫，但女性較為常見，這也包括由自體免疫疾病引起的其他類型甲狀腺腫，而不僅限於碘缺乏所致者。甲狀腺腫與潛在的甲狀腺疾病（甲狀腺功能低下或亢進）有關。若甲狀腺腫與甲狀腺功能亢進有關，還可能出現心搏過速、心悸、緊張、顫抖與高血壓。若與甲狀腺功能低下有關，則可能出現食慾不振卻體重增加、怕冷、便秘與疲勞。甲狀腺炎是一種發炎性疾病，可造成甲狀腺疼痛與腫脹，並可能使身體產生過多或過少的甲狀腺素。mayoclinic.org"
