    {
      "number": 360,
      "question_en": "A patient has a sudden cardiac arrest. An AED (Automatic External Defibrillator) is available. What is the correct sequence?",
      "question_hant": "一名患者突發心臟驟停，現場備有AED（自動體外電擊去顫器）。正確的處理順序為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "only apply AED and not CPR",
          "hant": "只施用AED，不進行CPR",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "apply CPR first and then apply AED",
          "hant": "先進行CPR，再施用AED",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "apply AED and CPR at the same time",
          "hant": "同時施用AED與CPR",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "apply AED first and then apply CPR",
          "hant": "先施用AED，再進行CPR",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "If CPR has not been started then apply AED first. If the AED prompts you to deliver a shock, after it is delivered follow with CPR. If the AED does not prompt you to deliver a shock, start CPR. Without immediate treatment, 90-95 percent of cardiac arrest victims will die. If CPR is in progress, continue with the CPR until the AED is turned on, pads are applied, and the AED is ready to do an analysis of the heart rhythm. If you are alone, an AED is available, and the patient has cardiac arrest use the AED as a first step. The steps to apply an AED: 1) Turn on the AED, 2) Wipe chest dry (remove any medication patches), 3. Attach pads to a bare chest (upper right side. lower left side). Use the appropriate pads for an adult or child, 4) Plug in the connector if necessary, 5) Say to everyone to stand clear and make sure no one (including you) is touching the person, 6) Push analyze button if necessary and let the AED analyze heart rhythm, 7) if the AED prompts you to do so then deliver shock if shock is advised. Make sure no one (including you) is touching the person. Say Everyone stand clear and push shock button, 8) After the shock is given or if the AED does not advise giving a shock, immediately resume CPR starting with chest compressions. You do not need to wait for the AED to prompt you to start CPR. Do 2 minutes of CPR (5 cycles of 30 compressions to 2 ventilations) until the AED prompts that it is reanalyzing or the patient shows signs of ROSC (return of spontaneous circulation). Signs of ROSC include breathing, coughing, or movement and a palpable pulse or a measurable blood pressure. Basic Life Support, Participant Manual, American Red Cross, 2019, page 24, 25",
      "exp_hant": "若尚未開始CPR，應先施用AED。若AED提示須電擊，電擊後應接續進行CPR；若AED未提示電擊，則開始CPR。若未立即治療，90%至95%的心臟驟停患者將死亡。若CPR已在進行中，應持續CPR直到AED開啟、貼上電極片並準備好分析心律。若您獨自一人、現場有AED且患者發生心臟驟停，應先使用AED作為第一步。施用AED的步驟：1）開啟AED；2）擦乾胸部（移除任何藥物貼片）；3）將電極片貼於裸露的胸部（右上側、左下側），並使用適合成人或兒童的電極片；4）如有需要，插入接頭；5）告知所有人退開，並確認沒有人（包括您自己）碰觸患者；6）如有需要按下分析鍵，讓AED分析心律；7）若AED提示應電擊，則進行電擊，並再次確認沒有人（包括您）碰觸患者，說「大家退開」後按下電擊鍵；8）電擊後或若AED未建議電擊，應立即從胸部按壓開始恢復CPR，無需等待AED提示才開始CPR。持續進行2分鐘的CPR（5個週期，每週期30次按壓配2次人工呼吸），直到AED提示正在重新分析，或患者出現自發性循環恢復（ROSC）的徵象。ROSC的徵象包括呼吸、咳嗽或動作，以及可觸摸到的脈搏或可測得的血壓。《基本救命術學員手冊》，美國紅十字會，2019年，第24、25頁"
    },
