      "exp_en": "Possible pneumonia. Pneumonia is a lung inflammation due to an infection caused by bacteria, viruses, fungi or parasites. Pneumonia is a particular concern if the patient is older than 65 or has a chronic illness or weak immune system. Pneumonia can range in seriousness from mild to life-threatening. Refer to a physician when the patient has a persistent cough, shortness of breath, chest pain, and fever, especially a lasting fever of 102 F or higher with chills and sweating. The risk of pneumonia complications increases if the patient is an older adult, smokes, drinks too much alcohol, taking any medication that suppresses the immune system such as prednisone. tcmtests.com, December 2019",
