        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "restricting type and purging type",
          "hant": "限制型與清除型",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "restricting type and obsessive-compulsive type",
          "hant": "限制型與強迫型",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "body dysmorphic type and restricting type",
          "hant": "身體臆形型與限制型",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "There are two main types of anorexia. The most common type is the restricting type where the patient severely restricts their food intake.Restriction may take the form of maintaining a very low calorie count, restricting types of food eaten, eating only one meal a day, or following obsessive and rigid rules such as only eating food of one color. The second form of anorexia nervosa is called the binge-eating or purging type. This type is less recognized. Here the patient severely restricts food intake but regularly engages in binge-eating or purging behavior (self-induced vomiting, over-exercise, misuse of laxatives, diuretics or enemas). This second type can be confused with another eating disorder, bulimia nervosa. The difference is that bulimia patients are usually of normal weight or overweight whereas anorexia patients are significantly underweight. Severe food restriction in anorexia patients can eventually affect the heart (bradycardia, hypotension, ventricular arrhythmia, mitral valve prolapse), the digestive system (bloating, constipation, fatty liver disease), hormones (amenorrhea, low testosterone levels, delayed puberty and physical growth, hypothyroidism, osteoporosis). The are no lab tests to specifically diagnose anorexia nervosa. However, tests are used to rule out other diseases as well as to evaluate the effects of the weight loss on the body. An electrocardiogram (ECG) could be ordered to check for slow heart rate or abnormal heart rhythm, for example, or lab tests to evaluate electrolytes and hormonal levels. DSM-5 (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders) Chapter 10",
      "exp_hant": "厭食症主要有兩種類型。最常見的是限制型，患者嚴格限制食物攝取，可能表現為維持極低熱量攝取、限制食物種類、每天只吃一餐，或遵循強迫且僵化的規則（如只吃某一種顏色的食物）。第二種類型稱為暴食／清除型，較不為人所知。此類型患者嚴格限制食物攝取，但同時經常出現暴食或清除行為（自我催吐、過度運動、濫用瀉藥、利尿劑或灌腸）。此類型容易與另一種飲食疾患「暴食症」（bulimia nervosa）混淆，差異在於暴食症患者通常體重正常或過重，而厭食症患者則明顯體重過輕。厭食症患者嚴重的食物限制最終可能影響心臟（心搏過緩、低血壓、心室性心律不整、二尖瓣脫垂）、消化系統（脹氣、便秘、脂肪肝）以及荷爾蒙（停經、睪固酮濃度過低、青春期與生理發育延遲、甲狀腺功能低下、骨質疏鬆）。目前並無專門診斷厭食症的實驗室檢測，但檢測可用於排除其他疾病，並評估體重減輕對身體的影響。例如可安排心電圖（ECG）以檢查心跳過慢或心律異常，或以實驗室檢測評估電解質與荷爾蒙濃度。《DSM-5精神疾病診斷與統計手冊》第10章"
    },
    {
      "number": 367,
      "question_en": "A 65 year-old female patient with osteoporosis has back pain that mimics intermittent claudication. The pain is triggered by standing for long periods or after walking. The pain improves with rest or when bending forward. There is also bilateral pain in the buttocks. This type of back pain is due to",
      "question_hant": "一名65歲女性骨質疏鬆症患者，其背痛症狀類似間歇性跛行。疼痛因久站或走路後誘發，休息或前彎時可改善，且雙側臀部亦有疼痛。此類背痛的成因為",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
