      "exp_en": "Viral encephalitis is an inflammation of the brain caused by a virus that can lead to permanent brain damage. Many patients with viral encephalitis have no symptoms or flu-like symptoms (fever) or more severe symptoms (seizures, hallucinations, severe headache, confused thinking, double vision, difficulty moving). Viral encephalitis results in brain damage which then can cause diabetes insipidus (frequent thirst, frequent urination). Normal fasting blood sugar levels is less than or equal to 100 milligrams per deciliter (mg/dL). Diabetes insipidus is an uncommon disorder, unlike diabetes mellitus. Diabetes insipidus that causes an imbalance of water in the body causing intense thirst even after drinking fluids (polydipsia), and large amounts of urine (polyuria). In this patient, the encephalitis damaged pituitary gland or hypothalamus. This damage has disrupted the normal production, storage and release of ADH (anti-diuretic hormone). The two primary functions of ADH are to retain water in the body and to constrict blood vessels. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 299, 709",
      "exp_hant": "病毒性腦炎是一種由病毒引起的腦部發炎，可能導致永久性腦損傷。許多病毒性腦炎患者並無症狀，或僅有類流感症狀（發燒），或有更嚴重的症狀（癲癇發作、幻覺、劇烈頭痛、思考混亂、複視、動作困難）。病毒性腦炎所造成的腦損傷，其後可能引發尿崩症（頻繁口渴、頻尿）。正常空腹血糖值應小於或等於每分升100毫克（mg/dL）。尿崩症是一種不常見的疾病，與糖尿病不同。尿崩症會造成體內水分失衡，導致即使飲水後仍感到強烈口渴（煩渴）及大量排尿（多尿）。此患者的腦炎已損傷腦下垂體或下視丘，這種損傷擾亂了抗利尿激素（ADH）的正常生成、儲存與釋放。ADH的兩項主要功能為使體內保留水分及使血管收縮。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學執業者教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第299、709頁"
