      "exp_en": "This is the best answer from the choices. White males over the age of 80 are at the greatest risk of all age/gender/race groups. Suicide and age are positively correlated, especially for males. Whites are at highest risk, followed by Native Americans, Hispanics, and Asians. The American Foundation of Suicide Prevention notes that in 2017, the highest suicide rate (20.2%) was among adults between 45 and 54 years of age. The second highest rate (20.1%) occurred in those 85 years or older. Younger groups have had consistently lower suicide rates than middle-aged and older adults. In 2017, adolescents and young adults aged 15 to 24 had a suicide rate of 14.5%. In terms of race, the highest U.S. age-adjusted suicide rate was among Whites (15.85%) and the second highest rate was among American Indians and Alaska Natives (13.42%). A much lower and roughly similar rates were found among Black or African Americans (6.61%) and Asians and Pacific Islanders (6.59%). www.afsp.org",
