      "exp_en": "The thyroid produces calcitonin, which plays a role in calcium homeostasis. Calcitonin suppresses resorption of bone by inhibiting the activity of osteoclasts, a cell type that \"digests\" bone matrix, releasing calcium and phosphorus into the blood. Calcium and phosphorus are prevented from being lost in the urine by resorption in the kidney tubules. The inner medulla of the adrenals produces epinephrine and norepinephrine (adrenaline). The adrenals also contain an outer cortex, which produces hormones such as cortisol, aldosterone, testosterone, DHEA, DHEAS, androstenedione and estrogens. The thymus gland is only active until puberty. After puberty, the thymus starts to slowly shrink and become replaced by fat. Thymosin is the hormone of the thymus and stimulates the development of disease-fighting T cells. The pituitary is often called master gland. It controls other hormone glands (eg adrenals, thyroid). It is about the size of a pea and consists of two lobes, anterior and posterior, each producing their own hormones. tcmtests.com, May 2020",
      "exp_hant": "甲狀腺會分泌抑鈣素，其在鈣恆定中扮演一定角色。抑鈣素透過抑制蝕骨細胞（一種能『消化』骨基質，釋放鈣與磷至血液中的細胞）的活性，來抑制骨質再吸收。鈣與磷透過腎小管的再吸收，可避免隨尿液流失。腎上腺髓質（內層）分泌腎上腺素與正腎上腺素（腎上腺素類激素）。腎上腺也含有外層皮質，可分泌如皮質醇、醛固酮、睪固酮、脫氫表雄酮（DHEA）、硫酸脫氫表雄酮（DHEAS）、雄烯二酮及雌激素等荷爾蒙。胸腺僅在青春期前活躍，青春期後開始逐漸萎縮並被脂肪組織取代。胸腺素是胸腺分泌的荷爾蒙，可刺激能對抗疾病的T細胞發育。腦下垂體常被稱為「主腺」，可控制其他荷爾蒙腺體（如腎上腺、甲狀腺），大小約如豌豆，由前葉與後葉兩部分組成，各自分泌不同的荷爾蒙。tcmtests.com，2020年5月"
