      "exp_en": "Short-term memory involves repeating of questions or stories and diminished ability to remember details. The short-term memory problems with Alzheimer's disease has been associated with a shrinking hippocampus. The hippocampus is part of the limbic system, and plays important roles in the consolidation of information from short-term memory to long-term memory. Word-finding involves problems associating names to people, places, object. Word-finding involves the left temporoparietal junction as it is involved with word retrieval and sentence repetition issues. Visuospatial symptoms include poor navigation, getting lost in familiar places, and impaired recognition of previously familiar building. The right parietal lobe is vital to complete images and understand maps (important to spatial relationship). If any injury occurs to this part of the lobe then it leads to loss of descriptions and visualization of spatial relationship. Executive dysfunction can manifest as impulsivity, mental rigidity, poor planning, and impaired judgment. It is the frontal lobes and not the occipital lobe that are the executive center of the brain. Called the pre-frontal cortex, it plays an important role in judging, reasoning, planning, decision-making and behavioral control. Current Medical Diagnosis and Treatment 2020, page 1040",
      "exp_hant": "短期記憶問題表現為反覆詢問相同問題或重複相同故事，以及記住細節的能力下降。阿茲海默症的短期記憶問題與海馬迴萎縮有關。海馬迴屬邊緣系統的一部分，在將短期記憶鞏固為長期記憶的過程中扮演重要角色。找詞困難涉及將名稱與人物、地點、物品連結的問題，與左側顳頂交界處有關，因該區域涉及詞語提取與句子重複的問題。視覺空間症狀包括方向感不佳、在熟悉的地方迷路，以及對先前熟悉建築物的辨識能力受損。右頂葉對於完整拼湊影像及理解地圖（對空間關係很重要）至關重要，若此部位受損，將導致對空間關係的描述與視覺化能力喪失。執行功能障礙可能表現為衝動、思維僵化、規劃能力不佳及判斷力受損。真正的執行中樞是額葉而非枕葉，稱為前額葉皮質，在判斷、推理、規劃、決策與行為控制方面扮演重要角色。《2020年當代醫學診斷與治療》第1040頁"
