      "exp_en": "The majority of breast cancer lumps are discovered either by the patient, during a physical examination, or during a mammography. Breast cancer is less commonly discovered by the symptom of breast pain or enlargement or thickening of the breast. Disease of the nipple (Paget's disease) which has breast skin changes such as erythema, crusting, scaling and nipple discharge occurs in about 50% of patients who have a palpable tumor. However, to the patient, the symptoms of Paget's disease are viewed as benign and ignored, thereby delaying diagnosis. A lump in the upper-outer quadrant of the breast is most characteristic of benign disorder (fibrocystic breast disease). One breast that is firmer and with a thick skin while the other breast is normal can be a cancer sign. As breast cancer progresses there is a fixed lump attached to the skin or chest wall, a satellite of nodules or skin ulcers, orange peel skin, and enlarged lymph nodes. There is also Paget's disease of the bones which is not related to breast tumors. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2113",
      "exp_hant": "大多數乳癌腫塊是由患者本人、理學檢查或乳房攝影檢查發現，較少是因乳房疼痛、增大或增厚等症狀被發現。乳頭疾病（佩吉特氏病），其乳房皮膚變化包括紅斑、結痂、脫屑及乳頭分泌物，出現於約50%可觸診到腫瘤的患者身上。然而，患者往往將佩吉特氏病的症狀視為良性而忽略，因而延誤診斷。乳房外上象限的腫塊最常見於良性疾病（纖維囊性乳房疾病）。若一側乳房較硬且皮膚增厚，而另一側乳房正常，可能是癌症的徵兆。隨著乳癌病程進展，會出現固定於皮膚或胸壁的腫塊、衛星結節或皮膚潰瘍、橘皮樣皮膚及淋巴結腫大。此外還有與乳房腫瘤無關的骨骼佩吉特氏病。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第2113頁"
