      "exp_en": "AST (aspartate amino transferase) is an enzyme found in high concentrations in the heart muscle, liver cells, and skeletal muscle cells. When a disease is present in the cells of these tissues (heart, liver, muscle cells) the cells start to come apart (lyse) and AST is released into the blood and AST levels rise. How much AST rises is related to the number of cells affected by the disease. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 112-114; 4th Edition, page 125-126",
      "exp_hant": "AST（天門冬胺酸轉胺酶）是一種在心肌、肝細胞與骨骼肌細胞中濃度較高的酵素。當這些組織（心臟、肝臟、肌肉細胞）出現疾病時，細胞開始崩解（溶解），AST便會釋放至血液中，導致AST濃度升高，升高的程度與受疾病影響的細胞數量有關。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢測手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第112-114頁；第4版，第125-126頁"
    },
