      "exp_en": "Genu varum (also called bow-leggedness) is a physical leg deformity marked by outward bowing of the lower leg in relation to the thigh. This gives the appearance of an archer's bow. In children learning to walk, genu varum can be a consequence of diseases such as Rickets. Rickets is a childhood bone disorder in which bones become soft and prone to fracture and deformity. It is usually due a lack of vitamin D, calcium, or phosphate. In adults, genu varum can be caused by disorders such as Blount's Disease which is a growth disorder of the tibia that causes the lower leg to angle inward (bowleg). Genu valgum or genu valgus (knock-knees) is a common lower leg abnormality that is seen in the toddler, preschool and early school age children. Hallux valgus refers to big toe deformity. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 803; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 627",
      "exp_hant": "膝內翻（也稱為弓形腿）是一種身體上的腿部畸形，特徵為小腿相對於大腿呈現向外弓起，形似弓箭手的弓。在學步中的兒童，膝內翻可能是佝僂病等疾病的後果。佝僂病是一種兒童骨骼疾病，骨骼變軟且易骨折與變形，通常是由於缺乏維生素D、鈣或磷所致。在成人中，膝內翻可能由白朗特氏病（Blount's Disease）等疾病引起，這是一種脛骨生長異常疾病，會導致小腿向內成角（弓形腿）。膝外翻（knock-knees）則是常見於學步期、學齡前及學齡早期兒童的下肢異常。拇趾外翻是指大拇趾的畸形。《貝茲身體檢查指南》第13版，第803頁；第10版，第627頁"
