    {
      "number": 401,
      "question_en": "A 62 year-old male patient has an aplastic anemia diagnosis. He reports that his tiredness, dizziness and shortness of breath have gradually worsened during the past month. Facial complexion is very pale, almost white. Review of systems is positive for frequent colds and recurring urinary tract infections. The physical exam reveals pinhead-sized bruising on the forearms. Which aspect of the clinical picture indicates a worsening of the aplastic anemia requiring a referral for further evaluation?",
      "question_hant": "一名62歲男性患者確診再生不良性貧血，表示其疲倦、頭暈與呼吸急促在過去一個月逐漸惡化。面色極為蒼白，幾近慘白。系統回顧顯示反覆感冒與復發性泌尿道感染，理學檢查在前臂發現針頭大小的瘀點。臨床表現中的哪一項顯示再生不良性貧血正在惡化，需轉診做進一步評估？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "worsening tiredness, dizziness, shortness of breath, complexion",
          "hant": "疲倦、頭暈、呼吸急促、面色惡化",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "worsening tiredness, frequent infections, skin bruising",
          "hant": "疲倦惡化、頻繁感染、皮膚瘀傷",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "age, complexion, frequent urinary tract infections and frequent colds",
          "hant": "年齡、面色、頻繁泌尿道感染與頻繁感冒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "age, complexion, frequent urinary tract infections but not frequent colds",
          "hant": "年齡、面色、頻繁泌尿道感染但不含頻繁感冒",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Aplastic anemia is a pancytopenia. Pancytopenia is a disorder that has low levels for all three types of blood cell lines: red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. With aplastic anemia there is not only actual anemia (low red blood cells) but also leukopenia (low white blood cells) and thrombocytopenia (low platelet cells). The symptoms and signs for aplastic anemia depend on the type of blood cells that are low. Red cells carry oxygen, white cells fight infections, and platelets prevent bleeding. Low red blood cell results in anemia (tiredness, weakness, pallor, breathlessness, tachycardia). Low white blood cell count results in recurrent or severe bacterial infections. Low platelet cell count results in easy bruising, petechiae, or bleeding from the nose and/or gums. The severity of the symptoms and signs will determine whether the referral is a high-priority same day referral or an urgent emergency referral. The most common cause of aplastic anemia is the autoimmune destruction of hematopoietic (blood formation) stem cells in the bone marrow. The definitive diagnosis is with a bone marrow biopsy. Healthy bone marrow has 30 to 70 percent blood stem cells. In aplastic anemia, these cells are almost gone and have been replaced by fat. Treatment involves either stem cell transplant or immunosuppressive therapy. The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 9, 49; www.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "再生不良性貧血屬於全血球減少症。全血球減少症是一種紅血球、白血球與血小板三種血球系列數量皆偏低的疾病。再生不良性貧血不僅有真正的貧血（紅血球偏低），還合併白血球減少症（白血球偏低）與血小板減少症（血小板偏低）。再生不良性貧血的症狀與徵象取決於哪一類血球數量偏低。紅血球負責攜帶氧氣、白血球對抗感染、血小板則防止出血。紅血球偏低會導致貧血（疲倦、無力、蒼白、呼吸困難、心搏過速）。白血球數量偏低會導致反覆或嚴重的細菌感染。血小板數量偏低會導致容易瘀傷、瘀點，或鼻部及／或牙齦出血。症狀與徵象的嚴重程度將決定轉診是屬於高優先的當日轉診，還是緊急轉診。再生不良性貧血最常見的病因是骨髓中造血幹細胞遭自體免疫破壞，確切診斷需仰賴骨髓切片。健康骨髓含有30%至70%的造血幹細胞，而在再生不良性貧血中，這些細胞幾乎消失，並被脂肪取代。治療包括幹細胞移植或免疫抑制療法。《補充療法師紅旗轉診指南》，Stephenson著，2013年，第9、49頁；www.webmd.com"
    },
