      "exp_en": "A person who knowingly obtains or discloses individually identifiable health information in violation of the Privacy Rule may face a criminal penalty of up to $50,000 and up to one-year imprisonment. The criminal penalties increase to $100,000 and up to five years imprisonment if the wrongful conduct involves false pretenses, and to $250,000 and up to 10 years imprisonment if the wrongful conduct involves the intent to sell, transfer, or use identifiable health information for commercial advantage, personal gain or malicious harm. Penalties for disclosing PHI (protected health information) such as accidentally leaving a patient's chart on the reception desk for others to see if reported are $100 to $50,000 per occurrence. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "任何人若明知故犯地違反隱私規則取得或揭露可識別個人身分的健康資訊，可能面臨最高5萬美元罰款及最高1年徒刑的刑事處罰。若不法行為涉及虛偽陳述，刑事罰則將提高至最高10萬美元及最高5年徒刑；若不法行為涉及意圖出售、轉讓或利用可識別的健康資訊以謀取商業利益、個人利益或惡意傷害，罰則將提高至最高25萬美元及最高10年徒刑。至於揭露受保護健康資訊（PHI），如不慎將患者病歷留在櫃檯讓他人看見，若經舉報，每次違規罰款為100至50,000美元。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
    },
    {
      "number": 403,
      "question_en": "What is an accurate comparison between Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo (BPPV) and Meniere's disease (MD)?",
      "question_hant": "良性陣發性姿勢性眩暈症（BPPV）與梅尼爾氏病（MD）之間，何者的比較正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "inner ear calcium crystals causes MD and inner ear fluid build up causes BPPV",
          "hant": "內耳鈣結晶造成MD，內耳液體積聚造成BPPV",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "BPPV is associated with hearing loss and MD is associated with tinnitus",
          "hant": "BPPV與聽力損失有關，MD與耳鳴有關",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "BPPV vertigo lasts about 1 minute and MD vertigo lasts more than 20 minutes",
          "hant": "BPPV的眩暈約持續1分鐘，MD的眩暈持續超過20分鐘",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "the Dix-Hallpike Test diagnoses BPPV and the Epley Maneuver diagnoses MD",
          "hant": "迪克斯－霍派克測試（Dix-Hallpike Test）用於診斷BPPV，愛普利手法（Epley Maneuver）用於診斷MD",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The classic provoking movements to induce BPPV are lying flat, sitting up from lying flat, turning over in bed, looking up or bending down, especially if also looking to the side. The duration of the vertigo is brief, usually one minute. Most vertigo episodes with MD are unrelated to head position as with BPPV. The MD episodes can occur without warning at any time and can last more than 20 minutes to several hours but not more than 24 hours. The cause for BPPV is the loosening of the calcium carbonate crystals into the inner ear and affecting balance. MD involves increased pressure in the inner ear due to a fluid build up in the ear. The Dix-Hallpike test (also called the Dix-Hallpike maneuver) checks for the vertigo associated with BPPV. In this test the patient sits on the exam table with legs stretched out with the head at 45 degrees to one side. The examiner then helps the patient lie back quickly so the head hangs slightly over the edge of the table. This movement loosens the crystals to move within the semicircular canals of the ear. If the movement produces vertigo and nystagmus (rapid, involuntary movements of the eye) it is indicative of BBPV. The Epley Maneuver does not help to diagnose Meniere's. Rather, the Epley Maneuver is a treatment for BBPV. It consists of four different head positions that help to loosen the calcium crystals and help to relieve the vertigo. Only MD is associated with tinnitus and one-sided hearing loss, not BPPV. BPPV and MD have similar symptoms. BPPV is characterized by vertigo, nausea, rhythmic eye movements, and loss of balance. MD symptoms include vertigo, tinnitus, nausea, and loss of balance. Both conditions usually affect only one ear. BPPV: The inner ear has three semicircular canals which help sense motion and maintain balance. When calcium crystals break free from the lining of the semicircular canals and into the canal itself it can cause vertigo. BPPV is characterized by dizziness, nausea, vomiting, vertigo, rhythmic eye movements, and loss of balance. These symptoms can be triggered by changing head position in relation to gravity. In most patients, only one ear is involved. BPPV is sometimes called \"top shelf vertigo\" because dizziness is triggered by looking up, getting out of bed and quick head movements. Generally, symptoms may last a few weeks, stop and then recur. Treatments include the Epley maneuver (sequential movement of the head), Foster maneuver (moving the head backward), and the home Epley maneuver. These maneuvers help 95% of patients resolve their BPPV. Surgery is also available for difficult to cure cases. MD: It is posited that MD is due to abnormal fluid in the inner ear causing increased ear pressure. Symptoms include recurring episodes of vertigo, hearing loss, tinnitus, and a feeling of fullness in the ear. Vertigo episodes occur without warning and can last 20 minutes to several hours, but not more than 24 hours. MD can be diagnosed through a hearing test, the electronystagmography (ENG) balance tests, and vestibular tests called the vestibular evoked myogenic potential tests which involves short, intense sound stimuli to produce a muscle reflex in the eye. The vestibular system provides information about motion, head position, and spatial orientation. No cure exists for MD. Treatments include medication (anti-motion sickness,anti-nausea, diuretics), physical therapy, hearing aids and if severe surgery (endolymphatic sac procedure). Lifestyle changes (no smoking, limit salt, caffeine, alcohol) are recommended. Differential Diagnosis of Common Complaints, Sellers and Symons, 7th Edition, page 137; mayoclinic.com",
      "exp_hant": "誘發BPPV的典型動作包括平躺、從平躺姿勢坐起、在床上翻身、抬頭或彎腰，尤其是同時轉頭看向一側時。眩暈持續時間短暫，通常僅約1分鐘。大多數MD的眩暈發作與頭部姿勢無關，這點與BPPV不同。MD發作可能毫無預警地隨時發生，可持續超過20分鐘至數小時，但不會超過24小時。BPPV的病因是碳酸鈣結晶鬆脫進入內耳，影響平衡；MD則涉及因內耳液體積聚導致內耳壓力增加。迪克斯－霍派克測試（也稱迪克斯－霍派克手法）用於檢查與BPPV相關的眩暈。此測試中，患者坐在檢查台上，雙腿伸直，頭部轉向一側呈45度角，檢查者接著協助患者迅速躺下，使頭部微微懸空於檢查台邊緣。此動作會使結晶在耳部半規管內鬆動移位。若此動作引發眩暈與眼球震顫（眼睛快速不自主的移動），則顯示為BPPV陽性。愛普利手法無助於診斷梅尼爾氏病，而是用於治療BPPV，它包含四種不同的頭部姿勢，有助於鬆動鈣結晶並緩解眩暈。只有MD與耳鳴及單側聽力損失有關，BPPV則無。BPPV與MD的症狀相似，BPPV的特徵為眩暈、噁心、規律的眼球運動及失去平衡；MD的症狀包括眩暈、耳鳴、噁心及失去平衡，兩種病症通常僅影響一側耳朵。BPPV：內耳有三個半規管，有助於感知運動並維持平衡。當鈣結晶從半規管內壁脫落進入管腔內，可能引發眩暈。BPPV的特徵為頭暈、噁心、嘔吐、眩暈、規律的眼球運動及失去平衡，這些症狀可因頭部相對於重力的位置改變而誘發，大多數患者僅一側耳朵受影響。BPPV有時被稱為「上層架眩暈」，因為抬頭看、起床及快速轉頭動作會誘發頭暈，症狀通常持續數週後停止並可能復發。治療方式包括愛普利手法（依序移動頭部）、福斯特手法（將頭向後移動）及居家愛普利手法，這些手法可幫助95%的患者緩解BPPV，對於難以治癒的病例也可考慮手術。MD：據推測MD是因內耳液體異常導致耳內壓力升高所致，症狀包括反覆發作的眩暈、聽力損失、耳鳴及耳部悶脹感。眩暈發作毫無預警，可持續20分鐘至數小時，但不超過24小時。MD可透過聽力測試、眼振電圖（ENG）平衡測試，以及一種稱為前庭誘發肌源性電位測試的前庭測試來診斷，該測試利用短暫而強烈的聲音刺激以引發眼部肌肉反射。前庭系統提供有關運動、頭部位置及空間定向的資訊，目前尚無治癒MD的方法，治療包括藥物（抗暈動症、止吐、利尿劑）、物理治療、助聽器，若嚴重則需手術（內淋巴囊手術）。建議進行生活型態改變（戒菸、限鹽、限咖啡因與酒精）。《常見主訴之鑑別診斷》，Sellers與Symons著，第7版，第137頁；mayoclinic.com"
    },
