      "exp_en": "The ELISA (enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay) tests for antibodies to the HIV virus in the blood. this test is used for diagnosing, to screen blood donors, and to test patients believed to be infected with HIV. This test is used to detect antibodies to HIV and not the virus. As such they cannot detect HIV infection in the earliest stage before antibodies are produced by the immune system. For most patients there is a time period of 2-12 weeks but as long as six months for the infected patient with the HIV virus to test positive to HIV antibodies which is what the ELISA test looks for. This time period between HIV infection and the antibody production is called the \"window period\". There are newer HIV tests. The CDC recommends the antibody/antigen combination blood tests. They can detect HIV earlier than the antibody screening tests such as ELISA. The antibody/antigen checks for an HIV antigen, a protein called p24 that's part of the virus and shows up 2 to 4 weeks after infection. They also check for HIV antibodies. There is also a rapid antibody/antigen test that can give results in 20 minutes. There is also the nucleic acid test (NAT), also known as an RNA test, that looks for the virus itself and can diagnose HIV about 10 days after exposure. It's an expensive test, so it's usually not the first choice. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 279-281; 4th Edition, page 312; webmd.com; cdc.gov",
      "exp_hant": "ELISA（酵素結合免疫吸附分析）用於檢測血液中對HIV病毒的抗體，此檢測用於診斷、篩檢捐血者，以及檢測疑似感染HIV的患者。此檢測是用來偵測HIV抗體，而非病毒本身，因此無法在免疫系統尚未產生抗體的最早階段檢測出HIV感染。對大多數患者而言，感染HIV病毒後需經過2-12週、甚至長達六個月的時間，才會對ELISA檢測所偵測的HIV抗體呈陽性反應。這段介於HIV感染與抗體產生之間的時間，稱為「窗口期」。目前也有更新的HIV檢測方式，CDC建議使用抗體／抗原聯合血液檢測，這類檢測比ELISA等抗體篩檢檢測更早偵測出HIV。抗體／抗原檢測會檢查一種稱為p24的HIV抗原蛋白（病毒的一部分），該蛋白在感染後2至4週即會出現，同時也會檢測HIV抗體。另有一種可在20分鐘內得出結果的快速抗體／抗原檢測。此外還有核酸檢測（NAT，亦稱RNA檢測），可直接偵測病毒本身，並可在暴露後約10天診斷出HIV，但此檢測費用昂貴，通常不作為首選。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢測手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第279-281頁；第4版，第312頁；webmd.com；cdc.gov"
    },
