      "exp_en": "Polyps normally do not cause pain. Fibroids can cause uterine cramping and discomfort. They can also press on nearby organs and tissue and cause abdominal pain, bladder pain, or back pain. Both polyps and fibroids can cause abnormal bleeding. Uterine fibroids grow in the uterine muscle while polyps grows from the endometrial tissue that lines the uterus. Both are non-cancerous. Many women with cervical polyps have no symptoms other than infertility. Endometriosis can cause pelvic scarring that damages the fallopian tubes or ovaries and lead to infertility. Polyps are usually very small and can regress while uterine fibroids can be large and do not regress. When numerous fibroids grow it can result in a uterus larger than normal. Polyps are usually too small to be palpated but can be palpated if they protrude through the cervix. Fibroids grow in the uterine muscle while polyps grow from the endometrial tissue. Differential Diagnosis, Rhoads, 2015 page 162",
      "exp_hant": "息肉通常不會造成疼痛，肌瘤則可能造成子宮絞痛與不適，也可能壓迫鄰近器官與組織，造成腹痛、膀胱疼痛或背痛。息肉與肌瘤皆可能造成異常出血。子宮肌瘤生長於子宮肌肉層，息肉則生長自子宮內膜組織。兩者皆為非癌性。許多罹患子宮頸息肉的女性除不孕外並無其他症狀，子宮內膜異位症則可能造成骨盆腔沾黏，損傷輸卵管或卵巢並導致不孕。息肉通常非常小且可自行消退，子宮肌瘤則可能長得很大且不會消退，多發性肌瘤可能導致子宮大於正常大小。息肉通常過小而無法觸診，但若突出於子宮頸則可被觸及。肌瘤生長於子宮肌肉層，而息肉則生長自子宮內膜組織。《鑑別診斷》，Rhoads著，2015年，第162頁"
