      "exp_en": "The motor cortex is that part of the cerebral cortex where nerve impulses initiate voluntary muscular activity. The corticospinal tract is a motor pathway which starts at the motor cortex and ends at the motor neurons in the neuromuscular junctions which control voluntary movements of the limbs and trunk. A stroke in affecting a particular area of the motor cortex will affect muscle activation in the body. Upper motor neuron disorders typically arise from a stroke, a tumor, or a blunt trauma to the head. Upper motor neurons (UMN) originate in the motor region of the cerebral cortex or in the brain stem. UMN transmit motor information down to the lower motor neurons. The lower motor neurons receive impulses from the UMN and connect the spinal cord and brain stem to the muscle fibers. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 847-849; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 661-662",
      "exp_hant": "運動皮質是大腦皮質中啟動隨意肌肉活動神經衝動的部位。皮質脊髓徑是一條運動路徑，起自運動皮質，終止於神經肌肉接合處的運動神經元，控制四肢與軀幹的隨意動作。中風若影響運動皮質的特定區域，將影響身體的肌肉活化。上運動神經元疾患通常源自中風、腫瘤或頭部鈍傷，上運動神經元（UMN）起源於大腦皮質的運動區或腦幹，UMN將運動訊息向下傳遞至下運動神經元，下運動神經元接收來自UMN的衝動，並連接脊髓、腦幹與肌纖維。《貝茲身體檢查指南》第13版，第847-849頁；第10版，第661-662頁"
