      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. A urinalysis can show evidence of RBCs which can indicate a possible damage to the glomeruli, WBCs which indicate an infection or inflammation, and increased protein (proteinuria) that can indicate nephron (glomerulus and its associated tubule) damage. Other lab tests will show increased creatinine or urea blood levels and low urine clearance of creatinine. In other words, acute glomerulonephritis is characterized by proteinuria (protein in the urine), hematuria (blood in the urine), elevated serum creatinine (indicating reduced kidney function), and low creatinine clearance (reflecting impaired glomerular filtration). These findings align with the typical clinical presentation of acute glomerulonephritis, such as in post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis. Decreased serum creatinine and high creatinine clearance, which suggest improved kidney function, not typical of acute glomerulonephritis. Granular casts, which are more characteristic of acute tubular necrosis or chronic kidney disease, not a hallmark of acute glomerulonephritis. Professional Guide to Diseases, 9th Edition, page 388",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。尿液分析可顯示紅血球存在的證據，顯示腎絲球可能受損；白血球則顯示感染或發炎；蛋白質增加（蛋白尿）可顯示腎元（腎絲球及其相連腎小管）受損。其他實驗室檢測會顯示肌酸酐或尿素血中濃度升高，以及尿液中肌酸酐清除率降低。換言之，急性腎絲球腎炎的特徵為蛋白尿（尿中含蛋白質）、血尿（尿中帶血）、血清肌酸酐升高（顯示腎功能下降）及肌酸酐清除率降低（反映腎絲球過濾功能受損）。這些發現與急性腎絲球腎炎的典型臨床表現一致，例如鏈球菌感染後腎絲球腎炎。血清肌酸酐降低及肌酸酐清除率升高顯示腎功能改善，並非急性腎絲球腎炎的典型表現。顆粒管型較常見於急性腎小管壞死或慢性腎臟病，並非急性腎絲球腎炎的特徵。《疾病專業指南》第9版，第388頁"
