      "number": 410,
      "question_en": "Your patient is waiting on the table to receive an acupuncture treatment. He starts complaining of nausea and chest pain. You notice beads of sweat on his forehead. You know that he does not have a stomach ulcer. He has a history of heart disease but not of heart attacks. You call 911. While waiting for 911 you ask if he is allergic to aspirin and if he is taking any blood thinners. He answers in the negative. He is able to swallow. What do you do next?",
