          "hant": "給他325毫克的阿斯匹靈並配一杯水",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A heart attack is due to blocked blood flow to the muscles of the heart as a consequence of coronary artery disease. It is important to call 911 when a patient has a heart attack. Most patients with a heart attack die within two hours of first experiencing the signs or symptoms. Never try to drive a person with a heart attack to the hospital. While waiting for EMS to arrive, the patient can be helped when showing the early signs of a heart attack by giving them a low dose of aspirin. Aspirin can prevent blood clotting and is effective when given soon after a heart attack. It is important to determine if the patient is responsive and able to chew and swallow. It is also important to determine if the patient has an allergy to aspirin, has a stomach ulcer, and if they are taking a blood thinner. Give the patient either two low doses of 81 mg aspirin tablets or one 325 mg aspirin tablet. Have the patient completely chew the aspirin as this speeds absorption. Do not give combination products which combine aspirin with another ingredient and do not give acetaminophen (Tylenol), ibuprofen (Advil), or naproxen (Aleve). These drugs are not beneficial in a heart attack. If the patient had a history of angina he would be taking nitroglycerin in this situation. First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 37, 39",
      "exp_hant": "心臟病發作是因冠狀動脈疾病導致心肌血流受阻所致。當患者發生心臟病發作時，撥打911十分重要。大多數心臟病發作患者會在首次出現徵象或症狀後兩小時內死亡，切勿嘗試自行開車送心臟病發作患者就醫。在等待緊急醫療救護（EMS）到達期間，若患者出現心臟病發作的早期徵象，可給予低劑量阿斯匹靈提供幫助。阿斯匹靈能防止血液凝結，在心臟病發作後盡快給予效果最佳。重要的是先確認患者是否清醒、能否咀嚼與吞嚥，也須確認患者是否對阿斯匹靈過敏、是否有胃潰瘍，以及是否正在服用抗凝血藥物。給予患者兩顆81毫克低劑量阿斯匹靈藥錠，或一顆325毫克的阿斯匹靈藥錠，讓患者將阿斯匹靈完全咀嚼碎，可加速藥物吸收。切勿給予將阿斯匹靈與其他成分混合的複方藥物，也不要給予乙醯胺酚（Tylenol，泰諾）、布洛芬（Advil，艾德維爾）或萘普生（Aleve，艾力福）。這些藥物對心臟病發作並無助益。若患者有心絞痛病史，此時他應正在服用硝酸甘油。《急救／CPR／AED學員手冊》，紅十字會，2016年，第37、39頁"
