          "key": "D",
          "en": "MDMA, LSD, cocaine",
          "hant": "MDMA、LSD、古柯鹼",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Substance abuse drugs affect the muscles in the eyes that make the pupils dilate (let in more light) or constrict (let in less light). Pupil constriction is called miosis. Pupil dilation is called mydriasis. Pupil constriction and dilation are controlled by the sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous systems. Normally, when the parasympathetic nervous system is activated, it causes pupils to constrict, or narrow. When the sympathetic nervous system is stimulated, pupils dilate. Pupil dilation and constriction controls the amount of light entering the eye. Cocaine, marijuana, amphetamines, ecstasy (MDMA), and LSD dilate the pupil. Opiates such as heroin, codeine, hydrocodone, oxycodone, morphine, demerol, fentanyl, and methadone constrict the pupils. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "濫用藥物會影響控制瞳孔擴張（讓更多光線進入）或收縮（減少光線進入）的眼部肌肉。瞳孔收縮稱為縮瞳，瞳孔擴張稱為散瞳。瞳孔收縮與擴張受交感神經與副交感神經系統控制，一般而言，副交感神經系統受刺激時會使瞳孔收縮（變窄），交感神經系統受刺激時則使瞳孔擴張。瞳孔擴張與收縮可控制進入眼睛的光量。古柯鹼、大麻、安非他命、搖頭丸（MDMA）與LSD會使瞳孔擴張。鴉片類藥物如海洛因、可待因、氫可酮、氧可酮、嗎啡、哌替啶（demerol）、吩坦尼與美沙冬則會使瞳孔收縮。tcmtests.com，2019年2月"
    },
    {
