      ],
      "exp_en": "The normal range of shoulder adduction is greater than or equal to 40 degrees and for shoulder abduction it is greater than or equal to 170 degrees. With the arm on the side of the body with fingertips pointing down the arm is lifted upward toward the ear so that the upper arm faces the side of the head. 170 degrees is the arm almost straight up with the upper arm touching the ear. Any range greater or equal than 170 degrees is considered within normal range for shoulder abduction. For shoulder adduction the arm is placed on the side of the body and raised up until at shoulder height. The patient then moves their whole arm medially toward the center of the body. A range equal or greater than 40 degrees is within normal range. A reading lower than these normal ranges is considered an impairment. American Medical Association Guides to the Evaluation of the Permanent Impairment, Sixth Edition, Robert Rondinelli, page 475",
      "exp_hant": "肩關節內收的正常活動範圍為大於或等於40度，肩關節外展的正常活動範圍為大於或等於170度。手臂置於身體側邊，指尖朝下，將手臂向上舉至耳朵旁，使上臂朝向頭部側面。170度即為手臂幾乎垂直向上舉，上臂觸及耳朵，任何大於或等於170度的活動範圍皆視為肩關節外展的正常範圍。肩關節內收則是將手臂置於身體側邊，抬高至肩膀高度，患者接著將整隻手臂向身體中線方向內移，達到或大於40度的範圍即屬正常範圍，若讀數低於這些正常範圍則視為功能障礙。《美國醫學會永久性功能障礙評估指南》第六版，Robert Rondinelli著，第475頁"
