    {
      "number": 414,
      "question_en": "What are the mechanisms of action for anticoagulant drugs?",
      "question_hant": "抗凝血藥物的作用機轉為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "drug binds with thrombin; drug binds to Factor Xa; drug binds blood platelets, drug activates antithrombin; drug impairs vitamin K synthesis",
          "hant": "藥物與凝血酶結合；藥物與第Xa因子結合；藥物與血小板結合；藥物活化抗凝血酶；藥物抑制維生素K合成",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "drug binds with thrombin; drug binds to Factor Xa; drug binds blood platelets, drug impairs vitamin K synthesis",
          "hant": "藥物與凝血酶結合；藥物與第Xa因子結合；藥物與血小板結合；藥物抑制維生素K合成",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "drug binds blood platelets, drug activates antithrombin; drug impairs vitamin K synthesis",
          "hant": "藥物與血小板結合；藥物活化抗凝血酶；藥物抑制維生素K合成",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "drug binds with thrombin; drug binds to Factor Xa; drug activates antithrombin; drug impairs vitamin K synthesis",
          "hant": "藥物與凝血酶結合；藥物與第Xa因子結合；藥物活化抗凝血酶；藥物抑制維生素K合成",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Drugs that bind blood platelets are called antiplatelet drugs. Antiplatelets and anticoagulants both prevent blood clots but by different actions. Antiplatelets interfere with the binding of platelets (the process that starts blood clot formation). Anticoagulants interfere with clotting proteins in the blood called clotting factors. Clotting factors convert fibrinogen to fibrin to form a mesh network at the site of injury. This traps blood cells along with other components to form a blood clot to prevent blood loss. Anticoagulants function by blocking these clotting factors. Anticoagulants are used to treat deep vein thrombosis, strokes, coronary heart disease, and patients with artificial heart valves. The major anticoagulant classifications are warfarin, heparin, Direct Thrombin Inhibitors, and Factor Xa Inhibitors. Warfarin has an effect on the the clotting factors (II, VII, IX,X) which are dependent on vitamin K for production in the liver. Warfarin is sometimes called a vitamin K antagonist. Brand names for warfarin include Coumadin, Jantoven, and Marevan. Heparin affects the clotting factors thrombin and Factor Xa. Heparin binds to antithrombin III which then increases its blocking action on thrombin and factor Xa. Brand names for heparin include Hep-Pak, Heparin Lock Flush, and Levonox. While heparin indirectly inhibits thrombin by first binding to the enzyme antithrombin III, Direct Thrombin Inhibitors (DTI) produce their anticoagulation by binding directly to thrombin and work independently from antiathrombin. Examples of DTI drugs include agatroban which treats lung and leg blood clots and bivalirudin which treats heart attack patients. Factor Xa Inhibitors also bypass antithrombin III and work directly on the clotting protein Factor Xa. Factor Xa Inhibitors are prescribed to patients to prevent lung or leg blood clots after a major surgery. Side effects of anticoagulants include bleeding, skin rash, easy bruising, and osteoporosis (warfarin). tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。與血小板結合的藥物稱為抗血小板藥物。抗血小板藥物與抗凝血藥物都能預防血栓形成，但作用機轉不同。抗血小板藥物干擾血小板結合（啟動血栓形成的過程），抗凝血藥物則干擾血液中稱為凝血因子的凝血蛋白，凝血因子將纖維蛋白原轉化為纖維蛋白，於損傷部位形成網狀結構，將血球細胞與其他成分困住形成血栓以防止失血。抗凝血藥物則透過阻斷這些凝血因子發揮作用。抗凝血藥物用於治療深部靜脈栓塞、中風、冠心病及裝有人工心臟瓣膜的患者。主要的抗凝血藥物分類為華法林、肝素、直接凝血酶抑制劑及第Xa因子抑制劑。華法林作用於依賴維生素K在肝臟合成的凝血因子（II、VII、IX、X），因此華法林有時被稱為維生素K拮抗劑，其商品名包括Coumadin（可邁丁）、Jantoven與Marevan。肝素作用於凝血酶與第Xa因子這兩種凝血因子，肝素與抗凝血酶III結合，進而增強其對凝血酶與第Xa因子的阻斷作用，其商品名包括Hep-Pak、Heparin Lock Flush與Levonox。肝素是先與抗凝血酶III這種酵素結合，間接抑制凝血酶，而直接凝血酶抑制劑（DTI）則是直接與凝血酶結合以產生抗凝血作用，其作用不依賴抗凝血酶。DTI藥物的例子包括治療肺部與腿部血栓的agatroban，以及治療心臟病發作患者的bivalirudin。第Xa因子抑制劑同樣繞過抗凝血酶III，直接作用於凝血蛋白第Xa因子，此類藥物常用於重大手術後預防患者發生肺部或腿部血栓。抗凝血藥物的副作用包括出血、皮疹、容易瘀傷及骨質疏鬆（華法林）。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
    {
      "number": 415,
      "question_en": "The Vitamin B12 and Folic Acid blood tests assess Vitamin B12 deficiency and Folic Acid deficiency which are associated with elevated levels of",
      "question_hant": "維生素B12與葉酸血液檢測用於評估維生素B12缺乏症與葉酸缺乏症，這兩者與下列何者的濃度升高有關？",
