      "exp_en": "Homocysteine (HCY) is an amino acid that the body generates, as a byproduct of consuming meat. Elevated blood levels of homocysteine (HCY) (&gt;10 micromoles/liter) may be associated with atherosclerosis, increased risk of cardiovascular disease, strokes, and incomplete blood clot formation. Vitamin B12 and folic acid break down homocysteine in the body. An insufficient intake of these vitamins can lead to a build up of homocysteine (HCY). Doctors order a homocysteine test (also called Plasma Total Homocysteine) to assess homocysteine blood levels. Related tests include Vitamin B12 and Folate tests, Cardiac Risk Assessment, MTHFR, and Intrinsic Factor Antibody. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 283-285; 4th Edition, page 321",
      "exp_hant": "同半胱胺酸（HCY）是一種身體代謝肉類時所產生的胺基酸副產品。血中同半胱胺酸（HCY）濃度升高（大於10微莫耳／公升）可能與動脈粥狀硬化、心血管疾病風險增加、中風及血栓形成不完全有關。維生素B12與葉酸能分解體內的同半胱胺酸，若這些維生素攝取不足，可能導致同半胱胺酸（HCY）累積。醫師會安排同半胱胺酸檢測（也稱血漿總同半胱胺酸檢測），以評估血中同半胱胺酸濃度。相關檢測包括維生素B12與葉酸檢測、心臟風險評估、MTHFR基因檢測及內因子抗體檢測。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢測手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第283-285頁；第4版，第321頁"
