        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Guidelines to follow: 1) The highest priority is the health and well being of the patient; 2) Respect the patient's right to self-determination; 3) Unless licensed to do so, do not diagnose or treat physical or mental disorders; 4) Encourage but do not pressure the patient towards any action or beliefs; 5) When appropriate, consult with other professionals for the benefit of the patient; 6) Check for personal biases, boundaries and professional limitations. If the acupuncturist continues to provide treatment, there is a high probability of more or worsening flashbacks and dissociations. This possibility puts into play the issue of whether it is in the interest of the patient that they continue with you except in the context of psychotherapy with a PTSD specialist. While it is the choice of the patient to seek psychotherapy, the acupuncturist also has the responsibility to no longer offer further acupuncture treatment. Their mental health issues could worsen if not professionally treated. The highest priority of the practitioner is the health and well being of the patient. PP It would be appropriate to direct the patient towards mental health services as the best course for them. Emphasize that they are not being rejected and not blamed being unable to afford both services. Ethics Handbook for Energy Healing Practitioners, Kindle Edition, Feinstein, page 107",
      "exp_hant": "應遵循的指導原則：1）最優先考量是患者的健康與福祉；2）尊重患者的自我決定權；3）除非取得執照，否則不應診斷或治療生理或心理疾病；4）鼓勵但不強迫患者採取任何行動或信念；5）於適當時機為患者利益諮詢其他專業人士；6）檢視自身的偏見、界線與專業限制。若針灸師持續提供治療，出現更多或更嚴重閃回及解離的可能性極高，這使得除非搭配創傷後壓力症候群（PTSD）專家的心理治療，否則是否應繼續由您治療便成為疑問。雖然是否尋求心理治療是患者的選擇，但針灸師也有責任不再提供進一步的針灸治療，因為若未經專業治療，其心理健康問題可能惡化。執業者的最優先考量是患者的健康與福祉，適當的做法是引導患者尋求心理健康服務，並強調這對她而言是最佳選擇，同時要向她表明她並未被拒絕或因無法同時負擔兩種服務而受到責備。《能量療癒執業者倫理手冊》Kindle版，Feinstein著，第107頁"
    },
