      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Bone density tests use X-rays to measure how much calcium (plus other bone minerals) is in a bone segment (spine, hip and forearm). Bone density testing helps to determine the risk of fractures and helps to confirm osteoporosis and follow the result of treatment for osteoporosis. The higher the bone mineral content, the more dense the bones are. BMD testing is recommended for all women over the age of 65. It is also recommended for postmenopausal women under 65 years who have risk factors for developing osteoporosis (history of fractures, low body weight, cigarette smoking, family history of fractures). Bone density tests are not the same as bone scans. Bone scans are used to discover fractures, bone infections, or cancer. Hyperparathyroidism occurs when the parathyroid glands produce too much parathyroid hormone (PTH). Secondary hyperparathyroidism occurs when there is an underlying condition that causes calcium levels to be abnormally low. Most cases of secondary hyperparathyroidism are due to chronic kidney failure that results in low vitamin D and calcium levels. With secondary hyperparathyroidism there can be skeletal abnormalities, such as fractures, swollen joints, and bone deformities. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition,Pagana, page 969-973; 4th Edition page 1055-1060",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。骨質密度檢測利用X光測量骨段（脊椎、髖部及前臂）中鈣質（及其他骨骼礦物質）的含量。骨質密度檢測有助於判斷骨折風險，並協助確診骨質疏鬆症及追蹤骨質疏鬆症的治療結果。骨礦物質含量越高，骨骼越緻密。BMD檢測建議所有65歲以上女性接受，也建議有骨質疏鬆症危險因子（骨折病史、體重過輕、吸菸、骨折家族史）的65歲以下停經後女性接受。骨質密度檢測與骨掃描不同，骨掃描用於發現骨折、骨感染或癌症。副甲狀腺功能亢進是指副甲狀腺分泌過多副甲狀腺素（PTH）。次發性副甲狀腺功能亢進發生於有潛在疾病導致鈣濃度異常偏低時，大多數次發性副甲狀腺功能亢進病例是由慢性腎衰竭所致，導致維生素D與鈣濃度偏低。次發性副甲狀腺功能亢進可能出現骨骼異常，如骨折、關節腫脹及骨骼變形。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢測手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第969-973頁；第4版，第1055-1060頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 418,
      "question_en": "Which enzyme in the endometrium inhibits the menstrual blood from clotting?",
      "question_hant": "子宮內膜中哪種酵素可抑制經血凝結？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
