      "exp_en": "Ascaris is roundworm. Strongyloides is tapeworm. Giardia is a parasite that lives in the intestines. Cryptosporidium is a microscopic parasite which causes diarrheal disease known as cryptosporidiosis. Cryptosporidiosis is also known as crypto. A person can become infected with cryptosporidium by touching something which has come in contact with contaminated feces. For healthy people, a cryptosporidium infection results in watery diarrhea which resolves within one week or two. Cryptosporidium is most commonly detected in HIV-positive patients with diarrhea. Cryptosporidiosis is a common cause of self-limited gastroenteritis in immunocompetent individuals. Mortality occurs in patients with CD4 counts below 180 cells/mm3. Above this level, the patient spontaneously recovers. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 823; 4th Edition page 896",
      "exp_hant": "蛔蟲（Ascaris）是圓蟲。糞線蟲（Strongyloides）是絛蟲。梨形鞭毛蟲（Giardia）是一種寄生在腸道中的寄生蟲。隱孢子蟲（Cryptosporidium）是一種顯微鏡下可見的寄生蟲，會引起稱為隱孢子蟲病的腹瀉性疾病，隱孢子蟲病也稱為「crypto」。人可能因接觸曾接觸受污染糞便的物品而感染隱孢子蟲。對健康人而言，感染隱孢子蟲會導致水樣腹瀉，通常在一到兩週內痊癒。隱孢子蟲最常見於伴有腹瀉的HIV陽性患者身上。隱孢子蟲病是免疫功能正常者常見的自限性腸胃炎病因，CD4計數低於180 cells/mm3的患者可能出現死亡，高於此數值則患者可自行痊癒。《Mosby診斷與實驗室檢測手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第823頁；第4版，第896頁"
