    {
      "number": 421,
      "question_en": "A 75 year-old male had his annual checkup. He is generally healthy with his hypertension and coronary disease under control. He denies dyspnea on exertion, chest pain, palpitations, dizziness, headache nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. He does complain of a little urinary hesitancy and difficulty starting. He denies pain during urination and any past history of urinary tract infections. He has regular bowel movements, occasionally using prune juice or extra fiber. He denies any allergies. He is sexually active with his wife and occasionally takes ED medication. He has a history of hypertension, erectile dysfunction, and dyslipidemia. His medications include Lipitor, the diuretic HCTZ, and Cialis. Digital rectal examination shows no abnormalities. The urinalysis results are all within normal range. The PSA (prostate-specific antigen) value is at 10 ng/mL, a two fold increase since the last exam. What is the most likely diagnosis for his urinary problem?",
      "question_hant": "一名75歲男性接受年度健康檢查。他整體健康狀況良好，高血壓與冠心病皆控制良好。他否認活動性呼吸困難、胸痛、心悸、頭暈、頭痛、噁心、嘔吐及腹瀉。他主訴稍有排尿猶豫及起始排尿困難。他否認排尿疼痛及過去有泌尿道感染病史。他排便規律，偶爾使用洋李汁或額外纖維。他否認任何過敏。他與妻子性生活正常，偶爾服用勃起功能障礙藥物。他有高血壓、勃起功能障礙及血脂異常病史。他的用藥包括立普妥（Lipitor）、利尿劑HCTZ及犀利士（Cialis）。肛門指診無異常。尿液分析結果皆在正常範圍。PSA（攝護腺特異抗原）數值為10 ng/mL，較上次檢查增加兩倍。他泌尿問題最可能的診斷為何？",
