      "exp_en": "What stands out the most in this case is the rapidly rising PSA values over the past year. Normal PSA is between 0 and 4.0 ng/mL. Values that are greater than 4 require follow up depending on age, BMI, and family history. The rapidly rising PSA levels make prostate cancer a strong possibility. Sometimes a prostate tumor is not detectable via a DRE because of it location. The next step for this patient is a referral to confirm the diagnosis with a transrectal ultrasound (TRUS) and a guided biopsy of the prostate gland. PSA levels can also be the result of BPH (benign prostatic hypertrophy). However, the DRE (digital rectal exam) revealed a normal sized prostate. Symptoms of BPH include an enlarged prostate, difficult to start urination, weak stream, stopping and restarting of the stream, and dribbles at the end. A UTI (urinary tract infection) usually caused by a bacterial infection. Symptoms most often include fever and flank tenderness. Other symptoms may include nausea, burning with urination, and frequent urination. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 235-238",
      "exp_hant": "本病例中最突出的是過去一年PSA值快速上升。正常PSA介於0至4.0 ng/mL之間。若數值大於4，需依年齡、BMI及家族史進行追蹤。PSA快速上升使攝護腺癌成為高度可能的診斷。有時攝護腺腫瘤因位置關係，肛門指診無法偵測到。此患者下一步應轉診以經直腸超音波（TRUS）及引導式攝護腺切片確診。PSA升高也可能是良性攝護腺增生（BPH）所致，然而肛門指診（DRE）顯示攝護腺大小正常。BPH的症狀包括攝護腺腫大、排尿起始困難、尿流微弱、排尿中斷再起及滴尿。泌尿道感染（UTI）通常由細菌感染引起，最常見症狀為發燒及腰側壓痛，其他症狀可能包括噁心、排尿灼熱感及頻尿。《Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner》，Leslie Neal-Boylan，2011年，第235-238頁"
