      "exp_en": "The viral load is a blood test which measures the amount of active HIV (human immunodeficiency virus) in the blood. The higher the value of the viral load test the more active HIV is present. The viral load test is first measured when there is a diagnosis of an HIV infection. This initial measurement will serve as the baseline reading. Future viral load measurements will be compared with the baseline. The viral load measurement test performed to monitor changes in the HIV infection, to help guide what treatment to give, and to monitor the effect of treatment. Zidovudine (also known as AZT) is used together with other medicines for the treatment of human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection. HIV is the virus that causes acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS). AZT is also used to help prevent pregnant women who have HIV from passing the virus to their babies during pregnancy and at birth. AZT will not cure or prevent HIV infection or AIDS, however, it helps keep HIV from reproducing and appears to slow down the destruction of the immune system. AZT is often used in combination with with other antiretroviral such as 3TC ((lamivudine) and ABC (abacavir). tcmtests.com, May 2020",
      "exp_hant": "病毒量是一項血液檢測，用於測量血液中活性HIV（人類免疫缺乏病毒）的數量。病毒量檢測值越高，代表體內活性HIV越多。首次測量病毒量是在診斷出HIV感染時進行，此初次測量將作為基準值，之後的病毒量測量會與此基準值比較。病毒量測量用於監測HIV感染的變化、協助指導治療方向，以及監測治療效果。齊多夫定（又稱AZT）與其他藥物併用，用於治療人類免疫缺乏病毒（HIV）感染。HIV是造成後天免疫缺乏症候群（AIDS）的病毒。AZT也用於協助防止感染HIV的孕婦於懷孕及生產過程中將病毒傳染給嬰兒。AZT不能治癒或預防HIV感染或AIDS，但它有助於阻止HIV複製，並似乎能減緩免疫系統的破壞。AZT通常與其他抗反轉錄病毒藥物如3TC（拉米夫定）及ABC（abacavir，阿巴卡韋）併用。tcmtests.com，2020年5月"
