    {
      "number": 426,
      "question_en": "Amanda is a 60 year-old librarian. She reports that she has had the flu for the last two weeks and that it has gone to the front of her chest where she feels a heavy, tight feeling in her heart. She does not have a history of any heart symptoms, no angina, no trouble breathing when lying flat but the chest pain increases. She does not have exertional dyspnea. She is not a smoker, nor overweight, and has no history of diabetes. She does not have varicose veins or deep venous problems. She also reports that she has vomited several times during the past few days and cannot keep anything in her stomach. She has swollen ankles. Listening to her lungs you can hear rales at the bases bilaterally, and a strange scraping sound over her chest that blocks out some of the normal heart sounds. Her radial and femoral pulses decrease with respirations. What is your presumptive diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "Amanda是一名60歲的圖書館員。她主訴過去兩週患有流感，且症狀已蔓延至前胸，感覺心臟部位有沉重、緊繃感。她沒有任何心臟症狀病史，無心絞痛，平躺時無呼吸困難，但胸痛加劇。她沒有運動性呼吸困難。她不吸菸、不過重，也無糖尿病病史。她沒有靜脈曲張或深部靜脈問題。她也主訴過去幾天嘔吐數次，無法留住任何食物。她的腳踝腫脹。聽診雙側肺底可聞及爆裂音，胸部則有一種奇怪的摩擦音，蓋過部分正常心音。她的橈動脈及股動脈脈搏隨呼吸而減弱。你初步診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
