      "exp_en": "The red flag is elbow swelling and pain with diminished radial pulse and/or hand numbness after a trauma. Supracondylar fracture is assumed until proven otherwise. The key sign for this fracture is extreme tenderness and swelling over the fracture. Fractures are always tender. It should be determined if there are any complications in the nerves or blood vessels due to the fracture. If so, there will be a diminished radial pulse if there is pressure on the brachial artery or abnormal sensation if there is a compression on the nerves. This is an urgent situation and patient should be transported immediately to the emergency room. 911 would be called only if there is cardiopulmonary compromise. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 111-112",
      "exp_hant": "紅旗警示為外傷後肘部腫脹疼痛，伴隨橈動脈脈搏減弱及／或手部麻木。在排除其他可能性之前，應假定為髁上骨折。此骨折的關鍵徵象為骨折處極度壓痛及腫脹，骨折處必定有壓痛。應確認骨折是否對神經或血管造成併發症，若肱動脈受壓則橈動脈脈搏會減弱，若神經受壓則感覺會異常。此為緊急情況，病患應立即轉送急診室。只有在出現心肺功能危及的情況下才需撥打911。《An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第111-112頁"
