      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Cortisol, a steroid hormone, is produced from cholesterol in the two adrenal glands. Cortisol is released in response to stress and its primary functions are to increase blood sugar, suppress the immune system, and aid with fat, protein, and carbohydrate metabolism. The hypothalamus secretes CRH (corticotropin-releasing hormone) which triggers the pituitary to release ACTH (adrenocorticotropic hormone) into the blood and then travels to the adrenal glands. Cortisol can weaken the immune system by blocking the proliferation of T-cells. Cortisol counteracts insulin and contributes to hyperglycemia by inhibiting the utilization of glucose (insulin resistance). Cortisol counteracts insulin, assesses adrenal function, is released in response to stress, affects blood levels of glucose, influences carbohydrate, protein, and fat metabolism, and suppresses the immune systam. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 888-890; 4th Edition page 965-967",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且準確的答案。皮質醇是一種類固醇激素，由兩側腎上腺以膽固醇為原料製造。皮質醇於壓力下釋放，其主要功能為升高血糖、抑制免疫系統，並協助脂肪、蛋白質及碳水化合物的代謝。下視丘分泌CRH（促腎上腺皮質激素釋放激素），刺激腦下垂體釋放ACTH（促腎上腺皮質激素）進入血液，再作用於腎上腺。皮質醇可藉由阻斷T細胞增殖而削弱免疫系統。皮質醇會拮抗胰島素，並透過抑制葡萄糖利用（胰島素阻抗）而導致高血糖。皮質醇拮抗胰島素、評估腎上腺功能、於壓力下釋放、影響血糖濃度、影響碳水化合物、蛋白質及脂肪代謝，並抑制免疫系統。《Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests》，第7版，Pagana著，第888-890頁；第4版，第965-967頁"
