        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Baroreceptors or baroceptors are sensors located in the blood vessels. They are a type of mechanoreceptor that detects the pressure of blood flowing in the vessels and can send messages to the central nervous system to increase or decrease total peripheral resistance and cardiac output. Baroreceptors detect the amount of stretch of the blood vessel walls, and send the signal to the nervous system in response to this stretch. If blood pressure falls, such as in orthostatic hypotension, baroreceptor firing rate decreases and baroreceptor reflexes act to help restore blood pressure by increasing heart rate. Signals from the carotid baroreceptors are sent via the glossopharyngeal nerve (cranial nerve IX). Signals from the aortic baroreceptors travel through the vagus nerve (cranial nerve X).",
      "exp_hant": "壓力感受器（baroreceptors）是位於血管中的感受器，屬於機械受器的一種，可偵測血管內血流的壓力，並可將訊息傳送至中樞神經系統，以增加或減少全身周邊阻力及心輸出量。壓力感受器偵測血管壁的伸展程度，並將此伸展訊號傳送至神經系統。若血壓下降，例如姿勢性低血壓，壓力感受器的放電頻率會降低，壓力感受器反射則會透過增加心跳速率協助恢復血壓。來自頸動脈壓力感受器的訊號經由舌咽神經（第九對腦神經）傳送，來自主動脈壓力感受器的訊號則經由迷走神經（第十對腦神經）傳送。"
    },
