          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Crepitus is a grating sound or sensation produced by friction between bone and cartilage. Bony bumps on the finger joint closest to the fingernail are called Heberden's nodes while bony bumps on the middle finger joint are called Bouchard's nodes. The main difference between osteoarthritis (OA) and rheumatoid arthritis (RA) is the causative factor behind the joint pain. OA is caused by mechanical wear and tear while RA is an auto-immune disease where the immune system attacks the joints. RA can begin at any age while OA usually begins later in life. RA has a rapid speed of onset spanning weeks or months while OA has a slow onset spanning years. RA has swollen-stiff-painful joints while OA has joint pain with very little swelling. RA affects small and large joints on both sides of the body (symmetrical) while OA the joint pain is usually on one side of the body. In RA morning stiffness can last longer than one hour while in OA stiffness lasts less than one hour and can return later on the day. RA has systemic symptoms such as frequent fatigue and a general feeling of being sick while in OA whole body symptoms are absent.",
      "exp_hant": "摩擦音是骨骼與軟骨摩擦所產生的一種摩擦聲響或感覺。靠近指甲的手指關節上的骨性凸起稱為海伯登結節（Heberden's nodes），中段手指關節上的骨性凸起則稱為布夏爾結節（Bouchard's nodes）。骨關節炎（OA）與類風濕性關節炎（RA）的主要差異在於引發關節疼痛的病因不同。OA是由機械性磨損所致，而RA則是免疫系統攻擊關節的自體免疫疾病。RA可於任何年齡發病，而OA通常於較晚的人生階段才開始出現。RA的發病速度快，僅需數週或數月，而OA的發病則緩慢，需歷經數年。RA的關節腫脹、僵硬且疼痛，而OA的關節疼痛則腫脹輕微。RA會對稱性地影響身體兩側的大小關節，而OA的關節疼痛通常僅侷限於身體一側。RA的晨僵可持續超過一小時，而OA的僵硬則持續不到一小時，且可能於當天稍晚再度出現。RA有全身性症狀，如經常性疲勞及整體不適感，而OA則無全身性症狀。"
