      "exp_en": "When blood vessels constrict and narrow, the heart must work harder to pump blood throughout the body resulting in high blood pressure. The blood vessels are affected by the angiotensin-converting enzymes (ACE). ACE converts Angiotensin I into Angiotensin II, which is a powerful vasoconstrictor. ACE inhibitors block the angiotensin-converting enzymes (ACE) from constricting the blood vessels. As the blood vessels relax and vasodilate, the heart can more easily pump the blood thereby decreasing pressure.",
      "exp_hant": "當血管收縮變窄時，心臟必須更用力幫浦血液至全身，導致高血壓。血管受到血管收縮素轉換酶（ACE）的影響。ACE會將血管收縮素I轉換為血管收縮素II，後者是一種強效的血管收縮劑。ACE抑制劑會阻斷血管收縮素轉換酶（ACE），使其無法收縮血管。當血管放鬆並擴張時，心臟便能更輕鬆地幫浦血液，進而降低血壓。"
