      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate answer. Oral stimulants such as bisacodyl (Dulcolax) and senna (Senokot) trigger rhythmic contractions of intestinal muscles to eliminate stool. Oral osmotics such as magnesium hydroxide (Phillips Milk of Magnesia) and polyethylene glycol (Miralax) draw water into the colon to allow easier passage of stool. Oral stool softeners such as docusate (Colace, Surfak) add moisture to stool to allow strain-free bowel movements. Bulk formers such as wheat dextrin (Benefiber), psyllium husk powder (Metamucil), and methylcellulose fiber (Citrucel) absorb water to form soft, bulky stool, prompting normal contraction of intestinal muscles.",
      "exp_hant": "這是最準確的答案。口服刺激劑，如比沙可啶（bisacodyl，Dulcolax）及番瀉葉（senna，Senokot），可觸發腸道肌肉的節律性收縮以排出糞便。口服滲透性瀉劑，如氫氧化鎂（磷酸鎂乳，Phillips Milk of Magnesia）及聚乙二醇（Miralax），可將水分引入結腸以使糞便更易排出。口服軟便劑，如多庫酯（docusate，Colace、Surfak），可為糞便增加水分，使排便時無需用力。膨鬆劑，如小麥糊精（Benefiber）、洋車前子殼粉（Metamucil）及甲基纖維素纖維（Citrucel），可吸收水分形成柔軟蓬鬆的糞便，促進腸道肌肉正常收縮。"
