      "exp_en": "Carbohydrate is stored as glycogen in both muscles and the liver. Glycogen is the first line of defense when blood glucose concentration falls. When we eat carbohydrates, the body converts them into a form of sugar called glucose that can be used for energy. Excess glucose, in turn, is converted to glycogen, a form of sugar that is stored by the liver and the muscles.Muscle glycogen is a fuel reserve and is degraded to glucose for energy for the muscles when needed. During fasting, liver glycogen is degraded to help maintain blood glucose levels. ATP transports chemical energy within cells for metabolism. Glycogen can be used to make ATP.",
      "exp_hant": "碳水化合物在肌肉及肝臟中皆以肝醣形式儲存。肝醣是血糖濃度下降時人體的第一道防線。當我們攝取碳水化合物時，人體會將其轉化為一種可供能量使用的糖，稱為葡萄糖。多餘的葡萄糖則會轉化為肝醣，這是一種由肝臟及肌肉儲存的糖類形式。肌肉肝醣是燃料儲備，於需要時分解為葡萄糖以供肌肉能量使用。禁食期間，肝臟肝醣會被分解以協助維持血糖濃度。ATP在細胞內運送化學能以供代謝使用，肝醣可用於製造ATP。"
