          "en": "a dull sound",
          "hant": "實音",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "a hyper-resonant sound",
          "hant": "過度共鳴音",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In percussing the chest, the basic sounds listened for is whether the sound is solid or hollow. However, a skilled practitioner can distinguish between five different sounds that result from percussing the chest. In pneumothorax, when the chest is percussed it will sound either hyper-resonant somewhat like a drum or with a high pitched bell-like sound called tympany due to air entering the pleural space (area around the lungs) when the lung collapses. The resonant sound is the normal sound when percussing the chest or abdomen. If a tympanic sound is elicited in the abdomen it can indicate trapped air bubbles. A flat sound is like the sound when percussing the muscle of the thigh. When the flat sound occurs on the chest it indicates pleural effusion in which the fluid in the lungs cushions the percussion. A dull sound is heard when the liver is percussed. The dull sound is more solid than the soft and flat sound. The dull sound can be elicited over the area of lobar pneumonia, the area filled with fluids, or percussing the base of the lungs when there is congestive heart failure.",
      "exp_hant": "叩診胸部時，最基本要聽的是聲音為實心還是空洞。然而，熟練的醫療人員可分辨出叩診胸部所產生的五種不同聲音。在氣胸時，叩診胸部會呈現過度共鳴音，類似鼓聲，或呈現高音調如鐘聲的鼓音（tympany），這是由於肺部塌陷時空氣進入胸膜腔（肺周圍區域）所致。共鳴音是叩診胸部或腹部時的正常音，若在腹部叩出鼓音，則可能提示有氣體積聚。實音類似叩診大腿肌肉時的聲音，若胸部出現實音，則提示有肋膜積液，肺部積液會緩衝叩診聲。濁音是叩診肝臟時所聽到的聲音，濁音比柔和的實音更為堅實。大葉性肺炎、液體填滿的區域，或充血性心衰竭時叩診肺底，皆可能叩出濁音。"
    },
