      "number": 463,
      "question_en": "A 55 year-old male comes to your office with a history of migraines and recent history of TIA's and has been put on Warfarin by his physician last month. During a visit to the UK one year ago, he saw an herbalist that put him on the following custom tincture formula: equal parts - Gingko, Feverfew, St. John's Wort and Green Tea, 1 teaspoon TID. While he took the formula for one year, he has stopped the combination since starting Warfarin. What herb has the strongest warning against combining with Warfarin as it can increase risk overall risk of bleeding?",
      "question_hant": "一名55歲男性因偏頭痛病史及近期短暫性腦缺血發作（TIA）病史前來就診，上個月起由其醫師開立華法林（Warfarin）治療。一年前他到英國旅遊時，曾看過一位草藥師，被開立以下等量成分的複方酊劑：銀杏、小白菊、聖約翰草及綠茶，每日三次各一茶匙。雖然他服用此複方一年，但自開始服用華法林後便已停用。哪一種草藥與華法林併用時警告最為強烈，因其可能增加整體出血風險？",
      "image": null,
