          "hant": "銀杏",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Gingko is a known inhibitor of platelet aggregation in vitro and ex vivo, therefore it is theorized to increase overall risk of bleeding. One case report of intracranial hemorrhage found concurrent use in the preceding 2 months. When both warfarin and gingko were removed, anti-coagulation reversed. Similarly, a case report of death by intracerebral bleed with the combination of Ibuprofen and gingko was thought to be from combined anti-platelet effects. Data is mixed however, preclinical trials in humans have not found increased bleeding times. Due to the potential seriousness of the additive effect of Gingko, it is still contraindicated for use with warfarin. Feverfew has demonstrated antiaggregatory effects in vitro, but there are no preclinical studies or clinical reports confirming the interaction. In one small study, 10 patients who had taken Feverfew for 3-8 years showed no difference in aggregation response than those who had not taken Feverfew in 6 mos. St. John's Wort may increase clearance of warfarin, requiring dose adjustment and increased monitoring of INR. There is an absence of reliable case reports on the interaction nor clear science on the mechanism of the interaction in the literature. Green tea has shown some antiaggregatory activity in vitro, but human studies have contradicted this effect. There is one case study of a patient drinking 1 gallon of green tea daily that had unstable INR's. The mechanism of this interaction is controversial. Vigilance is necessary in those who drink more than half gallon of tea daily. There is no interaction between cranberry and warfarin.",
      "exp_hant": "銀杏已知在體外及活體外皆能抑制血小板聚集，因此理論上會增加整體出血風險。曾有一篇病例報告顯示，前兩個月併用華法林與銀杏後發生顱內出血，當停用華法林與銀杏後，抗凝作用即逆轉。同樣地，一篇布洛芬（Ibuprofen）與銀杏併用導致腦內出血死亡的病例報告，被認為是抗血小板作用相加所致。然而數據並不一致，人體臨床前試驗並未發現出血時間增加。由於銀杏加成效應可能造成的嚴重後果，目前仍將其列為與華法林併用的禁忌。小白菊在體外實驗中顯示出抗凝血聚集作用，但並無臨床前研究或臨床報告證實此交互作用。在一項小型研究中，10名服用小白菊3至8年的病患，其凝血聚集反應與6個月內未服用小白菊者相比並無差異。聖約翰草可能增加華法林的清除率，因此需要調整劑量並加強國際標準化比值（INR）監測，但目前文獻中缺乏可靠的病例報告，其交互作用機轉亦不明確。綠茶在體外實驗中顯示出一定的抗凝血聚集活性，但人體研究結果與此相矛盾。曾有一篇病例報告顯示，一名每日飲用一加侖綠茶的病患出現不穩定的INR值，此交互作用的機轉仍存在爭議。每日飲用超過半加侖茶者需保持警覺。蔓越莓與華法林之間則無交互作用。"
