      "exp_en": "LDL cholesterol levels should be less than 100 mg/dL. Levels of 100 to 129 mg/dL are acceptable for people with no health issues but may be of more concern for those with heart disease or heart disease risk factors. A reading of 130 to 159 mg/dL is borderline high and 160 to 189 mg/dL is high. A reading of 190 mg/dL or higher is considered very high. HDL levels should be kept higher. A reading of less than 40 mg/dL is considered a major risk factor for heart disease. A reading from 41 mg/dL to 59 mg/dL is considered borderline low. The optimal reading for HDL levels is of 60 mg/dL or higher. There are two types of CHD risk factors. Those that can be controlled and those that cannot. Controllable risk factors include: high blood cholesterol and triglyceride levels, hypertension, diabetes and prediabetes, obesity, smoking, lack of physical activity, poor diet, alcohol, and stress. Risk factors that cannot be controlled are age, gender, and family history of CHD.",
      "exp_hant": "LDL膽固醇濃度應小於100 mg/dL，100至129 mg/dL對無其他健康問題者而言屬可接受範圍，但對已有心臟病或心臟病風險因子者則需更加留意。130至159 mg/dL屬邊緣性偏高，160至189 mg/dL屬偏高，190 mg/dL或以上則視為極高。HDL濃度則應維持較高，小於40 mg/dL被視為心臟病的重大風險因子，41至59 mg/dL屬邊緣性偏低，60 mg/dL或以上為理想數值。冠心病（CHD）風險因子可分為兩類，可控制及不可控制。可控制的風險因子包括：高血膽固醇及三酸甘油酯濃度、高血壓、糖尿病及糖尿病前期、肥胖、吸菸、缺乏身體活動、飲食不良、飲酒及壓力。不可控制的風險因子則包括年齡、性別及冠心病家族史。"
