          "en": "the right anterior superior iliac spine begins to move",
          "hant": "右側髂前上棘開始移動時",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The normal range of motion for hip flexion is more than 110 degrees. The procedure for assessing the right hip is for the patient to lie supine with legs extended. The goniometer is placed at the right hip. The pelvis is locked into a neutral position by having the patient flex the left hip and grasping the left knee until the lumbar spine is flat. The patient then flexes the right hip bringing the bent knee towards the chest. When the right anterior superior iliac spine of the pelvis moves the angle is recorded. The same procedure applies in reverse in assessing the left hip. Anything less than 110 degress is considered an impairment. The severity of impairment is graded by the percentage from which the ROM deviates from normal readings. 60-90% of the normal ROM is considered a mild impairment, 30-60% of normal motion is considered a moderate impairment, less than 30% of normal motion is considered a severe impairment, and joint ankylosis (frozen) is considered a very severe impairment.",
      "exp_hant": "髖屈曲的正常活動範圍為超過110度。評估右髖的程序為病患平躺、雙腿伸直，量角器置於右髖處。透過讓病患屈曲左髖並抓住左膝，直到腰椎平貼於檢查台，將骨盆固定於中立位置。接著病患屈曲右髖，將彎曲的膝蓋帶向胸部，當骨盆的右側髂前上棘開始移動時，記錄此角度。評估左髖時程序相反。低於110度即視為功能障礙，功能障礙的嚴重程度依ROM偏離正常讀數的百分比分級：正常ROM的60-90%為輕度障礙，30-60%為中度障礙，低於30%為重度障礙，關節僵直（凍結）則為極重度障礙。"
