      "number": 471,
      "question_en": "Ben is a 43 year-old tax accountant. He lives with his male partner in Venice, California. Ben complains of pain during swallowing. He has a past history of sore throats and has been treated for allergies which became worse when he moved to California saying that everything smells moldy and damp to him. Last week he coughed a few spots of blood. He enjoys smoking a pipe while working as it relaxes him. When he played baseball for about 10 years as a shortstop he chewed tobacco. He reports that he has unintentionally lost 10 pounds over the past three months and attributes it to his regular workouts. Which diagnostic tests help to establish the diagnosis?",
