      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. He has possible throat cancer. The AST/ALT ratio is used to diagnose liver problems. Throat cancer refers to cancerous tumors that develop in the pharynx (throat) or larynx (voice box) or in the tonsils. Symptoms include sore throat, cough (sometimes with blood), voice changes, difficulty swallowing, a lump or sore that does not heal, and weight loss. His tobacco chewing is the causative factor. An ENT exam will probably reveal lesions in the pharynx. Laryngoscopy is an examination that allows the examination of the pharynx throat and larynx with scope (laryngoscope). Sample tissues can be removed to perform a biopsy (tissue removed from a living body to discover the presence, cause, or extent of a disease). Less commonly used is an MRI scan to examine throat cancer. MRIs are useful in determining whether the cancer has spread.",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且準確的答案。他可能患有喉癌。AST/ALT比值用於診斷肝臟問題。喉癌是指發生於咽（喉嚨）或喉（發聲器官）或扁桃腺中的癌性腫瘤。症狀包括喉嚨痛、咳嗽（有時帶血）、聲音改變、吞嚥困難、無法癒合的腫塊或潰瘍，以及體重減輕。他嚼菸草的習慣是致病因素。耳鼻喉科檢查很可能會發現咽部病灶。喉鏡檢查是一種以內視鏡（喉鏡）檢查咽喉及喉部的檢查方式，可取樣組織進行切片（自活體取出組織以確認疾病的存在、原因或範圍）。較少使用的是以MRI掃描檢查喉癌，MRI有助於判斷癌症是否已擴散。"
