      "exp_en": "The option that is most helpful to the patient is to treat the energetic foundation of her breathing problem while working in conjunction with her psychiatrist to manage tapering off her SSRI. COPD is a medical diagnosis with an ICD-10-CM Diagnosis Code of J44.9. Unless licensed to do so, acupuncturists cannot treat medical diseases as it is outside the scope of practice. However, the acupuncturist can say to the patient that they can treat the yin and yang energetic configuration associated with her breathing problem. The considerations are: 1) the mental health and addiction issues are severe enough that they are outside of the scope of practice; 2) the acupuncturist can energetically assist the patient to better cope with their mental health issues; 3) the acupuncturist can tell the patient that they cannot treat diseases but can treat the energetic system. The relevant guidelines to follow: 1) the acupuncturist only treats based on their training and licensing; 2) unless licensed to do so, an acupuncturist does not diagnose or treat medical diseases; 3) the acupuncturist is open to providing TCM to all patients who can benefit; 4) the acupuncturist does not exaggerate or overstate the effectiveness of TCM; 5) the acupuncturist has a discussion with the patient to discover if they have any unrealistic expectations regarding TCM; 6) the acupuncturist has the right to refuse or accept any patient; 7) the acupuncturist can refer or consult and cooperate with other professionals.",
      "exp_hant": "對病患最有幫助的選項，是治療其呼吸問題的能量根本，同時與其精神科醫師合作，協助逐步減量停用SSRI。COPD是有ICD-10-CM診斷代碼J44.9的醫療診斷。除非取得執照，否則針灸師不得治療醫學疾病，因其超出執業範圍。然而，針灸師可以向病患說明，他們能治療與其呼吸問題相關的陰陽能量配置。考量因素包括：1）心理健康及成癮問題嚴重程度已超出執業範圍；2）針灸師可從能量層面協助病患更妥善地因應其心理健康問題；3）針灸師可告知病患，自己無法治療疾病，但可治療其能量系統。應遵循的相關準則為：1）針灸師僅依其所受訓練及執照範圍進行治療；2）除非取得執照，否則針灸師不對醫學疾病進行診斷或治療；3）針灸師願意為所有能從中醫獲益的病患提供服務；4）針灸師不誇大或過度陳述中醫的療效；5）針灸師會與病患討論，確認其對中醫是否存有不切實際的期望；6）針灸師有權接受或拒絕任何病患；7）針灸師可轉診或諮詢並與其他專業人員合作。"
