      "exp_en": "The central nervous system (CNS) has two types of tissue: grey matter and white matter. Grey matter contains the cell bodies, dendrites and axon terminals of the neurons. This is where all of the synapses are. A synapse is a small gap between two nerve cells across which flow neurotransmitters. White matter is made of axons connecting different parts of grey matter to each other. White matter is the nervous tissue through which nerve impulses pass between different grey matter areas. In the analogy, the grey matter is similar to computers while the white matter is like network cables that connect computers together. The white matter is white because of the fatty substance (myelin) that surrounds the nerve fibers (axons). The myelin lines long nerve fibers and functions like electrical insulation, allowing nerve impulses to travel quickly.",
      "exp_hant": "中樞神經系統（CNS）有兩種組織：灰質與白質。灰質包含神經元的細胞體、樹突及軸突終端，這是所有突觸所在之處。突觸是兩個神經細胞之間的一個小間隙，神經傳導物質經此間隙流動。白質由連接不同灰質區域的軸突所構成，白質是神經衝動在不同灰質區域之間傳遞所經的神經組織。在此比喻中，灰質類似於電腦本身，而白質則類似於連接各電腦的網路線。白質之所以呈白色，是因為包覆神經纖維（軸突）的脂肪物質（髓鞘）所致。髓鞘包覆長神經纖維，其功能類似電線絕緣層，使神經衝動得以快速傳遞。"
