      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. It is the liver which regulates the release of bile. The small intestine first absorbs about 90% of ingested water and the large intestine absorbs the rest. This process involves the conversion of liquid chyme into feces. Chyme is the semi-fluid mass of partly digested food from the stomach. The large intestine absorbs vitamins produced by its own beneficial and friendly bacteria that produce vitamin B and K in addition to biotin through fermentation. The large intestine absorbs water and the electrolytes of sodium and potassium via the sodium/potassium pump in the colon. Via pro-biotics in the gut, the large intestine makes up 60-70% of the immune system as a vast network of lymph tissue referred to as GALT (gut associated lymphatic tissue). The most crucial role probiotics seem to play for humans is that of training the immune system.",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且準確的答案。調節膽汁釋放的是肝臟。小腸首先吸收約90%攝入的水分，大腸則吸收剩餘部分，此過程涉及將液態食糜轉化為糞便。食糜是指來自胃部、部分消化後呈半流體狀的食物團。大腸可吸收由其自身有益且友善菌叢經發酵所產生的維生素，包括維生素B與K，以及生物素。大腸透過結腸中的鈉／鉀幫浦，吸收鈉與鉀等電解質及水分。透過腸道中的益生菌，大腸構成免疫系統的60-70%，形成一個龐大的淋巴組織網絡，稱為GALT（腸道相關淋巴組織）。益生菌對人體而言最重要的角色，似乎是訓練免疫系統。"
