      ],
      "exp_en": "Cholecystokinin is a hormone produced principally by the walls of the duodenum in response to the presence of fats, causing contraction of the gallbladder, release of bile, and secretion of pancreatic digestive enzymes. It causes the gallbladder to contract and its sphincter to relax which sends bile into the duodenum to emulsify the fat, and stimulates the pancreas to secrete enzymes that break down fat and proteins. Gastrin is a hormone secreted by glands in the mucous membrane of the stomach that stimulates the production of gastric juice. Secretin is a hormone that is produced in the duodenum that inhibits gastric acid secretion and stimulates secretion of bile, insulin, and pancreatic digestive enzymes. Bile is a bitter fluid that is secreted by the liver, stored in the gallbladder, and discharged into the duodenum to assist in the digestion and absorption of fats.",
      "exp_hant": "膽囊收縮素主要由十二指腸壁在偵測到脂肪存在時分泌，可引起膽囊收縮、膽汁釋放，以及胰臟消化酵素的分泌。它使膽囊收縮並使其括約肌放鬆，將膽汁送入十二指腸以乳化脂肪，並刺激胰臟分泌可分解脂肪與蛋白質的酵素。胃泌素是由胃黏膜腺體分泌的一種激素，可刺激胃液的生成。胰泌素是十二指腸產生的一種激素，可抑制胃酸分泌，並刺激膽汁、胰島素及胰臟消化酵素的分泌。膽汁是一種苦味液體，由肝臟分泌，儲存於膽囊中，並排入十二指腸以協助脂肪的消化及吸收。"
