    {
      "number": 489,
      "question_en": "Which statement is accurate in regards to immunoglobulins and antibodies?",
      "question_hant": "關於免疫球蛋白與抗體，下列敘述何者正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "both are attached to the B cell membrane",
          "hant": "兩者皆附著於B細胞膜上",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "immunoglobulins are attached to the C cell membrane while antibodies float in the circulation",
          "hant": "免疫球蛋白附著於C細胞膜上，而抗體則游離於循環中",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "they are both glycoproteins",
          "hant": "兩者皆為醣蛋白",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "they are both part of the innate immune system",
          "hant": "兩者皆屬於先天性免疫系統的一部分",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Immunoglobulin and antibody are disease-fighting in response to a particular antigen. Both immunoglobulin and antibody are glycoproteins. A glycoprotein is a protein strand with an attached sugar (glycan) molecule. Immunoglobulins are attached to the B cell membrane while antibodies float in the circulation. B-cells and T-cells function as part of the adaptive immune system. B-cells involve humoral immunity while T-cells involve cellular immunity. Intracellular pathogens can only replicate inside a host cell, whereas extracellular pathogens can replicate independent of the host cell. Pathogens can live and reproduce in the extracellular space. The extracellular body spaces are protected by humoral immunity. The extracellular pathogens are destroyed by antibodies produced by the B-cells. Many intracellular pathogens spread through the extracellular body fluids. Once inside the cell pathogens are no longer recognized by humoral immunity. T-cells are involved in the cell-mediated immune response. T-cells identify and destroy infected cells to prevent the further invasion of the pathogen. The infected cells are destroyed by cytotoxic T-cells. The intracellular pathogens are terminated by the activation of macrophages which engulf and digest the pathogen. The body makes different antibodies, or immunoglobulins, to fight different pathogens. The antibody for chickenpox is not the same as the antibody for mononucleosis. Sometimes, the immune system makes a mistake and make antibodies against itself. It can treat healthy organs and tissues like foreign invaders. This is classified as an autoimmune disease such as rheumatoid arthritis.",
      "exp_hant": "免疫球蛋白與抗體皆針對特定抗原發揮抗病作用。免疫球蛋白與抗體皆為醣蛋白，醣蛋白是一種附有醣（聚醣）分子的蛋白質鏈。免疫球蛋白附著於B細胞膜上，而抗體則游離於循環中。B細胞與T細胞屬於適應性免疫系統的一部分，B細胞涉及體液性免疫，T細胞則涉及細胞性免疫。細胞內病原體只能在宿主細胞內複製，而細胞外病原體則可獨立於宿主細胞進行複製，病原體可在細胞外空間中存活並繁殖。細胞外的身體空間受到體液性免疫的保護，細胞外病原體由B細胞產生的抗體所摧毀。許多細胞內病原體透過細胞外體液擴散，一旦進入細胞內，病原體便不再被體液性免疫所辨識。T細胞參與細胞媒介型免疫反應，T細胞辨識並摧毀受感染的細胞，以防止病原體進一步入侵，受感染的細胞由毒殺型T細胞摧毀。細胞內病原體則由活化的巨噬細胞終結，巨噬細胞會吞噬並消化病原體。人體會製造不同的抗體（即免疫球蛋白）來對抗不同的病原體，水痘的抗體與傳染性單核球增多症的抗體並不相同。有時免疫系統會出錯，製造出攻擊自身的抗體，將健康的器官與組織當作外來入侵者對待，這被歸類為自體免疫疾病，例如類風濕性關節炎。"
    },
    {
