      ],
      "exp_en": "Premenstrual symptoms only occur during the luteal phase, between ovulation and the start of menstrual bleeding, or soon after. PMS can occur during the entire luteal phase. PMS symptoms are thought to be caused by the rise and fall of hormones, specifically estrogen, throughout the menstrual cycle. Estrogen levels rise slowly after the period ends and it peaks two weeks later. Then estrogen levels begin to rise slowly before dropping again just before menstruation starts. These hormonal peaks and valleys are thought to cause mood swings and other menstrual symptoms.",
      "exp_hant": "經前症狀僅發生於黃體期，即排卵後至月經來潮開始或稍後的這段時間。經前症候群可能發生於整個黃體期。一般認為經前症候群的症狀是由月經週期中荷爾蒙（特別是雌激素）的升降所引起。雌激素在月經結束後緩慢上升，約兩週後達到高峰，接著在月經開始前又緩慢上升後再度下降。這些荷爾蒙的高低起伏被認為會導致情緒波動及其他經期症狀。"
    },
