          "en": "motor / sensory and motor",
          "hant": "運動／感覺與運動",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A gag reflex, also known as laryngeal spasm or pharyngeal reflex, is the contraction that occurs in the back of the throat, triggered by an object touching the back of the tongue, the roof of the mouth, the back of the throat, or the area around the tonsils. The function of the gag reflex is is to prevent choking since the gastrointestinal and respiratory systems have a common route to them at the pharynx of the throat which starts to split at the epiglottis. The gag reflex is a defense mechanism to prevent something from being swallowed and ingested. In gastroesophageal reflux disease, stomach acid reaches the throat, irritates the surrounding tissue which then stimulates the gag reflex.",
      "exp_hant": "嘔吐反射（又稱喉痙攣或咽反射）是指觸碰舌根、上顎、咽喉後壁或扁桃腺周圍區域時，喉嚨後方所產生的收縮反應。由於消化系統與呼吸系統在咽部（自會厭處開始分岔）共用一條通道，嘔吐反射的功能即在於防止嗆咳。嘔吐反射是一種防止異物被吞嚥、攝入的防禦機制。在胃食道逆流疾病中，胃酸逆流至喉部，刺激周圍組織，進而誘發嘔吐反射。"
