    {
      "number": 496,
      "question_en": "T-lymphocytes (T-cells) originate in the _________ and mature in the _________.",
      "question_hant": "T淋巴球（T細胞）源自於_________，並在_________成熟。",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "bone marrow, thymus",
          "hant": "骨髓，胸腺",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "thymus, spleen",
          "hant": "胸腺，脾臟",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "bone marrow, bone marrow",
          "hant": "骨髓，骨髓",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "spleen, thymus",
          "hant": "脾臟，胸腺",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Lymphocytes are small, round cells located in the peripheral blood, lymph, lymph nodes, lymphoid organs (thymus, spleen, tonsils, appendix) and in tissues. Based on their function and cell components lymphocytes are divided into three groups: T-lymphocytes or T-cells, B-lymphocytes or B-cells, and Natural killer cells (NK). T-cells originate in the bone marrow and mature and differentiate in the thymus. The name T- cells is derived from its site of maturation which is the thymus. Mature T-cells are located inside the lymph nodes and the lymphoid layer of spleen. All T-cells contain specific receptors on their surface to recognize and bind to an antigen. There are three types of T-cells: 1) Helper T-cells (TH), 2) Cytotoxic T-cells (Tc), and 3) Suppressor cells (Ts-cells). Helper T-cells (TH) and 2) Cytotoxic T-cells (Tc) are activated by the recognition of the antigen. The Suppressor cells (Ts-cells) suppress humoral and cell mediated immunity. T-lymphocytes assist in the regulation of immune reactions. The function of T-lymphocytes are to recruit and activate phagocytic cells which engulf the pathogen. Recruit and activate specialized cytotoxic cells to kill viruses or destroy cancer cell. And secrete cytokine which is responsible for the growth and differentiation of T- cells, monocytes, macrophages.",
      "exp_hant": "淋巴球是位於周邊血液、淋巴、淋巴結、淋巴器官（胸腺、脾臟、扁桃腺、闌尾）及組織中的小型圓形細胞。依其功能與細胞組成，淋巴球可分為三類：T淋巴球（T細胞）、B淋巴球（B細胞）及自然殺手細胞（NK細胞）。T細胞源自骨髓，並在胸腺中成熟分化，「T細胞」之名即源自其成熟部位——胸腺。成熟的T細胞位於淋巴結內及脾臟的淋巴層中。所有T細胞的表面皆帶有特定受體，可辨識並結合抗原。T細胞共有三種類型：1）輔助型T細胞（TH）、2）胞毒型T細胞（Tc）、3）抑制型細胞（Ts細胞）。輔助型T細胞（TH）與胞毒型T細胞（Tc）在辨識抗原後被活化，抑制型細胞（Ts細胞）則抑制體液性與細胞媒介性免疫。T淋巴球協助調節免疫反應，其功能包括：招募並活化能吞噬病原體的吞噬細胞；招募並活化專門的胞毒細胞以殺死病毒或摧毀癌細胞；並分泌細胞激素，負責T細胞、單核球及巨噬細胞的生長與分化。"
    },
    {
      "number": 497,
      "question_en": "What is a motor unit?",
      "question_hant": "何謂運動單位（motor unit）？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "a group of muscle fibers activated to produce a specific movement",
          "hant": "為產生特定動作而被活化的一組肌纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "a motor axon connecting upper and lower motor neurons",
          "hant": "連接上運動神經元與下運動神經元的運動軸突",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "one motor axon connecting and coupling to a secondary motor axon",
          "hant": "一條運動軸突與第二條運動軸突相連耦合",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "a single motor neuron and all the muscle fibers innervated by it",
          "hant": "單一運動神經元及其所支配的所有肌纖維",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Each individual muscle fiber in a muscle is innervated by one, and only one, motor neuron. A single motor neuron, however, can innervate many muscle fibers. The combination of an individual motor neuron and all of the muscle fibers that it innervates is called a motor unit. Motor means movement. A motor unit is where the nervous system meets the musculoskeletal system. The connection between the nervous system and the muscle is called the neuromuscular junction. A motor neuron is a cell in the central nervous system (CNS) that controls the contraction or relaxation of muscles. Motor neurons are also called efferent neurons as they carry information from the CNS to muscles while afferent neurons or sensory neurons carry information from sensory organs and tissues back to the CNS. A neuron is composed of three parts: the cell body, the dendrites, and the axon. The dendrites branch out from the cell body and receive electrochemical signals from the nervous system. The axon (nerve fiber) is the long thin fiber that conducts that electrochemical signal to a target muscle or gland. The contraction of skeletal muscle fibers is triggered by signaling from a motor neuron. Each muscle fiber is innervated by only one motor neuron but a single motor neuron can innervate multiple muscle fibers. A motor unit is defined as a single motor neuron and all of the muscle fiber (cells) innervated by it. When a motor unit is activated all of the muscle fibers controlled by it contract. Where the motor neuron connects to the muscle is called the neuromuscular junction. Small motor units are composed of a motor neuron and only a few muscle fibers. This allows for very fine motor control of muscles such as moving the eye or the fingers. The eye muscles, for example, have thousands of muscle fibers with every 5-10 fibers supplied by a single motor neuron. Large motor units are concerned with large movements such as moving parts of the body against gravity. The large motor units of the thigh muscles is where a single motor neuron supplies thousands of muscle fibers. Groups of motor units often work together to coordinate the contractions of a single muscle. All of the motor units within a muscle are considered a motor pool.",
      "exp_hant": "肌肉中的每一條肌纖維僅由一個運動神經元所支配。然而，單一運動神經元卻可支配許多條肌纖維。單一運動神經元與其所支配的所有肌纖維的組合，稱為運動單位。「運動」意指動作，運動單位是神經系統與肌肉骨骼系統交會之處，神經系統與肌肉之間的連接稱為神經肌肉接合處。運動神經元是中樞神經系統（CNS）中控制肌肉收縮或放鬆的細胞，又稱為傳出神經元，因其將訊息由中樞神經系統傳至肌肉，而傳入神經元（感覺神經元）則將訊息從感覺器官與組織傳回中樞神經系統。神經元由三部分組成：細胞本體、樹突與軸突。樹突自細胞本體分支而出，接收來自神經系統的電化學訊號；軸突（神經纖維）則是將該電化學訊號傳導至目標肌肉或腺體的細長纖維。骨骼肌纖維的收縮是由運動神經元的訊號所觸發。每條肌纖維僅由一個運動神經元支配，但單一運動神經元可支配多條肌纖維。運動單位的定義即為單一運動神經元及其所支配的所有肌纖維（細胞）。當運動單位被活化時，其所控制的所有肌纖維皆會收縮。運動神經元與肌肉相連之處稱為神經肌肉接合處。小型運動單位由一個運動神經元及少數幾條肌纖維組成，使肌肉能進行非常精細的運動控制，例如眼球或手指的移動；例如眼肌便有數千條肌纖維，每5至10條由單一運動神經元供應。大型運動單位則負責較大幅度的動作，例如對抗重力移動身體部位；大腿肌肉的大型運動單位中，單一運動神經元可供應數千條肌纖維。多個運動單位常協同運作以協調單一肌肉的收縮，一條肌肉內所有的運動單位則合稱為運動池（motor pool）。"
    },
