      "exp_en": "In vigorous exercise, the lungs cannot supply all the oxygen that the muscles need. The lungs and bloodstream supply sufficient oxygen for aerobic respiration in the muscles. In this situation the muscles can continue to break down glucose to liberate energy for a short time using anaerobic respiration. This partial breakdown produces lactic acid, which results in a sensation of fatigue when it reaches certain levels in the muscles and the blood. The additional oxygen that must be taken into the body after vigorous exercise to restore all systems to their normal states is called oxygen debt. In hypoxia the body or a region of the body is deprived of adequate oxygen supply at the tissue level. Aerobic respiration is a process that uses oxygen and anaerobic respiration is a process that does not use oxygen. These are two forms of cellular respiration. Glycolysis, which translates to splitting sugars, is the process of releasing energy within sugars.",
      "exp_hant": "在劇烈運動時，肺部無法供應肌肉所需的全部氧氣。肺部與血流通常能提供足夠的氧氣供肌肉進行有氧呼吸，但在氧氣不足的情況下，肌肉可短暫改以無氧呼吸繼續分解葡萄糖以釋放能量。這種不完全的分解會產生乳酸，當乳酸在肌肉與血液中達到一定濃度時，便會產生疲勞感。劇烈運動後身體為了恢復各系統至正常狀態所需額外攝入的氧氣，稱為氧債。缺氧則是指身體或身體某部位在組織層級得不到充足的氧氣供應。有氧呼吸是使用氧氣的過程，無氧呼吸則是不使用氧氣的過程，兩者為細胞呼吸的兩種形式。糖解作用（glycolysis，字面意為「分解糖類」）則是指糖類釋放能量的過程。"
