      "exp_en": "Thyroglobulin is not the same as thyroxine-binding globulin. Thyroxine-binding globulin is a carrier protein that carries the thyroid hormones in the blood while thyroglobulin is produced by and used entirely within the thyroid gland. In the thyroid, most of the T4 is stored bound to a protein called thyroglobulin. When there is a need for thyroid hormones in the body, the thyroid gland creates more T4 and/or releases some of what is stored. In the blood, most T4 is bound to a protein called thyroxine-binding globulin (TBG) and is mostly in an inactive form. T4 is converted to T3 by the liver and other tissues. It is T3 not T4 that primarily controls the rate of body functions.",
      "exp_hant": "甲狀腺球蛋白（thyroglobulin）與甲狀腺素結合球蛋白（thyroxine-binding globulin）並不相同。甲狀腺素結合球蛋白是在血液中運送甲狀腺荷爾蒙的載體蛋白，而甲狀腺球蛋白則完全由甲狀腺產生並在其內部使用。在甲狀腺中，大部分的T4以與甲狀腺球蛋白結合的形式儲存。當身體需要甲狀腺荷爾蒙時，甲狀腺會製造更多T4，並／或釋出部分儲存量。在血液中，大部分的T4與一種稱為甲狀腺素結合球蛋白（TBG）的蛋白質結合，大多呈非活性形式。T4會由肝臟及其他組織轉化為T3，而主要控制身體功能運作速率的是T3而非T4。"
