      ],
      "exp_en": "Lymphocytes are small, round cells located in the peripheral blood, lymph, lymph nodes, lymphoid organs (thymus, spleen, tonsils, appendix) and in tissues. Based on their function and cell components lymphocytes are divided into three groups: T-lymphocytes or T-cells, B-lymphocytes or B-cells, and Natural killer cells (NK). B-cells originate, differentiate, and mature in the bone marrow. The name B-cells is derived from its site of maturation which is the bone marrow. The form of B-cells are indistinguishable from T-cells. The difference between the two is their surface protein (immunoglobulin or antibody) which acts as a receptor for specific antigen. An immuglobulin is a protein produced by plasma cells and lymphocytes. They play an essential role in the immune system by binding to foreign substances (bacteria, virus) and assist in destroying them. The function of B-cells is antibody production against specific target antigen and provides the signal to activate T-Cells.",
      "exp_hant": "淋巴球是位於周邊血液、淋巴、淋巴結、淋巴器官（胸腺、脾臟、扁桃腺、闌尾）及組織中的小型圓形細胞。依其功能與細胞組成，淋巴球可分為三類：T淋巴球（T細胞）、B淋巴球（B細胞）及自然殺手細胞（NK細胞）。B細胞源自骨髓，並在骨髓中分化成熟，「B細胞」之名即源自其成熟部位——骨髓。B細胞的外形與T細胞難以區分，兩者的差異在於其表面蛋白（免疫球蛋白或抗體），此蛋白作為特定抗原的受體。免疫球蛋白是由漿細胞與淋巴球所產生的蛋白質，透過與外來物質（細菌、病毒）結合並協助將其摧毀，在免疫系統中扮演重要角色。B細胞的功能是針對特定目標抗原產生抗體，並提供活化T細胞的訊號。"
    },
