      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. It is the kidneys that produce erythropoietin, a hormone that helps make red blood cells. It is the kidneys and the lungs that help maintain the acid-base balance. The liver is largest glandular organ with a weight of about three pounds. The liver produces bile which helps to break down fats and carry waste away. The liver detoxifies the body by breaking down harmful substances excreted into the bile or blood. Bile by-products enter the intestine and leave the body in the form of feces. Blood by-products are filtered out by the kidneys, and leave the body in the form of urine. The liver converts poisonous ammonia to urea, which is the main component of urine. Urea is an end product of protein breakdown by the liver and is excreted in the urine. The liver converts excess glucose into glycogen for storage. Glycogen can later be converted back to glucose for energy. The liver has many roles, one being to make cholesterol while another is to remove excess amounts. The body needs cholesterol for every cell functioning. About 80 percent of the cholesterol is produced in the liver. The liver clears bilirubin from red blood cells. If there is an accumulation of bilirubin, the skin and eyes turn yellow.",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。產生紅血球生成素（一種協助製造紅血球的荷爾蒙）的是腎臟；維持酸鹼平衡的是腎臟與肺臟。肝臟是人體最大的腺體器官，重約三磅。肝臟分泌膽汁，有助於分解脂肪並帶走廢物；肝臟也透過分解排入膽汁或血液中的有害物質來為身體解毒。膽汁的代謝產物進入腸道後以糞便形式排出體外；血液中的代謝產物則由腎臟過濾，以尿液形式排出。肝臟會將有毒的氨轉化為尿素（尿液的主要成分），尿素是肝臟分解蛋白質後的最終產物，並經尿液排出。肝臟將多餘的葡萄糖轉化為肝醣儲存，肝醣日後可再轉化回葡萄糖以供能量所需。肝臟具有多種功能，其一是製造膽固醇，另一則是清除過多的膽固醇；人體每個細胞的運作都需要膽固醇，約有80%的膽固醇由肝臟製造。肝臟也負責清除紅血球所釋出的膽紅素，若膽紅素堆積，皮膚與眼睛便會出現黃疸。"
