      "exp_en": "Spasticity and rigidity are conditions where it is difficult to do a muscular movement. Spasticity has increased muscle tone (hypertonia) that is rate dependent. That is, spasticity is velocity-dependent. This means that the faster the patient moves or straightens a joint, the more tight or spastic the muscle feels. In rigidity the resistance to movement is felt regardless of the speed or direction that the joint is moving. Spasticity involves the upper motor neurons at any point from the cortex to the spinal cord. Spasticity occurs, for example, in strokes, particularly in the chronic or late stages. Rigidity involves the basal ganglia which is a group of structures linked to the thalamus in the base of the brain. It is involved in coordination of movement. Rigidity occurs, for example, in Parkinsonism.",
      "exp_hant": "痙攣與僵直皆屬於難以進行肌肉動作的病症。痙攣的肌肉張力增加（肌張力過高）且與動作速度有關，也就是說痙攣具有速度依賴性——患者移動或伸直關節的速度越快，肌肉感覺越緊繃、越痙攣。僵直則是無論關節移動的速度或方向為何，皆會感受到阻力。痙攣涉及由皮質至脊髓之間任一處的上運動神經元，例如常見於中風患者，尤其是慢性或後期階段。僵直則涉及基底核——一群與腦底部視丘相連的結構，參與動作的協調，例如常見於帕金森氏症。"
