      "exp_en": "Risk factors for osteoporosis include: 1) Sex: women are more likely to develop osteoporosis than men. 2) Age: the older a person is the greater the risk but it can occur at any age. One of every two women and one out of four men older than 50 will have a fracture associated with osteoporosis. 3) Race: Caucasian and Asians are at greater risk. 4) Family History: a parent or sibling with osteoporosis increases the risk, especially if one of the parents had a history of hip fractrue. 5) Body Frame: women or men with small body frames are at greater risk due to having less bone mass. Low body weight is the single best predictor of low bone density and low bone density at the hip (femoral neck) is an accurate predictor of hip fracture. 6) Life Style: smoking and diets low in vitamin D and calcium can increase risk. Basic screening questions for older women include: Have you ever had a hip fracture? Did either parent have a hip fracture? Do you smoke? What is your weight? Have you ever taken estrogen therapy?.",
      "exp_hant": "骨質疏鬆症的風險因子包括：1）性別：女性比男性更容易罹患骨質疏鬆症；2）年齡：年齡越大風險越高，但任何年齡皆可能發生，每兩名50歲以上女性中即有一人、每四名50歲以上男性中即有一人會發生與骨質疏鬆相關的骨折；3）種族：白種人與亞洲人風險較高；4）家族史：父母或手足有骨質疏鬆病史會增加風險，尤其若父母一方曾有髖部骨折病史；5）體型：體型較小的男女因骨量較少而風險較高，低體重是預測低骨密度最重要的單一指標，而髖部（股骨頸）骨密度偏低則能準確預測髖部骨折風險；6）生活方式：吸菸及維生素D、鈣質攝取不足的飲食皆可能提高風險。針對年長女性的基本篩檢問題包括：是否曾有髖部骨折？父母是否曾有髖部骨折？是否吸菸？體重為何？是否曾接受雌激素療法？"
