      "exp_en": "The correct answers are: Confabulation is filling the gap of an impaired memory. Neologisms are invented words or words with idiosyncratic meaning. Echolalia is the repetition of other people's words or phrases. Circumstantiality is speech with unnecessary details. Confabulation is fabrication of facts or events to fill the gap of an impaired memory. Confabulation can be found with Korsakoff syndrome caused by alcoholism. Neologism can be found in schizophrenia. Circumstantiability can be found in normal patients or those with obsessive-compulsive disorders. Other thought processes include: Flight of ideas is the continuous flow of fast speech going from topic to topic and can be associated with mania. Perseveration is persistent repetition of words or ideas which can be found in schizophrenia or psychosis.",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為：虛談症是以捏造內容填補受損記憶的空缺；新語症是自創詞語或帶有特殊個人意義的詞語；語意重複症（echolalia）是重複他人的話語或詞句；迂迴贅述則是言語中夾雜不必要細節。虛談症是捏造事實或事件以填補受損記憶的空缺，可見於酒精中毒引起的科沙可夫症候群（Korsakoff syndrome）。新語症可見於思覺失調症。迂迴贅述則可見於正常人或強迫症患者。其他思考過程包括：意念飛躍（flight of ideas），即言語快速且不斷從一個主題跳到另一個主題，可能與躁症有關；持續症（perseveration），即持續重複某些詞語或想法，可見於思覺失調症或精神病。"
