      ],
      "exp_en": "The scaphoid bone is one of the carpal bones in the wrist. It is the most common carpal bone to fracture. The anatomical snuff box is a triangular deepening of hand, at the level of the carpal bones (the scaphoid and trapezium bones). The most common signs and symptoms of a scaphoid fracture are pain with swelling and tenderness. There is noticeable tenderness to the touch over the \"anatomical snuff box\". A scaphoid fracture is an acute bone injury from trauma like a fall on an outstretched hand, presenting with sudden snuffbox tenderness and requiring imaging like X-rays for diagnosis and immobilization for treatment, whereas De Quervain's syndrome is a chronic inflammatory tendon disorder from repetitive thumb/wrist motions, diagnosed clinically via the Finkelstein test and managed with rest, splinting, or steroid injections. The key differentiator lies in the histor (traumatic onset for the fracture versus gradual overuse for the syndrom) along with the fracture's risk of complications like nonunion versus the syndrome's potential for persistent pain if untreated.",
      "exp_hant": "舟狀骨是手腕腕骨之一，也是最常發生骨折的腕骨。「解剖鼻煙盒」是位於腕骨（舟狀骨與大多角骨）處的手部三角形凹陷區。舟狀骨骨折最常見的徵象與症狀為疼痛併腫脹與壓痛，觸診「解剖鼻煙盒」處會有明顯壓痛。舟狀骨骨折是因創傷（如以伸直的手撐地跌倒）造成的急性骨損傷，表現為突發性鼻煙盒壓痛，需以X光等影像檢查診斷並以固定方式治療；相對地，狄奎凡氏症候群則是因拇指／手腕反覆動作所致的慢性肌腱發炎疾患，可透過芬克斯坦氏測試（Finkelstein test）於臨床診斷，並以休息、副木固定或類固醇注射治療。兩者的關鍵區別在於病史（骨折為創傷性發作，而狄奎凡氏症候群則為漸進性過度使用），以及骨折可能出現癒合不良等併發症，而該症候群若未治療則可能出現持續性疼痛。"
    },
