      "exp_en": "The Labral Clunk Test is done with the patient lying in a supine position and the examiner places one hand behind the proximal humerus while gently grasping the humerus at the bicondylar access of the elbow. The patient's humerus is abducted approximately 100 degrees with the elbow held steady, the examiner gently translocates the humeral head anterior and posterior with the examining hand behind the humeral head, palpates for a clunk as the other hand moves the humerus in a rotary motion, in effect, trapping the labral tear between the humeral head and the glenoid. This is analogous to the McMurray test for meniscal tears of the knee. The Sulcus sign is looking for a space or Sulcus that may appear depending on the inferior instability of the shoulder compared to the opposite arm. The Jobe's test is identification of anterior displacement of the shoulder with fear of anterior displacement and relief with posterior movement of the humerus in this test. Neer's Sign and Hawkin's Sign are good for identifying subacromial impingement.",
      "exp_hant": "關節唇碰撞測試的作法是讓患者仰臥，檢查者一手置於肱骨近端後方，另一手輕輕握住肘部的肱骨髁間軸。患者的肱骨外展約100度並固定肘部，檢查者以位於肱骨頭後方的手輕輕將肱骨頭前後移動，同時另一手以旋轉方式移動肱骨，觸診是否出現碰撞感，實際上即是使撕裂的關節唇夾在肱骨頭與關節盂之間，其原理類似用於檢測膝關節半月板撕裂的麥氏測試（McMurray test）。凹陷徵象是比較兩側肩關節，觀察是否因肩關節下方不穩定而出現凹陷或空隙。喬伯氏測試則是用於辨識肩關節前方不穩定，患者會因擔心肱骨前移而出現恐懼感，並在將肱骨向後移動時獲得緩解。尼爾氏徵象（Neer's Sign）與霍金氏徵象（Hawkin's Sign）則適合用於辨識肩峰下夾擠症。"
    },
