      "exp_en": "THC is the active psychoactive chemical in marijuana. THC attaches itself to a network of specialized receptors, cannabinoid 1 (CB1). CB1 receptors are located mostly in the brain while cannabinoid 2 (CB2) are found primarily in the immune system and its associated structures. Upon research, it was discovered that the brain produces a compound very similar to THC called anandamide, the brain's natural \"marijuana\". The original and natural function of CB1 receptors is to bind to the neurotransmitter anandamide. Anandamide activation of cannabanoid brain receptors help to control memory, learning, coordination, movement, appetite, pain sensation, and higher cognitive functions. THC fits into the receptors meant for anandamide. tcmtests.com, April 2020",
      "exp_hant": "THC是大麻中具精神活性的主要化學成分，會與一組特化受體——第一型大麻素受體（CB1）結合。CB1受體主要分布於腦部，而第二型大麻素受體（CB2）則主要見於免疫系統及其相關結構。研究發現，大腦會產生一種與THC非常相似的化合物，稱為花生四烯乙醇胺（anandamide），可視為大腦天生的「大麻」。CB1受體原本天然的功能即是與神經傳導物質花生四烯乙醇胺結合。花生四烯乙醇胺活化大麻素腦受體，有助於調控記憶、學習、協調、動作、食慾、痛覺及高階認知功能。THC恰好能與原本供花生四烯乙醇胺結合的受體相配。tcmtests.com，2020年4月"
    },
