    {
      "number": 546,
      "question_en": "Which of the following anti-diarrheal generic drugs are opioids?",
      "question_hant": "下列哪些止瀉學名藥屬於鴉片類藥物？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "attapulgite, diphenoxylate, loperamide",
          "hant": "attapulgite（矽酸鋁鎂）、diphenoxylate（苯乙哌啶）、loperamide（洛哌丁胺）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "diphenoxylate, loperamide",
          "hant": "diphenoxylate（苯乙哌啶）、loperamide（洛哌丁胺）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "attapulgite, loperamide",
          "hant": "attapulgite（矽酸鋁鎂）、loperamide（洛哌丁胺）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "difenoxin, diphenoxylate, loperamide",
          "hant": "difenoxin（地芬諾辛）、diphenoxylate（苯乙哌啶）、loperamide（洛哌丁胺）",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. There are two main types of anti-diarrheal drugs, ABSORBENTS and OPIOIDS. Absorbent substances include attapulgite (Di-Gon II, Diarrest, Donnagel), bismuth subsalicylate (Kaopectate, Kola-Pectin DS, Maalox Total Stomach Relief, Peptic Relief, Pepto-Bismol), activated charcoal (Actidose-Aqua, Activated Charcoal, Charcoal Plus DS). Bismuth subsalicylate is used to treat diarrhea, nausea, heartburn, indigestion, and upset stomach. These drugs bind and neutralize the actions of diarrhea-causing toxins preventing their adherence to the intestinal walls. Bismuth subsalicylate treats diarrhea, traveler's diarrhea, nausea, heartburn, and indigestion. This medication should not be given to a child or teenager with a fever, especially if there are flu symptoms or chicken pox. Salicylates can cause a serious and sometimes fatal condition called Reye's syndrome in children. OPIOIDS slow down bowel muscle contractions resulting in the contents moving more slowly in the intestines. LOPERAMIDE (Imodium) is an opioid agonist that only interacts with the mu opioid receptors in the smooth muscle cells of the intestinal wall. As such, loperamide cannot be used as an analgesic or abused by an addict. By loperamide blocking these receptors in the intestines, the contraction of the smooth muscle cells decrease and peristalsis is decreased, thereby reducing stool frequency. Most common side effects are constipation, dizziness, nausea, and abdominal cramps. DIPHENOXYLATE (Lomotil) is an opioid agonist that acts on both the intestinal wall mu receptors and on those in the brain. As such diphenoxylate has analgesic effects and can be abused by an opioid addict. To combat this effect, diphenoxylate is combined with the drug atropine which will produce severe weakness and nausea if standard dosage of diphenoxylate is exceeded. Atropine is an anticholinergics that helps to dry up body fluids and also slows gut movement. Common side effect include bloating, constipation, loss of appetite, stomach pain with nausea and vomiting, dry mouth, and drowsiness. DIFENOXIN (Motofen) works similarly to diphenoxylate (Lamotil). Difenoxin is an active metabolite of diphenoxylate (Lamotil). A metabolite is the metabolism of a drug in the body which results in a different molecule that may be more or less active than the parent drug. Motofen is stronger than Lomotil and with fewer side effects. Difenoxin is also combined with atropine to prevent substance abuse. Do not take anti-diarrheal agents when diarrhea has symptoms of fever, severe illness, abdominal pain, or with blood/mucous in the stool. If diarrhea from an infection is a possibility, only use anti-diarrheal drugs under the guidance of a healthcare professional. tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。止瀉藥主要分為兩大類：吸附劑（ABSORBENTS）與鴉片類藥物（OPIOIDS）。吸附性藥物包括attapulgite（矽酸鋁鎂，商品名Di-Gon II、Diarrest、Donnagel）、bismuth subsalicylate（次水楊酸鉍，商品名Kaopectate、Kola-Pectin DS、Maalox Total Stomach Relief、Peptic Relief、Pepto-Bismol）、活性碳（商品名Actidose-Aqua、Activated Charcoal、Charcoal Plus DS）。次水楊酸鉍用於治療腹瀉、噁心、火燒心、消化不良及胃部不適，這類藥物會結合並中和引起腹瀉的毒素，阻止其附著於腸壁。次水楊酸鉍可治療腹瀉、旅行者腹瀉、噁心、火燒心及消化不良，但不應用於發燒的兒童或青少年，尤其是有流感症狀或水痘者，因為水楊酸類藥物可能在兒童身上引起嚴重甚至致命的雷氏症候群（Reye's syndrome）。鴉片類藥物則會減緩腸道肌肉收縮，使腸內容物移動速度變慢。洛哌丁胺（loperamide，商品名Imodium）是一種鴉片類促效劑，僅作用於腸壁平滑肌細胞的mu鴉片受體，因此洛哌丁胺無法作為止痛藥使用，也不會被成癮者濫用。洛哌丁胺藉由阻斷腸道內的這些受體，使平滑肌細胞收縮減少、蠕動減緩，進而降低排便次數，最常見的副作用包括便秘、頭暈、噁心及腹部絞痛。苯乙哌啶（diphenoxylate，商品名Lomotil）是一種鴉片類促效劑，同時作用於腸壁及腦部的mu受體，因此具有止痛效果，可能被鴉片成癮者濫用；為抑制此效應，苯乙哌啶會與阿托品併用，若超過標準劑量，將引起嚴重虛弱與噁心。阿托品是一種抗膽鹼藥物，有助於使體液乾燥並減緩腸道蠕動，常見副作用包括腹脹、便秘、食慾不振、伴有噁心嘔吐的胃痛、口乾及嗜睡。地芬諾辛（difenoxin，商品名Motofen）的作用機轉與苯乙哌啶（Lomotil）類似，是苯乙哌啶的活性代謝物。代謝物是指藥物在體內經代謝後產生的不同分子，其活性可能較母體藥物更強或更弱。Motofen的藥效比Lomotil更強，且副作用較少。地芬諾辛同樣與阿托品併用，以防止藥物濫用。當腹瀉伴有發燒、重病徵象、腹痛或糞便中帶血／黏液時，不應服用止瀉藥；若懷疑腹瀉為感染所致，則應僅在醫療專業人員的指導下使用止瀉藥。tcmtests.com，2020年7月"
    },
    {
      "number": 547,
      "question_en": "The anti-depressant class of reuptake inhibitors is associated with",
      "question_hant": "屬於再吸收抑制劑（reuptake inhibitors）的抗憂鬱藥物類別與下列何者有關？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "serotonin",
          "hant": "血清素",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "serotonin and norepinephrine",
          "hant": "血清素與正腎上腺素",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "serotonin, dopamine, and norepinephrine",
          "hant": "血清素、多巴胺與正腎上腺素",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "serotonin and dopamine",
          "hant": "血清素與多巴胺",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The most commonly prescribed antidepressants are called reuptake inhibitors. Neurotransmitters travel between two nerve endings. A presynaptic ending contains neurotransmitters and a postsynapse ending contains receptor sites for the neurotransmitters. Between the two endings is a gap or cleft through which the neurotranmitters travel. Reuptake inhibitors block the reabsorption (reuptake) of neurotransmitters thereby increasing their levels in the brain. Instead of getting reabsorbed, the neurotransmitter temporarily stays longer in the synaptic gap. Current research has identified three neurotransmitters related to depression. These are serotonin, dopamine, and norepinephrine. The first reuptake inhibitor was SSRI (selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor) which only blocks serotonin. New reuptake inhibitors include SNRI (serotonin \"norepinephrine\" reuptake inhibitor) which blocks the reuptake of both serotonin and norepinephrine. NDRI (norepinephrine dopamine reuptake inhibitor) block the reuptake of both norepinephrine and dopamine. Examples of of SSRI include Celexa (citalopram), Lexapro (escitalopram), Paxil (faroxetine), Prozac (fluoxetine), and Zoloft (sertraline). Examples of SNRI include Cymbalta (duloxetine), Effexor (venlafaxine), and Khedezla (desvenlafaxine). An example of an NDRI is Wellbutrin (bupropion). Common side effects of reuptake inhibitors include sexual dysfunction (reduced sexual desire, difficulty reaching orgasm, inability to maintain an erection), GI problems (nausea, constipation, diarrhea), insomnia, headache, weight gain, sweating. The FDA requires that all antidepressants carry black box warnings (strictest warning for prescriptions). With reuptake inhibitors, children, teenagers and young adults under 25 years old can have an increase in suicidal ideation. Abruptly stopping antidepressants or missing several doses can cause withdrawal symptoms. This is sometimes called discontinuation syndrome (flu-like symptoms, insomnia, nausea, imbalance, sensory disturbances, hyperarousal). tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "最常見的處方抗憂鬱藥物稱為再吸收抑制劑。神經傳導物質在兩個神經末梢之間傳遞：突觸前末梢含有神經傳導物質，突觸後末梢則含有神經傳導物質的受體位點，兩者之間存在一道間隙（突觸間隙），神經傳導物質即經此傳遞。再吸收抑制劑會阻斷神經傳導物質的再吸收（重新回收），藉此提高腦內濃度——神經傳導物質不會被重新吸收，而是暫時在突觸間隙中停留較久。目前研究已確認三種與憂鬱症有關的神經傳導物質：血清素、多巴胺及正腎上腺素。最早的再吸收抑制劑是SSRI（選擇性血清素再吸收抑制劑），僅阻斷血清素。較新型的再吸收抑制劑包括SNRI（血清素正腎上腺素再吸收抑制劑），可同時阻斷血清素與正腎上腺素的再吸收；以及NDRI（正腎上腺素多巴胺再吸收抑制劑），可同時阻斷正腎上腺素與多巴胺的再吸收。SSRI的例子包括Celexa（citalopram）、Lexapro（escitalopram）、Paxil（faroxetine）、Prozac（fluoxetine）及Zoloft（sertraline）。SNRI的例子包括Cymbalta（duloxetine）、Effexor（venlafaxine）及Khedezla（desvenlafaxine）。NDRI的例子則有Wellbutrin（bupropion）。再吸收抑制劑常見的副作用包括性功能障礙（性慾降低、難以達到高潮、無法維持勃起）、腸胃問題（噁心、便秘、腹瀉）、失眠、頭痛、體重增加及流汗。美國FDA規定所有抗憂鬱藥物皆須標示黑框警語（處方藥中最嚴重的警語等級）。使用再吸收抑制劑時，25歲以下的兒童、青少年及年輕成人可能出現自殺意念增加的情形。突然停藥或漏服數次劑量可能引發戒斷症狀，有時稱為停藥症候群（類流感症狀、失眠、噁心、平衡失調、感覺異常、過度警覺）。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
    {
      "number": 548,
      "question_en": "Benzodiazepines and barbiturates can be addictive. They work by activating which receptor?",
      "question_hant": "苯二氮平類（benzodiazepines）與巴比妥類（barbiturates）藥物可能成癮，其作用機轉為活化下列何種受體？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "serotonin receptors",
          "hant": "血清素受體",
          "correct": false
