    {
      "number": 550,
      "question_en": "Which of the following has correct antiparkinson drug mechanism of action?",
      "question_hant": "下列何者正確描述抗帕金森藥物的作用機轉？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "COMT inhibitors: block an enzyme that breaks down dopamine in the brain",
          "hant": "COMT抑制劑：阻斷腦內分解多巴胺的酵素",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Levodopa: directly provides the body with the dopamine neurotransmitter",
          "hant": "左旋多巴（Levodopa）：直接為身體提供多巴胺神經傳導物質",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Dopamine agonists: activate and enhance dopamine receptors in the brain",
          "hant": "多巴胺促效劑：活化並增強腦內多巴胺受體",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "MAO-B inhibitors: block an enzyme that degrades the drug levadopa",
          "hant": "MAO-B抑制劑：阻斷分解左旋多巴藥物的酵素",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The correct answers are: Dopamine agonists: activate and enhance dopamine receptors in the brain. Levodopa: is a precursor to the dopamine neurotransmitter. MAO-B inhibitors: block an enzyme that breaks down dopamine in the brain. COMT inhibitors: block an enzyme that degrades the drug levadopa. Levadopa does not directly provide the body with dopamine. It is a precursor to dopamine. Most symptoms of Parkinson's disease (PD) are due to a a lack of dopamine in the brain. Dopamine is a neurotransmitter involved with fine motor control (as well as motivation, pleasure, and learning). When there is a depredation of dopamine-producing brain cells, there can be resting tremors, postural instability, and rigidity of the limbs and trunk. Many PD drugs focus at either replenishing dopamine or mimicking the action of dopamine. LEVODOPA is a chemical precursor of dopamine that is transported to the brain where it is transformed into dopamine. It is the gold standard for treating PD. Levadopa is most often combined with another drug carbidopa. The drug Sinemet or Rytary are a mix of levodopa and carbidopa. Carbidopa increases levadopa availability by blocking the break down of levadopa. The addition of carbidopa allows a lower dosage of levadopa to be effective and thus reduce the side effects (nausea, vomiting) of only using levadopa by itself. Common side effects of carbidopa-levodopa combination include nausea, dizziness, headache, insomnia, abnormal dreams, dry mouth, anxiety, and constipation. DOPAMINE AGONISTS activate and enhance dopamine receptors (D2, D3, D4) in the brain. While levodopa is converted into dopamine, dopamine agonists mimic the effects of dopamine without having to be converted. Dopamine agonists are often used instead of levodopa or in combination with levodopa. The most prescribed dopamine agonists are Mirapex (peramipexol), Requip (ropinirole), and Neupro patch (rotigotine). Both Mirapex and Requip are also prescribed for restless leg syndrome. Common side effects of dopamine agonists include excessive daytime sleepiness, visual hallucinations, and confusion. An interesting side effect of dopamine agonists is possible gambling and hypersexuality even in patients with no prior history of these behaviors. COMT INHIBITORS are only effective when used with levodopa. When a patient takes levodopa, the catechol-O-methyl transerase (COMT) enzyme in the body converts a part of the levadopa into a form that cannot be used. Thus, COMT inhibitors allow more levodopa to be converted to dopamine in the brain. Their effect is to prolong the duration of levodopa action. Examples of COMT inhibitors are Comtan (entacapone ) and Tasmar (tolcapone). Common side effects include confusion, hallucinations, diarrhea, and discolored urine. MAO-B INHIBITORS block the enzyme (MAO-B) that breaks down dopamine in the brain. This increases dopamine availability. MAO-B inhibitors can be used by themselves or combined with levodopa. Examples of MAO-B inhibitors are selegiline (brand names: Emsam, Eldepryl, Zelapar, Carbex) and Azilect (rasagaline). Common side effects are nausea, dry mouth, confusion, and hallucinations. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為：多巴胺促效劑——活化並增強腦內多巴胺受體；左旋多巴——是多巴胺神經傳導物質的前驅物；MAO-B抑制劑——阻斷腦內分解多巴胺的酵素；COMT抑制劑——阻斷分解左旋多巴藥物的酵素。左旋多巴並非直接為身體提供多巴胺，而是多巴胺的前驅物。帕金森氏症（PD）的大多數症狀皆源自腦內多巴胺不足。多巴胺是一種與精細動作控制（以及動機、愉悅感與學習）有關的神經傳導物質，當製造多巴胺的腦細胞退化時，可能出現靜止性震顫、姿勢不穩及四肢與軀幹僵硬。許多帕金森氏症藥物皆著重於補充多巴胺或模擬多巴胺的作用。左旋多巴是多巴胺的化學前驅物，被運送至腦部後轉化為多巴胺，是治療帕金森氏症的黃金標準藥物，通常與另一種藥物卡比多巴（carbidopa）併用。Sinemet或Rytary即為左旋多巴與卡比多巴的複方藥物。卡比多巴透過阻斷左旋多巴的分解，提高左旋多巴的可利用性；加入卡比多巴後，可使用較低劑量的左旋多巴即達到療效，從而降低單獨使用左旋多巴時的副作用（噁心、嘔吐）。卡比多巴—左旋多巴複方藥物常見的副作用包括噁心、頭暈、頭痛、失眠、異常夢境、口乾、焦慮及便秘。多巴胺促效劑會活化並增強腦內的多巴胺受體（D2、D3、D4）；左旋多巴需先轉化為多巴胺，而多巴胺促效劑則無需轉化即可模擬多巴胺的效果。多巴胺促效劑常用來取代左旋多巴，或與左旋多巴併用。最常見的處方多巴胺促效劑包括Mirapex（普拉克索）、Requip（羅匹尼羅）及Neupro貼片（羅替戈汀），Mirapex與Requip也用於治療不寧腿症候群。多巴胺促效劑常見的副作用包括白天過度嗜睡、視幻覺及意識混亂；一個值得注意的副作用是即使患者先前並無相關行為史，仍可能出現賭博及性慾亢進等衝動行為。COMT抑制劑僅在與左旋多巴併用時才有效——當患者服用左旋多巴時，體內的兒茶酚-O-甲基轉移酶（COMT）會將部分左旋多巴轉化為無法利用的形式，因此COMT抑制劑可使更多左旋多巴在腦內轉化為多巴胺，其作用在於延長左旋多巴的藥效持續時間。COMT抑制劑的例子包括Comtan（entacapone）與Tasmar（tolcapone），常見副作用包括意識混亂、幻覺、腹瀉及尿液變色。MAO-B抑制劑則阻斷腦內分解多巴胺的酵素（MAO-B），藉此增加多巴胺的可利用性，可單獨使用或與左旋多巴併用。MAO-B抑制劑的例子包括selegiline（商品名Emsam、Eldepryl、Zelapar、Carbex）及Azilect（rasagiline），常見副作用為噁心、口乾、意識混亂及幻覺。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
