      "exp_en": "Monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) are a class of antidepressant drugs. It is usually prescribed for atypical depression which is characterized by overeating, sleeping too much, sensitivity to rejection, and strong reactions to the environment. Because of potentially lethal dietary and drug interactions, MAOIs are usually reserved as a last line of treatment when other classes of antidepressant medications such as selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors and tricyclic antidepressants have failed. When a patient combines MAOIs with tyramine containing foods, it can result in an hypertensive crisis. Foods containing considerable amounts of tyramine include meats that are potentially spoiled or pickled, aged, smoked, fermented, or marinated. Most pork. Chocolate. Alcoholic beverages. And fermented foods, such as most cheeses. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "單胺氧化酶抑制劑（MAOIs）是一類抗憂鬱藥物，通常用於治療非典型憂鬱症，其特徵為暴食、嗜睡過度、對拒絕高度敏感，以及對環境有強烈反應。由於MAOIs可能與飲食及其他藥物產生致命的交互作用，通常僅作為選擇性血清素再吸收抑制劑及三環抗憂鬱藥等其他類別藥物治療失敗後的最後防線。若患者將MAOIs與含酪胺（tyramine）的食物併用，可能引發高血壓危象。含大量酪胺的食物包括可能已變質、醃漬、風乾、煙燻、發酵或醃泡的肉類、大多數豬肉、巧克力、含酒精飲料，以及大多數起司等發酵食品。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
