      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Beta agonists are prescribed for the treatment and control of asthma and COPD. Angina pain is caused by insufficient oxygen blood flow (ischemia) to the heart muscle caused by arterial plaques. The four main categories of antiangina drugs are nitrates, beta blockers, calcium channel blockers, and ranolazine. NITRATES improve blood flow by relaxing and dilating veins and arteries through the release of nitric oxyde (a vasodilator). Nitrates reduce the amount of blood returning to the heart. Nitrates come in different forms of nitroglycerin (NTG): 1) sublingual or spray form nitroglycerin is effective within 2-5 minutes and the effect can last 15-30 minutes, 2) oral or transdermal nitrates take about 15 minutes to take effect and can last up to 24 hours, if timed release. Continuous nitrate treatment can lead to tolerance of the drug within 24 to 48 hours. Nitrate tolerance does not usually develop with sublingual NTG. Side effects of nitrates are headache, lightheadedness (especially the elderly), flushing, and an increased heart rate. Imdur (timed release pill), Nitro-Dur (patch), and Nitro-Bid (cream). BETA BLOCKERS reduce the heart rate and reduce the force of heart contractions thereby decreasing heart oxygen requirement. Beta blockers work through the blocking epinephrine (another term for adrenalin) receptors. Examples of beta blockers include Cardura (doxasosin) and Minipress (prazosin), Capres (clonidine) and Aldomet (methyldopa). Beta blockers should not be used on asthmatic patients (block the effect of adrenalin on the lungs), certain heart conditions such as heart failure, and patients with a slow heart rate. Side effects of beta blockers include dry mouth, drowsiness, constipation, insomnia, palpitations, and a high risk of hypotension. CALCIUM CHANNEL BLOCKERS cause smooth muscle relaxation by blocking calcium receptors in the blood vessels preventing vasoconstriction, thereby improving blood flow to the heart. Examples of calcium channel blockers include Cardizem (diltiazem), Calan (reapamil), Vasoc, (berpdil), Procardia (nifedipine). Side effects include hypotension, tachycardia, constipation, nausea, rash, and edema. Both beta blockers and calcium channel blockers are also used to treat hypertension. RANOLOZINE (brand name Ranexa) is a new method in treating angina. Ranolazine inhibits the sodium in the heart muscles which leads to a reduction of elevated intracellular calcium levels that in turn relax heart muscle tension with a concomitant reduction of heart muscle oxygen requirement. Ranolozine can be combined with nitrates, beta blockers, and calcium channel blockers to help control chronic angina. The most common side effects are dizziness and constipation. tcmtests.com, June 2020",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。乙型促效劑是用於治療與控制氣喘及慢性阻塞性肺病（COPD）的藥物。心絞痛的疼痛是由於動脈斑塊造成心肌血流含氧量不足（缺血）所引起。抗心絞痛藥物主要分為四大類：硝酸鹽類、乙型阻斷劑、鈣離子通道阻斷劑及雷諾拉嗪。硝酸鹽類透過釋放一氧化氮（一種血管擴張劑）使靜脈與動脈放鬆並擴張，藉此改善血流，並減少回流至心臟的血量。硝酸鹽類的硝化甘油（NTG）有多種劑型：1）舌下錠或噴劑形式的硝化甘油約於2至5分鐘內見效，藥效可持續15至30分鐘；2）口服或經皮的硝酸鹽類則約需15分鐘見效，若為緩釋劑型，藥效可持續長達24小時。持續使用硝酸鹽類治療，可能於24至48小時內產生藥物耐受性，但舌下型NTG通常不會產生此耐受性。硝酸鹽類的副作用包括頭痛、頭暈（尤其是老年人）、臉部潮紅及心跳加快。常見藥物有Imdur（緩釋錠）、Nitro-Dur（貼片）及Nitro-Bid（藥膏）。乙型阻斷劑透過降低心率並減弱心臟收縮力，藉此降低心臟的耗氧需求，其作用機轉是阻斷腎上腺素（epinephrine，即adrenalin）受體。乙型阻斷劑的例子包括Cardura（doxazosin）與Minipress（prazosin）、Capres（clonidine）及Aldomet（methyldopa）。氣喘患者（因會阻斷腎上腺素對肺部的作用）、某些心臟疾病（如心衰竭）及心跳過慢的患者，皆不應使用乙型阻斷劑。乙型阻斷劑的副作用包括口乾、嗜睡、便秘、失眠、心悸，以及較高的低血壓風險。鈣離子通道阻斷劑透過阻斷血管中的鈣受體，造成平滑肌放鬆，防止血管收縮，藉此改善心臟的血流供應。鈣離子通道阻斷劑的例子包括Cardizem（diltiazem）、Calan（verapamil）、Vascor（bepridil）及Procardia（nifedipine）。其副作用包括低血壓、心搏過速、便秘、噁心、皮疹及水腫。乙型阻斷劑與鈣離子通道阻斷劑也都用於治療高血壓。雷諾拉嗪（商品名Ranexa）是治療心絞痛的新方法，其作用是抑制心肌中的鈉離子，進而降低升高的細胞內鈣離子濃度，使心肌張力放鬆，同時降低心肌的耗氧需求。雷諾拉嗪可與硝酸鹽類、乙型阻斷劑及鈣離子通道阻斷劑併用，以協助控制慢性心絞痛，其最常見的副作用為頭暈與便秘。tcmtests.com，2020年6月"
    },
