      "exp_en": "Iron toxicity caused by drinking too much alcohol can lead to damage of the liver and other organs. Repeated blood transfusions, taking an overdose of iron or certain diseases (hemochromotosis) can also lead to iron toxicity. Iron overdose is a common cause of poisoning in children and it can be fatal. Signs of an iron overdose include severe vomiting and diarrhea, stomach cramps, pale or bluish skin and fingernails, and weakness. Iron toxicity can also do damage to the intestines and other organs. In some patients taking even normal doses of iron can cause constipation. Vitamin C (ascorbic acid), strongly enhances the absorption of iron but it must be taken at the same time as the iron. Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 48-49, 54; www.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "因過量飲酒所導致的鐵中毒，可能造成肝臟及其他器官的損傷。反覆輸血、鐵劑服用過量，或某些疾病（如血色素沉著症）也可能導致鐵中毒。鐵劑過量是兒童中毒的常見原因，且可能致命。鐵劑過量的徵兆包括嚴重嘔吐與腹瀉、腹部絞痛、皮膚與指甲蒼白或發紺，以及虛弱無力。鐵中毒也可能損害腸道及其他器官。部分病人即使服用正常劑量的鐵劑，也可能引起便秘。維生素C（抗壞血酸）能大幅增強鐵的吸收，但必須與鐵劑同時服用才有此效果。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，第48-49、54頁；www.webmd.com"
