    {
      "number": 567,
      "question_en": "Niacin (vitamin B3)",
      "question_hant": "菸鹼酸（維生素B3）",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "is soluble in both water or lipids depending upon its chemical form (nicotinic acid or niacinamide)",
          "hant": "依其化學形式（菸鹼酸或菸鹼醯胺）不同，可溶於水或脂質",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "participates primarily in reactions involving amino acids",
          "hant": "主要參與涉及胺基酸的反應",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "is susceptible to destruction in foods exposed to light",
          "hant": "在食物中暴露於光線下時容易被破壞",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "can be synthesized in the body from the essential amino acid tryptophan",
          "hant": "可由必需胺基酸色胺酸在體內合成",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Vitamin B3 comes in two forms: nicotinic acid and niacinamide. Nicotinic acid goes by the common name of niacin. The body can convert niacin into niacinamide when niacin is taken in a greater amount than the body uses. Both types have the same functions but niacin is the one that can cause vasodilation (skin flushing, redness). Timed release niacin can reduce the flushing effect. Niacin is conditionally essential because the body can synthesize it through tryptophan in the diet. Like all of the B vitamins, niacin is a water soluble vitamin. Niacin is a precursor of important coenzymes (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate) which are important for metabolism. THERAPEUTIC: Vitamin B3 can treat abnormal levels of blood fat to reduce low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol levels. Vitamin B3 can treat metabolic syndrome by increasing high-density lipoprotein (HDL) levels and reduce triglycerides. Combining niacin with a omega-3 fatty acids improves the result. DEFICIENCY: As with vitamins in general, early manifestations of a deficiency are general and not specific. It can include poor appetite, weakness, and mouth sores. The classic niacin deficiency is pellagra which has a triad of symptoms: dermatitis, diarrhea, dementia. The dermatitis is dark and scaling. The diarrhea can be due to malabsorption. The dementia begins with insomnia, irritability, confusion, memory loss, and eventually psychosis. TOXICITY: High doses of vitamin B3 to treat hyperlipidemia has the common side effect of skin flushing and gastric irritation. With vitamin B3 doses of over 3 grams per day there can be more serious side effects such as liver problems, gout, digestive ulcers, vision loss, and heart rhythm problems. Long term (many years) of high doses can increase the risk of diabetes. DRUG INTERACTIONS: Long-term vitamin B3 can increase blood sugar levels which may decrease the effectiveness of diabetes drugs. Large doses of niacin can worsen gout and decrease the effectiveness of anti-gout medications (allopurinol). Niacin can lower blood pressure and taking it with the blood pressure drug clonidine can lower it too much. Current Medical and Diagnostic Treatment 2020, page 1297; wwww.webmd.com; ods.od.nih.gov",
      "exp_hant": "維生素B3有兩種形式：菸鹼酸（nicotinic acid）與菸鹼醯胺（niacinamide）。菸鹼酸的俗稱即為niacin。當菸鹼酸攝取量超過身體所需時，人體可將其轉化為菸鹼醯胺。兩種形式功能相同，但菸鹼酸是會引起血管擴張（皮膚潮紅、發紅）的形式。緩釋型菸鹼酸可減輕潮紅反應。菸鹼酸屬於條件性必需營養素，因為人體可透過飲食中的色胺酸自行合成。與所有B群維生素一樣，菸鹼酸為水溶性維生素。菸鹼酸是重要輔酶（菸鹼醯胺腺嘌呤二核苷酸及菸鹼醯胺腺嘌呤二核苷酸磷酸）的前驅物，這些輔酶對代謝十分重要。治療作用：維生素B3可用於治療血脂異常，以降低低密度脂蛋白（LDL）膽固醇濃度。維生素B3可透過提高高密度脂蛋白（HDL）濃度並降低三酸甘油酯，來治療代謝症候群。將菸鹼酸與Omega-3脂肪酸併用可提升療效。缺乏症：如同一般維生素缺乏，早期表現通常是非特異性的，可能包括食慾不振、虛弱及口腔潰瘍。典型的菸鹼酸缺乏症為糙皮病（pellagra），其三大症狀為皮膚炎、腹瀉、失智。皮膚炎表現為暗沉並脫屑；腹瀉可能因吸收不良所致；失智則從失眠、易怒、意識混亂、記憶喪失開始，最終可能發展為精神病。毒性：以高劑量維生素B3治療高血脂時，常見的副作用為皮膚潮紅與胃部刺激。若維生素B3劑量每日超過3公克，可能出現更嚴重的副作用，如肝臟問題、痛風、消化性潰瘍、視力喪失及心律問題。長期（多年）高劑量使用可能增加罹患糖尿病的風險。藥物交互作用：長期使用維生素B3可能提高血糖濃度，進而降低糖尿病藥物的療效。大劑量菸鹼酸可能使痛風惡化，並降低抗痛風藥物（如allopurinol）的療效。菸鹼酸可降低血壓，若與降血壓藥物clonidine併用，可能使血壓降得過低。《現行醫學診斷與治療》，2020年版，第1297頁；www.webmd.com；ods.od.nih.gov"
    },
    {
      "number": 568,
      "question_en": "Which of the following are trace minerals?",
      "question_hant": "下列何者屬於微量礦物質？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "zinc, fluoride, iron",
          "hant": "鋅、氟、鐵",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "iodine, calcium, magnesium",
          "hant": "碘、鈣、鎂",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "chloride, chromium, molybdenum",
          "hant": "氯、鉻、鉬",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "selenium, potassium, phosporus",
          "hant": "硒、鉀、磷",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Minerals are classified as macrominerals (calcium, phosphorus, sodium, potassium, magnesium, sulfur and chloride), trace minerals or microminerals (iron, copper, cobalt, iodine, zinc, molybdenum, fluoride, selenium) and ultra trace elements (boron, chromium, arsenic, silicon and nickel). Generally, minerals assist in the conversion of food into energy, prevent dehydration, regulate heart and thyroid function, and the muscular and nervous systems. Macrominerals are needed for fluid balance, nerve transmission, and muscle contraction. They regulate blood pressure. They maintain the health of teeth, bones and connective tissue. Trace minerals are essential for growth and development because they are involved in oxygen transport and various metabolic functions. Minerals function as coenzymes. That is, they participate in all enzyme reactions in the body and assist in the assimilation and use of vitamins and other nutrients. Generally, minerals are absorbed by plants from the soil and enter the body through diet. Many common disorders can be caused by a mineral deficiency: hypocalcemia and osteoporosis (calcium deficiency), low calcium in blood (severe magnesium deficiency), anemia (iron deficiency), poor immune system and increased susceptibility to illness (poor selenium status), goiter (iodine deficiency), hypophosphatemia (low phosphorus levels). Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 48-49, 54; www.webmd.com.",
      "exp_hant": "礦物質可分為巨量礦物質（鈣、磷、鈉、鉀、鎂、硫及氯）、微量礦物質（鐵、銅、鈷、碘、鋅、鉬、氟、硒）及超微量元素（硼、鉻、砷、矽及鎳）。一般而言，礦物質能協助將食物轉化為能量、預防脫水、調節心臟與甲狀腺功能，以及肌肉與神經系統的運作。巨量礦物質為維持體液平衡、神經傳導及肌肉收縮所必需，並能調節血壓，維持牙齒、骨骼及結締組織的健康。微量礦物質因參與氧氣運輸及各種代謝功能，對生長發育至關重要。礦物質可作為輔酶，也就是說，它們參與體內所有酶反應，並協助維生素及其他營養素的吸收利用。一般而言，礦物質由植物從土壤中吸收，再經由飲食進入人體。許多常見疾病可由礦物質缺乏所引起：低血鈣症與骨質疏鬆症（缺鈣）、血中低鈣（嚴重缺鎂）、貧血（缺鐵）、免疫力低落及易感染（硒狀態不佳）、甲狀腺腫（缺碘）、低磷血症（磷濃度過低）。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，第48-49、54頁；www.webmd.com。"
    },
    {
      "number": 569,
      "question_en": "A 49 year-old patient comes to your office complaining of anxiety and high stress. She was recently told by her Integrative medicine doctor that she has high cholesterol and was given time release Niacin 500mg BID. He wants her to work up to taking it 3x day, but the patient is having horrible flushing from the niacin that causes a lot of sweating. What OTC drug or supplement can be used to offset the Niacin flush?",
      "question_hant": "一位49歲病人前來就診，主訴焦慮及高壓力。她最近被整合醫學醫師告知患有高膽固醇，並開立了緩釋型菸鹼酸500毫克，每日兩次服用。醫師希望她逐漸增加到每日三次，但該病人服用菸鹼酸後出現嚴重的潮紅反應，並伴隨大量出汗。可使用下列哪種非處方藥物或補充品來抵消菸鹼酸引起的潮紅反應？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
