          "en": "Fiber Supplements",
          "hant": "纖維補充品",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Laxatives",
          "hant": "瀉藥",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Antacids",
          "hant": "制酸劑",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This also applies with other anti-inflammatory NSAIDs. Coadministration of Niacin with Aspirin causes a competitive inhibition and reduces cutaneous flushing. Ding et al's study on pharmacokinetics found that \"salicylic acid causes a concentration-dependent decrease of total nicotinic acid clearance that results in the saturation (and effective elimination) of the nicotinuric acid conjugation pathway. \" This combination is commonly used by health care professionals at a dose of 325mg of Aspirin per day, in divided doses. Caution is warranted in those at risk for bleeding given a theoretical possibility of an additive interaction between these two agents. Herb, Nutrient, and Drug Interactions: Clinical Implications and Therapeutic Strategies, 2008, Stargrove, Treasure, and McKee, pages 287-8",
      "exp_hant": "這也適用於其他非類固醇消炎藥（NSAIDs）。菸鹼酸與阿斯匹靈併用會產生競爭性抑制作用，減少皮膚潮紅反應。Ding等人針對藥物動力學所做的研究發現：「水楊酸會以濃度依存的方式降低菸鹼酸的總清除率，導致菸尿酸結合途徑達到飽和（進而有效地被清除）。」醫療專業人員常用此組合，每日以分次劑量服用325毫克阿斯匹靈。由於這兩種藥物理論上可能有加成的交互作用，對有出血風險的病人應謹慎使用。《藥草、營養素與藥物交互作用：臨床意涵與治療策略》，2008年，Stargrove、Treasure與McKee合著，第287-8頁"
    },
