          "en": "removes electrons from free radicals",
          "hant": "從自由基中移除電子",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "stabilizes cellular osmosis",
          "hant": "穩定細胞滲透作用",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "provides electrons to free radicals",
          "hant": "提供電子給自由基",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Vitamins are antioxidants. Antioxidant which means vitamins protect the cells from oxidation. For example, when an apple is cut and exposed to oxygen it starts to decompose and turn brown. This is a process of oxidation on a macro level. The atoms of healthy cells have paired electrons. Oxidation produces free-radicals which are group of atoms that have one or more unpaired electrons. To balance itself out, the free-radicals take electrons from healthy cells which then become injured. Free-radicals \"attack\" nearby molecules (proteins, lipids, carbohydrates, DNA). The \"attacked\" molecule loses its electron and thus also becomes a free radical itself. This begins a chain reaction. If free radicals overwhelm the body, then the result is oxidative stress. That is, there is an accumulation of free radicals greater than the body can neutralize. This can lead to premature aging and disease. The function of antioxidants is to provide the missing electron to a free-radical without the antioxidant becoming unstable itself. Antioxidants stabilize free-radicals. health.harvard.edu",
      "exp_hant": "維生素屬於抗氧化劑。所謂抗氧化，意指維生素能保護細胞免受氧化作用的傷害。舉例來說，當蘋果被切開並暴露於氧氣中時便開始腐敗變褐，這是巨觀層面的氧化過程。健康細胞的原子帶有成對的電子。氧化作用會產生自由基，也就是帶有一個或多個未成對電子的原子團。為了使自身達到平衡，自由基會從健康細胞中奪取電子，使該細胞受損。自由基會「攻擊」鄰近的分子（蛋白質、脂質、碳水化合物、DNA）。被「攻擊」的分子失去電子後，本身也變成自由基，於是展開連鎖反應。若自由基數量超過身體所能負荷，就會導致氧化壓力，也就是自由基的累積量超過身體所能中和的程度，這可能導致提早老化與疾病。抗氧化劑的功能是提供缺失的電子給自由基，而自身不會因此變得不穩定。抗氧化劑能使自由基趨於穩定。health.harvard.edu"
    },
