      "exp_en": "Infectious mononucleosis (IM) is also known as mono or glandular fever. It is an infection caused by the Epstein-Barr virus (EBV). The virus spreads through saliva, which is why it is also called the kissing disease. You can also get mono by being exposed to the virus through a cough/sneeze, sharing a glass or cutlery with a person who has been infected with EBV. Though you can get mono at any age, it often spreads mostly in teens and young adults. Symptoms of IM include fever, sore throat, and swollen lymph glands, swollen tonsils, a rash, and malaise. Complications include the spleen can become soft and swollen also (splenomegaly), jaundice, and hepatitis. The majority of patients improve within 2-4 weeks but there can be residual fatigue lasting months. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1610",
      "exp_hant": "傳染性單核球增多症（IM）又稱為「腺熱」或俗稱「單核症」，是由EB病毒（Epstein-Barr virus）所引起的感染。此病毒經由唾液傳播，因此也被稱為「接吻病」。也可能因咳嗽、打噴嚏，或與感染EB病毒者共用杯子或餐具而感染。雖然任何年齡都可能感染單核症，但大多發生於青少年及年輕成人。傳染性單核球增多症的症狀包括發燒、喉嚨痛、淋巴結腫大、扁桃腺腫大、皮疹及倦怠感。併發症包括脾臟可能變軟腫大（脾腫大）、黃疸及肝炎。大多數病人在2至4週內會好轉，但可能殘留數月的疲勞感。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，第1610頁"
