      "exp_en": "He has postural hypotension from his blood pressure medication reducing his blood pressure too much. In postural hypotension the BP suddenly falls when the patient stands causing dizziness and falls. He also likely has cirrhosis of the liver. Cirrhosis is a late stage fibrosis (scarring) of the liver. Cirrhosis is caused by different types of liver diseases (hepatitis, fatty liver) and conditions (chronic alcoholism). The scarring eventually prevents the liver from functioning properly. The scar tissue blocks liver blood flow and slows down its processing of hormones, nutrients, drugs, and naturally produced body toxins. Symptoms of cirrhosis include poor appetite, fatigue, weight loss or sudden weight gain, bruises, jaundice, itchy skin, edema (ankles, legs, abdomen), urine with an orange tint, light colored stools, blood in stool, confusion, and personality changes. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 695, 715",
      "exp_hant": "他的降血壓藥物使血壓下降過多，導致姿勢性低血壓。姿勢性低血壓是指病人站立時血壓驟然下降，引起頭暈與跌倒。他也很可能罹患肝硬化。肝硬化是肝臟晚期的纖維化（結疤）病變，可由多種肝臟疾病（肝炎、脂肪肝）及情況（慢性酗酒）所引起。結疤組織最終會妨礙肝臟正常運作，阻塞肝臟血流，並減緩其對荷爾蒙、營養素、藥物及體內自然產生毒素的代謝處理。肝硬化的症狀包括食慾不振、疲勞、體重減輕或突然增加、瘀傷、黃疸、皮膚搔癢、水腫（腳踝、腿部、腹部）、尿液呈橘色、糞便顏色變淺、糞便帶血、意識混亂及性格改變。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學從業人員教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第695、715頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 582,
      "question_en": "A 16 year-old patient has been brought to the clinic by his mother. She insists he should be tested for drugs. His grades have been terrible at school. She does not approve of his friends who she says are \"terrible\". The mother says that his grades have fallen during the past two months. She says that his teachers have commented to her that he appears \"zoned out\" in class and often falls asleep. She has noticed the same thing but she also says that he has been very busy with both school and helping her recover from a recent hip-replacement surgery. The doctor then interviews him without the mother present. He denies fatigue, has normal sleep, and takes occasional naps during the day when he has football practice. He says that he has been very responsible. He has taken his mother to physical therapy and has picked up her medications from the pharmacy for her. When asked about substance abuse, he says that he occasionally binge drinks and uses marijuana. He does not want you to tell his mother about his use of occasional drugs. He says that his mother had it rough and has been in a lot of pain. He denies depression or sadness. He reports that school has been more difficult since his mother's surgery. He denies taking any medication, vitamins, or OTC drugs. The doctor then just talked to the mother. She says that the post-surgery pain was less than she anticipated. She only needed to take medications for a few days. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位16歲病人由母親帶到診所，母親堅持要求為他做藥物檢驗。他的在校成績變得很差，母親也不認同他的朋友，認為他們「很糟糕」。母親說他的成績在過去兩個月內下滑，老師也向她反映他上課時常「恍神」，並經常打瞌睡。她自己也注意到同樣的情形，但也表示他最近既要應付學業，又要幫忙照顧她剛做完髖關節置換手術後的復原，非常忙碌。醫師接著在母親不在場的情況下單獨訪談這位病人。他否認疲勞，睡眠正常，只有在有美式足球練習的白天偶爾小睡。他表示自己一直很負責任，曾帶母親去做物理治療，也幫她到藥局領藥。當被問及物質濫用時，他表示自己偶爾會狂飲及使用大麻，但不希望醫師告訴母親他偶爾用藥的事。他說母親一直過得很辛苦，也承受很多疼痛。他否認有憂鬱或悲傷的情緒，並表示自母親手術以來學校課業變得更加吃力。他否認服用任何藥物、維生素或非處方藥物。之後醫師單獨與母親談話，母親表示術後疼痛比她預期的要輕，只服用了幾天的止痛藥。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
