      "exp_en": "There is an inconsistency between the mother's version and the son's version regarding her surgery and her use of pain medication. This points to him using his mother's prescription pain medication which would account for his \"zoning out\" during class. He does have a general substance abuse problem but in this case he is most likely abusing his mother's prescription drugs. In many states the doctor need not report to the mother about his drug use unless there is the possibility of hurting himself or another person. Most states allow minors to consent for care related to alcohol and drug abuse without getting the permission of the parent. The doctor can assure him of confidentiality and assist him in his care. The doctor should directly ask him if he has been taking his mother's pain medication and what was his emotional experience when his mother had surgery. However, the confidentiality agreement with adolescents needs to be broken if the doctor determines that he is at risk of harming himself or others. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 151-153",
      "exp_hant": "母親的說法與兒子的說法在她手術後及止痛藥使用情形上出現不一致。這暗示他可能一直在使用母親的處方止痛藥，這也能解釋他上課「恍神」的原因。他確實存在一般性的物質濫用問題，但就本案例而言，他最可能濫用的是母親的處方藥物。在許多州，除非有傷害自己或他人的可能，醫師無需將其用藥情形告知母親。大多數州允許未成年人在未經父母同意的情況下，自行同意接受與酒精及藥物濫用相關的照護。醫師可以向他保證保密，並協助其接受照護。醫師應直接詢問他是否一直在服用母親的止痛藥，以及母親手術期間他的情緒感受為何。然而，若醫師判斷他有傷害自己或他人的風險，則與青少年之間的保密協議必須被打破。《家庭護理師臨床病例研究》，Leslie Neal-Boylan著，2011年，第151-153頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 583,
      "question_en": "A 42 year-old male presents with a cough which he has had for 10 days. At first the cough was associated with fever. He expectorates green sputum on occasion and now the sputum has streaks of blood. He has increased shortness of breath with exertion. His cough interferes with his sleep. Several co-workers are also sick. He denies ear pain, sinus congestion, sore throat, palpitations, constipation, diarrhea, dysuria, and swelling of his limbs. He has been smoking 2 packs of cigarettes per day since he was 14 years old. He is taking medication for his hypertension . PHYSICAL EXAM: BP 150/95 mm Hg; HR 90 bpm and regular; respiratory rate 24 breaths/min; temperature is 101.5 F. Nasal mucosa is pink; sinuses are non-tender. Oral mucosa is pink with no enlarged tonsils and pharynx without exudates. Neck is without thyromegaly and there is no cervical supra-cervical lymphadenopathy. Symmetric thorax with increased AP diameter; Lungs are hyper resonant; wheezes in all lung fields; no egophony; has rales but no rhonchi. Based on the preceding history and limited physical examination prior to lab tests what is the most likely disease state?",
      "question_hant": "一位42歲男性出現咳嗽已10天。最初咳嗽伴隨發燒，偶爾咳出綠色痰液，現在痰中出現血絲，且活動時呼吸急促加劇，咳嗽也影響他的睡眠。有幾位同事也生病了。他否認耳痛、鼻竇充血、喉嚨痛、心悸、便秘、腹瀉、排尿困難及肢體腫脹。他自14歲起每天抽兩包菸，目前正服用高血壓藥物。理學檢查：血壓150/95 mmHg；心跳每分鐘90次，規律；呼吸速率每分鐘24次；體溫101.5°F。鼻黏膜呈粉紅色，鼻竇無壓痛。口腔黏膜呈粉紅色，扁桃腺無腫大，咽部無滲出物。頸部無甲狀腺腫大，也無頸部淋巴結腫大。胸廓對稱，前後徑增加；肺部叩診過度共鳴；全肺野可聞及喘鳴音，無胸膜摩擦音（egophony），有囉音但無鼾音。根據上述病史及檢驗前的理學檢查，最可能的疾病狀態為何？",
