      "exp_en": "He has a brain abscess which is a clump of pus, immune cells, and other substances in the brain. This is usually a result of a bacterial or fungal infection. This can lead to a swelling and inflammation. Infected brain cells, white blood cells, and both live and dead collect in an area of the brain where tissue forms around and creates a mass (abscess). This is a very serious condition. The signs and symptoms of a brain abscess vary, depending on where in the brain it is located. His diabetes made the infection worse and more severe. Glen was given the wrong antibiotic (amoxillin). He originally needed the drug Augmentin which is a combination of amoxicillin and clavulanate potassium and is used to treat bacterial infections in the airways (sinus infection or pneumonia) and brain infections. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 116, 707",
      "exp_hant": "他患有腦膿瘍，這是腦部聚集的一團膿液、免疫細胞及其他物質，通常是細菌或黴菌感染所致，可導致腫脹與發炎。受感染的腦細胞、白血球及存活與死亡的細胞會聚集在腦部某一區域，周圍形成組織，形成一個團塊（膿瘍），這是相當嚴重的病症。腦膿瘍的徵象與症狀依其在腦部的位置而異。他的糖尿病使感染更嚴重、更惡化。葛倫被開立了錯誤的抗生素（amoxicillin），他原本需要的是Augmentin，這是amoxicillin與clavulanate potassium的複方藥物，用於治療呼吸道（鼻竇感染或肺炎）及腦部感染的細菌感染。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學從業人員教科書》，2007年，Robinson著，第116、707頁"
