      "exp_en": "Focal dystonia, a neurological disorder, affects a muscle (or group of muscles) and causes involuntary muscular contractions and abnormal body postures. The contractions cause the muscle to move involuntarily, resulting in repetitive movements or abnormal postures. The cause is not known but it is believed to be due a misfiring of neurons in the sensorimotor cortex. Early symptoms can include leg dragging, foot cramping, blinking uncontrollably, speech problems, involuntarily movement of the neck. Torticollis is a common form of dystonia. Writer's cramp is dystonia that occurs only when writing. There is also musician focal dystonia. Dystonias are classified by which body area is affected: 1) generalized dystonia affects the whole body. 2) focal dystonia affects only one muscle group. 3) multifocal dystonia affects two unrelated body areas. 4) segmental dystonia affects body parts near each other. This disorder affects about 1% of the population (women are more prone than men). The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1880",
      "exp_hant": "局部肌張力不全症是一種神經系統疾病，會影響單一肌肉（或一組肌肉），造成不自主的肌肉收縮及異常的身體姿勢。這些收縮使肌肉不自主地移動，導致重複性動作或異常姿勢。病因尚不明確，但一般認為與感覺運動皮質神經元的錯誤放電有關。早期症狀可能包括拖行、腳部抽筋、不自主眨眼、言語障礙及頸部不自主運動。斜頸是肌張力不全症的常見表現形式；書寫痙攣則是僅在書寫時發生的肌張力不全症；此外還有音樂家局部肌張力不全症。肌張力不全症依受影響的身體部位分類：1）全身型肌張力不全影響全身；2）局部型肌張力不全只影響一組肌肉；3）多灶型肌張力不全影響兩個不相關的身體部位；4）節段型肌張力不全影響相鄰的身體部位。此病影響約1%的人口（女性較男性更易罹患）。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，第1880頁"
