      "exp_en": "Dysfunctional uterine bleeding (DUB) is irregular bleeding from the uterus. There can be polymenorrhea (menstrual cycle is less than 21 days long), menorrhagia (abnormally heavy bleeding at menstruation), hypermenorrhea (excessive long menstruation), or metrorrhagia (bleeding outside of the menstrual cycle) between periods. The hallmark characteristic of DUB is that it is a disorder of function (estrogen production unopposed by progesterone) and not of structure changes (fibroids, cancer, etc). Part of the diagnosis involves ruling out other causes of the bleeding (miscarriage, ectopic pregnancy, fibroids, etc.). A pelvic exam, ultrasound, and blood tests can be ordered. Treatment for DUB usually involves oral contraceptives and medicines to control bleeding. Surgical treatment is only advised when bleeding cannot be controlled with medicine or hormone therapy. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2077",
      "exp_hant": "功能性子宮出血（DUB）是指子宮不規則出血，可能表現為月經過頻（月經週期少於21天）、月經過多（經期出血量異常增多）、經期過長（月經持續時間異常延長），或經間期出血（兩次月經之間出血）。功能性子宮出血的主要特徵，是其屬於功能性障礙（雌激素分泌未受黃體素拮抗），而非結構性病變（如肌瘤、癌症等）所致。診斷的一部分是排除其他造成出血的原因（流產、子宮外孕、肌瘤等），可安排骨盆腔檢查、超音波及血液檢查。功能性子宮出血的治療通常包括口服避孕藥及控制出血的藥物；只有當出血無法以藥物或荷爾蒙療法控制時，才會建議手術治療。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，第2077頁"
