        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "place person in recovery position",
          "hant": "將病人置於復甦姿勢",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "check person for any injury",
          "hant": "檢查病人是否受傷",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "help patient slowly sit and give water",
          "hant": "協助病人慢慢坐起並給予飲水",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A fainting patient can appear pale, feel dizzy, feel weak, and begin to sweat. Sometimes it is possible to prevent fainting by having the patient sit down with their head near their knees or have the patient lie on their back. If there is fainting first check for responsiveness and for normal breathing. If that is OK, check their body from head to toe for any injury that could occur from the fall. If there are no injuries, place the patient in the recovery position and loosen any tight clothing. In the recovery position: 1) Extend the patient's arm closest to you and place it about their head. 2) Roll the patient toward yourself onto the side of the patient so that their head rests on their extended arm. 3) Bend both their knees to stabilize the body. If there are any injuries call 911. If the patient is unresponsive or is not breathing or gasping for air, then begin CPR immediately and use an AED (Automated External Defibrillator) if you are trained in these skills. First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 29, 86",
      "exp_hant": "暈倒的病人可能面色蒼白、感到頭暈、感覺虛弱，並開始出汗。有時可透過讓病人坐下、頭部靠近膝蓋，或讓病人平躺，來預防暈倒發生。若發生暈倒，應先檢查病人的反應能力及呼吸是否正常。若無異狀，應從頭到腳檢查病人是否因跌倒而受傷。若沒有受傷，可將病人置於復甦姿勢並鬆開緊身的衣物。復甦姿勢步驟：1）將病人靠近你這一側的手臂伸直，放置於頭部附近；2）將病人朝自己這一側翻轉至側臥，使其頭部枕在伸直的手臂上；3）彎曲病人雙膝以穩定身體。若有任何傷勢應撥打911。若病人無反應、沒有呼吸或呼吸喘促，應立即開始CPR，並在受過訓練的情況下使用AED（自動體外心臟去顫器）。《急救／CPR／AED學員手冊》，紅十字會，2016年，第29、86頁"
    },
    {
