      "exp_en": "BACK STRIKES: With choking give a 5 back strikes or blows between the shoulder blades. Position yourself behind the person on their side. Put one arm diagonally across the chest of the person to give support. Bend the person forward at the waist with the body of the person as parallel to the ground as much as possible. Firmly strike the area between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand. Each back strike should be separate from the others. For a child, you might need to kneel. ABDOMINAL THRUSTS: Stand behind the person with one foot in front of the other to give yourself balance and stability. Reach around the person's waist. Position one clenched fist above the navel and below the rib cage. Grasp your fist with your other hand. Pull the clenched fist sharply and directly backward and upward under the rib cage quickly. Continue uninterrupted until the obstruction is relieved or advanced life support is available. In either case, the person should be examined by a healthcare provider as soon as possible. Each thrust should be separate from the others. First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 63",
      "exp_hant": "拍背法：發生哽塞時，先在肩胛骨之間拍打或敲擊5次。站在患者側後方，一手斜放於患者胸前給予支撐，讓患者上半身盡量前彎，使身體與地面接近平行，再以掌根用力拍打肩胛骨之間的區域，每次拍背動作應各自獨立分開進行。若對象是兒童，可能需要蹲下操作。腹部推擠法：站在患者身後，雙腳前後張開以保持平衡與穩定，雙手環繞患者腰部，一手握拳放在肚臍上方、肋骨下方，另一手握住該拳頭，快速用力地將拳頭向後上方朝肋骨下方拉擠，持續不間斷地進行，直到異物排出或高級救命術到位為止。無論哪種情況，都應儘快讓病人接受醫療人員檢查。每次推擠動作應各自獨立分開進行。《急救／CPR／AED學員手冊》，紅十字會，2016年，第63頁"
