    {
      "number": 601,
      "question_en": "What are the two most common types of arrhythmias that an AED (Automatic External Defibrillator) treats?",
      "question_hant": "AED（自動體外心臟去顫器）主要治療的兩種最常見心律不整為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "ventricular tachycardia and premature atrial contractions",
          "hant": "心室頻脈與心房早期收縮",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "ventricular fibrillation and ventricular tachycardia",
          "hant": "心室顫動與心室頻脈",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "ventricular fibrillation and supraventricular arrhythmias",
          "hant": "心室顫動與室上性心律不整",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "supraventricular arrhythmias and premature atrial contractions",
          "hant": "室上性心律不整與心房早期收縮",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The types of arrhythmias that an AED will treat are usually limited to ventricular fibrillation (VF) and ventricular tachycardia (VT). These two types are shockable cardiac arrhythmia treatable by an AED. In a cardiac arrest, the heart is electrically active but is in a dysfunctional irregular pattern that prevents the heart from pumping and circulating blood. In ventricular fibrillation (VF), the heart rhythm is chaotic (fibrillating). The heart quivers instead of contracts. It then becomes unable to pump blood to the body and brain. Once a heart has entered VF, sudden cardiac arrest occurs. In ventricular tachycardia (VT) the heart beats too fast to effectively pump blood. Ultimately, ventricular tachycardia leads to ventricular fibrillation. The purpose of the electrical shock from the AED is to re-establish a normal heart rhythm when it become irregular in VF and VT. With cardiac arrest (unresponsive patient, no pulse, no breathing) an AED should be applied as soon as possible. An AED prompts the user to manually deliver a defibrillation shock if it determines that one is needed. Early uses increases survival rate. Basic Life Support, Participant Manual, American Red Cross, 2019, page 23",
      "exp_hant": "AED所能治療的心律不整類型，通常僅限於心室顫動（VF）與心室頻脈（VT），這兩種是AED可電擊治療的心律不整。在心臟停止時，心臟雖有電流活動，卻呈現功能失調的不規則模式，導致心臟無法有效泵送與循環血液。在心室顫動（VF）中，心律呈現混亂（顫動）狀態，心臟只是顫動而非收縮，因而無法將血液泵送至全身及腦部。一旦心臟進入心室顫動，便會發生猝發性心臟停止。在心室頻脈（VT）中，心跳過快而無法有效泵送血液，最終心室頻脈會演變為心室顫動。AED電擊的目的，是在心律因心室顫動或心室頻脈而變得不規則時，重新建立正常的心律。發生心臟停止（病人無反應、無脈搏、無呼吸）時，應儘快使用AED。若AED判斷需要電擊，會提示使用者手動施予去顫電擊。及早使用可提高存活率。《基本救命術學員手冊》，美國紅十字會，2019年，第23頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 602,
      "question_en": "In a sudden cardiac arrest (SCA), for every 1-minute of delay in the application of CPR and an AED the survival rate is reduced by",
