      "exp_en": "In a sudden cardiac arrest (unresponsive patient, no pulse, no breathing) every second counts. A person with SCA first loses their pulse, then consciousness, and then breathing.When the heart stops then breathing will soon stop. The organs will not receive oxygen. Without oxygen brain damage begins between 4 to 6 minutes. After 8 to 10 minutes brain damage becomes irreversible. Shortly thereafter death occurs if the person does not receive emergency and immediate care. In an SCA the heart suddenly and unexpectedly stops beating due to a malfunction in the electrical system of the heart. The malfunction that causes a SCA is a life-threatening abnormal heart rhythm or arrhythmia. Once the pads are placed on the chest and the AED is turned on it guides the user through each step of the defibrillation process. The AED gives voice and/or visual prompts. AEDs are designed for easy use by any \"first responder\" in medical emergency. A \"first responder\" can be an EMS (emergency medical service)a worker, a firefighter or police officer, or it can be an acupuncturist or a layperson with minimal AED training. Basic Life Support, Participant Manual, American Red Cross, 2019, page 23",
      "exp_hant": "在猝發性心臟停止（病人無反應、無脈搏、無呼吸）的情況下，每一秒都至關重要。發生SCA的患者會先失去脈搏，接著失去意識，然後停止呼吸。當心臟停止跳動，呼吸也將很快停止，各器官將無法獲得氧氣。缺氧狀態下，腦損傷約於4至6分鐘後開始出現，8至10分鐘後腦損傷即成為不可逆，隨後不久若未獲得緊急且即時的照護，便會死亡。在SCA中，心臟因電氣系統故障而突然、意外地停止跳動，導致SCA的故障即為具生命威脅性的異常心律或心律不整。將貼片貼於胸口並開啟AED後，AED會逐步引導使用者完成去顫流程的每一步驟，並以語音及／或視覺提示指引操作。AED的設計目的，是讓任何在醫療緊急情況下的「第一線應變人員」都能輕鬆使用。「第一線應變人員」可以是緊急醫療服務（EMS）人員、消防員或警察，也可以是針灸師或僅接受過基本AED訓練的一般民眾。《基本救命術學員手冊》，美國紅十字會，2019年，第23頁"
    },
