      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Gua sha is generally contraindicated in patients taking therapeutic anticoagulants. The INR (International Normalized Ratio) is a test that measures how long it takes for blood to clot. The higher the INR, the longer it takes for blood to clot. Gua sha is not contraindicated in patients with stable INR. Gua sha should be applied to clear skin only, not on rashes, lesions, infections, swellings, or broken skin. With patients taking NSAIDS, vitamin E, fish oils or patients who have bleeding disorders, gua sha should be applied with awareness by the acupuncturist who is able to evaluate subcutaneous bleeding and tissue response. As such, it is a critical recommendation to take a careful patient history regarding medications, supplements, bleeding disorders. The practitioner should follow standard precaution, maintain a clean field, and follow hand sanitation guidelines when applying gua sha. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 53",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且最正確的答案。刮痧一般禁忌用於正在服用治療性抗凝血劑的病人。國際標準化比值（INR）是一項測量血液凝固所需時間的檢驗，INR數值越高，血液凝固所需時間越長。對於INR穩定的病人，刮痧並非禁忌。刮痧只應施行於乾淨完整的皮膚上，不應施行於皮疹、病灶、感染、腫脹或破損的皮膚上。對於服用非類固醇消炎藥、維生素E、魚油，或有出血性疾病的病人，施行刮痧時，針灸師應具備評估皮下出血及組織反應的能力，謹慎進行。因此，仔細詢問病人的用藥史、補充品使用情形及出血性疾病史，是一項關鍵性建議。施行刮痧時，執業人員應遵循標準防護措施，維持清潔的操作區域，並遵守洗手消毒規範。《潔淨針法》，第7版，第53頁"
