      "exp_en": "Retain the lit moxa stick at least one hour in the extinguisher to ensure that the moxa stick is out. Put all moxa cones or moxa sticks that have not been flushed down the sink in a metal bucket with a tight metal lid after the one hour extinguishing period. Alternatively, use a metal receptacle that is used to get rid of cigarettes. When the metal bucket or cigarette container is 3/4 full you can dispose in the regular trash. Moxa sticks can be used in a couple of ways. 1) hold the stick 2-3 cm (around one inch) over the skin for about 15 minutes or do the treatment until the skin is slightly red to the touch of the acupuncturist. 2) the moxa stick is moved up and down over the point or circling around the acupuncture needle. During treatment, every few minutes tap any ash from the moxa stick into the moxa extinguisher. Even with moxa stick treatment, hand washing prior to treatment is a critical recommendation. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 110, 111",
