      "exp_en": "The patient must be informed that the state health department needs to be notified of sexually transmitted diseases.The state needs to know for surveillance and infection control. Patient confidentiality and ethical consideration require that her mother not be contacted without her consent. The information can be reported by the physician or by a physician designated appointee. It is a state and federal law that STIs be reported in a timely fashion. Partner reporting can be done by the patient contacting her partners for referral, diagnosis, and treatment. Another option is for the health department to contact her partners if she is not willing to do so herself. The health department will not identify her to the partners. Case Files in Family Medicine, Toy, Briscoe, Britton, Heidelbaugh, Fourth edition, page 91, 92, 97",
