      "exp_en": "The piriformis is a muscle located deep in the hip that runs in close proximity to the sciatic nerve. When the piriformis muscle becomes tight and/or inflamed, it can cause irritation of the sciatic nerve. This irritation leads to sciatica-like pain, tingling and numbness that run from the lower back, to the rear and sometimes down the leg and into the foot. Piriformis is a flat muscle and the most superficial muscle of the deep gluteal muscles. The piriformis muscle is part of the lateral rotators of the hip (obturator internus, superior and inferior gemelli, quadratus femoris, obturator externus, and gluteus maximus). The gluteus maximus muscle extends and laterally rotates the hip joint. The gluteus minimus muscle helps with abduction (movement away from the midline of the body) and medial (inward) rotation of the thigh at the hip. The psoas muscle flexes the thigh at the hip. tcmtests.com, August 2020",
      "exp_hant": "梨狀肌是位於髖部深處的一條肌肉，緊鄰坐骨神經走行。當梨狀肌變得緊繃或發炎時，可能刺激坐骨神經，這種刺激會導致從下背部延伸至臀部，有時甚至向下延伸至腿部及足部的坐骨神經痛樣疼痛、刺痛與麻木感。梨狀肌是一條扁平的肌肉，也是深層臀肌群中最淺層的一條，屬於髖部外旋肌群的一部分（其他外旋肌包括閉孔內肌、上孖肌、下孖肌、股方肌、閉孔外肌及臀大肌）。臀大肌可使髖關節伸展並向外旋轉；臀小肌則協助髖部大腿的外展（遠離身體中線的動作）及內旋；腰肌則使髖部大腿屈曲。tcmtests.com，2020年8月"
