      "exp_en": "Upon closer examination of the stomach, the muscular folds called rugae make up the stomach lining and are clearly visible. The rugae gradually smooth out as the stomach fills, permitting stomach distension and expansion. The pyloric sphincter acts as a valve and regulates the flow of partially digested food from the stomach to the duodenum. The muscularis layer is one of the four layers that line the digestive tract. The fundus is the base of the stomach. tcmtests.com, January 2020",
      "exp_hant": "仔細觀察胃部可見，稱為胃皺襞的肌肉皺褶構成胃黏膜並清晰可見。當胃部充盈時，胃皺襞會逐漸展平，使胃得以擴張。幽門括約肌如同一個閥門，調節部分消化的食物由胃流入十二指腸。肌層是消化道管壁四層結構之一。胃底是胃的基部。tcmtests.com，2020年1月"
