      ],
      "exp_en": "A blood type (also called a blood group) is a classification of blood based on the presence or absence of inherited antigenic substances on the surface of red blood cells (RBCs). Blood types are inherited and represent contributions from both parents. Blood types are determined by the presence or absence of certain antigens that can trigger an immune response if they are foreign to the body. Since some antigens can trigger the immune system to attack the blood that is being transfused, it is important to ensure that blood transfusions are based on blood typing. The ABO blood type system is the most important blood type classification. There are four major groups based on the presence or absence of two antigens, A and B, on the surface of red blood cells. In addition, there is a protein called the Rh factor, which can be either present (+) or absent (-), creating the 8 most common blood types (A+, A-, B+, B-, O+, O-, AB+, AB-). tcmtests.com, March 2020",
      "exp_hant": "血型（亦稱血型群）是根據紅血球表面是否存在遺傳性抗原物質來分類血液的方式。血型是遺傳而來，代表父母雙方的基因貢獻。血型是由某些抗原的有無決定的，若這些抗原對身體而言是外來的，便可能引發免疫反應。由於某些抗原可能促使免疫系統攻擊輸入的血液，因此輸血時必須依血型配對，這一點非常重要。ABO血型系統是最重要的血型分類法，依紅血球表面A、B兩種抗原的有無分為四大類。此外，還有一種稱為Rh因子的蛋白質，可為陽性(+)或陰性(-)，因而形成8種最常見的血型（A+、A-、B+、B-、O+、O-、AB+、AB-）。tcmtests.com，2020年3月"
    },
