      "exp_en": "Albumin is a general term for a type of protein that is water soluble. The two most familiar examples of albumin can be found in egg whites and in human blood. In the human body albumin helps to transport essential fatty acids from adipose tissue to muscle tissue. Albumin also contributes to the regulation of osmosis, helps to transport hormones, drugs, and other substances through the blood. tcmtests.com, March 2020",
      "exp_hant": "白蛋白是一種水溶性蛋白質的統稱，最常見的例子分別存在於蛋白與人體血液中。在人體內，白蛋白有助於將必需脂肪酸從脂肪組織運送至肌肉組織，也參與滲透壓的調節，並協助荷爾蒙、藥物及其他物質經血液運輸。tcmtests.com，2020年3月"
