      "exp_en": "The renin enzyme circulates in the blood stream and breaks down angiotensinogen secreted from the liver into angiotensin I. Angiotensin I is further broken down in the lungs by the ACE enzyme (endothelial-bound angiotensin-converting enzyme) into angiotensin II. Angiotensin II is a potent constrictor of all blood vessels. It acts on the smooth muscle thereby raising the resistance posed by these arteries to the heart. tcmtests.com, January 2020",
      "exp_hant": "腎素在血流中循環，將肝臟分泌的血管收縮素原分解為血管收縮素I。血管收縮素I再於肺部經ACE酶（附著於內皮細胞的血管收縮素轉化酶）進一步分解為血管收縮素II。血管收縮素II是強效的全身血管收縮劑，作用於平滑肌，提高動脈對心臟的阻力。tcmtests.com，2020年1月"
