      "exp_en": "Vital capacity is the maximum amount of air an individual can expel from the lungs after a maximum inhalation. Residual volume is the air still remaining in the lungs after maximum expiration. Tidal volume is the air exchanged during normal inspiration and expiration. Expiratory reserve volume is the air that can be expired after normal expiration (tidal volume expiration). Inspiratory reserve volume is the air that can be inspired passed normal inspiration (tidal volume inspiration). Total lung capacity is the maximum volume of air the lungs can hold. It is measured by the total amount of air in the lungs after taking the deepest breath possible. tcmtests.com, November 2020",
      "exp_hant": "肺活量是個體在最大吸氣後，能從肺部呼出的最大氣體量。殘餘容積是最大呼氣後仍留在肺中的空氣量。潮氣容積是正常吸氣與呼氣時交換的空氣量。呼氣儲備容積是在正常呼氣（潮氣呼氣）之後仍可再呼出的空氣量。吸氣儲備容積是在正常吸氣（潮氣吸氣）之後仍可再吸入的空氣量。肺總量是肺部所能容納的最大空氣量，以盡力深吸一口氣後肺中空氣的總量來測定。tcmtests.com，2020年11月"
    },
    {
