        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "antidiuretic hormone",
          "hant": "抗利尿激素",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Aldosterone is a steroid hormone secreted by the adrenal glands. Aldosterone serves as the main regulator of the salt and water balance in the body. The biological action of aldosterone is to increase the retention of sodium and water and to increase the excretion of potassium by the kidneys. It is categorized as a mineralocorticoid as it is produced in the adrenal cortex. Aldosterone is synthesized in the body from corticosterone which is derived from cholesterol. Aldosterone production is regulated by the renin-angiotensin system. Renin is secreted by the kidneys when there are changes in blood pressure and blood volume, and blood sodium and potassium levels. Renin acts on angiotensinogen (a protein) by splitting into angiotensin I. Angiotensin I is then converted to angiotensin II which stimulates the release of aldosterone from the adrenal glands. It is the antidiuretic hormone that tells the kidneys how much water to conserve. tcmtests.com, January 2020",
      "exp_hant": "醛固酮是由腎上腺分泌的一種類固醇激素，是體內鹽分與水分平衡的主要調節者。其生理作用是增加鈉與水的保留，並增加腎臟對鉀的排泄。因其產生於腎上腺皮質，故被歸類為礦物皮質激素。醛固酮是由源自膽固醇的皮質酮在體內合成而來。醛固酮的分泌受腎素-血管收縮素系統調控：當血壓、血容量及血中鈉鉀濃度發生變化時，腎臟會分泌腎素；腎素作用於血管收縮素原（一種蛋白質），將其裂解為血管收縮素I；血管收縮素I再轉化為血管收縮素II，進而刺激腎上腺釋放醛固酮。而告知腎臟應保留多少水分的，則是抗利尿激素。tcmtests.com，2020年1月"
