      "exp_en": "Red bone marrow helps produce blood cells. Yellow bone marrow helps to store fat. Red bone marrow is involved in hematopoiesis which is another name for blood cell production. Blood stem cells are also known as haematopoietic stem cells. Similar to other stem cells, they can self-renew. They also produce different types of cells found in the blood: both red blood cells and the many types of white blood cells needed by the immune system. tcmtests.com, March 2020",
      "exp_hant": "紅骨髓負責產生血球細胞，黃骨髓則負責儲存脂肪。紅骨髓參與造血作用，即血球生成的另一種說法。血液幹細胞又稱造血幹細胞，與其他幹細胞一樣具有自我更新的能力，並能產生血液中各種類型的細胞，包括紅血球以及免疫系統所需的多種白血球。tcmtests.com，2020年3月"
    },
    {
      "number": 641,
      "question_en": "Angiotensin causes the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone. What organ releases angiotensinogen?",
      "question_hant": "血管收縮素會使腎上腺皮質釋放醛固酮。哪個器官會釋放血管收縮素原？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "lung",
          "hant": "肺",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "blood vessels",
          "hant": "血管",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "liver",
          "hant": "肝臟",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "kidneys",
          "hant": "腎臟",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Angiotensinogen is a large protein produced by the liver. When blood pressure or volume falls, the kidneys release the enzyme renin, which cleaves angiotensinogen to form angiotensin I, a 10-amino-acid peptide. Angiotensin I is then converted into the active form, angiotensin II (an 8-amino-acid peptide), by angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE). ACE is found on the surface of endothelial cells in capillaries throughout the body, but it is particularly abundant in the lungs due to their extensive capillary network. Angiotensin II is a potent vasoconstrictor that raises systemic blood pressure. It also stimulates the adrenal cortex to release aldosterone, a hormone that promotes sodium reabsorption in the kidneys. This sodium retention leads to increased water retention, thereby expanding blood volume and helping restore blood pressure. Angiotensin II itself also directly stimulates thirst and the release of antidiuretic hormone (ADH). tcmtests.com, January 2020",
      "exp_hant": "血管收縮素原是由肝臟產生的一種大型蛋白質。當血壓或血容量下降時，腎臟會釋放腎素酶，將血管收縮素原裂解形成由10個胺基酸組成的血管收縮素I。血管收縮素I再經血管收縮素轉化酶（ACE）轉化為具活性的血管收縮素II（由8個胺基酸組成）。ACE存在於全身微血管內皮細胞表面，但因肺部微血管網絡極為豐富，故ACE在肺部特別多。血管收縮素II是強效的血管收縮劑，能提升全身血壓，並刺激腎上腺皮質釋放醛固酮，促進腎臟對鈉的再吸收。鈉的保留會導致水分保留增加，進而擴大血容量，協助恢復血壓。血管收縮素II本身也會直接刺激口渴感並促使抗利尿激素（ADH）釋放。tcmtests.com，2020年1月"
    },
    {
      "number": 642,
      "question_en": "During a viral infection you would expect to see increased numbers of",
      "question_hant": "在病毒感染期間，預期會看到何種細胞數量增加？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "neutrophils",
          "hant": "嗜中性球",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "eosinophils",
          "hant": "嗜酸性球",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "lymphocytes",
          "hant": "淋巴球",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "basophils",
          "hant": "嗜鹼性球",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Lymphocytes are small white blood cells that play a role in the immune response. They primarily reside in the lymph and lymph tissues. There are two main types of lymphocytes, known as B cells and T cells or also known as B lymphocytes and T lymphocytes. The B cells produce antibodies that attack foreign molecules. The T cells are more complicated, but they can attack the body's own cells when they are diseased. Basophils are white blood cells that help fight infections by releasing histamine and other chemicals that help dilate blood vessels when the immune response is triggered. Eosinophils are a type of white blood cell responsible for combating multicellular parasites and certain infections. Neutrophils are the most common form of white blood cell that respond to infection and heal damaged tissue. tcmtests.com, March 2020",
      "exp_hant": "淋巴球是一種小型白血球，在免疫反應中扮演重要角色，主要存在於淋巴液與淋巴組織中。淋巴球主要分為兩大類，稱為B細胞與T細胞（亦即B淋巴球與T淋巴球）。B細胞產生抗體以攻擊外來分子；T細胞的作用較為複雜，但當自身細胞發生病變時，T細胞也能加以攻擊。嗜鹼性球是一種白血球，於免疫反應被觸發時釋放組織胺及其他化學物質，協助擴張血管以對抗感染。嗜酸性球是負責對抗多細胞寄生蟲及某些感染的白血球。嗜中性球則是最常見的白血球，負責應對感染並修復受損組織。tcmtests.com，2020年3月"
    },
