      "exp_en": "KUB stands for Kidney, Ureters, and Bladder. A KUB X-ray can be ordered to help evaluate the urinary tract to provide information about the shape, size, and the position of the kidneys, ureters, and bladder. Also, a KUB X-ray is used to help diagnose the cause of abdominal pain. That is, KUB is typically used to evaluate GI conditions (bowel obstruction, masses, perforations, gallstones) and to help detect kidney stones. Further, the KUB is used to diagnose constipation as it is easy to see the stool. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Studies, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 1020; 4th Edition, page 1100",
      "exp_hant": "KUB代表腎臟（Kidney）、輸尿管（Ureters）與膀胱（Bladder）。醫師可安排KUB X光檢查以評估泌尿道，提供有關腎臟、輸尿管與膀胱的形狀、大小及位置等資訊。此外，KUB X光也用於協助診斷腹痛的原因，也就是說，KUB通常用來評估腸胃道病況（腸阻塞、腫塊、穿孔、膽結石）並協助偵測腎結石。再者，由於糞便在影像上容易辨識，KUB也可用於診斷便秘。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第1020頁；第4版，第1100頁"
