      "exp_en": "The antidiuretic hormone (ADH) is also known as vasopressin. The two main functions of ADH are 1) retain water in the body, and 2) constrict blood vessels. ADH helps regulate levels of water, glucose, and salts in the blood. ADH increases peripheral vascular resistance which then increases arterial blood pressure. It is synthesized in the hypothalamus and stored in the posterior pituitary and is released in the blood. ADH or vasopressin contributes to increased urine osmolality (increased concentration) and decreased water excretion. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 905; 4th Edition page 980",
      "exp_hant": "抗利尿激素（ADH）又稱為血管加壓素。ADH的兩項主要功能為：1）使體內保留水分；2）收縮血管。ADH有助於調節血液中水分、葡萄糖與鹽類的濃度，並能增加周邊血管阻力，進而提高動脈血壓。ADH是在下視丘合成，儲存於腦下垂體後葉，再釋放入血液中。ADH（血管加壓素）會使尿液滲透壓升高（濃度增加）並減少水分排出。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第905頁；第4版，第980頁"
    },
