      "exp_en": "The bones and the teeth are calcium reservoirs in the body. When blood levels of calcium decrease, PTH (parathryoid hormone) is triggered and signals the calcium reservoirs (bone and teeth) to release calcium in the blood. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 132-135; 4th Edition, page 148-150",
      "exp_hant": "骨骼與牙齒是體內鈣質的儲存庫。當血鈣濃度下降時，會觸發副甲狀腺激素（PTH）的分泌，訊號傳達至鈣儲存庫（骨骼與牙齒），使其釋放鈣質進入血液中。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第132-135頁；第4版，第148-150頁"
