      "exp_en": "Pregnanediol is an inactive metabolic byproduct of progesterone. The measurement of pregnanediol in the urine is an indirect way of measuring progesterone levels. The hormone progesterone is vital for normal menstruation and fertility. The release of the egg by the ovaries is associated with high levels of pregnanediol. Because the placenta releases pregnanediol, it is measured during pregnancy in women who have a history of miscarriages, premature delivery, and in women with difficult pregnancies. Low levels of pregnanediol are also observed in preeclampsia. Women treated for infertility also have their levels measured to evaluate sufficient progesterone levels. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 911-912; 4th Edition page 987-988",
      "exp_hant": "孕二醇是黃體素的一種無活性代謝副產物。測量尿中孕二醇濃度是間接估算黃體素濃度的方法。黃體素這種荷爾蒙對正常月經週期與生育能力至關重要，卵巢排卵時孕二醇濃度會隨之升高。由於胎盤也會分泌孕二醇，因此對於有流產史、早產史或妊娠困難的孕婦，會於孕期測量此指標。子癇前症患者的孕二醇濃度也會偏低。接受不孕症治療的婦女也會測量此濃度，以評估黃體素是否充足。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第911-912頁；第4版，第987-988頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 648,
      "question_en": "Which test is used for screening high-risk pregnancies?",
      "question_hant": "哪項檢查用於篩檢高風險妊娠？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
