        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "EEG",
          "hant": "腦電圖（EEG）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The NST (fetal nonstress test or fetal activity determination test) monitors the ability of the placenta to provide enough blood to the fetus. High risk pregnancies occur when the mother has diabetes, is hypertensive, there is an intra-uterine growth, a history of stillbirths, etc.. The NST monitors the fetal heart rate (FHR) when the fetus moves. If the NST test detects a non-reactive FHR within 40 minutes of fetal movement, then the patient is a candidate for a fetal contraction test (CST). A NST is routinely performed before a CST is administered. The CST test is also called the oxytocin challenge test or OCT. Intravenous oxytocin is administered to stimulate uterine contractions. Then the reaction of the fetus to the contractions is monitored by an external fetal heart monitor. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 529; 4th Edition, page 597",
      "exp_hant": "NST（胎兒無壓力測試，或稱胎動測定試驗）用於監測胎盤為胎兒提供充足血液的能力。高風險妊娠常見於母親患有糖尿病、高血壓、胎兒宮內生長遲滯、有死產病史等情況。NST會在胎動時監測胎心率（FHR）。若在胎動後40分鐘內NST檢測出無反應型胎心率，則患者需接受胎兒收縮測試（CST）。通常在進行CST之前會先例行實施NST。CST又稱為催產素激發試驗（OCT），透過靜脈給予催產素以誘發子宮收縮，再以體外胎心監視器監測胎兒對收縮的反應。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第529頁；第4版，第597頁"
    },
