      ],
      "exp_en": "This test is often done on patients who complain of polyuria (frequent urination) or polydipsia (great thirst). ADH is also known as vasopressin. The hypothalamus produces ADH and the posterior pituitary stores ADH. Vasopressin or ADH controls the amount of water that is reabsorbed by the kidneys. When ADH levels are low, water is excreted thereby diluting the urine and concentrating the blood. When the blood is over-concentrated there will be strong thirst. When ADH secretion is low or when the kidneys do not respond to ADH, it can result in diabetes insipidus (DI). Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 68-70; 4th Edition, page 75-76",
      "exp_hant": "此項檢測常用於主訴多尿（頻尿）或多飲（極度口渴）的患者。ADH又稱為血管加壓素，由下視丘產生，儲存於腦下垂體後葉。血管加壓素（ADH）控制腎臟對水分的再吸收量。當ADH濃度偏低時，水分會被排出，使尿液變稀、血液變濃；當血液過度濃縮時，便會產生強烈口渴感。當ADH分泌不足，或腎臟對ADH反應不佳時，可導致尿崩症（DI）。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第68-70頁；第4版，第75-76頁"
