      "exp_en": "The urine osmolality test measures the amount of dissolved particles per unit of water in the urine. This test measures urine concentration of osmotically electrolyte particles (mainly sodium, chloride, potassium, urea). Large test values mean that the urine is concentrated and small test values mean that the urine is diluted. Increased urine osmolality is seen, for example, in dehydration, adrenal insufficiency, glycosuria, hypernatremia (increased sodium level). Decreased urine osmolality is seen, for example, in diabetes insipidus, excessive fluid intake, acute renal insufficiency, glomerulonephritis. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 905; 4th Edition page 980",
      "exp_hant": "尿液滲透壓檢測測量每單位水分中溶解粒子的含量，用以評估尿中具滲透活性的電解質粒子濃度（主要為鈉、氯、鉀、尿素）。數值愈高表示尿液愈濃縮，數值愈低則表示尿液愈稀釋。尿液滲透壓升高常見於脫水、腎上腺功能不足、糖尿（尿糖）、高血鈉症（血鈉濃度升高）等情況；尿液滲透壓降低則常見於尿崩症、過量攝取液體、急性腎功能不全、腎絲球腎炎等情況。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第905頁；第4版，第980頁"
