      ],
      "exp_en": "Chlamydia is the most commonly reported bacterial-sexually transmitted infection in the US. Chlamydia prevalence among sexually-active young persons, 14-24 years old, is nearly three times more than among persons aged 25-39 years old. Looking at gender, chlamydia rates are three times higher in women than in men and, racially, eight times higher in African-Americans than in whites. If chlamydia is left untreated then 10-20% of chlamydia infections cause PID (pelvic inflammatory disease), pelvic pain, ectopic pregnancy, and infertility. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 662; 4th Edition, page 763",
      "exp_hant": "披衣菌感染是美國通報病例最多的細菌性性傳染病。在14至24歲、性行為活躍的年輕族群中，披衣菌盛行率約為25至39歲族群的近三倍。就性別而言，女性感染率約為男性的三倍；就種族而言，非裔美國人的感染率約為白人的八倍。若披衣菌感染未經治療，10%至20%的病例會導致骨盆腔發炎（PID）、骨盆腔疼痛、子宮外孕及不孕。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第662頁；第4版，第763頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 653,
      "question_en": "The allergic reaction is mediated primarily by",
      "question_hant": "過敏反應主要是由何者媒介？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "ribosomes",
          "hant": "核糖體",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "endoplasmic reticulum",
          "hant": "內質網",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Histamines",
          "hant": "組織胺",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "mitochondria",
          "hant": "粒線體",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Histamine is a chemical which produces an inflammatory response as a reaction to an allergen exposure. Histamine dilates the capillaries, contracts the smooth muscles, and can stimulate gastric secretion. Histamine is released by the immune system which protects the body from foreign bacteria and viruses. In allergies the immune system has a false alarm to substances which are usually not harmful. The immune system of a patient with allergies mistakes common substances for a disease causing invading agent. The immune system then mobilizes an attack against the allergen by releasing Immunoglobulin E (IgE) which is an antibody and protein. The IgE stores information about the invading substances so that the body can respond faster when it is \"attacked\" the next time by the same agent. IgE and the antigen work like a key fitting into a lock where each key can open only one lock. IgE attaches itself to tissue cells (mast cells) and blood cells (basophils). When the allergen locks into the IgE it initiates a cascade of reactions resulting in the destruction of mast cells and basophils that then releases their store of histamine and other allergy mediators into the blood and surrounding tissues. This release causes a dilation of surface blood vessels which lowers the blood pressure. The space between cells then fills with fluid. The symptoms produced depend on the type of allergen and which part of the body is affected. There can be sneezing, hives, diarrhea, vomiting, etc. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 1159; 4th Edition, page 1143",
      "exp_hant": "組織胺是一種化學物質，在暴露於過敏原後會引發發炎反應。組織胺會使微血管擴張、平滑肌收縮，並能刺激胃酸分泌。組織胺是由保護身體對抗外來細菌與病毒的免疫系統所釋放。在過敏反應中，免疫系統對通常無害的物質產生誤判的警訊，將常見物質誤認為致病的入侵原，進而透過釋放免疫球蛋白E（IgE，一種抗體蛋白）動員攻擊過敏原。IgE會儲存有關入侵物質的資訊，以便身體下次再遭遇同一物質「攻擊」時能更快做出反應。IgE與抗原的作用如同鑰匙與鎖，每把鑰匙只能開啟一把鎖。IgE會附著於組織細胞（肥大細胞）及血液細胞（嗜鹼性球）上。當過敏原與IgE結合鎖定時，便啟動一連串反應，導致肥大細胞與嗜鹼性球破裂，將其儲存的組織胺及其他過敏介質釋放到血液與周圍組織中。這種釋放會使表層血管擴張，導致血壓下降，細胞間隙隨即充滿液體。所產生的症狀則依過敏原種類及受影響的身體部位而異，可能包括打噴嚏、蕁麻疹、腹瀉、嘔吐等。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第1159頁；第4版，第1143頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 654,
      "question_en": "The Erythropoietin (EPO) blood test is used to differentiate the cause of",
      "question_hant": "紅血球生成素（EPO）血液檢測用於鑑別何種病因？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "thrombosis",
          "hant": "血栓形成",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Embolisms",
          "hant": "栓塞",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "bleeding",
          "hant": "出血",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "anemia",
          "hant": "貧血",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The erythropoietin (EPO) test measures the amount of a hormone called erythropoietin (EPO) in the blood. The kidneys produce EPO. When blood oxygen levels are low, the EPO hormone signals stem cells in the bone marrow to produce more red blood cells. The EPO test helps to determine the cause of 1) anemia. 2) polycythemia (high red blood cell count). 3) bone marrow disorders. If there is a change in the RBC count this will affect EPO release. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 214-215; 4th Edition, page 237-238",
      "exp_hant": "紅血球生成素（EPO）檢測測量血液中一種稱為紅血球生成素（EPO）的荷爾蒙含量。EPO由腎臟產生，當血氧濃度偏低時，EPO會向骨髓中的幹細胞發出訊號，促使其產生更多紅血球。EPO檢測有助於判定：1）貧血；2）紅血球增多症（紅血球數量過高）；3）骨髓疾病等病因。若紅血球數量發生變化，也會影響EPO的釋放。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第214-215頁；第4版，第237-238頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 655,
      "question_en": "The Triglycerides test measures the ability to store",
      "question_hant": "三酸甘油酯檢測測量儲存何者的能力？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "fat",
          "hant": "脂肪",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "complex carbohydrates",
          "hant": "複合碳水化合物",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "simple carbohydrates",
          "hant": "簡單碳水化合物",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "proteins",
          "hant": "蛋白質",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The triglycerides (TGs) test helps to identify CHD risk. This test is part of a lipid profile that includes measuring cholesterol and lipoproteins. TGs, a form of fat in the blood, are carried by LDLs (low-density lipoproteins). The liver produces triglycerides which are then stored in the body as a source of available energy. When TG levels are high, they are stored in the body as fatty tissue. TGs make up most of the fat in the body. A high TG level may lead to the development of atherosclerosis, which increases heart attack and stroke risk. A high TG level can also cause inflammation of the pancreas. Patients with high TG levels often have other diseases such as diabetes and obesity that also increase the risk of CHD. High TGs can be found in cirrhosis or liver damage, a diet low in protein and high in carbohydrates, in hypothyroidism, in nephrotic syndrome, or with poorly controlled diabetes. Low TGs with a low fat diet, hyperthyroidism, and digestive malabsorption syndromes. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 471-473; 4th Edition, page 522-523",
      "exp_hant": "三酸甘油酯（TG）檢測有助於判定冠心病（CHD）風險，屬於血脂檢查的一部分，血脂檢查還包括膽固醇與脂蛋白的測量。三酸甘油酯是血液中的一種脂肪形式，由LDL（低密度脂蛋白）運送。肝臟會製造三酸甘油酯，並將其儲存於體內作為可用的能量來源；當三酸甘油酯濃度過高時，便會以脂肪組織的形式儲存於體內，三酸甘油酯是體內脂肪的主要成分。三酸甘油酯濃度過高可能導致動脈粥狀硬化，進而增加心臟病發作與中風的風險，也可能引起胰臟發炎。三酸甘油酯濃度偏高的患者常合併其他疾病，例如糖尿病與肥胖，這些同樣會增加冠心病風險。三酸甘油酯偏高可見於肝硬化或肝損傷、低蛋白高碳水化合物飲食、甲狀腺功能低下、腎病症候群，或糖尿病控制不佳者；三酸甘油酯偏低則見於低脂飲食、甲狀腺功能亢進及消化道吸收不良症候群。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第471-473頁；第4版，第522-523頁"
    },
