          "hant": "貧血",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "White blood cells are disease-fighting cells. When there is an abnormal increase it could mean that there is 1) an infection. 2) some type of drug reaction that increase WBC. 3) a bone marrow disease. Or 4) an immune disorder that increases WBC. An increase WBC count is called leukocytosis while a decreased count is called leukopenia. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 809",
      "exp_hant": "白血球是負責對抗疾病的細胞。當白血球數量異常升高時，可能代表：1）感染；2）某種導致白血球增加的藥物反應；3）骨髓疾病；或4）造成白血球增加的免疫疾病。白血球數量增加稱為白血球增多症，數量減少則稱為白血球減少症。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第809頁"
