      "exp_en": "As soon as pregnancy starts, iron requirement may increase by up to 50%. An iron deficiency early in pregnancy can have long-lasting effects on child brain development, even if the lack of iron is not enough to cause severe anemia. Iron-deficient babies may have slow language development and have behavioral problems. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 224-226; 4th Edition, page 246-247",
      "exp_hant": "懷孕一旦開始，鐵質需求量可能增加達50%。若孕早期即出現缺鐵，即使程度尚不足以造成嚴重貧血，仍可能對胎兒腦部發育產生長期影響。缺鐵的嬰兒可能出現語言發展遲緩及行為問題。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第224-226頁；第4版，第246-247頁"
    },
