      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Osteoarthritis is degenerative joint disease or a wear-and-tear arthritis caused by joint cartilage breakdown which is mostly a consequence of aging. RA, scleroderma, and Raynaud's disease, on the other hand, are autoimmune diseases where the body attacks its own tissues. The ESR tests for rheumatoid factors that can be found not only in rheumatoid arthritis but also in other auto-immune disorders besides RA. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 84; 4th Edition, page 92",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且正確的答案。骨關節炎是一種退化性關節疾病，屬於因關節軟骨磨損而導致的「磨損型」關節炎，多為老化所致。相對地，類風濕性關節炎、硬皮症與雷諾氏病則屬於自體免疫疾病，是身體攻擊自身組織所致。ESR檢測的是類風濕因子，該因子不僅見於類風濕性關節炎，也可見於類風濕性關節炎以外的其他自體免疫疾病。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第84頁；第4版，第92頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 662,
      "question_en": "While EMG evaluates the electrical activity of muscles, the electroneurography (ENG) test evaluates",
      "question_hant": "肌電圖（EMG）評估肌肉的電活動，而神經電圖（ENG）檢測則評估",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Upper neuron fibers",
          "hant": "上運動神經元纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Ascending nerve fibers",
          "hant": "上行神經纖維",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Peripheral nerves",
          "hant": "周邊神經",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Smooth muscle of the heart",
          "hant": "心臟平滑肌",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The peripheral nervous system (PNS) is that part of the nervous system that consists of nerves and ganglia (group of nerve cells linked by synapses) outside the brain and spinal cord. This test is a nerve conduction study. It is used to identify peripheral nerve injuries in patients who have local or diffuse weakness. It helps to differentiate between primary nerve disease and primary muscle disease. This test measures the time for an electrical impulse to travel from area A of a nerve to area B of the same nerve. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 534",
      "exp_hant": "周邊神經系統（PNS）是神經系統中位於腦部與脊髓之外，由神經與神經節（以突觸相連的一群神經細胞）所組成的部分。此檢測屬於神經傳導檢查，用於辨識出現局部或瀰漫性無力患者的周邊神經損傷，並有助於區分原發性神經疾病與原發性肌肉疾病。此檢測測量電脈衝從同一神經的A點傳導至B點所需的時間。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第534頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 663,
      "question_en": "Lordosis is",
      "question_hant": "脊柱前凸是指",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Increased convexity in the curvature of the spine",
          "hant": "脊柱曲度的凸度增加",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Abnormal posterior curve",
          "hant": "異常的向後彎曲",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Increased concavity in the curvature of the spine",
          "hant": "脊柱曲度的凹度增加",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Abnormal lateral curve of the spine",
          "hant": "脊柱的異常側彎",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Scoliosis, kyphosis and lordosis all refer to the curvature of the spine. Lordosis is commonly called swayback. Kyphosis is commonly called humpback or round back. Scoliosis is an abnormal sideward curvature to either the left or right. In scoliosis the spine curves to the side like a C or S shape. In lordosis the spine deviates inwards to the body. In kyphosis the spine deviates outwards from the body. Scoliosis is an abnormal curvature of the spine in the coronal (lateral) plane. Scoliosis between 10-20 degrees is considered mild and less than 10 degrees is a normal postural variation. Lordosis or hyperlordosis is excessive curving of the lower spine. Lordosis is often associated with scoliosis or kyphosis. Kyphosis is an excess curvature of the spine in the sagittal (A-P) plane. Normally, the upper back has 20-45 degrees of curvature. Anything in excess of 45 degrees is called kyphosis. Combined kyphosis and scoliosis is termed kyphoscoliosi. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 1090; 4th Edition page 1166; webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "脊柱側彎、脊柱後凸與脊柱前凸皆是描述脊柱曲度的名詞。脊柱前凸俗稱「凹背」，脊柱後凸俗稱「駝背」或「圓背」，脊柱側彎則是指脊柱向左或向右的異常側向彎曲。脊柱側彎時，脊柱會呈C形或S形向側邊彎曲；脊柱前凸時，脊柱向身體內側偏移；脊柱後凸時，脊柱則向身體外側偏移。脊柱側彎是脊柱在冠狀（側向）面上的異常彎曲，介於10至20度視為輕度，低於10度則屬正常姿勢變異。脊柱前凸（或稱過度前凸）是下段脊柱的過度彎曲，常與脊柱側彎或脊柱後凸並存。脊柱後凸則是脊柱在矢狀（前後）面上的過度彎曲，正常上背部曲度約為20至45度，超過45度即稱為脊柱後凸。脊柱後凸合併脊柱側彎則稱為脊柱後側凸。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第1090頁；第4版，第1166頁；webmd.com"
    },
    {
      "number": 664,
      "question_en": "Excess blood levels of ammonia is due to a malfunctioning",
      "question_hant": "血氨濃度過高是由於何處功能失調所致？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "lungs",
          "hant": "肺臟",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Bladder",
          "hant": "膀胱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "heart",
          "hant": "心臟",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "liver",
          "hant": "肝臟",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The majority of the ammonia is formed through the breakdown of protein by bacteria in the intestines. In normal situations, the liver then converts ammonia into urea which is then eliminated in urine. Blood ammonia levels rise when the liver fails in converting ammonia to urea. This can occur when patient has cirrhosis or severe hepatitis. If a patient has hand tremors, is confused, has excessive sleepiness or in a coma then their ammonia level is measured. The ammonia blood test is also used when Reye's syndrome is suspected. Reye's syndrome is a life-threatening metabolic disorder in young children, triggered by the use of aspirin during an influenza episode that can lead to encephalitis and liver failure. This test is also used to monitor the treatment for liver disease (cirrhosis) and the prognosis of some liver diseases (liver failure). Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 1090; 4th Edition page 1166; webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "大部分的氨是由腸道細菌分解蛋白質所產生。在正常情況下，肝臟會將氨轉化為尿素，再經尿液排出體外。當肝臟無法有效將氨轉化為尿素時，血氨濃度便會升高，這種情況可見於肝硬化或重度肝炎患者。若患者出現手部顫抖、意識混亂、過度嗜睡或昏迷，通常會測量其血氨濃度。血氨檢測也用於懷疑雷氏症候群的病例。雷氏症候群是一種好發於幼童、可危及生命的代謝性疾病，通常因流感期間使用阿斯匹靈而誘發，可導致腦炎與肝衰竭。此檢測也用於監測肝病（肝硬化）的治療成效，以及某些肝臟疾病（肝衰竭）的預後評估。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第1090頁；第4版，第1166頁；webmd.com"
    },
    {
      "number": 665,
      "question_en": "Which of the following iron-related blood tests is the most accurate indicator of iron deficiency?",
      "question_hant": "以下哪項鐵相關血液檢測，是缺鐵最準確的指標？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Transferrin Saturation",
          "hant": "運鐵蛋白飽和度",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Serum Iron",
          "hant": "血清鐵",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Ferritin",
          "hant": "鐵蛋白",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Total Iron-Binding Capacity (TIBC)",
          "hant": "總鐵結合能力（TIBC）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The ferritin test is the best indicator of iron storage in the body. Ferritin is a protein that stores iron. The serum iron measures the amount of iron in the blood but this level may be normal even if the total amount of iron in your body is low. Total Iron Binding Capacity (TIBC) is a blood test to gauge how much iron is in the body by analysing transferrin, a protein that has iron attached to it. This test determines how effective that protein is in carrying iron. Transferrin Saturation is the ratio of blood iron and total iron-binding capacity. A value of 25% means that 25% of iron-binding sites of transferrin are being occupied by iron. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 224-226; 4th Edition, page 246-247",
      "exp_hant": "鐵蛋白檢測是評估體內鐵質儲存量最佳的指標。鐵蛋白是一種儲存鐵質的蛋白質。血清鐵測量血液中的鐵含量，但即使體內總鐵量偏低，此數值仍可能正常。總鐵結合能力（TIBC）是透過分析運鐵蛋白（一種可與鐵結合的蛋白質）來估算體內鐵含量的血液檢測，用以判定該蛋白質運送鐵質的效率。運鐵蛋白飽和度則是血鐵濃度與總鐵結合能力的比值，數值25%表示運鐵蛋白上25%的鐵結合位點已被鐵佔據。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第224-226頁；第4版，第246-247頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 666,
      "question_en": "The EMG test",
      "question_hant": "肌電圖（EMG）檢測",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Records the electrical impulses that stimulate the heart to contract",
          "hant": "記錄刺激心臟收縮的電脈衝",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Records the electrical activity of smooth muscles",
          "hant": "記錄平滑肌的電活動",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Records the electrical activity of the brain",
          "hant": "記錄腦部的電活動",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Records the electrical activity of a skeletal muscle",
          "hant": "記錄骨骼肌的電活動",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "EMG (electromyography) is used to evaluate patients with diffused or local muscle weakness. It measures the electrical activity of the skeletal muscles. EMG evaluates the health of the muscles and the motor neurons or nerve cells that control the muscles. EMG can show a nerve dysfunction, a muscle dysfunction or a dysfunction in the nerve-to-muscle signal transmission. This test is usually done to evaluate tingling, numbness, muscle weakness, and muscle pain/cramping. When combined with the electroneurography (ENG), the EMG can differentiate between primary muscle disease and primary neurological disorders. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 515; 4th Edition, page 577",
      "exp_hant": "肌電圖（EMG）用於評估出現瀰漫性或局部肌肉無力的患者，測量骨骼肌的電活動，藉此評估肌肉本身及控制肌肉的運動神經元（神經細胞）之健康狀況。EMG可顯示神經功能異常、肌肉功能異常，或神經至肌肉訊號傳遞的異常。此檢測通常用於評估麻刺感、麻木、肌肉無力及肌肉疼痛／抽筋等症狀。若與神經電圖（ENG）合併使用，EMG可協助區分原發性肌肉疾病與原發性神經系統疾病。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第515頁；第4版，第577頁"
    },
    {
