          "en": "Breast fibrocystic changes",
          "hant": "乳房纖維囊性變化",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Fistulas",
          "hant": "瘻管",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Breast skin cancer",
          "hant": "乳房皮膚癌",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A mammogram is an x-ray image of the breast. They are used to screen for breast tumors in women even though there are no signs/symptoms of cancer. The mammogram images allow for the detecting of tumors that cannot be felt. Among women ages 40 to 74, screening mammography has played a role in reducing deaths from breast cancer. In women under age 40, studies have shown no benefit from regular screening mammagrophy. The signs of breast cancer (breast pain, thick breast skin, nipple discharge, breast size change) can also be found in non-cancerous conditions. Mammograms can also help detect fibrocystic changes, cysts, in the breast. The limitations of mammogram screening for cancer is that they often give false-positive or false-negatives. Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Studies, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 1023; 4th Edition, page 1103",
      "exp_hant": "乳房攝影是一種乳房的X光影像檢查，用於在女性尚無癌症徵兆或症狀時篩檢乳房腫瘤，其影像可偵測到無法以觸診發現的腫瘤。在40至74歲的女性族群中，篩檢性乳房攝影已被證實有助於降低乳癌死亡率；而在40歲以下的女性中，研究顯示定期篩檢性乳房攝影並無明顯效益。乳癌的徵兆（乳房疼痛、乳房皮膚增厚、乳頭分泌物、乳房大小改變）也可能出現在非癌性病症中。乳房攝影也有助於偵測乳房的纖維囊性變化及囊腫。乳房攝影篩檢癌症的限制在於，其結果常出現偽陽性或偽陰性。《Mosby診斷與檢驗手冊》第7版，Pagana著，第1023頁；第4版，第1103頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 671,
      "question_en": "Pelvic ultrasonography is primarily used to measure",
      "question_hant": "骨盆超音波主要用於測量",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Fetal position, Fetal growth, Fetal umbilical cord blood flow",
