        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Cranial nerve IX (glossopharyngeal)",
          "hant": "第九對腦神經（舌咽神經）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Cranial nerve VIII (vestibulocochlear)",
          "hant": "第八對腦神經（前庭耳蝸神經）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Vagus is the Latin for \"wandering\". The vagus is very long, extending from the brain stem all the way to the viscera. Parasympathetic innervation of the heart is controlled by the vagus nerve. The parasympathetic system is responsible for stimulation of \"rest-and-digest\" activities that occur when the body is at rest, including sexual arousal, salivation, lacrimation, urination, digestion, and defecation. The vagus nerve acts to lower the heart rate. When the vagus nerve is stimulated, the response is often a reduction in heart-rate or breathing. tcmtests.com, September 2019",
      "exp_hant": "「迷走」（Vagus）在拉丁文中意為「遊走」。迷走神經非常長，從腦幹一路延伸至內臟。心臟的副交感神經支配是由迷走神經所控制。副交感神經系統負責刺激身體休息時發生的「休息與消化」活動，包括性喚起、唾液分泌、淚液分泌、排尿、消化與排便。迷走神經的作用是降低心率，當迷走神經受到刺激時，反應通常表現為心率或呼吸速率的下降。tcmtests.com，2019年9月"
    },
    {
      "number": 679,
      "question_en": "When asking the patient to say \"ah\" and watching the movement of the soft palette and the pharynx, what cranial nerve are you testing?",
      "question_hant": "請患者發出「啊」的聲音並觀察軟顎與咽部的活動，這是在測試哪一對腦神經？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Cranial nerves VII, X",
          "hant": "第七、第十對腦神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Cranial nerves V, VII",
          "hant": "第五、第七對腦神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Cranial nerves VII, IX",
          "hant": "第七、第九對腦神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Cranial nerves IX, X",
          "hant": "第九、第十對腦神經",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "CN IX is the glossopharyngeal nerve. The motor portion of CN IX innervates the pharynx. The pharynx is part of the digestive system and part of the conducting zone of the respiratory system. The conducting zone also includes the nose, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and bronchioles. The function of the conducting zone is to filter, warm, and moisten air and transmit air into the lungs. CN X is the vagus nerve. CN X enervates the larynx and the pharynx (swallowing and gagging). The voice box, or larynx, is part of the respiratory tract that contains the vocal cords. The larynx is located between the pharynx and the trachea. The trachea is a tube reinforced by rings of cartilage that extend from the larynx to the bronchial tubes and transmits air to and from the lungs. CN IX also has a sensory branch that goes to the posterior eardrum, the pharynx, and the posterior tongue. CN X also has a sensory branch to the pharynx and larynx. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 900; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 677",
      "exp_hant": "第九對腦神經（CN IX）為舌咽神經，其運動部分支配咽部。咽部屬於消化系統的一部分，也屬於呼吸系統傳導區的一部分；傳導區還包括鼻、喉、氣管、支氣管與細支氣管，其功能是過濾、溫暖並濕潤空氣，並將空氣輸送至肺部。第十對腦神經（CN X）為迷走神經，支配喉部與咽部（吞嚥與嘔吐反射）。喉（聲門）是呼吸道的一部分，內含聲帶，位於咽部與氣管之間。氣管是一條由軟骨環強化的管道，自喉部延伸至支氣管，負責輸送氣體進出肺部。CN IX還有一條感覺分支通往外耳道後側、咽部及舌後部；CN X也有一條感覺分支通往咽部與喉部。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第900頁；第10版，第677頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 680,
      "question_en": "Which of the following has the correct association between muscle testing and corresponding nerve(s)?",
      "question_hant": "以下何者正確配對了肌力測試與其對應的神經？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "The finger extension test assesses C7 and C8",
          "hant": "手指伸展測試評估C7與C8",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "The thumb opposition test assesses the ulnar nerve",
          "hant": "拇指對掌測試評估尺神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "The elbow extension test assesses C6",
          "hant": "肘部伸展測試評估C6",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "The finger abduction test assesses the median nerve",
          "hant": "手指外展測試評估正中神經",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The correct answers are: The finger extension test assesses C7 and C8 (radial nerve - extensor digitorum).. The thumb opposition test assesses the median nerve. The finger abduction test assesses the ulnar nerve. The elbow extension test assesses the radial nerve. The grip test is done by having the patient squeeze two fingers of the examiner and not let them go. Normally it should be difficult for the examiner to remove his or her fingers. The grip tests for C7, C8, and T1. A weak grip can be found in cervical radiculopathy, arthritis, carpal tunnel, and epicondylitis. In the thumb opposition test the patient tries to touch the tip of their little finger with their thumb against resistance given by the examiner on the thumb. Weak thumb opposition points to median nerve disorders such as carpal tunnel syndrome. In the finger abduction test the patient tries to spreads their fingers out with the examiner providing resistance. Weak finger abduction points to an ulnar nerve disorder. The elbow extension test evaluates the radial nerve as well as C6, C7, and C8. In this test the patient makes a fist and resist the examiner from trying to pull the elbow down. Weak extension is seen in peripheral nerve disease (radial nerve damage) or in nervous system disease (hemiplegia, stroke). Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 681-683; 8th Edition, page 574",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為：手指伸展測試評估C7與C8（橈神經－伸指肌）。拇指對掌測試評估正中神經。手指外展測試評估尺神經。肘部伸展測試評估橈神經。握力測試是請患者用力握住檢查者的兩根手指且不放開，正常情況下檢查者應難以將手指抽出；握力測試評估C7、C8與T1。握力減弱可見於頸神經根病變、關節炎、腕隧道症候群及肱骨外上髁炎。拇指對掌測試中，患者需在檢查者對拇指施加阻力的情況下，嘗試以拇指觸碰小指指尖；拇指對掌無力提示正中神經病變，如腕隧道症候群。手指外展測試中，患者需在檢查者提供阻力的情況下嘗試張開手指；手指外展無力提示尺神經病變。肘部伸展測試評估橈神經及C6、C7、C8；測試中患者握拳並抵抗檢查者將其肘部往下拉的力量，伸展無力可見於周邊神經疾病（橈神經損傷）或神經系統疾病（偏癱、中風）。《Bates身體檢查指南》第10版，第681-683頁；第8版，第574頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 681,
      "question_en": "With the patient in a supine position, the knee is flexed 15 degrees. Grasp the distal femur, just above the knee, with one hand and the upper tibia, just below the knee, with the other hand (thumb on this hand is on the tibia). Move the tibia forward and the femur back. What test is this?",
      "question_hant": "患者採仰臥姿勢，膝關節屈曲15度。一手握住股骨遠端（膝關節上方），另一手握住脛骨近端（膝關節下方，該手拇指置於脛骨上）。將脛骨向前推、股骨向後拉，這是什麼測試？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "McMurray test",
          "hant": "麥克莫瑞測試",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Lachman's test",
          "hant": "拉赫曼測試",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Anterior drawer sign",
          "hant": "前抽屜徵象",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Adduction stress test",
          "hant": "內收應力測試",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Lachman's test evaluates the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL). A significant forward excursion indicates an ACL tear. A positive Lachman's test increases the possibility of an ACL tear by 17 times. Symptoms of a severe and acute ACL injury is feeling/hearing a pop at the time of injury, knee buckling, knee swelling within first hours after injury, and limited knee movement. Immediate first aid for an ACL tear involves applying the PRICE therapy (Protection, Rest, Ice, Compression, Elevation). Cold therapy and compression wrap is done for at least the first 72 hours or until a specialist does an evaluation. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 807-809; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 632-634",
      "exp_hant": "拉赫曼測試用於評估前十字韌帶（ACL）。若出現明顯的前向位移，即表示前十字韌帶撕裂。拉赫曼測試呈陽性會使前十字韌帶撕裂的可能性提高17倍。急性嚴重前十字韌帶損傷的症狀包括受傷當下感覺／聽到「啪」聲、膝關節無法支撐、受傷後數小時內膝關節腫脹，以及膝關節活動受限。前十字韌帶撕裂的緊急處置為採用PRICE療法（保護、休息、冰敷、加壓、抬高），冷療與加壓包紮至少應持續72小時，或直到專科醫師完成評估為止。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第807-809頁；第10版，第632-634頁"
    },
    {
