        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "peripheral nervous system disease",
          "hant": "周邊神經系統疾病",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The central nervous system is composed of the brain and spinal cord. Upper motor neurons originate either in the motor region of the cerebral cortex or in the brain stem. Upper motor neurons carry motor information to the lower motor neurons. The upper motor neuron descends in the spinal cord to the appropriate spinal nerve root level at which point, the upper motor neuron connects with the lower motor neuron. Hyperactive reflexes or hyper-reflexia is an overactive reflex. Hyper-reflexia can indicate upper motor neuron disease as well as disinhibition (loss or lessening of control of higher brain centers of the lower neural pathways). Twitching, spastic tendencies, or a positive Babinski sign can indicate an upper motor neuron disease. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 850; 10th Edition page 696",
      "exp_hant": "中樞神經系統由腦部與脊髓組成。上運動神經元起源於大腦皮質的運動區或腦幹，負責將運動訊息傳遞給下運動神經元。上運動神經元沿脊髓下行至相應的脊神經根節段，並在該處與下運動神經元相接。反射亢進（即過度活躍的反射）可能提示上運動神經元疾病，也可能反映抑制作用喪失（即高位腦中樞對下位神經傳導路徑的控制減弱或喪失）。肌肉抽動、痙攣傾向或巴賓斯基徵象陽性，皆可提示上運動神經元疾病。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第850頁；第10版，第696頁"
    },
