          "key": "B",
          "en": "Cranial nerve X",
          "hant": "第十對腦神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Cranial Nerve V",
          "hant": "第五對腦神經",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Cranial nerve IX",
          "hant": "第九對腦神經",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "IX = glossopharyngeal. The glossopharyngeal nerve, cranial nerve IX, receives taste from the posterior 1/3 of the tongue, provides secretomotor innervation to the parotid gland, and provides motor innervation to the stylopharyngeus, a muscle in the head that stretches between the styloid process and the pharynx. Some sensations are also relayed to the brain from the palatine tonsils. Symptoms of dysfunction include loss of taste from posterior 1/3 tongue and swallowing dysfunction. It has both sensory and motor branches. tcmtests.com, September 2019",
      "exp_hant": "第九對腦神經即舌咽神經，負責接收舌後三分之一的味覺，提供腮腺的分泌運動神經支配，並支配莖突咽肌（一條位於頭部、連接莖突與咽部的肌肉）。部分感覺訊息也會由顎扁桃體傳回腦部。功能障礙的症狀包括舌後三分之一味覺喪失及吞嚥功能障礙，此神經兼具感覺與運動分支。tcmtests.com，2019年9月"
    },
    {
      "number": 686,
      "question_en": "What is the abdominal palpation procedure for detecting splenomegaly?",
      "question_hant": "偵測脾腫大的腹部觸診程序為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "press the area under the 11th and 12th ribs",
          "hant": "按壓第11、12肋骨下方區域",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "on the abdomen press inwards and upwards toward the left costal margin",
          "hant": "在腹部向內、向上朝左肋緣方向按壓",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "on the abdomen pinch and release the area below the left costal margin",
          "hant": "在腹部左肋緣下方區域進行捏放",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "press the area just below the xiphoid process",
          "hant": "按壓劍突正下方區域",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Splenomegaly refers to an enlarged spleen. A normal spleen is not palpable in most patients. The spleen is located within the left coastal margin. If the spleen is enlarged it will protrude beyond the coastal margin. To detect splenomegaly, with the patient lying supine, place the examining hand flat on the abdomen, well below the left coastal margin. Press inwards and upwards and ask the patient to breathe. Move the hand upwards after each inspiration until the fingertips are under the left coastal margin. An enlarged spleen should be felt against the fingertips during the inhale before reaching the coastal margin. During inhalation the diaphragm pushes the enlarged spleen downward. If an enlarged spleen is still not palpable, ask the patient to lie on their right side with the knees and hips slightly flexed. Palpate up into the left hypochondrium as before, asking for deep breaths on the way. Palpate for the spleen on the inhale. An enlarged spleen can be palpated with viral infections (mononucleosis), bacterial infections (endocarditis), malaria, cirrhosis of the liver, and different types of hemolytic anemia (early destruction of red blood cells). When spleen size is normal, percussion note usually remains tympanic. If it changes to dull on inspiration, it is suggestive of splenic enlargement. Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 75",
      "exp_hant": "脾腫大是指脾臟腫大的狀態。多數患者的正常脾臟是無法觸診到的，脾臟位於左肋緣之內；若脾臟腫大，則會突出於肋緣之外。偵測脾腫大時，讓患者採仰臥姿勢，檢查者將手掌平放於腹部，位置遠低於左肋緣，向內、向上按壓，並請患者呼吸；每次吸氣後將手往上移動，直到指尖抵達左肋緣下方。若脾臟腫大，應在吸氣過程中、指尖尚未到達肋緣前即可觸及；吸氣時橫膈膜會將腫大的脾臟向下推。若仍無法觸及腫大的脾臟，可請患者向右側臥、膝髖略為屈曲，再依前述方式向左季肋部觸診，並請患者深呼吸，於吸氣時觸診脾臟。脾腫大可見於病毒感染（傳染性單核球增多症）、細菌感染（心內膜炎）、瘧疾、肝硬化，以及各類溶血性貧血（紅血球提早破壞）。若脾臟大小正常，叩診音通常維持鼓音；若吸氣時叩診音轉為濁音，則提示脾腫大。《亞洲醫學從業者西醫體檢技能》，2009年，Robinson、Wolfe著，第75頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 687,
      "question_en": "Which of the following conditions most closely mimics this scenario? Joe has weakness and atrophy in the spinal cord segment and has a focal pattern of pain and fasciculations. His sensation is intact.",
      "question_hant": "以下何種病況與此情境最為相似？喬（Joe）出現脊髓節段相對應肌肉的無力與萎縮，並有局部性的疼痛與肌束顫動，但感覺功能完好。",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Cerebellar stroke",
          "hant": "小腦中風",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "multiple sclerosis",
          "hant": "多發性硬化症",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis",
          "hant": "肌萎縮性側索硬化症",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "muscular dystrophy",
          "hant": "肌肉失養症",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) or Lou Gehrig's disease is a progressive degeneration of central nervous system motor neurons responsible for controlling voluntary muscle movement leading to wasting of the muscles and paralysis. Fasciculations are brief and spontaneous muscle contractions that often cause a flicker of movement under the skin. It is a symptom of defective motor neurons. Fasciculations by themselves are not a sign of ALS but when associated with weakness and atrophy it can point to ALS. Fasciculations can also occur in Post-Polio Syndrome. ALS affects the nerves whereas muscular dystrophy (MD) affects the muscles. In MD, the muscle fibers weaken and can cause a problem with walking, breathing, gripping, and eating. ALS usually occurs late in life whereas MD occurs at birth or early childhood. Multiple Sclerosis (MS) is an auto-immune disorder affecting the protective nerve sheaths (myelin). MS causes problems with vision, sensation, memory, and coordination. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 908-909; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 728-729",
      "exp_hant": "肌萎縮性側索硬化症（ALS），又稱漸凍症（Lou Gehrig氏病），是中樞神經系統中負責控制隨意肌運動的運動神經元進行性退化的疾病，會導致肌肉萎縮與癱瘓。肌束顫動是短暫且自發性的肌肉收縮，常在皮膚下產生輕微的跳動，是運動神經元功能異常的徵兆。單獨出現肌束顫動並非ALS的徵象，但若合併無力與萎縮，則可能提示ALS；肌束顫動也可見於小兒麻痺後症候群。ALS影響的是神經，而肌肉失養症（MD）影響的則是肌肉本身；MD患者的肌纖維會逐漸無力，可能導致行走、呼吸、握力及進食方面的問題。ALS通常於晚年發病，MD則多於出生時或幼年期發病。多發性硬化症（MS）是一種影響神經保護鞘（髓鞘）的自體免疫疾病，會造成視力、感覺、記憶與協調方面的問題。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第908-909頁；第10版，第728-729頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 688,
      "question_en": "A 50 year old male complains of shoulder pain ever since he was in an auto accident one year ago. His shoulder struck the side of the door. He complains of shoulder pain. There is tenderness localized over the acromial clavicular joint. The motion of the glenoid humeral joint is free of pain. Movements of the scapula such as shoulder shrugging is painful however. The most likely diagnosis is",
      "question_hant": "一名50歲男性主訴自一年前發生車禍後即有肩部疼痛，當時肩部撞擊車門側邊。他主訴肩部疼痛，壓痛侷限於肩鎖關節，肩肱關節活動不受疼痛限制，但肩胛骨動作（如聳肩）會引發疼痛。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Acromial clavicular arthritis",
          "hant": "肩鎖關節炎",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Calcific tendinitis",
          "hant": "鈣化性肌腱炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Rotator cuff tendinitis",
          "hant": "旋轉肌袖肌腱炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "rotator cuff tear",
          "hant": "旋轉肌袖撕裂",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The acromial clavicular joint (AC joint) is located at the top of the shoulder where the clavicle and highest part of the scapula meet. Acromial clavicular arthritis occurs when there is trauma (often years earlier) to the shoulder with resulting degenerative changes. The main symptom is localized tenderness and pain of the acromioclavicular joint. Movements of the shoulder blade (shrugging, reaching the arm across the body, putting on a seat belt) can produce pain. Diagnosis is via physical exam, cross-body adduction test, x-ray, and MRI. Conservative treatment is rest, hot/cold therapy, physical therapy, NSAIDs, and, if necessary, surgery. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 831; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 647",
      "exp_hant": "肩鎖關節（AC關節）位於肩部頂端，是鎖骨與肩胛骨最高處相接之處。肩鎖關節炎的發生，通常源自於肩部曾經（往往是多年前）遭受創傷所導致的退化性變化。主要症狀為肩鎖關節局部壓痛與疼痛，肩胛骨的動作（如聳肩、將手臂橫越身體、繫安全帶）皆可能引發疼痛。診斷方式包括身體檢查、水平內收測試、X光及核磁共振（MRI）。保守治療包括休息、冷熱療法、物理治療、非類固醇消炎藥（NSAIDs），必要時則需手術治療。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第831頁；第10版，第647頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 689,
      "question_en": "Flexion of the hip tests which muscle group?",
      "question_hant": "髖關節屈曲測試的是哪一組肌群？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gluteus maximus",
          "hant": "臀大肌",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Hip abductors",
          "hant": "髖外展肌群",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Iliopsoas",
          "hant": "髂腰肌",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Adductors",
          "hant": "內收肌群",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The hip flexor muscles are attached to the hip joint to allow the femur to flex onto the pelvis region. Simply, the hip flexors allow the knee to be pulled up. The hip flexors are the iliopsoas, sartorius, and rectus femoris muscles. The iliopsoas muscle group consists of two muscles, the psoas muscle and the iliac muscle. These two muscles function together to flex the hip. The psoas muscle connects to the lumbar vertebrae (L1 through L5). The opposite end of the psoas muscle connects to the tendon on the femur bone. The upper end of the sartorius muscle attaches to the anterior superior iliac crest. The sartorius muscle crosses the upper leg to attach to the tibia. The sartorius muscle helps in knee and hip flexion and rotation of the thigh and tibia. The rectus femoris is one of the four quadriceps muscles (vastus intermedius, the vastus medialis, the vastus lateralis, and the rectus femoris) of the front of the upper leg. The rectus femoris attaches to the anterior inferior aspect of the iliac crest and traverses to the base of the patella. This muscle enables hip flexion and knee extension. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 793-794; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 618",
      "exp_hant": "髖屈肌群附著於髖關節，使股骨得以相對骨盆屈曲，簡言之，髖屈肌群可使膝蓋向上抬起。髖屈肌群包括髂腰肌、縫匠肌與股直肌。髂腰肌群由腰大肌與髂肌兩塊肌肉組成，這兩塊肌肉共同作用以完成髖關節屈曲；腰大肌連接於腰椎（L1至L5），另一端則連接至股骨上的肌腱。縫匠肌上端附著於髂前上棘，橫越大腿並附著於脛骨，有助於膝關節與髖關節的屈曲，以及大腿與脛骨的旋轉。股直肌是大腿前側四塊股四頭肌（股中間肌、股內側肌、股外側肌與股直肌）之一，附著於髂前下棘，向下延伸至髕骨基部，此肌肉能同時完成髖關節屈曲與膝關節伸展。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第793-794頁；第10版，第618頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 690,
      "question_en": "All patients with vertigo should receive which of the following physical examination tests?",
      "question_hant": "所有眩暈患者皆應接受以下哪項身體檢查測試？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
