        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Dix-Hallpike positional test",
          "hant": "迪克斯–霍派克體位測試",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Dix-Hallpike test helps to determine whether vertigo is triggered by certain movements of the head. The doctor observes any involuntary eye movements (nystagmus) that can occur during this test to determine if the cause of the vertigo is peripheral or central. Peripheral vertigo is due to an inner ear problem while central vertigo is caused by a problem inside the brain. The Dix-Hallpike test also helps to determine which ear is likely affected. The test is performed by the patient sitting with extended legs on the treatment table. The doctor turns the head 30 to 45 degrees toward one side. Then the doctor quickly helps the patient lie back so that the head hangs over the end of the table. During this movement the doctor watches for involuntary eye movements (called nystagmus). The timing and appearance of the eye movements help to identify the cause of vertigo as either the inner ear or the brain. The patient then sits upright for a few minutes to recover from the vertigo. Then the same procedure is repeated with the head turned in the opposite direction. The Romberg test diagnoses gait or movement disturbances. The Dynamic Illegible E test is an eye test for assessing the ocular reflex. Trendelenburg's tests for a drooping pelvis by standing on one leg.",
      "exp_hant": "迪克斯－霍派克測試有助於判定眩暈是否由特定頭部動作所誘發。醫師會在測試過程中觀察是否出現不自主眼球運動（眼震），以判定眩暈的成因屬於周邊性或中樞性：周邊性眩暈源自內耳問題，中樞性眩暈則源自腦部問題。此測試也有助於判定可能受影響的是哪一側耳朵。測試方式為請患者坐在治療床上，雙腿伸直，醫師將患者頭部轉向一側30至45度，接著迅速協助患者躺下，使頭部懸垂於床緣之外；在此動作過程中，醫師會觀察是否出現不自主眼球運動（眼震）。眼球運動出現的時機與型態有助於判定眩暈的成因為內耳或腦部問題。之後請患者坐直休息數分鐘以緩解眩暈感，再以相反方向重複同樣的程序。隆伯格測試用於診斷步態或動作障礙，動態視力E字測試是評估眼球反射的視力測試，特倫德倫伯格測試則透過單腳站立來檢測骨盆下垂。"
    },
