      "exp_en": "Muscle strength is graded on a scale of 0 to 5. 0/5 = no contraction; 1/5 = muscle flicker, but no movement; 2/5 = movement possible, but not against gravity; 3/5 = movement possible against gravity, but not against resistance by the examiner; 4/5 = movement possible against some resistance by the examiner; 5/5 = normal strength. Reflexes are graded using a 0 to 4+ scale: 0 is absence of a reflex; 1+ is a hypoactive reflex; 2+ is a normal reflex; 3+ is a hyperactive reflex without clonus; 4+ is a hyperactive reflex with clonus. Clonus is muscular spasm involving repeated, contractions. The wrist flexion is controlled by C7. The triceps tendon is controlled at C7 and the middle finger is the most innervated by C7 of all the digits. C6 is associated with arm pain on the side of the thumb, thumb and/or index finger. C7 is associated with pain located in the middle fingers. C8 is associated with pain in the ring and little finger. T1 is associated with arm pain on the little finger side. - Orthopaedic Neurology A Diagnostic Guide to Neurological Levels, Stanley Hoppenfield, 1977, J.Lippincott Company, page 17-19",
      "exp_hant": "肌力以0至5級評分：0/5為無收縮；1/5為肌肉輕微顫動但無動作；2/5為可動作但無法對抗重力；3/5為可對抗重力動作但無法對抗檢查者施加的阻力；4/5為可對抗檢查者部分阻力動作；5/5為正常肌力。反射則以0至4+級評分：0為反射消失；1+為反射減弱；2+為正常反射；3+為反射亢進但無陣攣；4+為反射亢進合併陣攣。陣攣是指反覆收縮的肌肉痙攣。腕關節屈曲由C7控制，肱三頭肌腱反射也由C7控制，而在所有手指中，中指主要由C7神經支配。C6與拇指側（拇指及／或食指）的手臂疼痛相關；C7與中指部位的疼痛相關；C8與無名指及小指的疼痛相關；T1則與小指側的手臂疼痛相關。——《骨科神經學：神經學節段診斷指南》，Stanley Hoppenfield著，1977年，J. Lippincott公司出版，第17-19頁"
    },
