          "hant": "糖尿病、利尿劑、中風",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Dysomia is not associated with diuretics. Dysomia is a disorder that qualitatively alters or distorts the perception of smell whereas anosmia is the loss of the sense of smell. Dysomia and anosmia can be caused by a number of different problems such as developmental and hereditary or degenerative disorders including Down's syndrome, Alzheimer's disease, Pick's disease, idiopathic Parkinson's disease, Huntington's disease or Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS). It can also occur from acquired metabolic and nutritional disorders such as diabetes, hypothyroidism, kidney disease, liver disease or toxic chemical exposure as well as cirrhosis of the liver. Infectious disorders that may also bring upon anosmia include: upper respiratory viral infection, acute viral hepatitis, acute poliomyelitis, bacterial meningitis, neurosyphilis, pneumonia, HIV and stroke. Neoplastic disorders can be primary or metastatic including Foster Kennedy syndrome or metastatic carcinoma. Demyelinating disorders such as multiple sclerosis, inflammatory diseases, associated with allergies, traumatic disorders associated with head trauma and epilepsy as well as drug-induced disorders because of neuroleptics, nasal surgery and rhinitis medications. Textbook of Clinical Neurology, Christopher G. Goetz, MD and Eric J. Pappert, 1999, W.B., Saunders Company, page 99",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整且正確的答案。嗅覺異常與利尿劑無關。嗅覺異常是一種使嗅覺感知產生質變或扭曲的病症，而嗅覺喪失則是指嗅覺功能的完全喪失。嗅覺異常與嗅覺喪失可由多種不同問題引起，例如發育性、遺傳性或退化性疾病，包括唐氏症、阿茲海默症、皮克病、原發性帕金森氏症、亨丁頓舞蹈症或肌萎縮性側索硬化症（ALS）；也可能源自後天性代謝與營養疾病，例如糖尿病、甲狀腺功能低下、腎臟疾病、肝臟疾病、毒性化學物質暴露，以及肝硬化。可能引發嗅覺喪失的感染性疾病則包括：上呼吸道病毒感染、急性病毒性肝炎、急性小兒麻痺症、細菌性腦膜炎、神經性梅毒、肺炎、HIV感染及中風。腫瘤性疾病可為原發性或轉移性，包括福斯特－甘迺迪症候群或轉移性癌症。此外，脫髓鞘疾病（如多發性硬化症）、與過敏相關的發炎性疾病、與頭部外傷及癲癇相關的創傷性疾病，以及因抗精神病藥物、鼻部手術與鼻炎藥物所致的藥源性疾病，皆可能造成嗅覺異常。《臨床神經學教科書》，Christopher G. Goetz醫師與Eric J. Pappert著，1999年，W.B. Saunders公司出版，第99頁"
