      ],
      "exp_en": "Myelopathy means damage to the spinal cord. In cervical myelopathy there is damage to the cervical part of the spinal cord. Cervical myelopathy is usually from spondylosis which arises from cervical degenerative disc disorder from spurs, disc herniation, cervical stenosis. The physical signs include clonus (muscular spasm) at the wrist, knee, or ankle. There can be a positive Babinski sign and gait disturbance (walking like a robot). Flexing the neck can produce an electrical shock radiating down the spine. Diagnosis is via x-ray, MRI, Treatment involves neck bracing and surgical evaluation. Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 827; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 643",
      "exp_hant": "脊髓病變是指脊髓受到損傷；頸髓病變則是指脊髓頸段受損。頸髓病變通常源自頸椎病，而頸椎病則起因於頸椎椎間盤退化性病變，包括骨刺、椎間盤突出及頸椎椎管狹窄。理學徵象包括手腕、膝關節或踝關節的陣攣（肌肉痙攣），可能出現巴賓斯基徵象陽性及步態障礙（如機器人般的步態）。頸部屈曲可能引發沿脊柱放射的電擊感。診斷方式包括X光與核磁共振（MRI），治療則包括頸部支架固定與手術評估。《Bates身體檢查指南》第13版，第827頁；第10版，第643頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 701,
      "question_en": "What is the lowest SPF (Sun Protective Factor) recommended to protect against UV-B?",
      "question_hant": "預防 UV-B 傷害所建議的最低防曬係數（SPF）為多少？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "30",
          "hant": "30",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "15",
          "hant": "15",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "35",
          "hant": "35",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "10",
          "hant": "10",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Individuals who live in areas with year-round, bright sunlight have a higher risk of skin cancer. Sunscreen is just a filter and it does not block all UV rays. Avoid using sunscreen to prolong your time in the sun. Even with sunscreen use, some of the UV rays still get through. A higher SPF number means more UVB protection. SPF 15 sunscreens filter out about 93 percent of UVB rays, while SPF 30 sunscreens filter out about 97 percent. The strength of UV-B is dependent on time of day (UV rays are strongest in the middle of the day, between 10am and 4pm), season of the year (UV rays are stronger during spring and summer months, though less of a factor near the equator), distance from the equator (UV exposure decreases the further away from the equator), altitude (more UV rays reach the ground at higher elevations), and cloud cover (effect of clouds can vary, but it is important to know that UV light can get through to the ground, even on a cloudy day). Bates's Guide to Physical Examination, 13th Edition, page 303; Bate's Guide to Physical Examination, 10th Edition, page 167",
      "exp_hant": "終年生活在陽光強烈地區的人罹患皮膚癌的風險較高。防曬乳只是一種過濾器，並無法阻擋所有紫外線。切勿因使用防曬乳而延長曝曬於陽光下的時間，即使使用防曬乳，仍有部分紫外線會穿透。防曬係數（SPF）數值越高，代表對UVB的防護力越強。SPF 15的防曬乳可過濾約93%的UVB，而SPF 30則可過濾約97%。UV-B的強度取決於一天中的時段（紫外線在上午10點至下午4點之間最強）、季節（春夏季紫外線較強，但在赤道附近影響較小）、與赤道的距離（離赤道越遠，紫外線暴露越低）、海拔高度（海拔越高，到達地面的紫外線越多），以及雲層覆蓋（雲層的影響程度不一，但須注意即使在陰天，紫外線仍可穿透到地面）。《Bates身體評估指南》第13版，第303頁；《Bates身體評估指南》第10版，第167頁"
    },
