    {
      "number": 705,
      "question_en": "Which of the following herbal sleep aids are contraindicated with liver disease?",
      "question_hant": "下列哪種草本安眠輔助品禁用於肝病患者？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "passion flower",
          "hant": "西番蓮（passion flower）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "kava kava",
          "hant": "卡瓦卡瓦（kava kava）",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "valerian",
          "hant": "纈草（valerian）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "chamomile",
          "hant": "洋甘菊（chamomile）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A patient taking kava kava with liver disease is taking a risk. Research suggests that kava may contain a chemical (Flavokawain B) that is harmful to the liver. The sale and use of kava kava has been banned in Germany, Canada, and the UK for the potential of causing liver damage. It has not been banned in the United States. Kava can aggravate symptoms of depression or Parkinson's disease. Kava has a synergistic effect with sedative medications. Chamomile can have a calming effect, which can help people feel relaxed and more prepared for sleep. It is very well tolerated by most people. Valerian is used for sleep disorders, anxiety, restlessness, PMS, or psychological stress. Valerian is likely safe for most patients when used in medicinal amounts in the short-term. In some patients valerian can have the side effects of headache, stomach upset, or excitability. When combined with sedatives (benzodiazepines, pentobarbital, etc) or alcohol, valerian can increase drowsiness and sedation. Some patients take passion flower for insomnia, anxiety, and attention deficit-hyperactivity disorder (ADHD). Passion flower can cause some side effects such as drowsiness, dizziness, and confusion. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "肝病患者服用卡瓦卡瓦具有風險。研究顯示卡瓦可能含有一種對肝臟有害的化學物質（Flavokawain B）。德國、加拿大與英國已因其可能造成肝損傷而禁止卡瓦卡瓦的銷售與使用，美國則尚未禁止。卡瓦可能加重憂鬱症或帕金森氏症的症狀，並與鎮靜藥物具有協同作用。洋甘菊具有鎮靜效果，有助於使人放鬆並更容易入睡，大多數人對其耐受性良好。纈草用於治療睡眠障礙、焦慮、躁動不安、經前症候群或心理壓力。短期以藥用劑量使用纈草對大多數患者而言可能是安全的，但部分患者可能出現頭痛、腸胃不適或興奮等副作用。與鎮靜劑（如苯二氮平類、戊巴比妥等）或酒精併用時，纈草可能增加嗜睡與鎮靜作用。部分患者服用西番蓮以治療失眠、焦慮及注意力不足過動症（ADHD），其副作用可能包括嗜睡、頭暈與意識混亂。tcmtests.com，2019年2月"
