    {
      "number": 712,
      "question_en": "Which of the following has the correct mechanism of action for the chemotherapy drug classes?",
      "question_hant": "下列何者正確描述化療藥物類別的作用機轉？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "antimetabolites destroy microtubules preventing their function",
          "hant": "抗代謝物（antimetabolites）破壞微管以阻止其功能",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "antitumor antibiotics bind with DNA and prevent RNA synthesis",
          "hant": "抗腫瘤抗生素（antitumor antibiotics）與DNA結合以阻止RNA合成",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "alkylating agents increase the DNA to prevent cancer cell multiplication",
          "hant": "烷化劑（alkylating agents）增加DNA以阻止癌細胞增殖",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "vinca alkaloids block cell growth by interfering with DNA synthesis",
          "hant": "長春花生物鹼（vinca alkaloids）藉由干擾DNA合成阻斷細胞生長",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The correct answers are: antitumor antibiotics bind with DNA and prevent RNA synthesis. Vinca alkaloids destroy microtubules preventing their function. Antimetabolites block cell growth by interfering with DNA synthesis. Alkylating agents damage the DNA to prevent the cell from reproducing. ANTITUMOR ANTIBIOTICS are not the same as antibiotics. The actual mechanism of action for this class of cancer drugs is that they bind with DNA and prevent RNA synthesis, which is a key step in cell protein creation necessary for cell survival. They are widely used for a variety of cancers (leukemia, GI, lung, and bladder cancers). Antitumor antibiotic drugs are given via IV. Examples include doxorubicin and epirubicin. It is another drug class, the MITOTIC INHIBITORS, that block protein building enzymes needed for cell reproduction. This class of drug prevents the formation of mitotic spindles without which the the cell cannot divide. These drugs are administered via IV. Examples include Paclitaxel, Docetaxel, Vincristine and Vinblastine. ALKYLATING AGENTS directly attack cellular DNA thus preventing the cell from reproducing. They treat Hodgkin's disease, lymphomas, chronic leukemias, and lung, breast, prostrate, and ovary cancers. Examples are Cyclophosphamide and Ifosamide. ANTIMETABOLITES block protein building enzymes needed for cell reproduction. These drugs inhibit production of an acid necessary for DNA to be synthesized. They are administered either orally or by IV. Examples include 6-mercaptopurine, floxuridine, and gemcitabine. Antimetabolites is the largest class of anti-cancer drugs. VINCA ALKALOIDS, derived from the periwinkle plant, destroy microtubules which are hollow cylinders in the cell that help to maintain cell shape integrity and help to move the chromosomes at either end of the call during mitosis. Examples include Paclitaxel, Docetaxel, Vincristine and Vinblastine. All vinca alkaloids are via IV. This class of drug treats melanoma, lung cancers, leukemia, Hodgkins's disease, and other lymphomas. tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "正確答案為：抗腫瘤抗生素與DNA結合以阻止RNA合成。長春花生物鹼破壞微管以阻止其功能。抗代謝物藉由干擾DNA合成阻斷細胞生長。烷化劑破壞DNA以阻止癌細胞繁殖。「抗腫瘤抗生素」與一般抗生素並不相同，此類抗癌藥物的實際作用機轉是與DNA結合，阻止RNA合成，而RNA合成是細胞蛋白質生成、進而維持細胞存活的關鍵步驟。此類藥物廣泛用於多種癌症（白血病、腸胃道、肺部及膀胱癌），皆以靜脈注射給藥，例如doxorubicin（阿黴素）及epirubicin（表柔比星）。另一類藥物「有絲分裂抑制劑」則會阻斷細胞複製所需的蛋白質建構酶，藉由阻止紡錘體形成使細胞無法分裂，此類藥物亦以靜脈注射給藥，例如Paclitaxel（紫杉醇）、Docetaxel（多西他賽）、Vincristine（長春新鹼）及Vinblastine（長春鹼）。「烷化劑」直接攻擊細胞DNA，阻止細胞複製，可治療何杰金氏病、淋巴瘤、慢性白血病，以及肺、乳房、前列腺與卵巢癌，例如Cyclophosphamide（環磷醯胺）及Ifosfamide（異環磷醯胺）。「抗代謝物」阻斷細胞複製所需的蛋白質建構酶，此類藥物抑制DNA合成所需酸的生成，可口服或靜脈注射給藥，例如6-mercaptopurine（6-巰基嘌呤）、floxuridine（氟尿苷）及gemcitabine（吉西他濱），抗代謝物是抗癌藥物中最大的類別。「長春花生物鹼」萃取自長春花，能破壞細胞內維持形狀完整並協助有絲分裂時移動染色體的中空圓柱狀微管，例如Paclitaxel、Docetaxel、Vincristine及Vinblastine，所有長春花生物鹼皆以靜脈注射給藥，此類藥物可治療黑色素瘤、肺癌、白血病、何杰金氏病及其他淋巴瘤。tcmtests.com，2020年7月"
    },
