      "exp_en": "One theory to explain what causes migraines focuses on the derangement of serotonin metabolism. During a migraine, serotonin levels are depressed in the brain, and certain drugs, called triptans, have been shown to reduce the symptoms of migraine. This theory is supported by the fact that the pineal gland releases both melatonin and serotonin. Melatonin is also reduced during a migraine, suggesting that the pineal gland is depressed in migraine patients. tcmtests.com, April 2020",
