      "exp_en": "How much calcium the body needs depends on age and sex. Calcium is a macromineral that is also an electrolyte. It is important for maintaining proper nerve and heart function, blood clotting, muscle contraction, and bone formation. THERAPEUTIC: Taking oral calcium can be effective for preventing bone loss and treating osteoporosis. Conditions like hypoparathyroidism, where the parathyroid glands do not produce enough parathyroid hormone, or after parathyroid surgery, can lead to low blood calcium levels. Calcium supplements, often in forms like calcium gluconate or calcium carbonate, are used to correct this deficiency. The combination of calcium and vitamin D supplementation can reduce the symptoms of PMS, especially menstrual cramps. Also, taking magnesium with the calcium is more effective for PMS than just calcium by itself.. CALCIUM DEFICIENCY: muscle spasms, confusion, bone loss. Severe calcium deficiency can lead to memory loss or confusion because low calcium levels affects the functioning of the nervous system. DRUG INTERACTIONS: Calcium has a moderate interaction with antibiotics and can decrease their absorption. Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 48-49, 54; www.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "人體所需鈣質的多寡取決於年齡與性別。鈣是一種巨量礦物質，同時也是一種電解質，對於維持正常的神經與心臟功能、血液凝固、肌肉收縮及骨骼形成十分重要。【治療用途】口服鈣質可有效預防骨質流失並治療骨質疏鬆症。副甲狀腺機能低下（副甲狀腺無法分泌足夠副甲狀腺荷爾蒙）或副甲狀腺手術後，可能導致血鈣過低，此時常使用碳酸鈣或葡萄糖酸鈣等形式的鈣質補充品來矯正此缺乏。鈣質與維生素D併用可減輕經前症候群的症狀，尤其是經痛；此外，鈣質搭配鎂質，比單獨使用鈣質更能有效改善經前症候群。【鈣質缺乏】肌肉痙攣、意識混亂、骨質流失。嚴重的鈣質缺乏可能因影響神經系統功能而導致記憶喪失或意識混亂。【藥物交互作用】鈣與抗生素有中度交互作用，可能降低抗生素的吸收。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第48-49、54頁；www.webmd.com"
