      "exp_en": "The pharmacokinetics of Amitriptyline is complex, involving a secondary metabolite nortriptyline with P450 and P-glycoprotein. St. John's wort induces CYP 450 3A4 and P-glycoprotein, thereby resulting in possible decreased bioavailability of the drug. This is complicated by well-known genetic polymorphisms in CYP 2D6, which can increase the unpredictability of how Amitriptyline is metabolized. For these reasons, coadministration of St. John's wort with tricyclics is contraindicated. Herb, Nutrient, and Drug Interactions: Clinical Implications and Therapeutic Strategies, 2008, Stargrove, Treasure, and McKee, pages 145-6",
      "exp_hant": "Amitriptyline的藥物動力學相當複雜，涉及次級代謝產物nortriptyline，並牽涉P450酵素與P醣蛋白。聖約翰草會誘導CYP450 3A4酵素及P醣蛋白，可能導致該藥物的生體可用率降低。此情況因CYP2D6眾所周知的基因多型性而更加複雜，可能增加Amitriptyline代謝方式的不可預測性。基於上述原因，聖約翰草與三環類抗憂鬱藥併用屬於禁忌。《草藥、營養素與藥物交互作用：臨床意義與治療策略》，2008年，Stargrove、Treasure與McKee合著，第145-146頁"
