        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "pernicious anemia but not macrocytic anemia",
          "hant": "惡性貧血，但不能治療巨球性貧血（macrocytic anemia）",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "pernicious anemia and megaloblastic anemia",
          "hant": "惡性貧血及巨球性貧血（megaloblastic anemia）",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Vitamin B12 is an essential vitamin that comes from the diet and is present in all animal foods. As such, vegetarians are most susceptible to a deficiency. Vitamin B12 is required for the proper functioning and development of the brain, nerves, and blood cells. In macrocytic anemia the red blood cells are larger than normal. Both pernicious anemia (lack of intrinsic factor) and megaloblastic anemia (inhibition of DNA that makes red blood cell) are a type of macrocytic anemia. Hemolytic anemia is due to the the abnormal breakdown of red blood cells. THERAPEUTIC: B12 treats pernicious anemia with low red blood cell counts caused by poor absorption of vitamin B12 in the stomach. Together B12, folic acid and B6 may lower blood levels of homocysteine, a marker for heart disease. DEFICIENCY: The main causes of vitamin B12 deficiency include vitamin B12 malabsorption from food, pernicious anemia, postsurgical malabsorption, and dietary deficiency. Pernicious anemia is due to a lack of the intrinsic factor in the stomach which is necessary for B12 absorption. A deficiency can cause anemia. This anemia has slow-onset with moderate to severe manifestations with a pale or sallow complexion, glossitis (sore, inflamed tongue), poor appetite, diarrhea, neurologic symptoms such as paresthesia and cognitive decline such as poor memory. TOXICITY: No adverse effects have been associated with excess vitamin B12 intake from food and supplements in healthy individuals. DRUG INTERACTIONS: Proton pump inhibitors, such as omeprazole (Prilosec) and lansoprazole (Prevacid), treat gastroesophageal reflux disease and peptic ulcer disease. These drugs can interfere with vitamin B12 absorption from food. Histamine H2 receptor antagonists that treat peptic ulcer disease, such as cimetidine (Tagamet), famotidine (Pepcid), and ranitidine (Zantac), can interfere with the absorption of vitamin B12 from food by slowing the release of hydrochloric acid into the stomach. There can be an interaction with the antibiotic chloramphenicol. This drug may decrease new blood cells while B12 is used to make new blood cells. Current Medical and Diagnostic Treatment 2020, page 522; wwww.webmd.com; ods.od.nih.gov",
      "exp_hant": "維生素B12是一種必需維生素，來自飲食，存在於所有動物性食物中，因此素食者最容易出現缺乏症。維生素B12是腦部、神經及血球正常功能與發育所必需的物質。巨球性貧血是指紅血球體積大於正常。惡性貧血（缺乏內在因子）與巨球性貧血（DNA合成受阻導致紅血球生成受抑制）皆屬於巨球性貧血的一種類型；溶血性貧血則是因紅血球異常破壞所致。【治療用途】B12可治療因胃部維生素B12吸收不良、造成紅血球數量偏低的惡性貧血。B12搭配葉酸與B6可能降低血中同半胱胺酸（一種心臟病指標）的濃度。【缺乏】維生素B12缺乏的主要原因包括食物中維生素B12吸收不良、惡性貧血、術後吸收不良，以及飲食攝取不足。惡性貧血是因胃部缺乏B12吸收所需的內在因子所致。缺乏會導致貧血，此貧血起病緩慢，中至重度表現包括臉色蒼白或萎黃、舌炎（舌頭疼痛發炎）、食慾不振、腹瀉，以及感覺異常、認知功能減退（如記憶力變差）等神經學症狀。【毒性】健康人由食物及補充品攝取過量維生素B12並無不良反應紀錄。【藥物交互作用】質子幫浦抑制劑，如omeprazole（Prilosec）及lansoprazole（Prevacid），用於治療胃食道逆流及消化性潰瘍，可能干擾食物中維生素B12的吸收。用於治療消化性潰瘍的組織胺H2受體拮抗劑，如cimetidine（Tagamet）、famotidine（Pepcid）及ranitidine（Zantac），可能藉由減緩胃酸釋放而干擾食物中維生素B12的吸收。此外也可能與抗生素chloramphenicol（氯黴素）產生交互作用，該藥物可能減少新血球的生成，而B12正是用於製造新血球。《當代醫學診斷與治療2020》，第522頁；wwww.webmd.com；ods.od.nih.gov"
    },
    {
      "number": 745,
      "question_en": "A 26 year-old patient comes to your office complaining of fatigue, brain fog and joint pain that started after a tick bite 8 years ago. At the time of the tick bite, she was treated for acute Lyme disease with doxycycline, but symptoms have persisted. Recently, her physician started her on a protocol of 100mg of minocycline twice daily plus Florastor probiotic BID ongoing to treat persistent Lyme. She also has a history of Type I diabetes, and lately has noticed increased diarrhea, loss of appetite and loss of sense of taste. What drug/nutrient interaction should you be thinking about?",
      "question_hant": "一名26歲患者前來就診，主訴自8年前被蜱蟲叮咬後出現疲勞、腦霧及關節痛。當時因急性萊姆病接受doxycycline（去氧羥四環素）治療，但症狀持續未癒。近期醫師開始為她進行療程：每日兩次、每次100毫克的minocycline（美滿黴素），並持續搭配Florastor益生菌每日兩次，以治療持續性萊姆病。她同時患有第一型糖尿病，近來出現腹瀉加劇、食慾不振及味覺喪失。你應考慮下列哪種藥物/營養素交互作用？",
      "image": null,
