      "exp_en": "Tetracycline and some related antibiotics tend to form insoluble chelates with zinc salts, thereby impairing absorption and therapeutic efficacy of both agents. While Doxycycline has not been found to interact with Zinc, minocycline does interfere with Zinc absorption. Patients with diabetes are more prone to Zinc depletion, as well as those with suppressed immunity, such as those with persistent Lyme. Hypogeusia (loss of taste) is a common sign of Zinc depletion. Patients taking tetracycline antibiotics other than doxycycline should take their Zinc containing supplements (or foods) 2 hours prior or 4 hours after taking their medication. Herb, Nutrient, and Drug Interactions: Clinical Implications and Therapeutic Strategies, 2008, Stargrove, Treasure, and McKee, pages 643-4",
      "exp_hant": "四環黴素及部分相關抗生素易與鋅鹽形成不溶性螯合物，進而降低兩者的吸收與治療效果。雖然doxycycline未被發現會與鋅產生交互作用，但minocycline確實會干擾鋅的吸收。糖尿病患者較易出現鋅缺乏，免疫功能受抑制者（如持續性萊姆病患者）亦然。味覺減退（喪失味覺）是鋅缺乏的常見徵象。服用除doxycycline以外之四環黴素類抗生素的患者，應在服藥前2小時或服藥後4小時再攝取含鋅補充品或食物。《草藥、營養素與藥物交互作用：臨床意義與治療策略》，2008年，Stargrove、Treasure與McKee合著，第643-644頁"
