      "exp_en": "The number after the \"T\" letter, means the number of iodine atoms in the molecule in thyroid hormones. The body cannot make iodine. The iodine must come from the diet or as supplement. Generally, there is very little iodine in our food, unless it has been added. THERAPEUTIC: The thyroid gland requres iodine. When it is severely lacking, it can cause an enlarged thyroid gland (goiter). In women, iodine deficiency can stop ovulation. During pregnancy an iodine deficiency will affect both the mother and fetus. For the mother, a deficiency can increase blood pressure during pregnancy. For the fetus, a deficiency can impair fetal growth and brain development. IODINE DEFICIENCY: goiter, infertility. DRUG INTERACTIONS: Iodine supplements are contraindicated with drugs that treat hyperthyroidism. Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 48-49, 54; www.webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "甲狀腺荷爾蒙名稱中「T」後方的數字，代表該分子中碘原子的數目。人體無法自行製造碘，必須從飲食或補充品中攝取。一般而言，除非額外添加，否則食物中碘含量極少。【治療用途】甲狀腺需要碘，若嚴重缺乏，可能導致甲狀腺腫大（甲狀腺腫）。在女性，碘缺乏可能使排卵停止。懷孕期間碘缺乏會同時影響母體與胎兒：對母體而言，缺乏可能升高懷孕期間的血壓；對胎兒而言，缺乏可能損害胎兒生長與腦部發育。【碘缺乏】甲狀腺腫、不孕。【藥物交互作用】碘補充品禁忌與治療甲狀腺機能亢進的藥物併用。《默克診療手冊》第18版，第48-49、54頁；www.webmd.com"
