      "exp_en": "One of the tests use to diagnose shoulder impingement is the Neer's test. In this test patient sits or stands with arm relaxed at side. The examiner stabilizes the scapula with a downward force while passively flexing the patient's internally rotated humerus into full elevation. Pain is positive. The Tinel's test helps to diagnose carpal tunnel syndrome. Biceps tendinitis most often affects the long head of the biceps tendon. Rotator cuff tears most often affect the supraspinatus tendon. BICEPS TENDINITIS: Occurs most commonly in the long head of the biceps tendon. Inflammation is caused by micro tears in the tendon due to repetitive motion (throwing, swimming, serving, swinging a golf club, etc). Also, arthritis can cause bone spurs that can impact the biceps tendon.Biceps tendonitis affects the anterior part of the shoulder. As tendinitis develops, the tendon sheath (covering) can thicken. Then the tendon itself can thicken. Pain or tenderness in the front of the shoulder worsens with overhead lifting or activity. There can also be an occasional snapping sound when moving the shoulder. TEST: In the Speed's test the arm is raised parallel to the floor with palm facing up. The examiner pushes the arm down while the patient resists. Pain in front of shoulder during test is positive. ROTATOR CUFF TEAR: The rotator cuff is a group of muscles and tendons (supraspinatus, infraspinatus, teres minor, subscapularis) that stabilize the shoulder joint. An injury or degeneration due to age can cause a tear to one of the rotator cuff tendons. The tear can be partial or a complete tear (full thickness) separating the tendon from the bone. With a complete tear there is significant weakness with an inability to raise the arm against gravity. The most common is a supraspinatus tendon tear. The supraspinatus is located at the top of the shoulder blade and inserts at the top humerus bone. The main action of the supraspinatus is to abduct the shoulder joint. There is weakness and pain (deep dull ache) making it difficult to comb one's hair or reaching behind the back. Common symptoms include pain during rest and at night, pain lying on affected shoulder, pain or weakness lifting and lowering arm, and crepitus (crackling sensation when moving shoulder). TEST: The drop arm test is used to assess for full thickness rotator cuff tears, particularly of the supraspinatus. Stand behind the seated patient and passively abduct the patients arm to 90 degrees and full external rotation while supporting the arm at the elbow. Release elbow support and ask patient to slowly lower the arm. The test is positive if there is a sudden dropping of the arm. SHOULDER IMPINGEMENT: Occurs when the acromion of the shoulder blade impinges (rubs against or pinches) the rotator cuff beneath it. This causes pain and irritation. When the rotator cuff is irritated or injured or from age-related wear and tear it becomes inflamed and swells. The swelling reduces the amount of space around the rotator cuff. This leads to rubbing against the acromion. The rubbing of the rotator cuff tendons result in swelling, which further narrows the space below the acromion. Other causes of the narrowing can be due to bone spurs on the acromion bone or the local bursa can become inflamed due to overuse of the shoulder or injury. Pain goes from front of shoulder to the side of the arm can be constant and worsens at night. There can be shoulder or arm weakness. Shoulder impingement can occur with a rotator cuff tear or bursitis. TEST: In the Hawkin-Kennedy Test the examiner moves the arm of the shoulder to be tested such in a 90 degrees of forward flexion and the elbow is flexed to 90 degrees. The examiner forcefully moves the patient's shoulder into internal rotation to the end or range of motion or until reports of pain. The test is positive if pain is reported in the superior and lateral aspect of the shoulder. ADHESIVE CAPSULITIS: Also known as \"frozen shoulder\". It refers to restricted shoulder mobility that causes pain and results in a functional disability. Patients with adhesive capsulitis often cannot raise their arm laterally past 90 degrees relative to their torso without elevating the entire shoulder girdle. TEST: One test that can be used is the Apley Scratch Test which is the inability to reach behind the back from below to scratch an itch between the shoulder blades. NOTE: Unexplained shoulder pain that does not change or that occurs with symptoms elsewhere in the body (such as in your abdomen or chest) may be referred shoulder pain. Ask every patient with left shoulder pain about chest pain and SOB to screen for cardiovascular causes. Ask every patient with right shoulder pain about nausea/vomiting and abdominal pain to screen for cholelithiasis.. Differential Diagnosis of Common Complaints, Sellers and Symons, 7th Edition, page 310; webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "用於診斷肩夾擠症候群的測試之一為尼爾氏測試（Neer's test）：測試時患者坐姿或站姿，手臂自然放鬆垂於身側，檢查者以向下的力量固定肩胛骨，同時被動地將患者內旋的肱骨屈曲至完全上舉，若出現疼痛則為陽性。蒂內爾氏測試（Tinel's test）有助於診斷腕隧道症候群。二頭肌肌腱炎最常影響二頭肌肌腱的長頭。旋轉肌袖撕裂最常影響棘上肌肌腱。【二頭肌肌腱炎】最常發生於二頭肌肌腱的長頭，其發炎源於重複動作（如投擲、游泳、發球、揮高爾夫球桿等）所造成的肌腱微小撕裂。此外，關節炎也可能引起骨刺並影響二頭肌肌腱。二頭肌肌腱炎影響肩部前側，隨著肌腱炎發展，肌腱鞘（包覆層）可能增厚，之後肌腱本身也可能增厚。肩部前側的疼痛或壓痛會因過頭舉物或活動而加劇，活動肩膀時偶爾也會出現彈響聲。【測試】斯皮德測試（Speed's test）：手臂與地面平行舉起、掌心朝上，檢查者向下推壓手臂，患者則予以抵抗，若肩部前方出現疼痛則為陽性。【旋轉肌袖撕裂】旋轉肌袖是一組穩定肩關節的肌肉與肌腱（棘上肌、棘下肌、小圓肌、肩胛下肌），因受傷或隨年齡退化，可能導致其中一條旋轉肌袖肌腱撕裂，可能為部分撕裂或完全撕裂（全層撕裂），使肌腱與骨骼分離。完全撕裂時會出現顯著無力，無法對抗重力舉起手臂，最常見的是棘上肌肌腱撕裂。棘上肌位於肩胛骨頂部，止於肱骨頂端，其主要作用是外展肩關節。患者會出現無力與疼痛（深部隱隱作痛），使梳頭或將手伸至背後變得困難，常見症狀包括休息及夜間疼痛、患側臥躺時疼痛、舉起與放下手臂時疼痛或無力，以及活動肩膀時的摩擦音。【測試】垂臂試驗（drop arm test）用於評估全層旋轉肌袖撕裂，尤其是棘上肌撕裂：站在坐姿患者身後，被動將患者手臂外展至90度並完全外旋，同時於肘部支撐手臂，隨後放開對肘部的支撐，請患者緩慢放下手臂，若手臂突然掉落則為陽性。【肩夾擠症候群】發生於肩胛骨的肩峰夾擠（摩擦或擠壓）其下方的旋轉肌袖，造成疼痛與刺激。當旋轉肌袖因刺激、受傷或隨年齡退化而發炎腫脹時，會使旋轉肌袖周圍的空間縮小，導致與肩峰摩擦。旋轉肌袖肌腱的摩擦會造成腫脹，進一步縮小肩峰下方的空間。其他造成空間縮小的原因，還包括肩峰骨刺，或因肩部過度使用或受傷而造成的局部滑囊發炎。疼痛從肩部前方延伸至手臂外側，可能持續存在並於夜間加劇，也可能出現肩部或手臂無力。肩夾擠症候群可能與旋轉肌袖撕裂或滑囊炎併發。【測試】霍金－甘迺迪測試（Hawkin-Kennedy Test）：檢查者將待測肩膀的手臂移至前屈90度、肘部彎曲90度的姿勢，隨後用力將患者肩部內旋至活動範圍終點或直到出現疼痛，若肩部上外側出現疼痛則為陽性。【沾黏性肩關節囊炎】又稱「冰凍肩」，指肩部活動受限，造成疼痛並導致功能障礙。沾黏性肩關節囊炎患者通常無法在不連動整個肩胛帶的情況下，將手臂側舉超過相對於軀幹90度的角度。【測試】阿普利搔背測試（Apley Scratch Test）是可用的測試之一，即無法從下方將手伸至背後搔抓兩肩胛骨之間的癢處。【注意】不明原因、性質不變的肩痛，或伴隨身體其他部位症狀（如腹部或胸部）的肩痛，可能是轉移性肩痛。對於左肩疼痛的患者，應詢問是否有胸痛及呼吸急促，以篩檢心血管疾病；對於右肩疼痛的患者，應詢問是否有噁心／嘔吐及腹痛，以篩檢膽結石。《常見主訴之鑑別診斷》，Sellers與Symons合著，第7版，第310頁；webmd.com"
    },
