      ],
      "exp_en": "The circadian rhythm is controlled by the hypothalamus. The circadian rhythm helps to regulate sleep, body temperature, digestion, and hormones. The circadian clock resets itself every 24 hours based on the the light and darkness cycle. The amount of time exposed to light, melatonin, cortisol, physical activity, and age influence the 24 hour circadian sleep-wake cycle. Normally, a person wakes up in the morning and will gradually become tired and sleepy in the evening when it is dark out. Circadian rhythm sleep disorders are a group of sleep disorders that share the common feature of a disruption in the timing of sleep. DELAYED SLEEP DISORDER: The sleep-wake cycle is delayed resulting in difficulty falling asleep at night. A \"night owl\" who can be alert, productive late at night may not be able to fall asleep until 2 AM or later but then sleeps until as late as 11 AM or later. In delayed sleep disorder the patient is most alert and creative late at night. If they wake up too early, they are sleepy during the day. It is most commonly seen in adolescents and young adults. ADVANCED SLEEP DISORDER: The sleep-wake cycles is advanced resulting in falling asleep too early. The person falls asleep in the early evening (6 PM to 9 PM) and then wakes up in the early morning (2 AM to 5AM). The person complains of early morning awakening or insomnia and are sleepy in late afternoon or early evening. Is most commonly seen in middle age patients and older adults. JET LAG: The 24-hour circadian rhythm has been disturbed from long air travel time to a destination that is two or more time zones different. This sleep-wake cycle disruption makes it difficult to adjust in the new time zone. Traveling eastward travel is more difficult than traveling westward because it is easier to delay sleep than to advance sleep. Jet lag is associated with appetite and digestive changes (bowel and stomach,general tiredness, uneasiness, and mood disturbance. SHIFT WORK DISORDER: The patient frequently rotates shifts or works at night. These work schedules conflict with the body's natural circadian rhythm which makes it difficult to adjust. In shift work disorder there is a recurrent pattern of interrupted sleep that causes insomnia or excessive sleepiness. Sleep work disorder is associated with ongoing tiredness, mood disorder, uneasiness, digestive problems, and decreased sex drive. TREATMENT: Treatment options include 1) Lifestyle and behavior therapy to develop good sleep habits which includes maintaining regular sleep-wake hours, avoiding naps or high intensity exercises one our before sleep, and avoiding nicotine, alcohol, and caffeine before bedtime. 2) Bright-light therapy (2,000 to 9,500 lux) can treat advanced or delayed circadian disturbances. Bright light therapy resets and syncs the circadian clock with the natural cycle of light and dark. Exposure to bright light in the morning and decreasing exposure to light in the evening can help the delayed sleep disorder. Exposure to bright light in the evening may help with advanced sleep disorder. 3) Medications such as OTC melatonin, prescription drugs that promote wakefulness such as modafinilor, and short-term sleep prescription drugs.. clevelandclinic.org; webmd.com; sleepfoundation.org",
      "exp_hant": "生理時鐘由下視丘控制，有助於調節睡眠、體溫、消化及荷爾蒙。生理時鐘會依據光線與黑暗的循環，每24小時重新校準一次。曝露於光線下的時間、褪黑激素、皮質醇、身體活動及年齡，皆會影響24小時的生理睡眠—清醒週期。正常情況下，人在早晨醒來，隨著夜晚天色變暗會逐漸感到疲倦與睏意。生理時鐘睡眠障礙是一類睡眠障礙的統稱，其共同特徵是睡眠時間點的紊亂。【睡眠期後移症候群】睡眠—清醒週期延後，導致夜間難以入睡。「夜貓族」在深夜仍能保持警醒、有生產力，可能直到凌晨2點或更晚才能入睡，但可能睡到上午11點或更晚才醒來。睡眠期後移症候群患者在深夜最為清醒且富創造力，若過早醒來，白天會感到嗜睡，此症最常見於青少年及年輕成人。【睡眠期前移症候群】睡眠—清醒週期提前，導致過早入睡。患者於傍晚早段（下午6點至9點）即入睡，並於凌晨（2點至5點）醒來，主訴為過早清醒或失眠，並於下午晚段或傍晚感到睏倦，最常見於中年患者及年長成人。【時差】長時間搭機前往兩個或以上時區之外的目的地，會擾亂24小時的生理時鐘，此種睡眠—清醒週期的紊亂使人難以適應新時區。向東旅行比向西旅行更為困難，因為延後睡眠比提前睡眠來得容易。時差與食慾及消化變化（腸胃問題）、整體疲倦、不適及情緒困擾有關。【輪班工作睡眠障礙】患者經常輪班或於夜間工作，此類工作時間表與人體自然的生理時鐘相衝突，使其難以適應。輪班工作睡眠障礙表現為反覆出現的睡眠中斷模式，導致失眠或過度嗜睡，並與持續性疲倦、情緒障礙、不適、消化問題及性慾降低有關。【治療】治療選項包括：1）生活型態與行為療法，以養成良好睡眠習慣，包括維持規律的睡眠—清醒時間、避免午睡或睡前一小時高強度運動、避免睡前使用尼古丁、酒精及咖啡因。2）強光療法（2,000至9,500勒克斯）可治療睡眠期前移或後移的紊亂，強光療法能重新校準並同步生理時鐘與自然的光暗週期；早晨曝露於強光下、傍晚減少光線曝露，有助於改善睡眠期後移症候群；傍晚曝露於強光下則可能有助於改善睡眠期前移症候群。3）藥物治療，如非處方褪黑激素、可促進清醒的處方藥（如modafinil）以及短期使用的安眠處方藥。clevelandclinic.org；webmd.com；sleepfoundation.org"
