      "exp_en": "MORTON'S NEUROMA: With Mortons neuroma, there is no growth or tumor. It is an actual growth around the nerve. Instead, the existing tissue around the nerve becomes inflamed. Normally, the neuroma usually occurs between the bones of the third and fourth but can also occur between the second and third. There is no visible sign such as a lump. It is often caused by excessive pressure or compression between the toes. The compression causes inflammation and irritation. It commonly occurs in women who wear high heels. When walking the patient may feel a pain near the ball of the foot as if there is a small pebble inside the shoe. Pain worsens when wearing high-heeled shoes or when the patient stands on the balls of the feet. CHARCOT FOOT: This often occurs in diabetic patients. The pain is diffuse and there is lack of sensation on the foot. The pain is worse with walking. The foot can be warm, red, and swollen. BONE SPURS: on the foot spurs usually occur on the heel. A heel spur is a pointy bone growth or calcium deposits that form on the calcaneus (heel). There is pain where the tendon attaches at the spur. They can exist on their own but most often they develop with either plantar fasciitis or with achilles tendonitis. PLANTAR FASCIITIS: The plantar fascia is a fibrous, soft tissue that stretches from the heel to the toes. If this tissue experiences small tears and inflammation it is called plantar fasciitis. Many people who have plantar fasciitis also have heel spurs that are visible on the X-rays. Patients with plantar fasciitis often have increased heel pain with their first steps in the morning or when they stand up after prolonged sitting. There is usually tenderness at the calcaneal tuberosity and pain is increased with passive dorsiflexion of the toes. Plantar fasciitis has pain localized in the foot and heel area. Symptoms of plantar fasciitis may be present for some time before the stabbing sensation of heel spurs manifests since untreated plantar fasciitis is the primary causes of heel spurs. Plantar fasciitis is common in runners.. Differential Diagnosis of Common Complaints, Sellers and Symons, 7th Edition, page 278, 279; webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "莫頓神經瘤：莫頓神經瘤並非真正的腫瘤或增生，而是神經周圍既有組織發炎所致。此神經瘤通常發生於第三與第四蹠骨之間，但也可能發生於第二與第三蹠骨之間。外觀上通常看不到腫塊等徵象，常因腳趾間受到過度擠壓或壓迫而引起發炎與刺激，好發於穿高跟鞋的女性。行走時患者可能感覺腳掌前部有如鞋內藏有一顆小石子般的疼痛，穿高跟鞋或以腳掌前部站立時疼痛會加劇。夏科氏足：常見於糖尿病患者，疼痛呈瀰漫性且腳部感覺喪失，行走時疼痛加劇，足部可能出現溫熱、發紅與腫脹。骨刺：足部的骨刺通常出現在足跟。足跟骨刺是跟骨上形成的尖狀骨質增生或鈣質沉積，疼痛出現在肌腱附著於骨刺之處。骨刺可單獨存在，但多半伴隨足底筋膜炎或跟腱炎而發生。足底筋膜炎：足底筋膜是一條從足跟延伸至腳趾的纖維軟組織，若此組織出現微小撕裂與發炎，即稱為足底筋膜炎。許多足底筋膜炎患者的X光也可見足跟骨刺。足底筋膜炎患者常在早晨起床邁出第一步，或久坐後站起時足跟疼痛加劇。通常在跟骨結節處有壓痛，被動背屈腳趾時疼痛會加劇。足底筋膜炎的疼痛侷限於足部與足跟區域。足底筋膜炎的症狀往往在足跟骨刺的刺痛感出現之前已存在一段時間，因為未經治療的足底筋膜炎正是足跟骨刺形成的主要原因。足底筋膜炎常見於跑步者。《常見主訴之鑑別診斷》，Sellers與Symons著，第7版，頁278-279；webmd.com"
