          "hant": "體重過輕",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Oral contraceptives are not recommended for women older than the age of 35 who smoke because it increases the risk of cardiovascular disease. Furthermore, women should be screened for high blood pressure before taking birth control pills because the combination of HBP and the pill increases the risk of stroke. Birth control pills are not recommended for women who have uncontrolled HBP (high blood pressure), diabetes, or polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS). Neither are they recommended to women who have a history of heart disease, stroke, or blood clots or risk factors for heart disease (high cholesterol levels, obesity). They are not recommended to women who have migraines with aura. The pill can also predispose a women to have DVT (deep vein thrombosis) because the hormones in the pill increase the clotting ability of blood. As such, it is generally not recommended or will require close monitoring by a physician if the patient is overweight, has a history of deep vein thrombosis (DVT), or has a family history of blood clotting disorders. Clotting risk increases with larger doses of estrogen. tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "35歲以上且吸菸的女性不建議服用口服避孕藥，因為這會增加心血管疾病的風險。此外，女性在服用避孕藥前應先篩檢是否有高血壓，因為高血壓與避孕藥併用會增加中風風險。口服避孕藥不建議用於患有未控制高血壓、糖尿病，或多囊性卵巢症候群（PCOS）的女性；也不建議用於有心臟病史、中風史、血栓病史，或具有心臟病危險因子（高膽固醇、肥胖）的女性；亦不建議有先兆偏頭痛（migraine with aura）的女性服用。避孕藥中的荷爾蒙會增加血液凝固能力，因此也可能使女性容易發生深部靜脈栓塞（DVT）。因此，若患者體重過重、有深部靜脈栓塞病史，或有血栓疾病家族史，通常不建議服用，或需由醫師密切監測。雌激素劑量越高，凝血風險也越高。tcmtests.com，2020年7月"
    },
