      "exp_en": "A female patient younger than 30 will usually get an ultrasound (US) instead of a mammogram. US is better at evaluating the dense breast tissue of younger women. US also helps in distinguishing between fluid-filled cysts and solid masses. Fibrocystic breast disease occurs most often in women in their 20s to 50s. Fibrocystic breast disease rarely occurs in postmenopausal women unless they are on HRT (hormone replacement therapy). Fluctuating hormone levels during the menstrual cycle can cause lumpy breast tissue that feels tender, sore and swollen. The breast lumps fluctuate in size with the menstrual cycle, both breasts have similar changes with generalized breast tenderness, possible dark-brown and non-bloody nipple discharge that leaks with squeezing. Fibrocystic breasts do not increase the risk of breast cancer. Breast lumps and thickenings that do not change with the menstrual cycle, are new, or are a change in what is normal for the patient should be evaluated. Differential Diagnosis, Rhoads, 2015 page 20-24",
      "exp_hant": "年齡小於30歲的女性通常會安排超音波檢查而非乳房攝影，因為超音波較能評估年輕女性緻密的乳房組織，也有助於區分含液囊腫與實質性腫塊。纖維囊性乳房病最常見於20至50多歲的女性，在停經後女性中較少見，除非正在接受荷爾蒙補充療法（HRT）。月經週期中荷爾蒙濃度的波動，可導致乳房組織出現觸痛、痠痛與腫脹的腫塊感。此類乳房腫塊會隨月經週期而大小變化，雙側乳房通常有類似的變化並伴有普遍性乳房觸痛，擠壓時可能出現深褐色、非血性的乳頭分泌物。纖維囊性乳房並不會增加乳癌風險。若乳房腫塊或增厚不隨月經週期變化、屬新發現，或與患者原本正常的狀態不同，則應加以評估。《鑑別診斷》，Rhoads著，2015年，頁20-24"
