      ],
      "exp_en": "With an MI there can be the possibility of SOB, nausea, indigestion and vomiting. GERD patients can have the sensation of food stuck in the throat and a feeling of choking with a tight throat. The pain from GERD moves up toward the throat from the chest and typically does not radiate to the shoulder, neck, or arms like it can with an MI. Troponins and myoglobins are cardiac proteins. When the heart is damaged, both can be released into the blood and become markers for the presence of an MI. H-2 receptor blocker (Tagamet, Pepcid AC, Axid AR) are prescribed for GERD. MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION: A heart attack or myocardial infarction occurs when there is a blockage in the heart arteries. This reduces or stops heart blood flow which deprives the heart of oxygen resulting in heart attack pain. Symptoms include a tightness, a pressure, a squeezing sensation, stabbing pain, or dull pain that is usually located at the center of the chest. The chest pain can spread to shoulders, neck or the arms. There can be an irregular heart beat. The patient can have a cold sweat or clammy skin with dizziness and weakness. There can be SOB, nausea, indigestion and vomiting is possible. The symptoms are triggered with physical exertion or extreme stress. RISK FACTORS: The major risk factors include high blood pressure, high cholesterol, diabetes, and obesity. DIAGNOSIS: Diagnosis is done through medical history of signs and symptoms, blood tests (troponin, MB, serum myoglobin), coronary angiography (uses dye injected into arteries with special x-ray). IMMEDIATE TREATMENT: Call 911, give aspirin to prevent further blood clotting and nitroglycerin, if patient has it. Clot-busters (thrombolytic drugs) via IV are used to dissolve arterial blood clots. These work best if given within a couple of hours of the heart attack. LONG-TERM TREATMENT: ACE inhibitors to control blood pressure, anti-coagulatants to thin the blood, beta-blockers to treat arrhythmias and decrease the heart's workload, and statins for coronary blockages. GERD: Gastroesophageal reflux disease or chronic acid reflux occurs when the acid-containing contents of the stomach persistently leak back up into your esophagus. The main symptoms include persistent heartburn and acid regurgitation, and awakening with acid reflux during the night which disturbs sleep. Burning chest pain starts at the breastbone and can moves up toward the throat. Typically the pain does not radiate to shoulder, neck, or arms. There can be a bitter/acidic taste in back of the throat. Pain worsens lying down or bending over. GERD symptoms can appear after a spicy or a large meal. However, some patients can have GERD without heartburn. These patients experience chest pain, morning hoarseness, or difficulty swallowing. GERD patients have the sensation of food stuck in the throat, a feeling of choking with a tight throat. GERD can injure the lining of the throat, lungs and airways which can result in breathing difficulties and a persistent cough. GERD is usually but not always relieved by antacids. DIAGNOSIS: Diagnosis is through medical history. If diet and lifestyle changes or drug treatment do not alleviate GERD, then lab tests can be done such as an upper gastrointestinal GI endoscopy and biopsy, an upper GI series, an esophageal pH monitoring, and an esophageal manometry that tests the lower esophageal sphincter. TREATMENT: The most common GERD drugs include antacids to quickly neutralize stomach acids (Tums, Rolaids, Maalox), H-2 receptor blocker (Tagamet, Pepcid AC, Axid AR), and proton pump inhibitors (Prevacid, Prilosec, Nexium). Even experienced doctors cannot always tell the difference between a heart attack and GERD based only on a medical history and a physical exam. In these situations it is best to do an emergency referral. webmd.com; mayoclinic.com; nih.gov",
      "exp_hant": "心肌梗塞可能出現呼吸急促、噁心、消化不良與嘔吐。胃食道逆流患者則可能感覺食物卡在喉嚨，並有喉嚨緊縮、哽塞的感覺。胃食道逆流的疼痛會從胸部向上延伸至喉嚨，通常不會像心肌梗塞那樣放射至肩膀、頸部或手臂。肌鈣蛋白（troponin）與肌紅蛋白（myoglobin）都是心臟蛋白質，當心臟受損時，兩者皆可能釋放至血液中，成為心肌梗塞存在的指標。H-2受體阻斷劑（Tagamet、Pepcid AC、Axid AR）是用於治療胃食道逆流的藥物。心肌梗塞：心臟病發作（心肌梗塞）發生於心臟動脈阻塞時，導致心臟血流減少或中斷，使心臟缺氧而產生心臟病發作的疼痛。症狀包括胸部正中央出現緊繃感、壓迫感、擠壓感、刺痛或悶痛。胸痛可能擴散至肩膀、頸部或手臂，也可能出現心律不整。患者可能出現冷汗或皮膚濕黏，並伴隨頭暈與虛弱。也可能出現呼吸急促、噁心、消化不良，甚至嘔吐。這些症狀常在體力消耗或極度壓力下被誘發。危險因子：主要危險因子包括高血壓、高膽固醇、糖尿病與肥胖。診斷：診斷依據病史中的徵象與症狀、血液檢查（肌鈣蛋白、CK-MB、血清肌紅蛋白），以及冠狀動脈血管攝影（將顯影劑注入動脈後以特殊X光攝影）。緊急處置：撥打911，給予阿斯匹靈以防止血栓進一步形成，若患者備有硝化甘油則予以使用。可透過靜脈注射血栓溶解劑（溶栓藥物）來溶解動脈血栓，若在心臟病發作後數小時內給藥效果最佳。長期治療：使用ACE抑制劑控制血壓、抗凝血劑稀釋血液、乙型阻斷劑治療心律不整並減輕心臟負荷，以及使用他汀類藥物治療冠狀動脈阻塞。胃食道逆流：胃食道逆流疾病，或稱慢性胃酸逆流，是指含酸的胃內容物持續逆流至食道所引起。主要症狀包括持續性的火燒心與胃酸逆流，並可能於夜間因胃酸逆流而驚醒，干擾睡眠。灼熱的胸痛始於胸骨處，並可能向上延伸至喉嚨，通常不會放射至肩膀、頸部或手臂。喉嚨後方可能出現苦澀或酸味感，平躺或彎腰時疼痛會加劇。胃食道逆流的症狀可能在食用辛辣食物或大餐後出現。然而，部分患者可能沒有火燒心症狀，而是出現胸痛、晨間聲音沙啞或吞嚥困難。胃食道逆流患者會感覺食物卡在喉嚨，並有喉嚨緊縮、哽塞的感覺。胃食道逆流可能損傷喉嚨、肺部與呼吸道的黏膜，導致呼吸困難與持續性咳嗽。胃食道逆流通常（但非絕對）可藉由制酸劑緩解。診斷：診斷依據病史。若飲食與生活型態調整或藥物治療無法緩解胃食道逆流，可進行上消化道內視鏡檢查與切片、上消化道攝影系列、食道酸鹼度監測，以及測試下食道括約肌的食道測壓檢查等實驗室檢測。治療：常見的胃食道逆流藥物包括可快速中和胃酸的制酸劑（Tums、Rolaids、Maalox）、H-2受體阻斷劑（Tagamet、Pepcid AC、Axid AR），以及質子幫浦抑制劑（Prevacid、Prilosec、Nexium）。即使經驗豐富的醫師，也未必能單憑病史與理學檢查就分辨心臟病發作與胃食道逆流。在這種情況下，最好進行緊急轉診。webmd.com；mayoclinic.com；nih.gov"
    },
    {
      "number": 787,
      "question_en": "A 55 year-old female presents to you with knee/joint pain one the left side that is dull and characterized by morning stiffness, pain during weight-bearing activities, and mild joint space narrowing on X-ray and a negative Lachman test. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位55歲女性因左側膝關節疼痛前來就診，疼痛性質為鈍痛，伴有晨僵、負重活動時疼痛，X光顯示輕度關節間隙變窄，Lachman測試為陰性。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Septic arthritis",
          "hant": "化膿性關節炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Early Rheumatoid Arthritis",
          "hant": "早期類風濕性關節炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "ACL tear",
          "hant": "前十字韌帶撕裂",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Uncomplicated osteoarthritis",
          "hant": "單純性骨關節炎",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The patient’s symptoms—dull knee pain, morning stiffness, and pain during weight-bearing activities—along with X-ray findings of mild joint space narrowing and no evidence of severe deformity, infection, or ligament instability, are classic for uncomplicated osteoarthritis. OA is a degenerative joint disease common in middle-aged and older adults, particularly women, and is characterized by cartilage breakdown and mild bone changes. The absence of systemic symptoms, severe structural damage, or instability supports a straightforward, uncomplicated presentation of OA. Why Rheumatoid Arthritis is Incorrect: RA is a systemic autoimmune inflammatory condition that typically presents with symmetrical joint involvement, prolonged morning stiffness (&gt;30–60 minutes), and systemic symptoms like fatigue or fever. RA often affects smaller joints (e.g., hands, wrists) before larger ones like the knee and is associated with positive inflammatory markers (e.g., elevated ESR/CRP) and specific X-ray findings (e.g., erosions, periarticular osteopenia). The patient’s isolated knee pain, mild X-ray changes, and lack of systemic or inflammatory signs make RA unlikely. Why Septic Arthritsi is Incorrect: Septic arthritis is an infectious condition causing acute, severe joint pain, swelling, warmth, and restricted movement, often with systemic symptoms like fever or chills. It typically involves a single joint but is associated with significant inflammation and requires urgent intervention (e.g., joint aspiration). The patient’s chronic, dull pain, mild X-ray findings, and absence of infection signs (e.g., no warmth, fever, or severe swelling) rule out septic arthritis. Why Anterior Cruciate Ligament (ACL) Tear is Incorrect: An ACL tear typically presents with acute knee pain, swelling, and instability (e.g., a sensation of the knee “giving way”), often following trauma or injury. The Lachman test, which assesses ACL integrity, would likely be positive in an ACL tear, showing excessive anterior tibial translation with a soft or absent endpoint. The patient’s symptoms are chronic, weight-bearing-related, and lack instability or trauma history, and the X-ray findings of joint space narrowing suggest a degenerative process (OA) rather than a ligamentous injury. Dutton's Orthopaedic Examination, Evaluation and Intervention, 3rd Edition, 2012, pages 854-855",
      "exp_hant": "患者的症狀——膝部鈍痛、晨僵、負重活動時疼痛——加上X光顯示輕度關節間隙變窄，且無明顯變形、感染或韌帶不穩定的證據，屬於典型的單純性骨關節炎表現。骨關節炎是一種常見於中老年人（尤其是女性）的退化性關節疾病，特徵為軟骨破壞與輕微骨質變化。由於缺乏全身性症狀、嚴重結構性損傷或不穩定現象，支持此為單純、無併發症的骨關節炎表現。為何不是類風濕性關節炎：類風濕性關節炎是一種全身性自體免疫發炎性疾病，通常表現為對稱性關節受侵犯、晨僵時間延長（超過30至60分鐘），並伴有疲勞或發燒等全身性症狀。類風濕性關節炎常先侵犯手部、腕部等小關節，之後才波及膝關節等大關節，並常伴有發炎指標升高（如ESR/CRP升高）以及特定的X光表現（如骨侵蝕、關節周圍骨質疏鬆）。此患者僅有單側膝痛、X光變化輕微，且無全身性或發炎徵象，因此類風濕性關節炎的可能性較低。為何不是化膿性關節炎：化膿性關節炎是一種感染性疾病，會造成急性且劇烈的關節疼痛、腫脹、發熱與活動受限，通常伴有發燒或發冷等全身性症狀。此病通常侵犯單一關節，但伴隨明顯發炎反應，需緊急處置（如關節抽吸）。此患者為慢性鈍痛、X光變化輕微，且無感染徵象（如無發熱、發燒或嚴重腫脹），可排除化膿性關節炎。為何不是前十字韌帶（ACL）撕裂：前十字韌帶撕裂通常表現為急性膝痛、腫脹與不穩定感（如膝關節「軟腳」的感覺），常於外傷或受傷後發生。用於評估前十字韌帶完整性的Lachman測試，在前十字韌帶撕裂時通常會呈陽性，顯示脛骨前移過度且終末點鬆軟或消失。此患者的症狀為慢性、與負重相關，且無不穩定感或外傷病史，加上X光顯示關節間隙變窄，提示為退化性病程（骨關節炎），而非韌帶損傷。《Dutton骨科檢查、評估與介入》，第3版，2012年，頁854-855"
    },
