      "exp_en": "An x-ray of the affected joints can show a loss of joint cartilage, a narrowing of the joint space, and bone spur formation. Observing the location, duration, and character of the joint pain and joint appearance (heberden and bouchard nodes) can assist in making the diagnosis. Other tests can be performed to exclude other diseases. For example, arthrocentesis fluid analysis can be ordered to exclude gout or an infection. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 294",
      "exp_hant": "受影響關節的X光可顯示關節軟骨流失、關節間隙變窄，以及骨刺形成。觀察關節疼痛的部位、持續時間與性質，以及關節外觀（如希伯登氏結節與布夏氏結節），有助於做出診斷。也可安排其他檢查以排除其他疾病，例如可透過關節穿刺液分析來排除痛風或感染。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁294"
