        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Bronchiectasis arises when there is a dilation and destruction of the bronchi (the two primary divisions of the trachea that go into the right and the left lung) caused by a chronic infection and inflammation arising, most commonly, from cystic fibrosis (an inherited disease of the secretory glands), immune system defects, and infections. The main symptoms are: chronic cough that produces copious-thick-tenacious-purulent mucus. SOB and wheezing are also common. There can also be bleeding from the lungs (hemoptysis). There can also be halitosis (bad breath) and abnormal breath sounds such as lung crackles, wheezing, and rhonchi (coarse rattling breathing sounds like snoring). Bronchiectasis can look like chronic bronchitis. The difference is that bronchiectasis produces large amounts of purulent (contains pus) every day with a CT scan showing bronchial varicosities (vein swellings). The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 439",
      "exp_hant": "支氣管擴張症是指支氣管（氣管分出通往左右兩肺的兩條主要分支）因慢性感染與發炎而發生擴張與破壞，最常見的病因包括囊腫性纖維化（一種分泌腺遺傳性疾病）、免疫系統缺陷與感染。主要症狀為：慢性咳嗽並產生大量濃稠、黏膩、化膿性的痰液。呼吸急促與喘鳴也很常見，也可能出現肺部出血（咳血）。此外還可能有口臭，以及異常呼吸音，如肺部囉音、喘鳴音與類似鼾聲的粗糙囉音（rhonchi）。支氣管擴張症可能與慢性支氣管炎相似，差別在於支氣管擴張症每天會產生大量化膿性（含膿）痰液，且電腦斷層掃描會顯示支氣管靜脈曲張樣擴張。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁439"
