    {
      "number": 795,
      "question_en": "A 72 year-old male complains of worsening constipation. From having one BM daily he now has a BM every three days only with laxative use. There is no blood in the stool even though he strains. He has poor appetite and has lost 30 pounds during the past few months. He has low energy. He denies fever, night sweats, dysuria, leg pain or edema. PHYSICAL EXAM: BP 110/75 mm Hg; Heart rate is 100 bpm and regular; respiratory rate 18 breaths/min; temperature 97.6 F. Abdomen is soft with liver span of 12 cm; liver edge is palpable 3 finger breaths below Right Costal Margin; there is fullness in the lower left quadrant and non-tender; external hemorrhoids at 8 o'clock; stool is brown and guaiac-positive; prostate gland not palpable due to presence of mass. Based on the preceding history and limited physical examination prior to lab tests what is the most likely disease state?",
      "question_hant": "一位72歲男性主訴便秘逐漸惡化。原本每日排便一次，現在需使用瀉藥才能三天排便一次。雖然用力排便，但糞便中並無血液。他食慾不振，過去幾個月體重減輕30磅，並感到活力低下。他否認發燒、夜間盜汗、排尿困難、腿痛或水腫。理學檢查：血壓110/75 mmHg；心跳每分鐘100下，節律規則；呼吸速率每分鐘18次；體溫97.6°F。腹部柔軟，肝臟長度12公分，肝緣於右肋緣下方三指幅可觸及；左下腹有飽脹感但無壓痛；肛門8點鐘方向有外痔；糞便呈棕色且癒創木脂試驗（guaiac）陽性；因有腫塊存在，攝護腺無法觸診。根據上述病史與實驗室檢查前的有限理學檢查結果，最可能的疾病狀態為何？",
