      "exp_hant": "指向大腸癌的線索包括：排便習慣改變、體重減輕、可觸及腫塊、糞便癒創木脂試驗陽性，仍需進一步檢查確認。並非憂鬱症或甲狀腺功能低下，因為這兩者不會出現直腸腫塊，也不會有糞便潛血陽性的表現。攝護腺癌的診斷則不包含糞便潛血陽性此項表現。《搭配Bate氏理學檢查指南之病例研究》，第9版，頁54、55、121"
    },
    {
      "number": 796,
      "question_en": "A 70 year-old male retired patient presents with \"just not feeling right\" for the past three days. Last week he had lunch with his daughter who had an upper respiratory tract infection. He developed a cold and was treated with Mucinex DM which helped. Since last week he has had increased fatigue with difficulty accomplishing his usual morning routine of taking a short walk. Yesterday, he forgot a scheduled lunch with his daughter and also forgot to take his medications. He denies any changes in vision and hearing. He denies headaches and muscle pain. He denies fever. He denies chest pain, cough, or palpitations but does report shortness of breath. He denies chills and fever. His appetite, bowel habits, and urination are normal. He drinks 4-6 ounces of wine per day and does not smoke. He has a history of hypertension and osteoarthritis, both controlled with medication. Respiratory exam shows no fremitus; mild dullness to percussion in right lower lobe; basilar crackles and expiratory wheezes in right lung; respiratory rate of 30; heart rate of 100. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位70歲退休男性主訴過去三天「就是覺得不對勁」。上週他曾與罹患上呼吸道感染的女兒共進午餐，之後他也感冒了，使用Mucinex DM治療後有改善。自上週起，他感到疲勞加重，難以完成平常早晨散步的例行活動。昨天他忘記了與女兒約好的午餐，也忘記服藥。他否認視力與聽力有任何改變，否認頭痛與肌肉痠痛，否認發燒。他否認胸痛、咳嗽或心悸，但主訴有呼吸急促。他否認畏寒與發燒。食慾、排便習慣與排尿皆正常。他每天飲用4至6盎司的葡萄酒，不吸菸。他有高血壓與骨關節炎病史，兩者皆以藥物控制良好。呼吸系統檢查顯示：無觸覺震顫；右下肺葉輕度叩診濁音；右肺底部有囉音與呼氣性喘鳴；呼吸速率每分鐘30次；心跳每分鐘100下。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "influenza",
          "hant": "流行性感冒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "pneumonia",
          "hant": "肺炎",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Acute bronchitis",
          "hant": "急性支氣管炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "COPD",
          "hant": "慢性阻塞性肺病",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The most likely diagnosis is pneumonia. Many older patients do not realize having pneumonia. Pneumonia, however, can be life threatening if not treated immediately. Confirming the diagnosis of pneumonia in older adults is usually done with a chest x-ray. The patient has the classic presentation of pneumonia for an older adult. There is no rapid onset, no chills, no fever, no pleuritic chest pain, or productive cough of lobar pneumonia often found in younger adults. The older adult, instead, may report a slow onset, poor appetite, weakness, fatigue. The physical exam in older patients with pneumonia shows tachypnea (abnormally rapid breathing) and tachycardia (increased heart rate). A respiratory rate of above 28 is often the earliest clue in older patients with pneumonia. Fever and chills is often absent in a large number of patients. Because of this presentation, it can be difficult to differentiate pneumonia in older adults from bronchitis. Acute bronchitis, however, has chest congestion, coughing with expectoration, shortness of breath, wheezing, body aches, chills and low fever. In all of the different age groups, influenza is an acute manifestation with sudden symptoms of fever, headache, fatigue, dry cough, dysphagia, nasal congestion, and body aches. Acute bronchitis and influenza would be excluded via diagnostic testing. About 80% of older adults with pneumonia have one or more concomitant illnesses such as COPD, diabetes, or cardiovascular disease. COPD (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease) and pneumonia often occur together because those with COPD are more likely to contract bacterial pneumonia, the most common type. COPD is a chronic lung condition with chronic cough, wheezing, shortness of breath and excess mucus, often with a history of cigarette smoking. When symptoms and signs of COPD fail to respond to treatment or there are symptoms of pneumonia, the patient needs to be immediately diagnosed and treated for pneumonia. Tactile fremitus is a vibration that can be felt with the palm when the patient says \"blue moon\" or \"99\". Increased fremitus is a sign of consolidation. Decreased fremitus is a sign of pleural effusion (excess fluids in pleural cavity) or pneumothorax. When there is pleural effusion such as with pneumonia, percussion of the lungs will give a dull sound. Basal crackles are crackles that originate in or near the base of the lung and are caused by the \"popping open\" of small airways and alveoli which have been collapsed by fluid. Crackles can be heard in patients who have pneumonia, acute bronchitis, bronchiectasis, or pulmonary edema secondary to congestive heart failure. A wheeze is a high-pitched, continuous whistling sound during breathing which occurs most of the time during exhalation can also occur during inhalation. Wheezing usually is a sign of narrowing airways. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 341-344",
      "exp_hant": "最可能的診斷為肺炎。許多老年患者本身並未察覺自己罹患肺炎，然而若未及時治療，肺炎可能危及生命。老年人肺炎的診斷通常透過胸部X光確診。此患者呈現老年人肺炎的典型表現：沒有快速發病、沒有畏寒、沒有發燒，也沒有年輕人大葉性肺炎常見的肋膜性胸痛或有痰咳嗽。相反地，老年患者常表現為緩慢發病、食慾不振、虛弱與疲勞。老年肺炎患者的理學檢查會顯示呼吸過速（呼吸異常加快）與心搏過速（心跳加快）。呼吸速率超過每分鐘28次，通常是老年肺炎患者最早出現的線索。許多患者常沒有發燒與畏寒的表現。由於這種表現方式，老年人的肺炎有時難以與支氣管炎區分。然而急性支氣管炎的表現則是胸悶、有痰咳嗽、呼吸急促、喘鳴、全身痠痛、畏寒與輕度發燒。在各年齡層中，流行性感冒都是急性發作，症狀包括突發性發燒、頭痛、疲勞、乾咳、吞嚥困難、鼻塞與全身痠痛。急性支氣管炎與流行性感冒可透過診斷檢測加以排除。約有80%的老年肺炎患者合併有一種以上的其他疾病，如慢性阻塞性肺病、糖尿病或心血管疾病。慢性阻塞性肺病（COPD）與肺炎常同時發生，因為COPD患者更容易罹患最常見的細菌性肺炎。COPD是一種慢性肺部疾病，表現為慢性咳嗽、喘鳴、呼吸急促與痰液過多，患者通常有吸菸史。當COPD的症狀與徵象對治療沒有反應，或出現肺炎症狀時，應立即對患者進行肺炎的診斷與治療。觸覺震顫是指患者說出「blue moon」或「99」時，用手掌可感覺到的震動。震顫增強是肺實變的徵象；震顫減弱則是肋膜積液（肋膜腔內體液過多）或氣胸的徵象。當出現如肺炎般的肋膜積液時，肺部叩診會呈濁音。肺底部囉音是指起源於肺底部或其附近的囉音，是因體液使小氣道與肺泡塌陷後又「彈開」所產生。肺炎、急性支氣管炎、支氣管擴張症，或繼發於鬱血性心臟衰竭的肺水腫患者，都可能聽到囉音。喘鳴是一種呼吸時出現的高音調、連續性哨音，多發生於呼氣時，但也可能發生於吸氣時，通常是氣道狹窄的徵象。《家庭護理師臨床病例研究》，Leslie Neal-Boylan著，2011年，頁341-344"
    },
    {
      "number": 797,
      "question_en": "A 33 year-old male patient has the chief complaint of facial pain for the previous five days. He reports a headache and tooth pain that worsen when bending down. He confirms having had a cold two weeks ago with rhinorrhea with clear drainage, mild sore throat, ear pressure, and a mild headache. After one week the symptoms cleared and felt healthy. Then some of the symptoms returned about five days later with facial pain, headache in the morning, tooth pain, and blood streaked nasal discharge. He has a history of seasonal allergic rhinitis. The HEENT exam shows clear sclera, clear and intact tympanic membranes, tenderness of the sinuses, erythmatous and swollen nares without discharge, cobblestoning in the throat but without erythema. He is taking Advil which has provided no relief. What is the most likely diagnosis for the facial pain?",
      "question_hant": "一位33歲男性主訴過去五天出現臉部疼痛。他表示有頭痛與牙痛，彎腰時症狀會加劇。他確認兩週前曾感冒，出現清澈鼻涕的流鼻水、輕微喉嚨痛、耳部壓迫感與輕微頭痛。一週後症狀消退並感覺恢復健康。約五天後部分症狀復發，出現臉部疼痛、晨間頭痛、牙痛，以及帶血絲的鼻分泌物。他有季節性過敏性鼻炎病史。頭頸五官（HEENT）檢查顯示：鞏膜清澈、鼓膜清晰完整、鼻竇有壓痛、鼻孔紅腫但無分泌物、咽喉有卵石樣外觀但無紅腫。他正服用Advil但未見改善。造成臉部疼痛最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "upper respiratory tract infection",
          "hant": "上呼吸道感染",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Allergic rhinitis",
          "hant": "過敏性鼻炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "acute sinus infection",
          "hant": "急性鼻竇感染",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "vasomotor rhinitis",
          "hant": "血管舒縮性鼻炎",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The diagnosis of acute sinus infection is supported by symptoms and the course of the disease. The symptoms that point to the sinus infection are headache, sinus pain and pressure, and dental pain. The typical course for an acute sinus infection includes starting with a cold or upper respiratory tract infection (URI) followed by improvement and the patient feeling better. Then the symptoms return and include worsening sinus pressure and pain. A sinus infection needs time to develop after the initial URI. No lab tests are required at this time. However, repeated sinus infections can be evaluated with a CT scan of the sinuses. The patient may also have allergic rhinitis which is characterized by itchy eyes, scratchy throat, clear drainage, boggy mucosa, and cobblestoning in the throat. Cobblestoning describes an irritated throat with visible bumps and lumps at the back. The patient's allergies are superseded by the acute sinus infection symptoms. Vasomotor rhinitis is an inflammation of the inner nose that is not caused by an allergy. Vasomotor rhinitis involves symptoms including chronic sneezing or having a congested, drippy nose without an identified allergic reaction. Other common terms are nonallergic rhinitis and perennial rhinitis. Clinical Case Studies for the Family Nurse Practitioner, Leslie Neal-Boylan, 2011, page 259-261",
      "exp_hant": "急性鼻竇感染的診斷可由症狀與病程加以支持。指向鼻竇感染的症狀包括頭痛、鼻竇疼痛與壓迫感，以及牙痛。急性鼻竇感染的典型病程是先出現感冒或上呼吸道感染，隨後症狀改善、患者感覺好轉，接著症狀復發，出現加劇的鼻竇壓迫感與疼痛。鼻竇感染通常需要在初次上呼吸道感染後經過一段時間才會發展出來，此時無需進行實驗室檢查；但若鼻竇感染反覆發生，可透過鼻竇電腦斷層掃描評估。此患者也可能同時患有過敏性鼻炎，其特徵為眼睛搔癢、喉嚨刺癢、清澈鼻涕、黏膜浮腫，以及咽喉卵石樣外觀。「卵石樣」是指咽喉受刺激後，後壁可見明顯凸起與腫塊的外觀。此患者的過敏症狀已被急性鼻竇感染的症狀所掩蓋。血管舒縮性鼻炎則是一種非過敏引起的鼻腔內部發炎，其症狀包括慢性打噴嚏，或有鼻塞、流鼻水但找不到明確過敏原因。其他常見名稱包括非過敏性鼻炎與常年性鼻炎。《家庭護理師臨床病例研究》，Leslie Neal-Boylan著，2011年，頁259-261"
    },
    {
      "number": 798,
      "question_en": "Mildred is 97 years old. She walks to the grocery store every day. She got a flu shot in October because there were predictions of a bad flu year. At Christmas she got the flu anyway. She felt miserable with chills, fever, muscle aches and pains. On the third day, she developed a productive cough and shortness of breath. She coughed up rust colored, purulent sputum. Her grandson took her to the doctor the next day. She is feeling worse, with inspiratory chest pain, and more shortness of breath and has mild confusion. Her temperature is 101 degree F. The doctor hears rales and decreased breath sounds in the lower left lung. Blood count shows a WBC count of 14,500 with 65% mature neutrophils and 10% bands. An x-ray shows consolidation of her left lower lobe with fluid in the pleura. A gram stain of her sputum shows a large number of gram positive diplococci. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "米爾德雷德（Mildred）今年97歲，每天都會走路去雜貨店。由於預測今年流感疫情嚴重，她在十月時接種了流感疫苗。然而聖誕節時她還是感染了流感，出現畏寒、發燒、肌肉痠痛等不適症狀。第三天，她開始出現有痰咳嗽與呼吸急促，咳出鐵鏽色的化膿性痰液。她的孫子隔天帶她去看醫生。此時她的情況更加惡化，出現吸氣時胸痛、呼吸更為急促，並有輕度意識混亂。她的體溫為101°F。醫師在其左下肺聽到囉音，並發現呼吸音減弱。血球計數顯示白血球數為14,500，其中成熟嗜中性球佔65%，桿狀核嗜中性球佔10%。X光顯示左下肺葉實變，並有肋膜積液。痰液的革蘭氏染色顯示大量革蘭氏陽性雙球菌。最可能的診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Acute uremia",
          "hant": "急性尿毒症",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Acute Viral pneumonia",
          "hant": "急性病毒性肺炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Acute bronchitis",
          "hant": "急性支氣管炎",
          "correct": false
