        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Acute pneumococcal pneumonia",
          "hant": "急性肺炎鏈球菌性肺炎",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Pneumococcal pneumonia is a bacterial infection caused by the bacteria streptococcus pneumoniae. This bacteria can enter the bloodstream (bacteremia), invade the tissues and fluids (brain and spinal cord) and causes meningitis. Symptoms when limited to the lungs include fever, chills, sweat, body aches, headache, malaise, cough, SOB, and blood in the sputum. A bacterial infection tends to be unilateral involving one lung while a viral lung infection tends to be bilateral, involving both lungs. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 117, 708",
      "exp_hant": "肺炎鏈球菌性肺炎是由肺炎鏈球菌（streptococcus pneumoniae）所引起的細菌感染。此細菌可進入血流（菌血症），侵犯組織與體液（腦部與脊髓），導致腦膜炎。若感染僅侷限於肺部，症狀包括發燒、畏寒、盜汗、全身痠痛、頭痛、倦怠、咳嗽、呼吸急促，以及痰中帶血。細菌性感染通常為單側、僅侵犯一側肺部，而病毒性肺部感染則多為雙側，侵犯兩側肺部。《生物醫學：針灸與東方醫學從業者教科書》，Robinson著，2007年，頁117、708"
    },
    {
      "number": 799,
      "question_en": "A 67 year-old female has had an Ischemic Stroke. What are her symptoms?",
      "question_hant": "一位67歲女性發生缺血性中風，其症狀為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "hemiparesis, nystagmus, intention tremor, ataxia, visual impairment, incontinence",
          "hant": "半身輕癱、眼球震顫、意向性震顫、共濟失調、視力障礙、失禁",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "unconsciousness, clenched jaws and fingers, increased salivation, increased bronchial secretion, apnea",
          "hant": "意識喪失、下顎與手指緊握、唾液分泌增加、支氣管分泌物增加、呼吸暫停",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "fainting, confusion, dizziness, severe epistaxis, cold-pale skin, rapid heartbeat, dizziness",
          "hant": "昏厥、意識混亂、頭暈、嚴重鼻出血、皮膚冰冷蒼白、心跳加快、頭暈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "contralateral sensory loss and disturbance, contralateral paralysis and weakness, aphasia, hemianopia",
          "hant": "對側感覺喪失與感覺障礙、對側癱瘓與無力、失語症、偏盲",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Ischemic strokes involve a constriction of blood supply to the brain, causing an interruption in the oxygenation of brain cells. An ischemic stroke occurs when an artery that supplies blood to the brain becomes blocked by a blood clot. A clot can originate in the brain or it can travel from another area such as the heart. Blood clots can be formed by atherosclerosis caused by high cholesterol, obesity, or a poor diet. The fatty deposits from atherosclerosis can cause two types of obstructions: 1) in cerebral thrombosis the thrombus (blood clot) develops at the clogged part of the blood vessel. 2) in cerebral embolism the thrombus forms at another location in the circulatory system (ie heart, etc). 85% of strokes are ischemic strokes. Symptoms can include sudden numbness or weakness of the face/arm/leg (especially involving one side of the body), sudden confusion, trouble talking (aphasia) or understanding vision loss (hemiopia), difficulty walking, loss of balance. Ischemic strokes are emergency situations and require calling 911 and hospitalization. A Transient Ischemic Attack refers to neurological deficits caused by cerebral ischemia that resolves within 24 hours. A TIA has the same causative origin (atherosclerotic arterial plaque build up) as that of an ischemic stroke. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 1792",
      "exp_hant": "缺血性中風是指腦部血流供應受限，導致腦細胞供氧中斷。當供應腦部血液的動脈被血栓阻塞時，即發生缺血性中風。血栓可能形成於腦部，也可能由其他部位（如心臟）隨血流移動而來。動脈粥狀硬化（因高膽固醇、肥胖或不良飲食所致）所形成的脂肪沉積，可造成兩種阻塞：1）腦血栓形成，即血栓在血管阻塞處直接形成；2）腦栓塞，即血栓形成於循環系統中的其他部位（如心臟等），再隨血流移動至腦部造成阻塞。約85%的中風屬於缺血性中風。症狀包括：臉部/手臂/腿部（尤其是身體單側）突然出現麻木或無力、突然意識混亂、說話困難（失語症）或理解困難、視力喪失（偏盲）、行走困難、失去平衡感。缺血性中風屬於緊急狀況，需撥打911並住院治療。短暫性腦缺血發作（TIA）是指因腦部缺血所引起、於24小時內恢復的神經功能缺損。TIA與缺血性中風有相同的致病原因（動脈粥狀硬化斑塊堆積）。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁1792"
    },
    {
      "number": 800,
      "question_en": "A 67 year-old male has Pneumonia. How is the diagnosis confirmed?",
      "question_hant": "一位67歲男性罹患肺炎，其診斷如何確診？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "chest MRI",
          "hant": "胸部核磁共振",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "pulmonary function tests",
          "hant": "肺功能檢查",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "chest ultra-sound",
          "hant": "胸部超音波",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "chest x-ray",
          "hant": "胸部X光",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A diagnosis of pneumonia can be overlooked as the symptoms resemble the flu (fever, shaking chills, etc). The physical exam will show crackling-bubbling sounds in the chest during the inhalation. Lung ausculation will produce dull sounds. These signs usually point to pneumonia. The suspected diagnosis of pneumonia is confirmed with a chest x-ray which will show various degrees of pulmonary infiltrate (a substance denser than air such as pus, blood, or protein, which lingers within the lungs and is associated with pneumonia and tuberculosis). There will be pulmonary infiltrate whether the pneumonia is bacterial, viral, or fungal in origin. But a chest x-ray will not differentiate the type of pneumonia. For that, blood and sputum tests give a better picture of the pneumonia type. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 427",
      "exp_hant": "肺炎的診斷有時容易被忽略，因為其症狀（發燒、寒顫等）與流感相似。理學檢查會發現吸氣時胸部有爆裂音／泡沫聲，肺部聽診則會出現濁音，這些徵象通常指向肺炎。疑似肺炎的診斷可透過胸部X光確診，X光會顯示不同程度的肺部浸潤（一種比空氣密度更高的物質，如膿、血或蛋白質，滯留於肺部，與肺炎及肺結核相關）。無論肺炎是細菌、病毒或黴菌所引起，都會出現肺部浸潤，但胸部X光無法區分肺炎的類型；若要判斷肺炎類型，血液與痰液檢查可提供更明確的資訊。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁427"
    },
    {
      "number": 801,
      "question_en": "A 59 year-old male has Diabetic Nephropathy. Symptoms consist of edema and",
      "question_hant": "一位59歲男性罹患糖尿病腎病變，其症狀除水腫外，還包含：",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "hypertension",
          "hant": "高血壓",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "normal blood pressure",
          "hant": "血壓正常",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "variable blood pressure",
          "hant": "血壓不穩定",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "hypotension",
          "hant": "低血壓",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Diabetic nephropathy or diabetic kidney disease (DKD) is a progressive kidney disease caused by angiopathy (disease of the blood vessels) in the kidney glomeruli (a cluster of capillaries around the end of a kidney tubule, where waste products are filtered from the blood). Diabetic nephropathy is caused by chronic diabetes mellitus. Diabetic nephropathy is often an indication for dialysis. In the early stages, diabetic nephropathy has no symptoms which only develop later as the disease worsens. These symptoms include: edema around the eyes, the legs, or overall. Excessive frothing of the urine which is caused by excess protein in the urine (proteinuria). Hypertension is very prevalent in patients with diabetic nephropathy. Other symptoms can include weight gain, poor appetite, fatigue, malaise, and headaches. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2007",
      "exp_hant": "糖尿病腎病變（或稱糖尿病腎臟病，DKD）是一種漸進性腎臟疾病，起因於腎小球（腎小管末端周圍的微血管叢，負責從血液中過濾廢物）發生血管病變。糖尿病腎病變是慢性糖尿病所引起，也是常見需要透析的病因之一。在早期階段，糖尿病腎病變通常沒有症狀，隨著病情惡化才會逐漸出現症狀，包括：眼周、雙腿或全身水腫；因尿蛋白過多（蛋白尿）而導致尿液產生過多泡沫。高血壓在糖尿病腎病變患者中相當常見。其他症狀還可能包括體重增加、食慾不振、疲勞、倦怠與頭痛。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁2007"
    },
