      "exp_en": "Human papilloma virus (HPV) is an infection transmitted between individuals through skin-to-skin contact. Generally, an HPV infection causes warts. Depending on the type of HPV (there are more than 100 different types of viruses) will determine where the warts appear (feet, hands, face, genitals). About 90% of infections resolve on their own without manifesting any sign-symptoms. Infected individuals may, without knowing it, pass HPV to sexual partners. For about 10% of patients the virus remains and can cause symptoms. These symptoms include genital warts and throat warts (through oral sex). Only certain types of HPV infections can lead to cervical cancer. Some HPV infections just cause warts and do not progress to cancer. HPV is almost always the cause of cervical cancer. HPV caused cancers are usually not detected until they are at a later stage. To prevent HPV the use of condoms is recommended as well as limiting sexual partners. tcmtests.com, April 2020",
      "exp_hant": "人類乳突病毒（HPV）是一種透過皮膚接觸在人與人之間傳播的感染。HPV感染通常會引起疣。疣出現的部位（腳、手、臉、生殖器）視HPV的類型而定（HPV共有超過100種不同型別）。約90%的感染會自行痊癒，不會出現任何徵象或症狀。感染者可能在不知情的狀況下將HPV傳染給性伴侶。約10%的患者體內病毒持續存在並可能引發症狀，包括生殖器疣與（透過口交傳播的）喉部疣。只有某些型別的HPV感染會導致子宮頸癌，部分HPV感染僅引起疣而不會發展為癌症。子宮頸癌幾乎都是由HPV所引起。由HPV所導致的癌症通常要到較晚期才會被發現。為預防HPV感染，建議使用保險套並減少性伴侶數量。tcmtests.com，2020年4月"
