      "exp_en": "In atherosclerosis, hardening of the arteries, plaque builds on arterial walls. Cholesterol, fatty substances, cellular waste by-products, calcium and fibrin (blood clotting chemical) make up plaque. The danger of atherosclerosis is that the plaque can block arterial blood flow to the body (heart, legs, brain, kidneys) which can result in coronary heart disease (CHD), angina pectoris, peripheral artery disease (PAD) and chronic kidney diseases. When a part of the plaque breaks off or a thrombus (blood clot) forms the result can be a heart attack, stroke, or TIAs (transient ischemic attacks). The causative factors can include high cholesterol and triglycerides blood levels, hypertension, and cigarette smoking. Atherosclerosis is a slowly progressing disease that can start as early as childhood with the disease becoming dangerous in the 50s or 60s. The symptoms of moderate to severe atherosclerosis depend on which arteries are affected by the plaque build up. Xanthomas are yellow skin patches or nodules caused by fatty deposits. Atherosclerosis in the heart arteries can lead to angina or a heart attack. Atherosclerosis in brain arteries can lead to a stroke. Atherosclerosis in leg and arm arteries can lead to limb pain. Atherosclerosis in kidney arteries lead to hypertension or kidney failure. Atherosclerosis in genital arteries can lead to impotence in men or unpleasurable sex in women. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 623, 1301",
      "exp_hant": "動脈粥狀硬化（動脈硬化）是指斑塊堆積於動脈壁上。斑塊是由膽固醇、脂肪物質、細胞代謝廢物、鈣質與纖維蛋白（血液凝固化學物質）所組成。動脈粥狀硬化的危險之處在於斑塊可能阻塞流向全身（心臟、腿部、腦部、腎臟）的動脈血流，進而導致冠狀動脈心臟病（CHD）、心絞痛、周邊動脈疾病（PAD）與慢性腎臟疾病。當部分斑塊剝落或形成血栓時，可能導致心臟病發作、中風或短暫性腦缺血發作（TIA）。致病因子包括高膽固醇與高三酸甘油酯血症、高血壓與吸菸。動脈粥狀硬化是一種進展緩慢的疾病，最早可從兒童時期開始發展，並在50或60多歲時變得危險。中重度動脈粥狀硬化的症狀取決於受斑塊影響的動脈部位。黃色瘤是因脂肪沉積所造成的黃色皮膚斑塊或結節。心臟動脈的動脈粥狀硬化可導致心絞痛或心臟病發作；腦部動脈的動脈粥狀硬化可導致中風；四肢動脈的動脈粥狀硬化可導致肢體疼痛；腎臟動脈的動脈粥狀硬化可導致高血壓或腎衰竭；生殖器動脈的動脈粥狀硬化則可能導致男性陽痿或女性性交無法獲得愉悅感。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁623、1301"
