      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Salt is restricted because one of the complications is hypertension. Only if the preeclampsia is severe that hospitalization is required. Patients with eclampsia (possibility of seizures) are treated with hospitalization, BP meds, IV Mg sulfate, and usually rapid delivery. The Merck Manual, 18th Edition, page 2198",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。限制鹽分攝取是因為其併發症之一為高血壓。只有在子癲前症病情嚴重時才需要住院治療。子癲症患者（有抽搐風險）則需住院治療，包括使用降血壓藥物、靜脈注射硫酸鎂，並通常需要儘速分娩。《默克診療手冊》，第18版，頁2198"
