      "exp_en": "Roger has Hirschsprung's disease. This is a congenital (present at birth) disorder which affects the large intestine and causes problems with passing stool. Hirschsprung's disease is the result of missing nerve cells in the muscles of the large intestine. Roger is showing signs of an impending rupture of the colon. This is a serious condition and requires surgery to bypass part of the colon that has no nerve cells. Roger should immediately be referred to a hospital emergency department. Biomedicine: A Textbook for Practitioners of Acupuncture and Oriental Medicine, 2007, Robinson, page 369, 710",
