      "exp_en": "The red flag is posterior calf pain that is reliably triggered after walking a specific distance. Intermittent claudication is assumed present until proven otherwise. The examination for peripheral artery disease (PAD) starts by checking for weak pulses in the feet and legs by comparing right and left. Patients with PAD and no chest pain should have a timely consult with their PCP (primary care physician). If there are symptoms and signs of coronary and carotid insufficiency, chest pain and SOB then patient transport (911) to an ED (emergency department) is required.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 124-125",
      "exp_hant": "此案例的紅旗警訊為小腿後方疼痛，且穩定地於行走特定距離後誘發，應假定為間歇性跛行，直到排除為止。周邊動脈疾病（PAD）的檢查首先要比較雙腳雙腿的脈搏是否減弱。若PAD患者無胸痛，應及時轉診至基層照護醫師（PCP）；若出現冠狀動脈與頸動脈供血不足的症狀與徵象，如胸痛與呼吸急促，則需撥打911將患者送往急診室（ED）。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，頁124-125"
    },
    {
      "number": 820,
      "question_en": "A 37 year-old male steel worker had mild GRADE-1 neck pain with tingling in the right shoulder, arm, and hand from a work related event. The neck pain was better for the past several days before the appointment but still had numbness of the hand and arm which came and went. Sleeping on the stomach worsened the pain. He did not notice any weakness in the hand. Physical examination showed a slightly weaker grip strength in the right hand when compared to the left. Light pinprick to the right ulnar aspect showed decreased sensation when compared to the left. Biceps and triceps reflexes were normal. He had adequate movement and arm strength. Which action would you take?",
