      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is a child with sore throat, high fever (> 102 degrees F), inspiratory stridor, and drooling. Acute epiglottitis is assumed present until proven otherwise. In epiglottitis drooling, reluctance to talk or swallow food or fluids are common. There is often a history of upper respiratory infection preceding the epiglottitis. Acute epiglottitis occurs in children between the ages of 3 -7. A narrowing of the space between the epiglottitis and trachea causes the noise while breathing. Acute epiglottitis is a medical emergency and the patient should be driven by a family member to an ED. Calling 911 is required with the presence of air hunger and cyanosis.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 53-54",
      "exp_hant": "此案例的紅旗警訊為孩童喉嚨痛、高燒（超過102°F）、吸氣性喘鳴，以及流口水，應假定為急性會厭炎，直到排除為止。會厭炎常見流口水、不願說話或不願吞嚥食物或液體的表現，發病前常有上呼吸道感染病史。急性會厭炎好發於3至7歲的孩童。會厭與氣管之間的空間變窄，是呼吸時發出聲音的原因。急性會厭炎屬於醫療緊急狀況，應由家人開車將患者送往急診室；若出現空氣飢渴感與發紺，則需撥打911。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，頁53-54"
    },
    {
      "number": 828,
      "question_en": "Mary is a 32-year-old female. She just returned from China. Her flight was delayed multiple times. She was in good health until arriving home when she began experiencing a sharp left sided chest pain and shortness of breath. The pain is worse with motion and deep breathing. The pain has been progressively getting worse and she now has left shoulder pain. She complains of shortness of breath and is very apprehensive about dying. She denies any cough, fever, sputum production or hemoptysis. She is married and has been on birth control pills since the birth of her 3-year-old child. She smokes 1/2 pack of cigarettes per day. She should be referred to the emergency department because she most likely has",
      "question_hant": "瑪麗（Mary）是一位32歲女性，剛從中國返家，班機多次延誤。返家前她身體狀況良好，返家後開始出現左側尖銳胸痛與呼吸急促。此疼痛在活動與深呼吸時會加劇，且逐漸惡化，現在她還出現左肩疼痛。她主訴呼吸急促，並對死亡感到十分焦慮不安。她否認咳嗽、發燒、痰液或咳血。她已婚，自三歲孩子出生後便持續服用口服避孕藥。她每天吸半包菸。因為她最可能罹患下列何者，應轉診至急診室：",
