      "exp_en": "Pulmonary embolism is a blockage of the main artery of the lung or one of its branches by a substance that has traveled from elsewhere in the body through the bloodstream (embolism). Usually this is due to embolism of a thrombus or blood clot from the deep veins in the legs. Risk factors include birth control pills, smoking, and prolonged sitting resulting in the formation of a blood clot.tcmtests.com, December 2019",
      "exp_hant": "肺栓塞是指肺部主動脈或其分支，被隨血流從身體其他部位移動而來的物質（栓子）所阻塞，通常是因腿部深靜脈形成的血栓（栓塞）所致。危險因子包括口服避孕藥、吸菸，以及長時間久坐導致血栓形成。tcmtests.com，2019年12月"
    },
    {
      "number": 829,
      "question_en": "A 75-year old male complains of constipation, poor appetite, and mild lower-abdominal colicky pain. He had a prior history of cholecystectomy and appendectomy. Before the patient could finish filling out the intake history, he became ill, vomited, and the abdominal pain worsened. What condition should be assumed present until proven otherwise?",
      "question_hant": "一位75歲男性主訴便秘、食慾不振，並有輕度下腹絞痛。他過去曾接受過膽囊切除術與闌尾切除術。在他尚未填完問診病史時，便開始出現不適、嘔吐，且腹痛加劇。應假定存在何種狀況，直到排除為止？",
