      "exp_en": "Verbal contracts are legally binding. For a verbal agreement to be binding, the health care provider and client simply need to agree on two things: 1) the services you will perform. 2) what you will receive in exchange. However, a verbal contract can be hard to enforce without a reliable witness, and ideally there should be several. Written contracts are easier to enforce because a clear record of the agreement exists.tcmtests.com, January 2016",
      "exp_hant": "口頭契約具有法律約束力。口頭協議要具有約束力，醫療照護提供者與患者只需就以下兩點達成共識：1）您將提供的服務內容；2）您將獲得的報酬內容。然而，若沒有可靠的目擊者（理想上應有多位），口頭契約可能難以執行。書面契約則因有明確的協議紀錄而較容易執行。tcmtests.com，2016年1月"
