      "exp_en": "The red flag is unilateral ankle/distal calf swelling or asymmetric bilateral swelling greater than 3cm. Deep vein thrombosis (DVT) is assumed present until proven otherwise. In DVT, swelling may be limited to the ankle but usually extends to the calf. In DVT there is often tenderness and skin discoloration of the posterior calf muscle. The edema is pitting. A positive Homan's sign is usually found. In the Homan's sign a forceful dorsiflexion of the ankle produces pain. Pitting ankle edema can be a sign of serious conditions. One sided ankle/distal calf swelling or asymmetric bilateral swelling > 3cm difference is a red flag. DVT without chest pain or shortness of breath should be handled with same-day care in a nearby hospital. DVT with chest pain and SOB requires 911 emergency medical services.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 173-174",
      "exp_hant": "此案例的紅旗警訊為單側腳踝／遠端小腿腫脹，或雙側不對稱腫脹差異大於3公分，應假定為深部靜脈栓塞（DVT），直到排除為止。DVT的腫脹可能僅侷限於腳踝，但通常會延伸至小腿；DVT患者常有小腿後側肌肉的壓痛與膚色改變，水腫呈凹陷性，通常可測得陽性的霍曼氏徵象（Homan's sign）——即強力使腳踝背屈時會誘發疼痛。凹陷性腳踝水腫可能是嚴重疾病的徵象。單側腳踝／遠端小腿腫脹，或雙側不對稱腫脹差異大於3公分，都屬於紅旗警訊。若DVT患者無胸痛或呼吸急促，應於當天至鄰近醫院就醫；若合併胸痛與呼吸急促，則需撥打911緊急送醫。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，頁173-174"
    },
