      "exp_en": "Guidelines for this situation include: 1) The highest priority is the health of the patient; 2) Practitioners should not engage in dual relationships that can influence objectivity and the effectiveness in delivering health services; 3) The practitioner needs to monitor their need to be liked, admired and their romantic and sexual needs. If need be the practitioner can seek guidance and consultation with a trusted source. The default rule to follow is that the health care provider does not use their professional practice as as a source of meeting romantic needs. Entering a personal relationship with the caregiver brother can be hazardous. One, it signals to the patient that her well being is not top priority. The action of starting a relationship with the brother can have a negative impact in taking care of her health needs. If the dual relationship blossoms into a new love, the romantic bond with the brother can surpass the bonding between the doctor and patient. In such scenario, the patient is taking a lesser role in the triad. If the the dual relationship starts off ok but then becomes conflicted, the conflict can spill over into the doctor-patient relationship. The \"One-Year-Rule\" does not apply to a family member who was never one of your patients. However, a relationship with the brother AFTER completing work with the sister is also hazardous. Consider this: what if the patient has a setback and needs to resume her health care with you? What if the patient felt betrayed by you entering a romantic relationship with her brother? When ethical considerations do not provide a clear direction, it is wise to maintain boundaries between professional practice and personal life.Ethics Handbook for Energy Healing Practitioners, Kindle Edition, Feinstein, page 105",
      "exp_hant": "此情境的處理原則包括：1）患者的健康永遠是最優先考量；2）從業人員不應涉入可能影響其客觀性與服務效果的雙重關係；3）從業人員需留意自身想被喜愛、被讚賞，以及浪漫或性方面需求的傾向，必要時可尋求值得信賴人士的指導與諮詢。應遵循的預設原則是：醫療從業人員不應將自己的專業執業，作為滿足浪漫需求的來源。若與擔任照護者角色的哥哥（弟弟）展開私人關係，可能帶來風險。首先，這會向患者傳遞出「她的福祉並非首要考量」的訊息，與其哥哥（弟弟）展開關係的行為，可能對她的健康照護造成負面影響。若這段雙重關係發展成新的戀情，與其哥哥（弟弟）的浪漫連結可能凌駕於醫病之間的連結之上，如此一來，患者在這段三角關係中將淪為次要角色。若這段雙重關係一開始尚可，但後來出現衝突，這種衝突也可能波及到醫病關係。「一年原則」並不適用於從未成為您患者的家屬。然而，即使是在完成對妹妹（姊姊）的治療之後，才與其哥哥（弟弟）展開關係，同樣存在風險：試想，若患者病情復發而需要重新接受您的治療，該怎麼辦？若患者因您與她的哥哥（弟弟）展開戀情而感到被背叛，又該怎麼辦？當倫理考量無法提供明確方向時，明智的做法是維持專業執業與個人生活之間的界線。《能量療癒從業者倫理手冊》，Kindle版，Feinstein著，頁105"
