        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. An acrochordon or a skin tag is a small, soft, common, benign, and usually pedunculated (attaches to the body via an elongated stalk) neoplasm (growth) that is usually found in obese patients. It is often skin colored or hyperpigmented. Most acrochordons are from 2-5 mm in diameter, although some maybe larger. The most frequent location of skin tags are the neck, axillae or groin. Painful lumps are more characteristic of an inflammation or an infection rather than cancer. The general advise for skin tags is that they are benign tumors. Assessing skin growths for possible cancer follows the ABCDE parameters. A IS FOR ASYMMETRY: Moles or freckles are usually symmetrical. In skin cancers one half of the spot is different than the other half of the growth. Some birthmarks will be irregular in shape and are non-cancerous. B IS FOR BORDER: Moles or beauty marks are usually round. Cancerous skin growths have irregular borders, have jagged edges, or have poorly defined borders. C IS FOR COLOR: Normal moles and spots are normally one color. A mole with more than one color should be considered suspicious. Color changes include the darkening of a spot, sometimes to dark purple to black, or a the spot getting lighter in certain areas of the growth. D IS FOR DIAMETER: Skin growths larger than a pencil eraser (about 1/4 inch or greater than 1 cm) need to be referred. This includes skin areas that do not even have the other characteristics of melanoma (asymmetry, color, border). This does not indicate that smaller skin growths should not be investigated. E IS FOR ELEVATED: Elevation means that the growth is raised with an uneven surface. It is both the irregularity of the surface and changes in sizes that raises the red flag. Some sources have E for evolving. That is, the growth over time changes in size, shape, or color.The Complementary Therapist's Guide to Red Flag Referrals, Stephenson, 2013, page 8",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。軟纖維瘤（acrochordon，又稱皮膚贅疣）是一種小型、柔軟、常見的良性增生，通常帶蒂（透過細長的莖與身體相連），多見於肥胖患者，顏色通常與膚色相同或呈色素沉澱。多數軟纖維瘤直徑約2至5毫米，但有些可能更大，最常出現於頸部、腋下或腹股溝。疼痛的腫塊較可能是發炎或感染，而非癌症的特徵。一般而言，皮膚贅疣被視為良性腫瘤。評估皮膚增生是否可能為癌症，可依循ABCDE原則：A代表不對稱（Asymmetry）：痣或雀斑通常是對稱的，皮膚癌則會出現病灶一半與另一半不同的情形；部分胎記形狀不規則，但並非癌症。B代表邊緣（Border）：痣或美人痣的邊緣通常是圓形的，癌性皮膚增生則邊緣不規則、呈鋸齒狀，或邊界模糊不清。C代表顏色（Color）：正常的痣與斑點通常只有一種顏色，若痣出現一種以上的顏色，應視為可疑；顏色變化包括斑點顏色加深（有時呈深紫色至黑色），或病灶某些區域顏色變淺。D代表直徑（Diameter）：直徑大於鉛筆橡皮擦（約1/4吋或大於1公分）的皮膚增生都需要轉診，即使該區域不具備黑色素瘤的其他特徵（不對稱、顏色、邊緣）亦然；但這並不代表較小的皮膚增生就不需要檢查。E代表隆起（Elevated）：隆起是指增生物凸起且表面不平整，表面的不規則性與大小的變化，都是需要警覺的紅旗徵象。部分資料來源將E解釋為演變（evolving），即病灶隨時間在大小、形狀或顏色上發生變化。《輔助療法師紅旗轉診指南》，Stephenson著，2013年，頁8"
    },
