      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. An AED is a small portable electronic device that 1) analyzes heart rhythm and 2) provides an electrical shock. It does not monitor brain rhythm or oxygen levels. The purpose of the electrical shock is to re-establish a normal heart rhythm when it become irregular due to two types of arrhythmias: ventricular fibrillation (VF) and ventricular tachycardia (VT). With cardiac arrest (unresponsive patient, no pulse, no breathing) an AED should be applied as soon as possible. An AED prompts the user to manually deliver a defibrillation shock if it determines that one is needed. Early uses increases survival rate.Basic Life Support, Participant Manual, American Red Cross, 2019, page 23",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。AED是一種小型可攜式電子裝置，其功能為：1）分析心律；2）提供電擊。它並不會監測腦波或血氧濃度。電擊的目的是在心律因兩種心律不整——心室顫動（VF）與心室頻脈（VT）——而變得不規則時，重新建立正常心律。當發生心臟停止（患者無反應、無脈搏、無呼吸）時，應儘快使用AED。若AED判定需要電擊，會提示使用者手動施行去顫電擊。及早使用可提高存活率。《基本救命術學員手冊》，美國紅十字會，2019年，頁23"
    },
    {
