          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "have family member transport patient to emergency department (ED)",
          "hant": "請家屬將病患送往急診室",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "advise patient to resume medication, avoid salt, and caution with exercise",
          "hant": "建議病患恢復服藥、避免鹽分攝取，並小心運動",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency transport",
          "hant": "撥打911緊急送醫",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is sudden SOB in the middle of the night, cough, and bilateral ankle swelling. Paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea (PND) from congestive heart failure (CHF) is assumed present until proven otherwise. Fatigue, SOB, ankle swellings, and exercise intolerance are the symptoms and signs presented with CHF leading to PND. If the patient has chest pain, moderate to severe SOB, pallor, sweating, cyanosis of the lips or nail beds a 911 emergency transport is required. In this situation a same day or next day referral to the PCP is required for evaluation and to resume previously prescribed medications for blood pressure. As an acupuncturist it is not within your legal scope of practice to advise the patient to resume their medication.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 42-43",
      "exp_hant": "警訊為半夜突然呼吸急促、咳嗽及雙側腳踝腫脹。在排除其他可能之前，應假設為鬱血性心衰竭（CHF）所致之陣發性夜間呼吸困難（PND）。疲勞、呼吸急促、腳踝腫脹及運動耐受不良，都是導致PND之CHF的症狀與徵象。若病患出現胸痛、中重度呼吸急促、面色蒼白、出汗、嘴唇或甲床發紺，則需撥打911緊急送醫。在此情況下，應於當天或隔天轉診至基層醫師以進行評估並恢復先前開立的降血壓藥物。身為針灸師，建議病患恢復服藥並不在你的合法執業範圍之內。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第42-43頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 843,
      "question_en": "A patient without a history of allergic reaction calls you and says he has swollen lips. What would help confirm an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis?",
      "question_hant": "一名沒有過敏反應病史的病患打電話告訴你他嘴唇腫脹。以下何者有助於確認為過敏反應與過敏性休克？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "trouble breathing",
          "hant": "呼吸困難",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "swollen face",
          "hant": "臉部腫脹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "skin breaks out in hives",
          "hant": "皮膚出現蕁麻疹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "swollen tongue",
          "hant": "舌頭腫脹",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In this situation the trouble breathing with the swollen lips indicate an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis. Symptoms and signs of shock include excessive thirst, skin feels cool or moist and looks pale or bluish with a possible altered level of consciousness, and rapid-weak heartbeat. There are three situations to consider in assessing an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis depending on whether you know or do not know that the patient has been exposed to an allergen or you suspect that they have. In this situation neither you or the patient knows if they have been exposed to an allergen. YOU DO NOT KNOW IF PATIENT EXPOSED TO ALLERGEN: Any skin reaction (hives, itching, flushing) OR swollen face, neck, tongue or lips PLUS trouble breathing OR symptoms and signs of shock indicates an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis. YOU SUSPECT PATIENT EXPOSED TO ALLERGEN: any two of the following indicates an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis: 1) skin reaction, 2) swelling of face, neck, tongue, or lips, 3) trouble breathing, 4) signs and symptoms of shock, 5) nausea, vomiting, cramping, or diarrhea. YOU KNOW THAT PATIENT EXPOSED TO ALLERGEN: Trouble breathing OR signs and symptoms of shock are an indication for an allergic reaction and anaphylaxis.First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 80-82",
      "exp_hant": "在此情況下，嘴唇腫脹合併呼吸困難顯示為過敏反應與過敏性休克。休克的症狀與徵象包括口渴加劇、皮膚感覺冰冷或濕潤且顏色蒼白或發青、意識程度可能改變，以及心跳快而弱。評估過敏反應與過敏性休克時，依你或病患是否知道（或懷疑）曾暴露於過敏原，可分為三種情況考量。在本情況中，你和病患都不知道是否曾暴露於過敏原。若不知道病患是否暴露於過敏原：任何皮膚反應（蕁麻疹、搔癢、潮紅）或臉部、頸部、舌頭或嘴唇腫脹，合併呼吸困難或休克的症狀與徵象，即顯示為過敏反應與過敏性休克。若懷疑病患曾暴露於過敏原：下列任兩項即顯示為過敏反應與過敏性休克：1）皮膚反應；2）臉部、頸部、舌頭或嘴唇腫脹；3）呼吸困難；4）休克的徵象與症狀；5）噁心、嘔吐、腹絞痛或腹瀉。若已知病患曾暴露於過敏原：呼吸困難或休克的徵象與症狀即為過敏反應與過敏性休克的指標。《急救／心肺復甦術／自動體外心臟去顫器學員手冊》，紅十字會，2016年，第80-82頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 844,
      "question_en": "A 57 year-old male patient had a gradual onset of weakness in his legs accompanied with low back pain. He had difficulty standing from a seated position. During the past 20 years he injured his back several times but with no particular trauma that triggered his back pain. His only other complaint was ED (erectile dysfunction) for the past year. The patient was 5 feet and 9 inches tall and weighed 215 pounds. He had bilateral and slightly decreased muscle strength in the quadriceps muscles. What do you suspect?",
      "question_hant": "一名57歲男性病患逐漸出現雙腿無力，並伴隨下背痛，從坐姿站起有困難。過去20年間他曾多次背部受傷，但並無特定外傷誘發其背痛。他唯一的其他主訴是過去一年來的勃起功能障礙（ED）。病患身高5呎9吋，體重215磅，雙側股四頭肌肌力略為下降。你懷疑是什麼問題？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "cauda equina syndrome",
          "hant": "馬尾症候群",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "osteoarthritis",
          "hant": "骨關節炎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "piriformis syndrome",
          "hant": "梨狀肌症候群",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Sciatica",
          "hant": "坐骨神經痛",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is back pain and progressive bilateral leg weakness and erectile dysfunction in a man >40 years old. Cauda equina syndrome is assumed present until proven otherwise. Cauda equina is a narrowing of the lower spinal canal (spinal stenosis) that puts pressure on sacral nerves causing neurological symptoms and signs. In spinal stenosis there is radiating bilateral leg pain which is worse with standing and walking and improves with rest. At an advanced stage, bowel and bladder problems with impotence may occur. Saddle anesthesia may be detected. Referral to the primary care physician should be made in a timely manner, within a few weeks if cauda equina syndrome has developed. The final consultant will be an orthopedic surgeon.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, page 100",
      "exp_hant": "警訊為背痛、漸進性雙側腿部無力，以及40歲以上男性出現勃起功能障礙。在排除其他可能之前，應假設為馬尾症候群。馬尾症候群是下段脊椎管道狹窄（脊椎狹窄），壓迫薦椎神經，引發神經學症狀與徵象。脊椎狹窄會出現雙側放射性腿痛，站立與行走時加重，休息時緩解。進展至後期可能出現大小便問題及陽痿，並可能檢查出鞍狀麻木。若已發展為馬尾症候群，應及時（數週內）轉診至基層醫師，最終會診對象為骨科醫師。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第100頁"
    },
    {
