      "exp_hant": "無論何種年齡，在下一次按壓前都應讓胸部回彈至正常位置。無論成人、兒童或嬰兒，皆施行30次胸部按壓（雙人CPR則為15次按壓）。《急救／心肺復甦術／自動體外心臟去顫器學員手冊》，紅十字會，2016年，第44頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 846,
      "question_en": "A 19 year-old recently married female requested acupuncture treatment for a two-day old episodes of aching and burning sensation when she urinated. She did not want to take antibiotics because they resulted in a yeast infection later. The patient also reported having chills and feeling slightly feverish. During the interview she complained of right flank pain. Her temperature was 99.5 degrees F. All other vital signs (pulse, breathing, heart rate) are stable. There was tenderness upon palpation at the right costovertebral angle and mild suprapubic tenderness. Which action would you take?",
      "question_hant": "一名19歲剛結婚的女性因兩天前開始出現排尿時刺痛及灼熱感前來要求針灸治療。她不想服用抗生素，因為之前服用後曾導致陰道念珠菌感染。病患也表示有寒顫及輕微發燒的感覺。問診時她主訴右側肋腹疼痛。體溫為華氏99.5度，其餘生命徵象（脈搏、呼吸、心率）皆穩定。觸診發現右側肋脊角壓痛，恥骨上方輕度壓痛。你會採取什麼行動？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "call 911 for emergency transport",
          "hant": "撥打911緊急送醫",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "provide acupuncture treatment for bladder damp-heat",
          "hant": "針對膀胱濕熱進行針灸治療",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "timely (1 week) referral to PCP",
          "hant": "及時（一週內）轉診至基層醫師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "same day referral to PCP",
          "hant": "當天轉診至基層醫師",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is dysuria with high fever, chills, frequent urination, back pain, and malaise. A kidney infection is assumed present until proven otherwise. Patients with a kidney infection have symptoms not shared with simple cystitis. Patients with a kidney infection have pain in the flank or over the kidney as well as significant fever while patients with simple cystitis do not. Chills, nausea, and vomiting combined with dysuria and flank pain greatly increases the possibility of acute pyelonephritis (kidney infection). The patient should be encouraged to drink liquids until the referral is made. The type of referral depends on the severity. Patients with mild fever, dysuria, and stable vital signs should get a same day referral to the PCP or to an urgent care center. If the patient has high fever, shaking chills, and appears septic the patient should be sent directly to the ED with a friend of family member driving. 911 would be called if the patient had cardiopulmonary complaints (low BP, SOB, chest pain).An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 133-134",
      "exp_hant": "警訊為排尿疼痛合併高燒、寒顫、頻尿、背痛及倦怠感。在排除其他可能之前，應假設為腎臟感染。腎臟感染的病患會出現單純膀胱炎所沒有的症狀。腎臟感染的病患會有肋腹或腎臟部位疼痛，並伴隨明顯發燒，而單純膀胱炎則不會。寒顫、噁心、嘔吐合併排尿疼痛與肋腹疼痛，大幅增加急性腎盂腎炎（腎臟感染）的可能性。在轉診之前應鼓勵病患多喝水。轉診的緊急程度依嚴重度而定：輕度發燒、排尿疼痛且生命徵象穩定的病患，應於當天轉診至基層醫師或緊急照護中心；若病患高燒、寒顫發抖並呈現敗血症表現，應由親友駕車直接送往急診室；若病患有心肺方面的主訴（低血壓、呼吸急促、胸痛），則應撥打911。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第133-134頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 847,
      "question_en": "A 30 year-old male requested acupuncture treatment for pain. Prior to the appointment he ate lunch and had a hot dog, potato chips, and a soda. During the interview he complained of his skin itching and feeling hot. He began developing red welts. He remembered having a similar episode last year after eating lobster that required him going to an ED. The patient then developed an itchy throat with his lips beginning to swell but did not have SOB. He did not have any medications to self-administer. His wife was asked to take him to the nearest ED. Which possible condition does the patient have?",
      "question_hant": "一名30歲男性因疼痛前來要求針灸治療。就診前他吃了午餐，內容有熱狗、洋芋片及汽水。問診時他主訴皮膚搔癢並感覺發熱，開始出現紅色風團。他記得去年吃龍蝦後曾發生類似的情況，當時需要送急診。此次病患接著出現喉嚨發癢、嘴唇開始腫脹，但沒有呼吸急促。他沒有可自行使用的藥物，於是請妻子送他到最近的急診室。此病患可能罹患下列何種情況？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Food poisoning",
          "hant": "食物中毒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "anaphylactic shock",
          "hant": "過敏性休克",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "urticaria",
          "hant": "蕁麻疹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "COPD",
          "hant": "慢性阻塞性肺病（COPD）",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The red flag is swelling and itching of the lips after an insect bite or food, herb, supplement, or drug. An impending anaphylactic reaction is assumed present until proven otherwise. The sequence for anaphylactic shock is: 1) flushing, feeling hot, hives, and itching. 2) feeling anxiety and doom. 3) swelling of throat and tongue with hoarseness. 4) difficulty breathing. 5) falling BP, respiratory distress. Dizziness, loss of consciousness. All stages of anaphylaxis are urgent. Not treating the condition can result in death. 911 should be called if the patient has acute respiratory distress. Patients without respiratory distress can be taken the ED by car with a friend or family member driving. If the patient has an epinephrine injector he should immediately self-administer.An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 178-179",
      "exp_hant": "警訊為蟲咬或食物、藥草、保健品、藥物之後出現嘴唇腫脹與搔癢。在排除其他可能之前，應假設為即將發生的過敏性反應。過敏性休克的進程為：1）潮紅、發熱感、蕁麻疹及搔癢；2）出現焦慮及大難臨頭感；3）喉嚨與舌頭腫脹合併聲音沙啞；4）呼吸困難；5）血壓下降、呼吸窘迫、頭暈、意識喪失。過敏性休克的所有階段皆屬緊急狀況，若不治療可能導致死亡。若病患出現急性呼吸窘迫應撥打911；沒有呼吸窘迫的病患可由親友駕車送往急診室；若病患備有腎上腺素注射器，應立即自行注射。《針灸師醫療警訊與轉診指南》，2012年，Anzaldua著，第178-179頁"
