      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate answer. The original record refers to the original notes taken and are the property of medical practitioner. The practitioner can provide COPIES of the original record or the patient can take photos with their smart phone. The fees that can be charged to individuals exercising their right of access to their PHI apply only in cases where the individual is to receive a copy of the PHI, versus merely being provided the opportunity to view and inspect the PHI. A medical offfice may not charge an individual who, while inspecting their PHI, takes notes, uses a smart phone or other device to take pictures of the PHI, or uses other personal resources to capture the information. If the individual is making the copies of PHI using their own resources, the medical office may not charge a fee for those copies, as the copying is being done by the individual and not the entity.www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "這是最準確的答案。病歷正本是指最初撰寫的紀錄，屬於醫療人員的財產。醫療人員可提供病歷正本的「副本」，或病患也可用智慧型手機拍照。針對個人行使查閱其PHI權利所能收取的費用，僅適用於個人要求取得PHI副本的情況，而非僅提供查看與檢視PHI的機會。若病患在查閱其PHI時自行做筆記、使用智慧型手機或其他裝置拍攝PHI，或使用其他自身資源擷取資訊，醫療機構不得就此收費。若個人是以自身資源複製PHI，醫療機構也不得就該複製行為收費，因為複製是由個人自行完成，而非由該機構完成。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
