      "exp_en": "Blood can contain pathogens which can spread and cause infection and illness. Bloodborne pathogens are contained in body fluids containing, visible blood, semen and vaginal secretions, and torn or loose skin. The most common bloodborne pathogens are HIV, HBV, and HCV.Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 69",
      "exp_hant": "血液可能含有病原體，會傳播並導致感染與疾病。血液傳染病原體存在於含有可見血液的體液、精液及陰道分泌物，以及破損或鬆脫的皮膚中。最常見的血液傳染病原體為HIV、HBV及HCV。《針灸風險管理》，CMS Press，Kailin著，1997年，第69頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 864,
      "question_en": "The most commonly used personal protective equipment (PPE) in a health care setting is",
      "question_hant": "在醫療照護場所中最常使用的個人防護裝備（PPE）是",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "goggles",
          "hant": "護目鏡",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "face shields",
          "hant": "面罩",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "gloves",
          "hant": "手套",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "glasses",
          "hant": "眼鏡",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The purpose of standard precautions is to prevent the spread of common infectious pathogens to health care workers, patients, and visitors in any health care setting. PPE is specialized equipment or clothes to protect against infectious pathogens. A lot of patient care involves possible contact with blood, mucous membranes, and other potentially infectious materials (OPIM). Gloves should be used when touching body fluids, blood, excretions, secretions, non-intact skin.Once contaminated, gloves themselves can spread infectious pathogens. Due to possible allergies, avoid the use of latex gloves. Gloves offer no protection for needle stick injuries. Gloves are not required to insert acupuncture needles. However, gloves should be worn when possible contact with blood or OPIM is expected during acupuncture or other treatment modalities. Gloves are not required to remove acupuncture needles. Wearing goggles or face shields should be used with activities such as wet cupping where splashes or sprays of blood can be expected. If the glove tears during use, wash your hands before putting on a new set of gloves.Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 181-183",
      "exp_hant": "標準防護措施的目的，是防止常見感染性病原體傳播給醫護人員、病患及訪客。個人防護裝備是用於防範感染性病原體的專用設備或衣物。許多病患照護工作可能接觸到血液、黏膜及其他潛在感染性物質（OPIM）。接觸體液、血液、排泄物、分泌物或非完整皮膚時應戴手套。手套一旦受到污染，本身也可能傳播感染性病原體。由於可能引發過敏，應避免使用乳膠手套。手套無法防範針扎傷害。插入針灸針時不需要戴手套，但若預期在針灸或其他治療過程中可能接觸到血液或OPIM，則應戴手套。拔除針灸針時也不需要戴手套。從事濕拔罐等可能有血液噴濺的活動時，應配戴護目鏡或面罩。若手套在使用中破裂，應先洗手後再戴上新手套。《潔淨針法》，第七版，第181-183頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 865,
      "question_en": "When should a medical office's privacy policies and procedures be reviewed?",
      "question_hant": "醫療診所的隱私政策與程序應於何時進行檢討？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
