          "hant": "在新進員工受僱之前",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "every other year",
          "hant": "每隔一年",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Every year",
          "hant": "每年",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "when HIPAA regulations are amended",
          "hant": "當HIPAA法規修訂時",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Health care providers should have privacy policies and procedures drafted and in place in their organizations. As certain administrative changes are made, new physical and security measures are implemented, new computer systems, medical record storage, fax machines and other physical arrangements are changed, the privacy policy should reflect these changes. The Privacy Rules require that all employees be trained regarding the HIPAA Privacy Rules.",
      "exp_hant": "醫療照護提供者應在其機構內制定並施行隱私政策與程序。隨著行政上的變更、新的實體及安全措施的實施、新的電腦系統、病歷儲存方式、傳真機及其他實體配置的改變，隱私政策也應反映這些變化。隱私規則要求所有員工皆須接受HIPAA隱私規則的相關訓練。"
    },
    {
      "number": 866,
      "question_en": "You are treating a 37 year-old female patient for migraine headaches. She brought her 9 year-old child with her. You notice that the child looks gaunt and pale. You ask about his health. She says he is doing very well ever since he began fasting on fruits and distilled water for four weeks. What should you do about the child?",
      "question_hant": "你正在為一名37歲女性偏頭痛病患進行治療，她帶著9歲的孩子一同前來。你注意到孩子看起來消瘦蒼白，於是詢問他的健康狀況。母親表示，自從孩子開始只吃水果並喝蒸餾水禁食四週以來，狀況一直非常好。對於這個孩子，你應該怎麼做？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "ask mother if you can start treating the child",
          "hant": "詢問母親是否可以開始為孩子治療",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "refer mother and child to a nutritionist",
          "hant": "將母親與孩子轉介給營養師",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "give mother choice to either get nutritional help for the child or you will need to report it to the state",
          "hant": "讓母親選擇尋求營養協助，否則你將會通報州政府",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "report incident to child protective services",
          "hant": "向兒童保護機構通報此事件",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "All States, Puerto Rico, and the U.S. Virgin Islands have statutes that require health care providers to report suspected child maltreatment to an appropriate agency, such as child protective services, a law enforcement agency, or a State's toll-free child abuse reporting hotline. When child abuse or neglect is suspected in a clinical setting, the physician may determine that release of information without consent is necessary to ensure the health and safety of the child in general. HIPAA permits disclosure of information without legal guardian authorization in matters that affect the treatment of, and medical intervention for, the child and the intervention and investigation of matters that relate to abuse or neglect, public health, and safety. HIPAA also regulates release of information to the legal guardian of the child for situations in which such disclosure may jeopardize the safety of the child.tcmtests.com, August 2017",
      "exp_hant": "美國所有州、波多黎各及美屬維京群島皆有法規要求醫療照護提供者向適當機構（如兒童保護機構、執法機關或該州的兒童虐待通報免付費專線）通報疑似兒童虐待事件。當臨床場合中懷疑有兒童虐待或疏忽情形時，醫師可能認定即使未經同意揭露資訊，也是確保孩子整體健康與安全所必要的。HIPAA允許在未經法定監護人授權的情況下揭露資訊，若該資訊涉及對孩子的治療與醫療介入，以及涉及虐待或疏忽、公共衛生與安全相關事務的介入與調查。HIPAA也規範了在揭露可能危及孩子安全的情況下，向孩子法定監護人揭露資訊的相關規定。tcmtests.com，2017年8月"
    },
    {
      "number": 867,
      "question_en": "In what ways can the HBV (hepatitis B virus) spread?",
      "question_hant": "HBV（B型肝炎病毒）可透過哪些方式傳播？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "sharing razors, sharing toothbrushes, infected mother giving birth",
          "hant": "共用刮鬍刀、共用牙刷、受感染母親生產",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "sharing razors, sharing toothbrushes",
          "hant": "共用刮鬍刀、共用牙刷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "sharing razors, sharing toothbrushes, through kissing",
          "hant": "共用刮鬍刀、共用牙刷、透過接吻",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "through saliva and kissing, sharing toothbrushes, infected mother giving birth",
          "hant": "透過唾液與接吻、共用牙刷、受感染母親生產",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. HBV does not spread via saliva and kissing. HBV spreads through blood and body fluids contaminated with the virus. Patients engaging in high risk behavior such as IV drug use and unprotected sex with multiple partners can spread HBV. Although the virus can be found in saliva, it is not believed to be spread through kissing or sharing utensils. However, kissing an infected person with open sores on the lips can spread the virus. An infected mother can pass the virus to her baby at birth. A toothbrush or razor from an infected person can contain microscopic amounts of blood. Also, an infected person sharing syringes or glucose monitors can transmit the virus. HBV is not spread via contaminated water or food, breast feeding, or casual contact.Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 135 ; www.cdc.gov",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整的答案。HBV不會經由唾液及接吻傳播。HBV是透過受病毒污染的血液及體液傳播。從事高風險行為（如靜脈注射毒品及與多重性伴侶發生無保護性行為）的病患可能傳播HBV。雖然唾液中可檢測到病毒，但一般認為並不會透過接吻或共用餐具傳播；不過，若與嘴唇有開放性傷口的感染者接吻，仍可能傳播病毒。受感染的母親可在生產時將病毒傳給嬰兒。受感染者使用過的牙刷或刮鬍刀可能帶有微量血液。此外，受感染者若與他人共用注射器或血糖監測器，也可能傳播病毒。HBV不會透過受污染的水或食物、哺乳或一般接觸傳播。《潔淨針法》，第七版，第135頁；www.cdc.gov"
    },
    {
      "number": 868,
      "question_en": "Which statement is TRUE about the medical practice personnel (assistants, nurses) having access to PHI (protected health information) ?",
      "question_hant": "關於醫療機構工作人員（助理、護理師）取得PHI（受保護健康資訊）的權限，下列敘述何者正確？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "They have access to all the patient's PHI",
          "hant": "他們可取得病患所有的PHI",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "They have access only those portion of PHI that the patient has agreed to",
          "hant": "他們僅可取得病患同意的那部分PHI",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "They have access to the minimum PHI necessary to perform treatment",
          "hant": "他們可取得執行治療所需之最低限度的PHI",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "There is no regulation",
          "hant": "沒有相關規範",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Access to health care information by health care providers is based on \"need to know\" and \"minimum necessary\" principles. Health care providers are to have access only to information that is necessary in providing patient care. Only the minimum amount of necessary information should be retrieved. The minimum necessary standard is derived from confidentiality codes and practices in common use today. It states that protected health information should not be used or disclosed when it is not necessary to satisfy a particular purpose or carry out a function. The minimum necessary standard requires covered entities to evaluate their practices and enhance safeguards as needed to limit unnecessary or inappropriate access to and disclosure of protected health information. The Privacy Rule requirement for minimum necessity are designed to be sufficiently flexible to accommodate the various circumstances of any covered entity. The Privacy Rule generally requires covered entities to take reasonable steps to limit the use or disclosure of, and requests for, PHI to the minimum necessary to accomplish the intended purpose. The minimum necessary standard DOES NOT APPLY to the following: 1) Disclosures to or requests by a health care provider for treatment purposes. 2) Disclosures to the individual who is the subject of the information. 3) Uses or disclosures made pursuant to an individual's authorization. 4) Uses or disclosures required for compliance with the Health Insurance 5) Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) Administrative Simplification Rules. 6) Disclosures to the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) when disclosure of information is required under the Privacy Rule for enforcement purposes. 7) Uses or disclosures that are required by other law.www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "醫療照護提供者取得健康照護資訊的權限，是依據「知悉需求」與「最低必要」原則。醫療照護提供者僅能取得提供病患照護所必要的資訊，且只能調閱最低限度的必要資訊。「最低必要」標準源自現今普遍使用的保密規範與做法，規定若受保護健康資訊並非達成特定目的或執行某項功能所必需，則不應使用或揭露該資訊。「最低必要」標準要求受保護實體評估其做法，並依需要強化防護措施，以限制對受保護健康資訊不必要或不當的取得與揭露。隱私規則對於最低必要性的要求，設計上具有足夠彈性，可因應各受保護實體的不同情況。隱私規則通常要求受保護實體採取合理措施，將PHI的使用、揭露及索取限制在達成預期目的所需的最低限度內。「最低必要」標準並不適用於下列情形：1）醫療照護提供者為治療目的所做之揭露或索取；2）向資訊當事人本人所做之揭露；3）依個人授權所做之使用或揭露；4）為遵循HIPAA行政簡化規則所需之使用或揭露；5）依隱私規則因執法目的須向美國衛生與公共服務部（HHS）所做之揭露；6）依其他法律要求所做之使用或揭露。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
    },
    {
      "number": 869,
      "question_en": "How long should email communications from the clinic to the patients be retained?",
      "question_hant": "診所寄給病患的電子郵件通訊應保存多久？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "At least six years",
          "hant": "至少六年",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "at least fifteen years",
          "hant": "至少十五年",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "at least ten years",
          "hant": "至少十年",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "at least twenty years",
          "hant": "至少二十年",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Email retention is not specifically mentioned in HIPAA. However, HIPAA does have a data retention and backup policy which applies to PHI (protected health information) regardless of where that information is stored, including email accounts. HIPAA recommends that PHI, privacy notices, breach notifications, patient requests, informed consents, patient complaints, patient authorizations, security reviews, and policies should be retained for at least six years. This includes emails. This means that PHI data and policies should be archived for at least six years. If your state requires a longer retention period then the state regulation takes precedence.www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "HIPAA並未特別針對電子郵件的保存期限做出規定，但HIPAA確實訂有資料保存與備份政策，適用於PHI（受保護健康資訊），無論其儲存於何處，包括電子郵件帳戶在內。HIPAA建議PHI、隱私聲明、資料外洩通知、病患請求、知情同意書、病患投訴、病患授權書、安全審查及相關政策，皆應至少保存六年，這也包括電子郵件在內。也就是說，PHI資料及相關政策應至少保存並封存六年。若所在州法規要求更長的保存期限，則以州法規為準。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
    },
