      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "infected mother to baby, oral contact, sexual contact, HCV can be spread through sharing drug needles",
          "hant": "受感染母親傳給嬰兒、口腔接觸、性接觸、共用毒品針具可傳播HCV",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "sexual contact, HCV can be spread through sharing drug needles",
          "hant": "性接觸、共用毒品針具可傳播HCV",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "infected mother to baby, sexual contact, HCV can be spread through sharing drug needles",
          "hant": "受感染母親傳給嬰兒、性接觸、共用毒品針具可傳播HCV",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "oral contact, sexual contact, HCV can be spread through sharing drug needles",
          "hant": "口腔接觸、性接觸、共用毒品針具可傳播HCV",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "HCV is considered to be transmitted by blood. Any source of blood (like from a razor) can be capable of carrying the virus. However, injecting drug use through the sharing of syringes is the most common form of transmission. If there is poor infection-control practices then tattooing, body piercing practices, and ear-piercing can be vehicles for the transmission of HCV as well as the use of unsterile acupuncture needles. Otherwise, these practices do not increase the risk for HCV infection. Health care settings that use inadequate sterilization of medical equipment is another source as well as needle stick injuries. In some countries, HCV is transmitted via the transfusion of unscreened blood. The hepatitis C virus does not spread through food or water. HCV does not spread by sharing forks/spoons/plates, breast feeding, hugging, kissing, hand holding, coughing, or sneezing. The risk of transmission through sexual contact is believed to be low. Sexual contact risk increases for those who have multiple sex partners, have a sexually transmitted disease or are infected with HIV.Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 140",
      "exp_hant": "HCV被認為是透過血液傳播。任何血液來源（如刮鬍刀）都可能帶有病毒，但透過共用注射器進行藥物注射是最常見的傳播方式。若感染管制措施不佳，刺青、穿環及耳洞等行為也可能成為HCV的傳播途徑，使用未消毒的針灸針同樣可能傳播；但若管制得當，這些行為並不會增加HCV感染風險。醫療場所若醫療器材消毒不當，也是另一項傳染來源，針扎傷害亦然。在某些國家，HCV是透過未經篩檢的輸血傳播。C型肝炎病毒不會透過食物或水傳播；HCV也不會透過共用叉子／湯匙／盤子、哺乳、擁抱、接吻、牽手、咳嗽或打噴嚏傳播。一般認為透過性接觸傳播的風險較低，但有多重性伴侶、患有性傳染病或感染HIV者，其性接觸傳播風險會增加。《潔淨針法》，第七版，第140頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 872,
      "question_en": "The incubation period for HAV is",
      "question_hant": "HAV的潛伏期為",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
