          "key": "D",
          "en": "60 - 100 days",
          "hant": "60至100天",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "HAV (hepatitis A) transmission is most often through food and water which has been contaminated with feces. It can be common in conditions of poor sanitation and overcrowding. In prisons, HAV can spread through sexual contact. HAV has a 15-50 days incubation period (average is 28 days). The symptoms of HAV have an abrupt onset and usually lasts less than two months but can last 6-9 months. Symptoms include an abrupt onset of appetite loss, fatigue, nausea, dark urination, and yellow skin and eyes (jaundice). Once a patient becomes infected with HAV they cannot get the HAV infection again.Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 134",
      "exp_hant": "HAV（A型肝炎）最常見的傳播途徑是透過受糞便污染的食物與水，在衛生條件不佳及過度擁擠的環境中較為常見。在監獄中，HAV可透過性接觸傳播。HAV潛伏期為15至50天（平均為28天）。HAV症狀通常突然發作，一般持續不到兩個月，但也可能持續6至9個月。症狀包括突然出現的食慾不振、疲勞、噁心、深色尿液及皮膚與眼睛發黃（黃疸）。病患一旦感染過HAV，便不會再度感染HAV。《潔淨針法》，第七版，第134頁"
    },
