      "exp_en": "Single use disposable paper towels are recommended to dry hands, not dry linen towels. Any paper/disposable chair, treatment table or any towel, cloth, sheet, gown that comes into patient skin contact has to be new or laundered before use for each patient. OSHA requires a clean and sanitary work space and requires a written schedule for cleaning and decontamination. If an external cleaning service is used, the office manager needs to provide written notification regarding the handling of sharps container. A sink with both hot and cold water needs to be located in or near the treatment rooms. Liquid hand soap and paper towels (no dry linen towels) are to be available at hand washing stations. Also to be provided are alcohol based hand disinfectants.Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 189",
